window.BANK=[{"id":"computer-science","name":"Computer Science","group":"uni","college":"Computing & Informatics","q":[["What is the worst-case time complexity of binary search on a sorted array of n elements?",["O(n)","O(log n)","O(n log n)","O(1)"],1,"Each comparison halves the search range, so at most log2(n) comparisons are needed.","Algorithms"],["Which data structure follows the Last-In, First-Out (LIFO) principle?",["Queue","Stack","Linked list","Binary tree"],1,"A stack adds and removes items at the same end (the top), so the last item pushed is the first popped.","Data structures"],["Which layer of the OSI model is mainly responsible for routing packets between networks?",["Data link layer","Transport layer","Network layer","Session layer"],2,"The network layer (layer 3) uses logical addresses such as IP addresses to route packets across networks.","Networking"],["In SQL, which clause is used to filter groups after a GROUP BY has been applied?",["WHERE","HAVING","ORDER BY","DISTINCT"],1,"WHERE filters individual rows before grouping; HAVING filters the groups produced by GROUP BY, for example on an aggregate such as COUNT(*).","Databases"],["Which CPU scheduling algorithm can cause starvation of long processes?",["First-Come First-Served","Round Robin","Shortest Job First","None of them can"],2,"With Shortest Job First, a steady stream of short jobs can keep a long job waiting indefinitely. FCFS and Round Robin always give every process a turn.","Operating systems"],["How many edges does a complete undirected graph with n vertices have?",["n","n(n - 1)/2","n^2","2n"],1,"Every pair of vertices is joined by one edge, and the number of pairs is n choose 2 = n(n - 1)/2.","Discrete mathematics"],["A relation is in Second Normal Form (2NF) if it is in 1NF and has no ______ dependencies.",["transitive","partial","multivalued","functional"],1,"2NF removes partial dependencies: no non-key attribute may depend on only part of a composite candidate key.","Databases"],["Which of the following is a valid IPv4 address?",["192.168.1.256","10.0.0.1","172.16.300.1","1.2.3"],1,"An IPv4 address has four decimal numbers from 0 to 255 separated by dots. Only 10.0.0.1 meets that rule.","Networking"]]},{"id":"information-technology","name":"Information Technology","group":"uni","college":"Computing & Informatics","q":[["What is the default port number of HTTPS?",["21","80","25","443"],3,"HTTPS uses port 443. HTTP uses 80, FTP uses 21 and SMTP uses 25.","Networking"],["The Domain Name System (DNS) is used to:",["Translate domain names into IP addresses","Encrypt web traffic","Assign MAC addresses","Send email"],0,"DNS works like a phonebook: it turns names such as example.com into the IP addresses computers use to find each other.","Networking"],["What is the decimal value of the binary number 1010?",["8","12","10","5"],2,"1010 in binary = 1x8 + 0x4 + 1x2 + 0x1 = 10.","Number systems"],["Which RAID level mirrors data across two disks?",["RAID 0","RAID 1","RAID 5","RAID 6"],1,"RAID 1 writes identical data to two disks, so the data survives the failure of one disk. RAID 0 only stripes data and has no redundancy.","Systems"],["Which protocol is used to SEND email between servers?",["POP3","IMAP","SMTP","FTP"],2,"SMTP sends mail between servers. POP3 and IMAP are used by clients to retrieve mail.","Networking"],["The subnet mask 255.255.255.0 is written in CIDR notation as:",["/16","/8","/32","/24"],3,"Three full octets of 1s = 24 bits, so the mask is /24, which leaves 8 host bits (254 usable addresses).","Networking"]]},{"id":"software-engineering","name":"Software Engineering","group":"uni","college":"Computing & Informatics","q":[["Which software process model completes each phase fully before moving to the next?",["Spiral model","Waterfall model","Scrum","Prototyping model"],1,"The waterfall model moves in sequence from requirements through design, implementation, testing and maintenance, with little going back.","Process models"],["Black-box testing:",["Tests the code paths line by line","Needs full knowledge of the source code","Tests functionality without knowledge of the internal code","Is performed only by the developer"],2,"Black-box testing checks inputs and outputs against requirements without looking at the internal structure.","Testing"],["Good software design aims for:",["High coupling and low cohesion","Low coupling and high cohesion","High coupling and high cohesion","Low coupling and low cohesion"],1,"Modules should depend on each other as little as possible (low coupling) and each should do one well-defined job (high cohesion).","Design"],["Which UML diagram shows how users interact with a system?",["Class diagram","Sequence diagram","State diagram","Use case diagram"],3,"A use case diagram shows actors and the functions the system provides to them.","Modelling"],["Which of the following is a distributed version control system?",["Git","Excel","Photoshop","Zoom"],0,"Git keeps the full history of a project on every developer's machine, which makes it distributed.","Tools"]]},{"id":"civil-engineering","name":"Civil Engineering","group":"uni","college":"Engineering & Technology","q":[["What is the approximate unit weight of water?",["1 kN/m3","9.81 kN/m3","98.1 kN/m3","0.981 kN/m3"],1,"Water has a density of about 1000 kg/m3. Multiplying by g = 9.81 m/s2 gives a unit weight of about 9.81 kN/m3.","Fluid mechanics"],["A simply supported beam of span L carries a uniformly distributed load w per unit length. What is the maximum bending moment?",["wL^2/2","wL^2/4","wL^2/8","wL/8"],2,"For a simply supported beam with a uniformly distributed load, the maximum bending moment is at mid-span and equals wL^2/8.","Structural analysis"],["Poisson's ratio is the ratio of:",["lateral strain to axial strain","axial stress to lateral stress","shear stress to shear strain","volumetric strain to axial strain"],0,"When a material is stretched it becomes thinner. Poisson's ratio is the magnitude of lateral strain divided by axial strain.","Strength of materials"],["The slump test is used to measure which property of fresh concrete?",["Compressive strength","Durability","Workability","Setting time"],2,"The slump test measures how much a cone of fresh concrete settles, which indicates its workability (consistency).","Concrete technology"],["The plasticity index of a soil is calculated as:",["Liquid limit + Plastic limit","Liquid limit - Plastic limit","Plastic limit - Shrinkage limit","Liquid limit x Plastic limit"],1,"Plasticity index (PI) = Liquid limit (LL) - Plastic limit (PL). It is the range of water content over which the soil behaves plastically.","Soil mechanics"],["Young's modulus E is defined as:",["Strain / Stress","Stress x Strain","Stress / Strain","Force / Length"],2,"Within the elastic limit, stress is proportional to strain (Hooke's law). The constant of proportionality, stress divided by strain, is Young's modulus.","Strength of materials"]]},{"id":"electrical-engineering","name":"Electrical & Computer Engineering","group":"uni","college":"Engineering & Technology","q":[["A 12 V battery is connected across a 4 ohm resistor. What current flows?",["48 A","0.33 A","8 A","3 A"],3,"By Ohm's law I = V / R = 12 / 4 = 3 A.","Circuit analysis"],["Three resistors of 10, 20 and 30 ohms are connected in series. What is the total resistance?",["60 ohms","5.45 ohms","20 ohms","600 ohms"],0,"In series, resistances add: 10 + 20 + 30 = 60 ohms.","Circuit analysis"],["An AC signal has a period of 20 ms. What is its frequency?",["20 Hz","100 Hz","50 Hz","200 Hz"],2,"Frequency is the reciprocal of the period: f = 1 / 0.02 s = 50 Hz.","AC fundamentals"],["An ideal transformer has 100 primary turns and 500 secondary turns. With 220 V on the primary, what is the secondary voltage?",["44 V","110 V","660 V","1100 V"],3,"Vs / Vp = Ns / Np, so Vs = 220 x 500 / 100 = 1100 V. More secondary turns than primary turns makes it a step-up transformer.","Machines"],["Which logic gate gives a HIGH output only when all of its inputs are HIGH?",["AND gate","OR gate","NAND gate","XOR gate"],0,"An AND gate outputs 1 only if every input is 1. An OR gate needs just one high input.","Digital electronics"],["The capacitive reactance of a capacitor C at frequency f is given by:",["2 pi f C","1 / (2 pi f C)","2 pi f / C","C / (2 pi f)"],1,"Xc = 1 / (2 pi f C). Reactance falls as frequency or capacitance rises, so capacitors pass high frequencies more easily.","AC fundamentals"]]},{"id":"mechanical-engineering","name":"Mechanical Engineering","group":"uni","college":"Engineering & Technology","q":[["The first law of thermodynamics is a statement of:",["Conservation of energy","Conservation of momentum","Increase of entropy","Heat flows from hot to cold"],0,"The first law says energy cannot be created or destroyed: the change in internal energy equals heat added minus work done by the system.","Thermodynamics"],["A Carnot engine works between 600 K and 300 K. What is its efficiency?",["25%","75%","100%","50%"],3,"Carnot efficiency = 1 - Tc / Th = 1 - 300 / 600 = 0.5, or 50%. Temperatures must be in kelvin.","Thermodynamics"],["What is the SI unit of torque?",["Newton-metre (N m)","Newton per metre","Joule per second","Pascal"],0,"Torque is force multiplied by perpendicular distance, so its unit is the newton-metre.","Mechanics"],["The Reynolds number is the ratio of:",["Gravity forces to inertial forces","Inertial forces to viscous forces","Viscous forces to surface tension forces","Pressure forces to gravity forces"],1,"Re = rho v D / mu is the ratio of inertial to viscous forces. Low values mean laminar flow; high values mean turbulent flow.","Fluid mechanics"],["A force of 10 kN acts on a cross-section of 500 mm2. What is the stress?",["0.02 MPa","5 MPa","50 MPa","20 MPa"],3,"Stress = Force / Area = 10 000 N / 500 mm2 = 20 N/mm2 = 20 MPa.","Strength of materials"],["What is the correct order of the strokes in a four-stroke petrol engine?",["Intake, compression, power, exhaust","Intake, power, compression, exhaust","Compression, intake, exhaust, power","Power, intake, compression, exhaust"],0,"The piston draws in the mixture (intake), compresses it, the spark ignites it to push the piston (power), and the burnt gases are expelled (exhaust).","Engines"]]},{"id":"accounting-finance","name":"Accounting & Finance","group":"uni","college":"Business & Economics","q":[["Which equation is the basic accounting equation?",["Assets = Liabilities - Equity","Assets = Liabilities + Owner's equity","Equity = Assets + Liabilities","Liabilities = Assets + Equity"],1,"Everything a business owns (assets) is financed either by outsiders (liabilities) or by the owner (equity): Assets = Liabilities + Owner's equity.","Fundamentals"],["Which of the following is a current asset?",["Land","Cash","Building","Goodwill"],1,"Current assets are cash and items expected to be turned into cash within one year or one operating cycle. Land, buildings and goodwill are long-term assets.","Fundamentals"],["What is the normal balance of a revenue account?",["Debit","Credit","Either, depending on the month","Revenue accounts have no normal balance"],1,"Revenue increases owner's equity, and equity increases with credits, so revenue accounts normally have credit balances.","Double entry"],["A business buys equipment on credit. What is the effect on the accounting equation?",["Assets up, Liabilities down","Assets up, Liabilities up","Assets down, Equity up","No effect"],1,"Equipment (an asset) increases and Accounts Payable (a liability) increases by the same amount, so both sides of the equation rise equally.","Double entry"],["Equipment costs 50,000 birr, has a salvage value of 5,000 birr and a useful life of 5 years. What is the annual straight-line depreciation?",["10,000 birr","9,000 birr","11,000 birr","5,000 birr"],1,"Straight-line depreciation = (cost - salvage value) / useful life = (50,000 - 5,000) / 5 = 9,000 birr per year.","Depreciation"],["Which principle requires expenses to be recorded in the same period as the revenues they helped to earn?",["Going concern","Matching principle","Materiality","Consistency"],1,"The matching principle links expenses to the revenue they generate so that profit for each period is measured fairly.","Principles"],["What is the main purpose of a trial balance?",["To show the financial position of the business","To check that total debits equal total credits","To calculate net profit","To record transactions"],1,"A trial balance lists all ledger balances to test the arithmetic accuracy of double entry: total debits must equal total credits.","Double entry"],["How is gross profit calculated?",["Net sales - Operating expenses","Net sales - Cost of goods sold","Net sales + Cost of goods sold","Revenue - Taxes"],1,"Gross profit = Net sales - Cost of goods sold. Operating expenses are deducted afterwards to reach operating profit.","Financial statements"]]},{"id":"management","name":"Management","group":"uni","college":"Business & Economics","q":[["Which of the following is NOT one of the four classic functions of management?",["Planning","Organizing","Marketing","Controlling"],2,"The four classic functions are planning, organizing, leading (directing) and controlling. Marketing is a business function, not a management function.","Fundamentals"],["In Maslow's hierarchy, which need is at the top?",["Safety","Self-actualization","Esteem","Social"],1,"The hierarchy runs from physiological and safety needs, through social and esteem needs, to self-actualization at the top.","Motivation"],["Scientific management is associated with:",["Frederick W. Taylor","Henri Fayol","Max Weber","Elton Mayo"],0,"Taylor developed scientific management. Fayol is known for administrative principles, Weber for bureaucracy and Mayo for the Hawthorne studies.","Management theories"],["In a SWOT analysis, which pair describes INTERNAL factors?",["Opportunities and threats","Strengths and opportunities","Weaknesses and threats","Strengths and weaknesses"],3,"Strengths and weaknesses lie inside the organization. Opportunities and threats come from the external environment.","Strategy"],["Span of control refers to:",["The number of subordinates a manager directly supervises","The length of a manager's career","The budget a manager controls","The number of departments in a firm"],0,"A wide span of control means a manager supervises many people directly, which tends to give a flatter organization.","Organizing"],["In Herzberg's two-factor theory, salary is mainly a:",["Motivator","Hygiene factor","Achievement factor","Growth factor"],1,"Hygiene factors (pay, conditions, policies) prevent dissatisfaction but do not by themselves motivate. Motivators include achievement and recognition.","Motivation"]]},{"id":"economics","name":"Economics","group":"uni","college":"Business & Economics","q":[["According to the law of demand, when the price of a good rises (ceteris paribus), the quantity demanded:",["Rises","Stays the same","Falls","Doubles"],2,"Price and quantity demanded move in opposite directions, which gives the downward-sloping demand curve.","Microeconomics"],["GDP is best defined as:",["The value of all goods and services a country exports","The market value of final goods and services produced within a country in a period","The total income of the government","The total savings of households"],1,"GDP measures the market value of all final goods and services produced inside a country's borders in a given period, usually a year.","Macroeconomics"],["The price of a good rises by 10% and the quantity demanded falls by 20%. What is the price elasticity of demand (absolute value)?",["0.5","2","10","30"],1,"Elasticity = %change in quantity / %change in price = 20 / 10 = 2. Because it is greater than 1, demand is elastic.","Microeconomics"],["Which of the following is a feature of perfect competition?",["A single seller","Differentiated products","Barriers to entry","Many buyers and sellers selling identical products"],3,"Perfect competition has many small buyers and sellers, a homogeneous product, free entry and exit, and firms that are price takers.","Market structures"],["In economics, inflation is best described as:",["A sustained rise in the general price level","A fall in the exchange rate only","A rise in the price of one good","An increase in unemployment"],0,"Inflation is a sustained increase in the general level of prices, which reduces the purchasing power of money.","Macroeconomics"],["In economics, opportunity cost is:",["The money paid for a good","The cost of production","The value of the next best alternative given up","The tax on a good"],2,"Because resources are scarce, choosing one option means giving up others. The value of the best forgone option is the opportunity cost.","Fundamentals"]]},{"id":"medicine","name":"Medicine","group":"uni","college":"Health Sciences","q":[["What is the normal resting heart rate of a healthy adult?",["40-50 beats per minute","60-100 beats per minute","110-140 beats per minute","150-180 beats per minute"],1,"The accepted normal range for adults at rest is 60 to 100 beats per minute.","Physiology"],["Deficiency of which vitamin causes scurvy?",["Vitamin A","Vitamin D","Vitamin K","Vitamin C"],3,"Vitamin C is needed for collagen synthesis. Its deficiency causes scurvy, with bleeding gums and poor wound healing.","Nutrition"],["Which organism is the most common cause of community-acquired bacterial pneumonia?",["Streptococcus pneumoniae","Escherichia coli","Pseudomonas aeruginosa","Candida albicans"],0,"Streptococcus pneumoniae (pneumococcus) is the leading cause of community-acquired bacterial pneumonia worldwide.","Infectious disease"],["Insulin is secreted by which cells?",["Alpha cells of the pancreas","Hepatocytes of the liver","Beta cells of the pancreas","Cells of the adrenal cortex"],2,"Beta cells of the islets of Langerhans in the pancreas make insulin. Alpha cells make glucagon.","Endocrinology"],["Malaria is transmitted to humans by the bite of:",["The female Anopheles mosquito","The male Anopheles mosquito","The tsetse fly","The female Aedes mosquito"],0,"Plasmodium parasites are carried by female Anopheles mosquitoes, which need a blood meal to develop their eggs.","Infectious disease"],["Which heart chamber pumps oxygenated blood into the aorta?",["Right atrium","Right ventricle","Left atrium","Left ventricle"],3,"The left ventricle has the thickest wall and pumps oxygen-rich blood through the aortic valve into the systemic circulation.","Anatomy"]]},{"id":"nursing","name":"Nursing","group":"uni","college":"Health Sciences","q":[["What is the normal respiratory rate of a resting adult?",["12-20 breaths per minute","5-8 breaths per minute","25-35 breaths per minute","40-50 breaths per minute"],0,"A healthy resting adult breathes about 12 to 20 times per minute.","Vital signs"],["What is the single most effective way to prevent the spread of infection in a health facility?",["Wearing a gown at all times","Using antibiotics routinely","Cleaning floors once a day","Hand hygiene"],3,"Hand hygiene before and after patient contact is the most effective and simplest measure against healthcare-associated infection.","Infection prevention"],["Which of the following is one of the \"rights\" of safe medication administration?",["Right doctor's signature","Right dose","Right hospital","Right colour"],1,"The classic rights are right patient, right drug, right dose, right route and right time.","Pharmacology for nurses"],["Which position is most helpful for a patient who has difficulty breathing?",["Supine (flat on the back)","Prone (face down)","Fowler's (semi-sitting)","Lithotomy"],2,"Sitting upright lets the diaphragm move down and the lungs expand more easily, which eases breathing.","Fundamentals of nursing"],["Standard precautions should be applied to:",["All patients, whatever their diagnosis","Only patients known to have HIV","Only patients in isolation rooms","Only surgical patients"],0,"Standard precautions treat blood and body fluids of every patient as potentially infectious, so they apply to everyone.","Infection prevention"],["The normal axillary body temperature of a healthy adult is about:",["32 degrees C","36.5 degrees C","39 degrees C","41 degrees C"],1,"Normal body temperature is roughly 36.5 to 37.5 degrees C. Readings of 38 degrees C or more suggest fever.","Vital signs"]]},{"id":"pharmacy","name":"Pharmacy","group":"uni","college":"Health Sciences","q":[["Which route of administration gives 100% bioavailability?",["Oral","Intramuscular","Intravenous","Rectal"],2,"An intravenous dose goes straight into the circulation, so all of it is available. Other routes lose some drug to absorption or first-pass metabolism.","Pharmacokinetics"],["What is the antidote for paracetamol (acetaminophen) overdose?",["Naloxone","N-acetylcysteine","Atropine","Flumazenil"],1,"N-acetylcysteine replenishes glutathione and protects the liver from the toxic paracetamol metabolite. It works best when given early.","Toxicology"],["Amoxicillin belongs to which class of antibiotics?",["Penicillins (beta-lactams)","Macrolides","Tetracyclines","Aminoglycosides"],0,"Amoxicillin is an aminopenicillin, a beta-lactam that blocks bacterial cell-wall synthesis.","Pharmacology"],["The half-life of a drug is the time taken for:",["The drug to be fully eliminated","The drug to start working","The plasma concentration to fall by half","The drug to reach its peak concentration"],2,"Half-life is the time for the plasma concentration to fall to 50% of its value, assuming first-order elimination.","Pharmacokinetics"],["Naloxone is used to reverse the effects of:",["Benzodiazepines","Opioids","Anticoagulants","Organophosphates"],1,"Naloxone is a competitive opioid antagonist that reverses respiratory depression caused by opioid overdose.","Toxicology"],["What fraction of a drug remains after four half-lives (first-order elimination)?",["1/4","1/8","1/32","1/16"],3,"Each half-life halves the amount: 1/2, 1/4, 1/8, 1/16. That is 6.25% remaining.","Pharmacokinetics"]]},{"id":"public-health","name":"Public Health","group":"uni","college":"Health Sciences","q":[["Incidence is the number of:",["New cases of a disease in a population during a period","All existing cases at one point in time","Deaths from all causes","People vaccinated"],0,"Incidence counts new cases over a period of time. Prevalence counts all existing cases, new and old.","Epidemiology"],["Immunization is an example of which level of prevention?",["Secondary prevention","Tertiary prevention","Primary prevention","Rehabilitation"],2,"Primary prevention stops disease before it occurs. Secondary prevention finds disease early (screening) and tertiary reduces the impact of established disease.","Prevention"],["The 1978 Declaration of Alma-Ata promoted:",["Mandatory vaccination","Primary health care as the key to \"Health for All\"","The eradication of smallpox","Private health insurance"],1,"The Alma-Ata Declaration set primary health care as the approach to achieving \"Health for All\".","Health systems"],["The crude birth rate is usually expressed per:",["100 people","1 000 population","100 000 population","10 women"],1,"Crude birth rate = live births in a year divided by mid-year population, multiplied by 1 000.","Demography"],["Sensitivity of a screening test is:",["True negatives / all people without the disease","True positives / all positive results","True positives / (true positives + false negatives)","False positives / all people tested"],2,"Sensitivity is the proportion of people who truly have the disease whom the test correctly identifies.","Epidemiology"],["Which study design gives the strongest evidence of cause and effect?",["Randomized controlled trial","Case report","Cross-sectional survey","Ecological study"],0,"Random allocation balances known and unknown confounders between groups, so the randomized controlled trial is the strongest design for testing cause and effect.","Epidemiology"]]},{"id":"mathematics","name":"Mathematics","group":"uni","college":"Natural & Computational Sciences","q":[["What is the derivative of x^3 with respect to x?",["x^2","3x^2","3x","x^3/3"],1,"By the power rule, d/dx of x^n is n x^(n-1), so d/dx of x^3 = 3x^2.","Calculus"],["Evaluate the integral of 2x dx.",["x^2 + C","2x^2 + C","x + C","2 + C"],0,"The integral of x^n is x^(n+1)/(n+1), so the integral of 2x is 2 * x^2/2 = x^2, plus the constant C.","Calculus"],["What are the solutions of x^2 - 5x + 6 = 0?",["x = 1 and x = 6","x = 2 and x = 3","x = -2 and x = -3","x = 5 and x = 6"],1,"Factor: x^2 - 5x + 6 = (x - 2)(x - 3). Setting each factor to zero gives x = 2 and x = 3.","Algebra"],["What is the determinant of the matrix [[2, 1], [3, 4]]?",["5","11","8","-5"],0,"For a 2x2 matrix [[a, b], [c, d]] the determinant is ad - bc = 2*4 - 1*3 = 5.","Linear algebra"],["What is the limit of sin(x)/x as x approaches 0?",["0","1","Infinity","It does not exist"],1,"This is a standard limit: sin(x)/x approaches 1 as x approaches 0 (it can be shown with the squeeze theorem).","Calculus"],["What is the sum of the interior angles of a hexagon?",["540 degrees","720 degrees","900 degrees","360 degrees"],1,"The sum of interior angles of an n-sided polygon is (n - 2) * 180 degrees. For n = 6 that is 4 * 180 = 720 degrees.","Geometry"],["In how many different ways can 4 distinct books be arranged on a shelf?",["16","24","12","4"],1,"The number of arrangements of 4 distinct objects is 4! = 4 * 3 * 2 * 1 = 24.","Combinatorics"],["What is the derivative of ln(x) for x > 0?",["ln(x)/x","1/x","x","e^x"],1,"The natural logarithm is the inverse of e^x, and its derivative is 1/x.","Calculus"]]},{"id":"physics","name":"Physics","group":"uni","college":"Natural & Computational Sciences","q":[["What is the SI unit of force?",["Joule","Watt","Pascal","Newton"],3,"Force is measured in newtons: 1 N is the force that gives a 1 kg mass an acceleration of 1 m/s2.","Mechanics"],["A car starts from rest and accelerates at 2 m/s2 for 5 s. What is its final speed?",["10 m/s","5 m/s","2.5 m/s","25 m/s"],0,"v = u + at = 0 + 2 x 5 = 10 m/s.","Kinematics"],["What is the kinetic energy of a 2 kg object moving at 3 m/s?",["6 J","12 J","9 J","18 J"],2,"KE = (1/2) m v^2 = 0.5 x 2 x 9 = 9 J.","Energy"],["Newton's third law states that:",["Force equals mass times acceleration","Every action has an equal and opposite reaction","An object stays at rest unless acted on by a force","Energy is conserved"],1,"When one body exerts a force on another, the second exerts an equal and opposite force on the first.","Mechanics"],["The speed of light in vacuum is approximately:",["3 x 10^8 m/s","3 x 10^6 m/s","3 x 10^5 m/s","340 m/s"],0,"Light travels at about 299 792 458 m/s, which is roughly 3 x 10^8 m/s.","Modern physics"],["Which of the following is a vector quantity?",["Mass","Speed","Temperature","Velocity"],3,"Velocity has both magnitude and direction. Mass, speed and temperature have magnitude only.","Mechanics"]]},{"id":"chemistry","name":"Chemistry","group":"uni","college":"Natural & Computational Sciences","q":[["The atomic number of an element is the number of:",["Neutrons in the nucleus","Protons in the nucleus","Electrons in the outer shell","Protons plus neutrons"],1,"The atomic number is the number of protons, which defines the element. Protons plus neutrons give the mass number.","Atomic structure"],["What is the pH of pure water at 25 degrees C?",["0","14","1","7"],3,"Pure water is neutral: [H+] = [OH-] = 10^-7 mol/L, so pH = 7.","Acids and bases"],["Avogadro's number is approximately:",["6.022 x 10^23","3.0 x 10^8","1.6 x 10^-19","9.81"],0,"One mole of any substance contains 6.022 x 10^23 particles.","Mole concept"],["What is the molar mass of water (H2O)? (H = 1, O = 16)",["16 g/mol","34 g/mol","18 g/mol","20 g/mol"],2,"2 x 1 + 16 = 18 g/mol.","Mole concept"],["What type of bond holds sodium chloride (NaCl) together?",["Covalent bond","Ionic bond","Metallic bond","Hydrogen bond"],1,"Sodium gives an electron to chlorine, forming Na+ and Cl- ions that attract each other: an ionic bond.","Chemical bonding"],["Which of the following is a noble gas?",["Neon","Nitrogen","Oxygen","Chlorine"],0,"Neon is in group 18 and has a full outer shell, so it is almost completely unreactive.","Periodic table"]]},{"id":"biology","name":"Biology","group":"uni","college":"Natural & Computational Sciences","q":[["Which organelle is known as the \"powerhouse of the cell\"?",["Nucleus","Ribosome","Golgi apparatus","Mitochondrion"],3,"Mitochondria carry out aerobic respiration and make most of the cell's ATP.","Cell biology"],["In DNA, adenine pairs with:",["Thymine","Guanine","Cytosine","Uracil"],0,"In DNA, adenine pairs with thymine (two hydrogen bonds) and guanine pairs with cytosine (three). Uracil replaces thymine in RNA.","Genetics"],["Photosynthesis takes place mainly in the:",["Mitochondria","Chloroplasts","Nucleus","Vacuole"],1,"Chloroplasts contain chlorophyll, which captures light energy to make glucose from carbon dioxide and water.","Plant biology"],["Two heterozygous parents (Aa x Aa) have children. What is the probability of an aa child?",["1/2","3/4","1/4","0"],2,"The cross gives AA : Aa : aa in the ratio 1 : 2 : 1, so aa has a probability of 1/4.","Genetics"],["The movement of water across a semipermeable membrane from low to high solute concentration is called:",["Osmosis","Diffusion of solutes","Active transport","Endocytosis"],0,"Osmosis is the net movement of water through a semipermeable membrane toward the region with more solute.","Cell biology"],["Enzymes speed up reactions by:",["Adding energy to the reaction","Being used up in the reaction","Changing the products","Lowering the activation energy"],3,"Enzymes are biological catalysts. They lower the activation energy and are not used up.","Biochemistry"]]},{"id":"statistics","name":"Statistics","group":"uni","college":"Natural & Computational Sciences","q":[["What is the mean of 2, 4, 6, 8 and 10?",["5","6","7","30"],1,"Sum = 30 and there are 5 values, so the mean is 30 / 5 = 6.","Descriptive statistics"],["What is the median of 3, 7, 1, 9 and 5?",["5","7","1","25"],0,"Sorted: 1, 3, 5, 7, 9. The middle value is 5.","Descriptive statistics"],["The standard deviation is:",["The square of the variance","The difference between the largest and smallest value","The square root of the variance","The average of the data"],2,"Standard deviation = square root of variance, so it is in the same units as the data.","Descriptive statistics"],["Two fair coins are tossed. What is the probability of getting two heads?",["1/2","1/3","1/2 or 1/3","1/4"],3,"Each toss has probability 1/2 of heads and the tosses are independent, so P = 1/2 x 1/2 = 1/4.","Probability"],["A Type I error occurs when we:",["Reject a true null hypothesis","Accept a false null hypothesis","Reject a false null hypothesis","Accept a true null hypothesis"],0,"A Type I error is a false positive: rejecting H0 when it is actually true. Its probability is the significance level alpha.","Hypothesis testing"],["What is the mode of 2, 3, 3, 4, 5, 3, 6?",["4","3","5","2"],1,"The mode is the most frequent value. The number 3 appears three times.","Descriptive statistics"]]},{"id":"law","name":"Law","group":"uni","college":"Social Sciences & Humanities","q":[["Under the FDRE Constitution, the supreme law of the land is:",["The Civil Code","The Criminal Code","The Constitution","Federal proclamations"],2,"Article 9 of the FDRE Constitution states that the Constitution is the supreme law of the land and any law or decision contrary to it is of no effect.","Constitutional law"],["In criminal law, \"actus reus\" means:",["The guilty mind","The guilty act","The burden of proof","The standard of proof"],1,"Actus reus is the physical element of a crime (the act or omission). Mens rea is the mental element (the guilty mind).","Criminal law"],["In a criminal trial the burden of proof lies on the prosecution and the standard is:",["Balance of probabilities","Beyond reasonable doubt","Reasonable suspicion","Preponderance of opinion"],1,"The prosecution must prove guilt beyond reasonable doubt, a higher standard than the balance of probabilities used in civil cases.","Criminal procedure"],["The doctrine that courts should follow earlier decisions on similar facts is called:",["Stare decisis","Res judicata","Ultra vires","Habeas corpus"],0,"Stare decisis means \"to stand by things decided\". Res judicata bars re-litigating a matter already decided between the same parties.","Legal theory"],["The separation of powers divides government into:",["Federal, regional and local","Civil, criminal and administrative","Legislative, executive and judicial","Public, private and mixed"],2,"The legislature makes law, the executive carries it out and the judiciary interprets and applies it.","Constitutional law"],["Which body has the power to interpret the FDRE Constitution?",["The Federal Supreme Court","The Council of Ministers","The House of Peoples' Representatives","The House of Federation"],3,"Article 62 of the FDRE Constitution gives the House of Federation the power to interpret the Constitution, assisted by the Council of Constitutional Inquiry.","Constitutional law"]]},{"id":"psychology","name":"Psychology","group":"uni","college":"Social Sciences & Humanities","q":[["Who is regarded as the founder of psychoanalysis?",["Sigmund Freud","Carl Rogers","B. F. Skinner","Jean Piaget"],0,"Sigmund Freud developed psychoanalysis, which emphasizes unconscious processes and early childhood experience.","History of psychology"],["Classical conditioning was first described by:",["Albert Bandura","Ivan Pavlov","Abraham Maslow","Erik Erikson"],1,"Pavlov showed that dogs learn to salivate to a neutral stimulus (a bell) paired with food.","Learning"],["In Piaget's theory, the first stage of cognitive development is the:",["Concrete operational stage","Formal operational stage","Sensorimotor stage","Preoperational stage"],2,"The stages are sensorimotor (0-2 years), preoperational, concrete operational and formal operational.","Developmental psychology"],["Operant conditioning, in which behaviour is shaped by its consequences, is associated with:",["Ivan Pavlov","Sigmund Freud","Carl Jung","B. F. Skinner"],3,"Skinner showed that reinforced behaviour becomes more likely and punished behaviour less likely.","Learning"],["The reliability of a psychological test refers to its:",["Consistency of results","Length","Popularity","Cost"],0,"A reliable test gives consistent results when repeated. Validity is a separate question: whether it measures what it claims to measure.","Research methods"]]},{"id":"geography","name":"Geography & Environmental Studies","group":"uni","college":"Social Sciences & Humanities","q":[["Which is the largest ocean on Earth?",["Atlantic Ocean","Pacific Ocean","Indian Ocean","Arctic Ocean"],1,"The Pacific covers about one third of the Earth's surface and is larger than all the land combined.","Physical geography"],["Which is the longest river in Africa?",["Congo","Niger","Zambezi","Nile"],3,"The Nile, at about 6 650 km, is the longest river in Africa.","Physical geography"],["The Blue Nile (Abay) rises from which lake?",["Lake Tana","Lake Ziway","Lake Abaya","Lake Langano"],0,"The Blue Nile flows out of Lake Tana in the northwestern highlands of Ethiopia.","Geography of Ethiopia"],["The lowest point in Ethiopia is in the:",["Rift Valley lakes","Ogaden lowlands","Danakil Depression","Omo Valley"],2,"The Danakil Depression in the Afar region lies well below sea level, among the lowest places on land in the world.","Geography of Ethiopia"],["The highest peak in Ethiopia is:",["Mount Zuqualla","Ras Dashen","Mount Entoto","Mount Batu"],1,"Ras Dashen in the Simien Mountains, at about 4 550 m, is the highest peak in Ethiopia.","Geography of Ethiopia"],["Lines of latitude are imaginary lines that:",["Run from pole to pole","Measure east-west position","Run parallel to the equator","Divide the earth into time zones"],2,"Lines of latitude run east-west parallel to the equator and measure how far north or south a place is. Longitude runs pole to pole.","Map work"]]},{"id":"english","name":"English Language & Literature","group":"uni","college":"Social Sciences & Humanities","q":[["What is the past tense of the verb \"go\"?",["Goed","Gone","Went","Going"],2,"\"Go\" is irregular: go - went - gone. \"Gone\" is the past participle.","Grammar"],["Which word is closest in meaning to \"rapid\"?",["Slow","Quick","Heavy","Quiet"],1,"\"Rapid\" means moving or happening fast, so \"quick\" is its synonym.","Vocabulary"],["Which sentence is grammatically correct?",["She doesn't like coffee.","She don't like coffee.","She not like coffee.","She no likes coffee."],0,"With a third-person singular subject (she), the auxiliary is \"doesn't\" (does not).","Grammar"],["Which word is the opposite of \"ancient\"?",["Old","Historic","Elderly","Modern"],3,"\"Ancient\" means very old. Its antonym is \"modern\".","Vocabulary"],["Which sentence is in the passive voice?",["He wrote the book.","The book was written by him.","He is writing a book.","He will write the book."],1,"In the passive voice the object of the action becomes the subject: \"The book was written by him.\"","Grammar"],["Choose the correct word: \"Neither of the boys ___ here.\"",["is","are","were","be"],0,"\"Neither\" is treated as singular when used as a pronoun, so it takes a singular verb: \"Neither of the boys is here.\"","Grammar"]]},{"id":"civics","name":"Civics & Ethical Education","group":"uni","college":"Social Sciences & Humanities","q":[["The FDRE Constitution was adopted in December 1994. In which year did it come into force?",["1991","1995","1987","2000"],1,"The Constitution was adopted on 8 December 1994 and came into force in August 1995, when the FDRE was established.","Constitution"],["The Federal Parliamentary Assembly of Ethiopia consists of:",["The House of Peoples' Representatives and the House of Federation","The Senate and the Congress","The Council of Ministers and the House of Federation","The Supreme Court and the House of Peoples' Representatives"],0,"Parliament has two chambers: the House of Peoples' Representatives and the House of Federation.","Government structure"],["The word \"democracy\" literally means:",["Rule by the army","Rule by one person","Rule by the wealthy","Rule by the people"],3,"It comes from the Greek demos (people) and kratos (rule): government by the people, directly or through elected representatives.","Democracy"],["The rule of law means that:",["Only the government must obey the law","Laws apply to everyone, including those in power","Courts make all laws","The law changes with each leader"],1,"Under the rule of law, everyone, including officials, is subject to the law and is treated equally before it.","Constitutionalism"],["Which of the following is a civic duty of a citizen?",["Paying taxes","Choosing the government's budget","Writing laws alone","Appointing judges"],0,"Citizens have duties as well as rights, such as respecting the law, paying taxes and respecting the rights of others.","Citizenship"]]},{"id":"plant-science","name":"Plant Science","group":"uni","college":"Agriculture & Natural Resources","q":[["Rhizobium bacteria in the root nodules of legumes:",["Cause leaf diseases","Fix atmospheric nitrogen","Absorb phosphorus from the air","Break down cellulose"],1,"Rhizobium lives in nodules on legume roots and converts atmospheric nitrogen into forms the plant can use, which is why legumes enrich soil.","Soil fertility"],["The loss of water vapour from the aerial parts of a plant, mainly through stomata, is called:",["Transpiration","Translocation","Guttation","Respiration"],0,"Transpiration is evaporation of water from leaves, mostly through the stomata. It drives water uptake and cools the plant.","Plant physiology"],["Which three elements are the primary macronutrients in fertilizers (N-P-K)?",["Calcium, magnesium, sulphur","Iron, zinc, copper","Carbon, hydrogen, oxygen","Nitrogen, phosphorus, potassium"],3,"N-P-K stands for nitrogen, phosphorus and potassium, the nutrients plants need in the largest amounts from the soil.","Soil fertility"],["What is the scientific name of teff?",["Eragrostis tef","Zea mays","Triticum aestivum","Sorghum bicolor"],0,"Teff, the staple grain of Ethiopia, is Eragrostis tef. Zea mays is maize, Triticum aestivum is bread wheat and Sorghum bicolor is sorghum.","Crop science"],["Coffea arabica is believed to have originated in the highlands of:",["Brazil","Colombia","Ethiopia","Vietnam"],2,"Arabica coffee is native to the highland forests of southwestern Ethiopia, which is why Ethiopia is called the birthplace of coffee.","Crop science"]]},{"id":"g12-english","name":"English","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["II. Language Focus (Questions 33–65)\nIn summer, she usually moves away ______ her family to attend a special camp.",["of","in","at","from"],3,"The preposition \"from\" is used with \"move away\" to indicate the person or place being left. \"Move away from\" means to leave a place or person behind. \"In summer, she usually moves away from her family...\" (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["the take Bikila first to Abebe gold ever an was Olympic home African",["Abebe Bikila was ever the first African gold to take home an Olympic medal.","The first African Abebe Bikila was ever to take home an Olympic gold medal.","Abebe Bikila was the first African to ever take home an Olympic gold medal.","Abebe Bikila ever take an Olympic gold medal to home was the first African."],2,"Option D represents the standard grammatical structure for this historical fact: 'Abebe Bikila was the first African to ever take home an Olympic gold medal.'","2015 EC entrance"],["Lilu: Do you speak Italian? You:_____________.",["I speak five languages","I speak Arabic, too","Just a little","I've never been to Italy"],2,"'Just a little' is a standard short response indicating limited proficiency when asked 'Do you speak Italian?'.","2006 EC entrance"],["in/ can/ her/ and/ talk/ bring/ we.",["We and her talk can bring in","We can talk her and bring in","Bring her in and we can talk","We bring her in and can talk"],2,"Option D successfully links an imperative clause and a coordinate clause ('Bring her in and we can talk') using all of the given words correctly.","2016 EC entrance"],["Our agricultural products are mostly ______ to Europe and the Middle East.",["exported","transferred","disseminated","scattered"],0,"Goods or agricultural products sold and sent to other countries or regions (like Europe and the Middle East) are 'exported'.","2018 EC entrance"],["The professor __________ I met is from Kenya.",["whom","which","where","whose"],0,"The relative pronoun 'whom' is used because the professor is the object of the verb 'met' in the relative clause.","2018 EC entrance"],["The main factor that led to the disbanding of the union is unfair distribution of income among members. Some of \nthe leaders were absurdly egocenteric:",["direct","principal","best","simple"],1,"The word 'main' is synonymous with 'principal,' which means first in order of importance or chief.","2015 EC entrance"],["During the last century vaccination programs were introduced in most countries around the world. Before this,\nthousands f people, especially children, used to die of infectious diseases every year. This is most likely taken\nfrom the ______________ section of an essay.",["introduction","details","conclusion","Body"],0,"Providing historical context and general background information about a topic is characteristic of the introduction of an essay.","2007 EC entrance"],["My father is not ________old______ yours; he is only 53 years old.",["such...so","as...so","as...as","such...as"],2,"The comparison of equality in the negative is formed using 'not as + adjective + as', making 'as...as' the correct choice. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Daba: Students at university should be totally free to choose their field of study so that they can be successful.\nAdugna: ________but we should also consider the needs of society so that we have skilled human power in\nevery field.",["How can you say that","I disagree completely","That's rubbish","That's a good point"],3,"Adugna starts with a concession and uses 'but' to introduce a counterargument. 'That's a good point' acknowledges Daba's opinion before offering this contrasting perspective. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is taken form an informal letter?",["wish me good luck for my math exam.","I would like to apply for the positon of assistant secretary.","I am writing to complain about the following damages.","I enclose my curriculum vitae for your attention."],0,"'Wish me good luck for my math exam' uses an informal, conversational tone appropriate for a personal letter to a friend or family member.","2010 EC entrance"],["I wish I were not your teacher.",["my sister was to be your teacher.","A. I am unhappy that I were not your teacher","A am your teacher","B. I am very happy that I am not your teacher"],2,"The subjunctive \"I wish I were not...\" expresses a regret about the present reality, meaning the actual fact is \"I am your teacher\" (written with a minor typographical error as \"A am your teacher\").","2016 EC entrance"],["I will never forget my stay in this company. I enjoyed working with you as my boss and I ____________ meeting\nyou again sometime in my life.",["like","look forward to","wish","will wait until"],1,"The phrasal verb 'look forward to' is grammatically followed by a gerund noun phrase, which fits perfectly with 'meeting you again'. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["I was__________when I heard the news of her mother's death.",["ashamed","surprised","shocked","impressed"],2,"'Shocked' expresses the profound grief and sudden distress typically caused by tragic news such as a death.","2006 EC entrance"],["He seems to be __________ cooking but I am quite the opposite. I rather enjoy eating.",["inclined to","bored with","mad with","fond of"],3,"The phrase 'fond of' means liking something. The speaker contrasts the other person's love of cooking with their own love of eating instead.","2016 EC entrance"],["As used in paragraph 1, which word from those given below is similar in meaning to 'gorge' ?",["stuff","gather","cheat","hunt"],0,"The verb \"gorge\" means to eat greedily or to fill oneself to capacity, which is synonymous with \"stuff\" in this context.","2014 EC entrance"],["My holiday was never_______________. I could use every minute for something enjoyable.",["thrilling","annoying","boring","worrying"],2,"'Boring' provides the exact antonymous contrast to spending 'every minute for something enjoyable'.","2006 EC entrance"],["I would like _________________ her before she leaves. There is a big secret she didn't want to tell the family.",["seeing","to be seeing","see","to see"],3,"The expression 'would like' is followed by a 'to'-infinitive, making 'to see' the correct grammatical choice.","2016 EC entrance"],["You: I know your favourite pastime. Your friend:_________________",["No, you aren't.","I like swimming.","I don't play tennis.","no, you don't."],3,"The statement 'I know...' is naturally challenged or replied to with the auxiliary verb 'do': 'No, you don't.' (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["They kept trying hard to bring him to the position of chairmanship. Unfortunately, however, members chose\nsomeone else so much unexpected.",["struggling","manipulating","working","propagating"],0,"In this context, 'trying hard' is best represented by 'struggling', which means making strenuous or great efforts to achieve a difficult goal.","2016 EC entrance"],["Everybody understands that most of you worked very hard _______ you would pass this test. But you don't have \nto lose hope if the result happens to be against your expectation.",["as a result of which","which means","so that","despite"],2,"The conjunction 'so that' is used to introduce a clause of purpose, explaining why they worked very hard (with the goal of passing the test).","2015 EC entrance"],["If the Ethiopian government collected taxes with a great effort, the country’s ______ would rise by a higher\npercentage.",["returns","revenue","money","finance"],1,"The income generated by a government, especially through taxes, is formally referred to as 'revenue'.","2018 EC entrance"],["Mustefa: Excuse me, can you tell me where the Registrar's office is? Hallima: ________ I am stranger here",["I'm sorry I don't know.","Yes, I can.","How should I know?","Why do you want to go there?"],0,"Because Hallima is a stranger and cannot provide directions, 'I'm sorry I don't know' is the most polite and appropriate response.","2016 EC entrance"],["Kebede: Do you think their plan is going to work out? Nigist: _____________________",["Good plans can sometimes fail.","Who knows? Let's wait and see.","By the way, who has masterminded it?","Plans should be carefully discussed."],1,"The question asks for a prediction on whether a plan will succeed, and 'Who knows? Let's wait and see' is a common idiomatic expression used when the future outcome is uncertain.","2015 EC entrance"],["Out in the office behind his house, Lemma is sweating over his newspaper column. His feet are propped up on\nhis desk, and his computer keyboard sits on his lap. This is most likely taken from a piece of writing that is",["expository","narrative","descriptive","argumentative"],2,"The passage uses visual and sensory details ('sweating', 'feet are propped up', 'sits on his lap') to paint a vivid picture of a scene, which is typical of descriptive writing.","2006 EC entrance"],["Us him and go up and pick",["Let him go and pick up us.","Let him up and go pick us.","Let him go up and us pick.","Let us go and pick him up"],3,"'Let us go and pick him up' is the only grammatically correct rearrangement. In phrasal verbs with a pronoun object, the pronoun must go between the verb and the particle ('pick him up', not 'pick up him/us').","2006 EC entrance"],["You smoke a lot; you should stop _____ and you will feel much healthier.",["smoking","for smoking","to smoked","smoked"],3,"Stop + the -ing form means end the activity, which is what a heavy smoker should do. Stop + to + verb would mean pause in order to do something else. Option B, smoked, cannot follow stop at all, because stop takes either -ing or to + verb.","2018 EC entrance"],["Reservationist: Can I have the dates for your departure and return? Customer: Yes, I want to leave on July 27\nand return on 30. Reservationist: ______________________ Did you say you wanted to return on July 30.\nCustomer: Sorry. I didn't make myself clear. I want to return on August 30.",["I'm sorry; I didn't follow what you said.","Why did you confuse me?","Do you have a flight phobia?","That is your first time to book a ticket."],0,"The reservationist's request for clarification ('Did you say you wanted to return on July 30') naturally follows the polite statement 'I'm sorry; I didn't follow what you said.'","2013 EC entrance"],["I would have married her ________________ I had known her dad was one of the wealthiest in the town. I was\njust unlucky.",["before","because","if only","unless"],2,"In this third conditional sentence, 'if only' acts as an emphatic conditional conjunction meaning 'if indeed' or 'I wish', expressing regret about not knowing the father's wealth.","2016 EC entrance"],["Where would you write a request for an action in the format of a formal letter?",["in the Body of the letter","in the Complementary closure","in the Subject line","in the Salutation"],0,"Any request for action or detailed communication in a formal letter belongs in the body of the letter, typically in the concluding paragraph of the body.","2014 EC entrance"],["My classmate goes to school by bus_______ I walk every day.",["since","whereas","because","so"],1,"The conjunction 'whereas' is used to contrast two facts directly in a single sentence.","2013 EC entrance"],["same passage\nWhat concerns are there about the long-term environmental impact of GMOs?",["GMOs may reduce biodiversity.","There are no concerns.","GMOs have no effect on the environment.","GMOs improve biodiversity."],3,"The last paragraph names two long-term worries about GMOs: the environmental impact and 'the potential loss of biodiversity'. Option B states that loss. Option C says GMOs improve biodiversity, which is the opposite of what the passage raises as a concern. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["If you send a plagiarist to jail for one-year service, the most likely, what is the consequence of the decision?",["Legal","Ethical","Personal","Professional"],0,"Sending a person to jail is a criminal penalty, which represents a legal consequence of plagiarism.","2015 EC entrance"],["The whole building collapsed when it was hit by a missile. Only two __________ children were found alive in.",["miraculous","fortunate","fearless","mysterious"],1,"In this context, 'fortunate' (meaning lucky or favored by fortune) is the most appropriate adjective to describe the children who luckily survived the building collapse.","2016 EC entrance"],["Mother:_______________? You: I put in just a little.",["when did you put in salt","Did you put in salt","why did you put in salt","how much salt did you put in"],3,"The answer 'just a little' specifies a quantity of an uncountable noun (salt), which answers the question 'How much salt did you put in?'.","2006 EC entrance"],["I don't have a long standing acquaintance with Lojo, but I already feel that I _______ her for years.",["have known","knew","had known","have been knowing"],0,"'Know' is a stative verb and cannot be used in continuous tenses. The present perfect 'have known' represents a state that started in the past and continues to the present.","2014 EC entrance"],["When the police arrived, the burglars _______ away with the money. But there is hope that they would be\ncaught.",["have been making","had already made","are already making","have already made"],1,"The past perfect tense 'had already made' is used to show that the burglars' escape occurred before the police arrived in the past.","2015 EC entrance"],["Let me withdraw some money from ATM______ we come across something interesting in the super market.",["in case","if","unless","when"],0,"'In case' is used to talk about doing something as a precaution against a possible future situation.","2016 EC entrance"],["Tadesse: Why is the roof leaking? Carpenter: _______________ it hasn't been serviced for long.",["The reason as a fact is that","This is due to the fact that","Yes, it is because of the reason that","I think because of"],1,"'This is due to the fact that' is a correct and formal prepositional phrase used to introduce a clause explaining a cause.","2016 EC entrance"],["My grade this semester is _______ than my first semester's.",["much better","best","so good","so much better"],0,"When comparing two things (this semester's grade and the first semester's), the comparative form 'better' is used. 'Much' acts as an intensifier, making 'much better' the correct choice.","2014 EC entrance"],["Doctor: _____ Bonsa: About four days now.",["What is your problem?","How often do you see these symptoms?","Have you seen these symptoms for about four days?","How long have you had these symptoms?"],3,"\"About four days now\" gives a length of time, so the question has to ask about length. The present perfect in \"How long have you had these symptoms?\" fits something that started in the past and is still going on. B is tempting because it also asks about time, but \"how often\" would be answered with something like \"twice a day\".","2017 EC entrance"],["Brother: life is getting more and more expensive here. Shall we leave for another place?\nSister:____________________.",["I guess it is the same everywhere.","How much do you need for your food?","how much do you earn now?","True! Everybody is complaining these days."],0,"The brother asks a question: shall we leave for another place? The reply has to answer that proposal, and \"I guess it is the same everywhere\" answers it with a reason for staying. D is tempting because it agrees that prices are high, but agreeing about the cost says nothing about moving, which is what was asked.","2005 EC entrance"],["in you girl about slim, are pretty the talking neighborhood tall, this?",["Are you this pretty, tall, slim girl talking about in the neighborhood?","Are you talking about this tall, slim, pretty girl in the neighborhood?","You are about the pretty, talking, tall girl in this slim neighborhood?","This pretty, tall, girl in the neighborhood talking about you are slim?"],1,"This option is the only one that uses all the words from the stem to form a grammatically correct, natural question in English: \"Are you talking about this tall, slim, pretty girl in the neighborhood?\" (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Cub is to a Lion: __________ is to a Cow.",["Calf","Veal","Bull","Kitten"],0,"This is an analogy question comparing animals to their offspring: a cub is the offspring of a lion, and a calf is the offspring of a cow.","2016 EC entrance"],["New situations always made me nervous. Which sentences is like to come next?",["I stood timidly by the side of the changing room.","I changed into my bathing suit.","my first swimming lesson was no exception.","after a couple of minutes the teacher came over."],2,"Option B provides a smooth transition from the general opening claim ('New situations always made me nervous') to a specific illustrative experience ('my first swimming lesson was no exception').","2009 EC entrance"],["Sosina: Do you like that funky hairstyle? Hirut: _______________",["Gosh! It is so weird to me.","I see so many girls wearing it.","Mom always makes fun of such a style.","It is all over now! What fashion is that?"],0,"Sosina asks for Hirut's personal opinion about a hairstyle. Option C directly answers with Hirut's reaction (\"Gosh! It is so weird to me\"), indicating a dislike for it.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following words can be synonymous with the word ' dedicated ' in paragraph 3, line 4?",["decided","stubborn","desperate","committed"],3,"To be 'dedicated' to a task or goal means to be deeply 'committed' and devoted to it.","2016 EC entrance"],["\"Just a moment, please!\" \"The room _______,\" said the teacher.",["has been cleaned","is being cleaned","is cleaned","is cleaning"],1,"The exclamation 'Just a moment, please!' indicates that the action is currently in progress, requiring the present continuous passive form 'is being cleaned'.","2014 EC entrance"],["My friend is sometimes hard to convince, but I like him ___.",["even","nonetheless","likewise","although"],1,"'Nonetheless' is an adverb meaning 'in spite of that' or 'nevertheless', which correctly contrasts liking the friend despite him being hard to convince.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is similar in meaning to \" glossy \" as used in paragraph 2?",["soft","harsh","rough","smooth"],3,"\"Glossy\" refers to a shiny, smooth surface, making \"smooth\" the closest synonym in the context of paper types.","2014 EC entrance"],["It was all tiring, but we had no other option. I really hate such ___________________tasks.",["Boring","Exhausting","demanding","Uninspiring"],1,"The word 'exhausting' is synonymous with 'extremely tiring', perfectly matching the context of performing very tiring tasks.","2008 EC entrance"],["Thanks to technology, we ________ carry a lot of cash with us when we go shopping. We can use mobile\nbanking to make payments.",["don't have to","ought not to","must","haven't to"],0,"'Don't have to' is used to express an absence of necessity or obligation. Since mobile banking is available, carrying cash is no longer necessary.","2016 EC entrance"],["Belay: My house has been broken into. I am thinking of hiring security. Amare:____________________________.",["when does that happen?","Why do they do such a nasty thing?","You may also report to the police.","In fact, that happens to a number of people."],2,"Recommending that the victim also notify law enforcement ('You may also report to the police') is the most constructive and appropriate conversational response.","2007 EC entrance"],["You: What does our new English teacher look like? Friend: ___________",["He's 30 years old, approximately","He speaks English fluently","He has grey hair","He's short, but well-built"],3,"The question 'What does he look like?' asks for a physical description, which is perfectly answered by 'He's short, but well-built.'","2014 EC entrance"],["I am giving up the idea of starting an MA programme at Jombola University. Admission with them is in August,\nbut I ____________ from here by then. I will still have one more course to do.",["won't have graduated","wouldn't graduate","won't graduate","won't be graduating"],0,"The future perfect tense ('won't have graduated') is required here because of the time reference 'by then' (by August).","2011 EC entrance"],["Due to economic and cultural factors, many children in the countryside __________ of school.",["leave out","run out","fall out","drop out"],3,"The phrasal verb 'drop out' means to abandon a course of study before finishing it, which fits the context of leaving school due to economic and cultural factors.","2016 EC entrance"],["I have no doubt he would win the scholarship. He is the_______________ of all.",["most so talented","more talented","most talented","Very talented"],2,"When comparing one individual against all members of a group ('of all'), the superlative degree 'the most talented' is required. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["He was doing the washing up _______ she was cleaning the house. We like that they help one another.",["since","during","while","before"],2,"The conjunction 'while' is used to connect two continuous actions occurring at the same time in the past.","2015 EC entrance"],["Kidist: _______________ Hana: With sugar, please.",["Is it good to drink coffee without sugar","Do you like your coffee with sugar","How much sugar do you like in your coffee","Would you prefer your coffee with or without sugar"],3,"The question 'Would you prefer your coffee with or without sugar?' is an alternative question that is naturally resolved with the response 'With sugar, please.'","2017 EC entrance"],["Kuku: Are you she is arriving this weekend? Eleni: ____________________",["No doubt! She has her seat confirmed.","The weekend is going to be rainy.","They have prepared a lot of things to welcome her.","I think she is taking a plane to change at Dubai."],0,"Kuku asks for confirmation of certainty (\"Are you [sure] she is arriving this weekend?\"), and \"No doubt! She has her seat confirmed\" directly expresses full certainty.","2008 EC entrance"],["Driver: My Toyota car is still perfect after 10 years on the road.\nMechanic: _____________________________________",["Do they also drive Toyota?","My brother also has one.","I have a Volkswagen.","Toyota cars are the best."],3,"As a professional, the mechanic's generalization that 'Toyota cars are the best' directly validates the driver's experience of their car being perfect after ten years.","2011 EC entrance"],["I have _______ things to do before I leave for the meeting. So, I have to lock myself in and work with no\ninterruption.",["Some","much","a few","a lot of"],3,"'A lot of' is used with plural countable nouns like 'things' to show a large quantity, which justifies the need to work with no interruption.","2013 EC entrance"],["Student 1: I'm sorry. I don't remember. Have you seen them?\nStudent 2: ___________________________",["What were they doing? They must be our friends.","I was busy doing my homework.","Probably, It was an empty room.","Sure. I've seen them with my naked eyes."],3,"Student 2's response 'Sure. I've seen them with my naked eyes' directly and emphatically answers Student 1's question 'Have you seen them?'. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["It is sad that COVID-19 has already caused a lot of damage to many countries of the world. _______ due to the\nvaccines administered all over the world, there are signs that the rate of infection is declining.",["However","On the contrary","But","Surprisingly"],0,"'However' is used at the start of a sentence to introduce a contrasting idea, separated by a comma or introducing a contrasting adverbial phrase.","2013 EC entrance"],["___________________ Would i say about this exam later at home.",["Not word","Not a word","None a word","Nothing word"],1,"Negative inversion occurs when a negative phrase like 'Not a word' begins the sentence, inverting the subject and auxiliary verb ('would I say').","2009 EC entrance"],["My grandfather's face was ______________ with age.",["frowned","wrinkled","confused","surprised"],1,"With advancing age, a person's skin loses elasticity and becomes 'wrinkled.'","2013 EC entrance"],["Belay: everybody should contribute. This is for the good of the community. Kiros: ________________.",["Health centres are important.","I can't agree more.","Can everybody offer it?","Each of us is to pay birr 5,000"],1,"\"I can't agree more\" means complete agreement, which is the natural reply to somebody calling for a contribution for the good of the community. D is tempting because it also sounds like taking part, but naming a figure of 5,000 birr answers a question about the amount that nobody has asked. (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["Student: Sir, We've won the inter-school competition. Our school stood first. Director: _____________________",["What great news! I'm pleased to hear that.","Really? I actually knew two of the judges.","This is our first time to participate.","Wasn't the competition stiff as such?"],0,"As the director of the school, expressing delight and congratulating the students with 'What great news! I'm pleased to hear that' is the most appropriate and supportive reaction to winning a competition.","2015 EC entrance"],["We cannot be talking about failure of plans every year. What have you done about them and where and when did \nyou succeed?",["impracticality","shallowness","miscarriage","weakness"],2,"A 'miscarriage' of a plan refers to its failure or lack of success, making it the closest synonym to 'failure' in this context.","2015 EC entrance"],["You: Guess what! I bought a car.\nFriend: _____________________",["Where are cars sold in this city?","Cars are very important.","Are you serious? You must be joking!","I also want to buy a new one."],2,"Buying a car is a major accomplishment, and expressing surprise with 'Are you serious? You must be joking!' is a typical, friendly response.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following could be an opening to your informal letter?",["How are you darling?","I am writing this to complain…","this is in response to your…","I have received your letter of 28 May."],0,"'How are you darling?' is highly affectionate and informal, making it perfect for opening an informal letter, while the other options are typical of business or formal correspondence.","2016 EC entrance"],["It to wanted you today me do.",["you wanted me to do it today.","it wanted me today you to do.","today you wanted it me to do.","me wanted you to do it today."],0,"The standard English word order for this sentence is subject ('you'), verb ('wanted'), object pronoun ('me'), to-infinitive clause ('to do it'), and adverb of time ('today'): 'You wanted me to do it today.'","2010 EC entrance"],["In Paragraph 3, the author says, \"With the latter, it seems everyone loses out in one way or ...\" What does \"with\nthe latter\" show?",["Harnessing the limited resources","Learning from our differences","Creating disadvantages for others","Combating global challenges"],2,"\"The latter\" refers to the second of two options; since the author notes that with the latter \"everyone loses out,\" it must refer to a negative action like \"creating disadvantages for others.\" (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Tutu: I am leaving for US on Monday. US, California. Titi: ________ Could you repeat that, please?",["That is too good to be true","Are you trying to fool me?","Are you leaving on Monday?","Sorry, I didn't catch that"],3,"'Sorry, I didn't catch that' is a polite expression used when you did not hear or understand what someone said, prompting them to repeat it. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["At least half of the first year students surveyed reported adopting writing strategies that involved the use of\ntheir first language. This could be a typical example of a research report based on a research topic entitled:",["First Year Students' Writing Strategies.","First Year students' First Language in Writing","First Year students' First Language Use.","First Year students' Strategies of Using First Language"],0,"The finding reports a specific strategy (using the first language) identified among students, fitting under an overarching investigation of 'First Year Students' Writing Strategies.'","2007 EC entrance"],["______________you and your wife have concocted this. I have never said that.",["Both","nor","either","all"],0,"The correlative conjunction 'both' correctly pairs with 'and' when referring to two subjects ('you and your wife').","2008 EC entrance"],["Stranger: excuse me, _______________ You: I'm a stranger her myself",["tell me where is the post office?","Do you tell me where the post office is?","you tell where post office is","Can you tell me where the post office is?"],3,"'Can you tell me where the post office is?' is a standard polite indirect question asking for directions, which elicits the common response 'I'm a stranger here myself'.","2006 EC entrance"],["Choose the correctly spelt word.",["traditionial","expenditure","fotograph","particularily"],1,"'Expenditure' is correctly spelled. The others are misspelled versions of 'particularly', 'traditional', and 'photograph'.","2017 EC entrance"],["Mother:______________? Daughter: well, I placed the egg carefully in the jar.",["What did you do next","when did you place the egg in the jar","who placed the egg in the jar","did you place the egg in the jar"],0,"The daughter describes an action in a sequence of events, which best answers 'What did you do next?'.","2006 EC entrance"],["Mine is from Germany, __________ hers is from China. Can't you see the difference then?",["nonetheless","whereas","similarly","even then"],1,"The conjunction 'whereas' is used to contrast two facts directly in a single sentence. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Interviewer: You said that you left your previous work place because the organization was old-fashioned. What\ndo you mean? Candidate: _______. The management is not open to change; they always want to do things the\nold way.",["Let me repeat what I just said","Let me say it again loudly","Let me re-phrase what I just said","I will say that again if you want"],2,"When an interviewer asks 'What do you mean?', they are asking for clarification, so the candidate naturally introduces their explanation with 'Let me re-phrase what I just said'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Each one of us______________________ help those affected by the drought. It is immoral to leave them to\nstarve.",["can","will","Ought to","must"],2,"'Ought to' is the modal verb specifically used to express moral obligation and duty, which directly corresponds to the context given: 'It is immoral to leave them to starve.'","2008 EC entrance"],["Shito: we're going to Lalibela for a tour Next week. Isn't that marvellous? Aster:",["It might take a few days to get there.","When are you planning to come back?","Brilliant. You may also consider seeing BahirDar.","Why do people spend money going around?"],2,"'Brilliant. You may also consider seeing BahirDar' directly agrees with the excitement ('Isn't that marvellous?') and offers a helpful travel suggestion.","2007 EC entrance"],["the elsewhere is of unfriendly town people full from.",["The town is unfriendly full of people from elsewhere.","The town is full of unfriendly people from elsewhere.","Unfriendly people from elsewhere is full of the town.","From elsewhere is the town full of unfriendly people."],1,"Reassembling the words in Option D gives 'The town is full of unfriendly people from elsewhere', which is a grammatically perfect and natural English sentence. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["The price of goods are known for their variability because they increase and decrease every other day.",["evenness","fluctuation","certainty","transition"],1,"Prices that increase and decrease constantly are characterized by 'variability,' which is synonymous with 'fluctuation.'","2013 EC entrance"],["Roberto was__________from his job for being caught red handed stealing confidential document.",["promoted","sacked","defamed","released"],1,"To be \"sacked\" means to be dismissed or fired from a job, which is the appropriate consequence for being caught stealing confidential documents.","2016 EC entrance"],["Peter has reorganized his files ______ he can easily find what he is looking for.",["such that","so that","at that","that is"],1,"The conjunction 'so that' is used to introduce a clause of purpose, explaining why Peter reorganized his files.","2013 EC entrance"],["School buses should always be driven by a/an _______ driver.",["licensed","entrusted","engaged","enthused"],0,"For safety and legal reasons, school buses must always be driven by a 'licensed' driver.","2014 EC entrance"],["I don't understand why he suspected us. ____________________ From among us would want his money.",["No one","No anyone","Anyone","Not someone"],0,"'No one' provides the negative subject needed to explain why the suspicion was baseless ('No one from among us would want his money').","2009 EC entrance"],["Chaltu is very considerate but she could not tolerate people who do not have a sense of ______. That’s why she\nalways cracks jokes and makes her audiences laugh.",["generosity","purposeful","humor","sincerity"],2,"The phrase 'cracks jokes and makes her audiences laugh' directly indicates that she values and possesses a 'sense of humor'.","2018 EC entrance"],["Getahun: what was your hliday like? Fetiha: ________",["rarely so!","Kedija came to our house.","it was nice but the weather was not good.","we liked it very much."],2,"The question 'What was it like?' asks for a description of the holiday; 'it was nice but the weather was not good' properly provides that description.","2010 EC entrance"],["For and join come us celebration the?",["Come and join the celebration for us.","Come and join for us the celebration.","Come and join us for the celebration.","For us the celebration come and join."],2,"'Come and join us for the celebration' is the standard imperative construction with the transitive verb 'join' taking the direct object 'us' followed by the prepositional phrase 'for the celebration'.","2006 EC entrance"],["If Sofia worked hard, she ________ good mark.",["would get","would have got","will get","good marks"],0,"This is a second conditional sentence ('If' + simple past + 'would' + base verb) used to describe a hypothetical situation. Thus, 'would get' is the correct verb form.","2016 EC entrance"],["If you go to a new place, your behavior and manner should harmonize with that of the people you meet there.",["contradict","consider","integrate","go against"],2,"To 'harmonize with' means to blend in well or fit with, which is closely synonymous with 'integrate'.","2017 EC entrance"],["His brothers are running ___________ money. Therefore, they need some.",["get along","up with","out of","back on"],2,"The phrasal verb 'run out of' means to use up a supply of something so that none is left, which fits the context of needing money.","2016 EC entrance"],["A witness was able to____________my story that the accident was not my fault.",["suspect","supplement","Sustain","substantiate"],3,"'Substantiate' means to provide evidence to prove the truth of a claim or story.","2006 EC entrance"],["Manager: What happened to those new machines?\nTechnician: ____________________",["Very frustrating! None of them is working.","May be, they are not good machines.","Shall we put them on auction?","Amazing! They are new and well-designed."],0,"The technician's role is to report the status of the machines to the manager. Saying 'Very frustrating! None of them is working' directly answers what happened to them.","2011 EC entrance"],["If we are not able to ______________ ideas accurately, misunderstandings would naturally crop up.",["enunciate","propagate","communicate","inform"],2,"'Communicate' is the most suitable verb here because failing to transmit or share ideas accurately leads directly to misunderstandings.","2015 EC entrance"],["Aleltu:________________? Thomas: sorry. I am busy with my assignment.",["Have you seen the report I compiled?","Could you help me organize the report?","Have you finished ding your assignment?","Would you read the report when you are ready?"],1,"Thomas's response is an apology declining a request for help due to being busy, which logically follows a polite request like 'Could you help me organize the report?'.","2006 EC entrance"],["Way there similar co Way there similar cold apes in humans be no which to are.",["There could be no way in which humans are similar to apes.","There are apes which could no way be in similar to humans.","There could be humans which no way are in similar to apes.","There are no humans which could be in way similar to apes."],0,"\"There could be no way in which humans are similar to apes\" is the only grammatically correct and meaningful arrangement of the scrambled words. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["I wanted to buy the car, but it cost an arm and a leg. What should I do, Leliko? (cost an arm and a leg means)",["a negotiable price","a very low price","a fair price","a very high price"],1,"To cost an arm and a leg is to be very expensive, which explains why the speaker wanted the car but is asking what to do instead of buying it. Option C, a very low price, would leave the hesitation in the sentence unexplained.","2018 EC entrance"],["Driver: What's the matter? Policeman: You have violated a traffic rule._________________",["How can we allow people like you?","When you see a red light, you should stop.","It is not my business. It is the minimum penalty.","I am sorry. The road is free. I failed to notice you."],1,"The policeman's role is to explain the violation; stating 'When you see a red light, you should stop' is a direct and logical follow-up to 'You have violated a traffic rule.' (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["If you were to be a teacher, you ____________________have to join a college of education and take the\nnecessary training. You can't jump into the profession from the street.",["will","shall","could","Would"],3,"'If you were to be...' is an unreal/hypothetical conditional (second conditional), which takes 'would' in the main clause ('you would have to...').","2008 EC entrance"],["We have known each other________childhood.",["as","while","since","when"],2,"'Since' is used with the present perfect tense to indicate the starting point in time of an action or state (childhood).","2010 EC entrance"],["It appears the combined effort exerted by the team significantly contributed to their success. In fact, we need to\ntake a lesson and reshape our strategy.",["power","dismay","synergy","disarray"],2,"'Synergy' refers to the interaction or cooperation of two or more agents to produce a combined effect greater than the sum of their individual effects.","2016 EC entrance"],["_______ she came home, I made her coffee. Then we sat together and had hours of talk and talk.",["Suddenly","Prior","While","When"],3,"'When' is the correct temporal conjunction to show a sequence of events in the past (first she came home, then I made her coffee).","2015 EC entrance"],["Clean air ______ the well-being of people everywhere.",["substantiates","sustains","differentiates","maintains"],1,"'Sustains' is the most appropriate verb here, meaning to strengthen, support, or keep something going over time.","2014 EC entrance"],["\"My coat was no the seat next to me. I took my passport out my pocket and put it in my bag in the luggage\nrack.\" These lines are taken from a piece of writing that is most likely",["argumentative","expository","description","narrative"],3,"The excerpt recounts a chronological sequence of actions ('took my passport out', 'put it in my bag'), which is characteristic of narrative writing. (1)","2010 EC entrance"],["According to the passage, what does the word 'manure' in the fourth paragraph mean?",["flood","ruminant","dung","residue"],2,"The word 'manure' refers to organic matter, typically animal dung, used as an agricultural fertilizer to enrich the soil.","2018 EC entrance"],["The doctor told the nurse to have all the gadgets sterilized and make them ready for the operation this morning.",["well organized","speck-free","germ-free","disassembled"],2,"In medical contexts, 'sterilized' means to be made free from bacteria or other microorganisms, which is synonymous with 'germ-free'.","2011 EC entrance"],["My mother was furious when she found out her friend hadn't told her the truth.",["brave","extremely angry","excessive carelessness","frighten"],1,"'Furious' means extremely angry or full of wild, fierce anger.","2016 EC entrance"],["People going to many invite party are to your you?",["Are your many people going to invite you to party?","Are you going to invite many people to your party?","Are your many party going to you people to invite?","Are you going to many party to invite your people?"],1,"'Are you going to invite many people to your party?' correctly follows standard English question order: Auxiliary (Are) + Subject (you) + Verb phrase (going to invite) + Direct Object (many people) + Prepositional Phrase (to your party).","2006 EC entrance"],["I think she did an excellent job on her presentation.",["neither did I.","neither do I.","So do I.","So did I."],2,"To agree with a positive statement starting with 'I think' (present simple), we use the auxiliary verb 'do' in the form 'So do I' (meaning 'I also think so').","2013 EC entrance"],["Do you know __________ she had when she started the investment? In fact, she is so much business-minded\nand now she has become a millionaire.",["her money","how many","how much","the bir"],2,"The phrase 'how much' is used to ask or talk about uncountable quantities, such as money, which fits the context of investment and becoming a millionaire.","2016 EC entrance"],["Teacher: ________________. Student: I get out of bed.",["What time do you get up?","What do you do first in the morning?","Who gets up first in your family?","Do you ever get up before six?"],1,"The student's answer, \"I get out of bed\", names an action, not a time and not a person. The question that such an answer fits is \"What do you do first in the morning?\" A is the trap because it is about the same moment of the day, but a question with \"what time\" expects a clock time in the answer.","2005 EC entrance"],["Boss: What was their argument in brief?\nSubordinate: ________________________",["They just kept talking. Nothing brief.","Majority were not arguing strongly.","Yes, they always like to argue.","They want the group to leave now."],3,"The subordinate summarizes the core point of the argument ('They want the group to leave now') in response to the boss's request for a brief summary.","2011 EC entrance"],["After waiting for two hours, mom grew ________________ with my sister and decided to call her.",["Irresponsible","Unfriendly","unkind","Impatient"],3,"Waiting for two hours makes a person 'impatient' (restless or irritated by delay). (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["pass / so that / working / the / can / hard / am / I / test.",["I am hard working so that I can the test pass.","I am working hard so that I can pass the test.","I can pass the test so that I am working hard.","I can pass so that I am working hard the test."],1,"The correct sentence order is 'I am working hard so that I can pass the test,' where 'so that' introduces a purpose clause showing the reason for working hard.","2018 EC entrance"],["Did you know that Mary and Bedlu________________ married next week?",["Are going to get","Get","Will get","Will be getting"],0,"'Are going to get' is the standard way to express a planned future arrangement or event, such as a scheduled wedding next week.","2009 EC entrance"],["The disagreement between the warring parties should be solved amicably. That seems to be the only way that\ncould lead to a win-win solution",["success","dispute","hatred","assault"],1,"A 'disagreement' between opposing or warring parties is synonymous with a 'dispute.'","2015 EC entrance"],["When you buy an item from a shop, you are usually given a one-year assurance so if it stops working, you can\nget it fixed for free.",["replacement","guarantee","service","certificate"],1,"An 'assurance' given by a seller to fix a product for free if it stops working within a specified period is called a 'guarantee'.","2016 EC entrance"],["When we take an entrance examination like this, the results are almost always dual . So, we need to work hard\nto be in the pass group and avoid failing.",["binary","both","teamed","paired"],0,"The context describes an exam with two possible outcomes (pass or fail); 'binary' means relating to or consisting of two components, which is synonymous with 'dual' here.","2015 EC entrance"],["Teacher: how far is the school from your home? Student: ___________________",["I always travel by bus.","3kms.","I often arrive.","2hours."],1,"'How far' asks for physical distance, making '3kms.' the correct answer.","2007 EC entrance"],["II. Language Focus (Questions 33–65)\nBy the time the police arrived, the thief ______ away.",["has run","runs","had run","ran 2018 First Round"],2,"This sentence uses the past perfect tense to show that one past action happened before another past action. \"By the time the police arrived\" (later past action), \"the thief had run away\" (earlier past action). The past perfect is formed with \"had\" + past participle.","2018 EC entrance"],["Muktar went to Jimma ______ see his old friends,",["for","in order to","as to","because"],1,"The phrase 'in order to' is used to express purpose followed by a bare infinitive verb ('see').","2014 EC entrance"],["They didn't want to pay us the money back. However, after many rounds of discussion, we __________ convince\nthem and now they have deposited it into our account.",["would be able to","can be able to","are able to","were able to"],3,"The past tense 'were able to' is used to express success in achieving something in a specific past situation, which fits the context of 'didn't want to pay us... but now they have deposited it.'","2016 EC entrance"],["Secretary: May I help you? Visitor: ________________.",["why do you ask?","What do you mean?","Can I see the boss, please?","What kind of help?"],2,"\"May I help you?\" is an offer, and the natural reply states what you have come for. \"Can I see the boss, please?\" does that. B is the trap because it sounds polite, but it hands the question back to the secretary, who has already offered, so the conversation stops instead of moving on.","2005 EC entrance"],["Dandir: is Addis Ababa getting more and more dangerous? People say there are gangs everywhere. Gemechu:\nNo, no. ________",["it's simply an exaggeration","this kind of behaviour simply won't be tolerated.","that's simply the best city can afford","it simply a misunderstanding"],0,"Gemechu disagrees with the claim about dangerous gangs by stating that 'it's simply an exaggeration.'","2010 EC entrance"],["According to a recent survey, young drivers are_______________ likely to have an accident.",["The most","The worst","The more","The worse"],0,"'Likely' forms its superlative with 'most'; hence, 'the most likely' is the correct form to express the highest probability.","2009 EC entrance"],["Why should the poor pay as much as the rich? First, the poor is already poor and nothing is to be drawn out of\npoverty. Second, there is also a moral question of whether it would be just to add another burden to this group\nalready saddled with... This is taken a piece of writing that is most likely:",["argumentative","descriptive","narrative","expository"],0,"The passage poses a rhetorical question and lays out numbered points ('First...', 'Second...') to persuade the reader of a moral viewpoint, which is characteristic of argumentative writing.","2006 EC entrance"],["You : How old are you? Lidet: __________________.",["I'm the youngest in the family","Twenty-two","old enough for marriage","My sister is 18"],1,"The question 'How old are you?' directly asks for the speaker's age, making 'Twenty-two' the correct and direct response.","2006 EC entrance"],["_____ you study diligently, you'll never understand trigonometry.",["Unless","If so","Otherwise","If"],0,"\"Unless\" means \"if not\", and it works with the negative main clause: if you do not study diligently, you will never understand trigonometry. C is tempting because \"if\" fits the same slot in the sentence, but \"If you study diligently, you'll never understand trigonometry\" turns the advice upside down.","2017 EC entrance"],["Everybody reacted in a strange way. It was a really ____________ blast that I could hear almost nothing of the\nscreams and yells around. It took me five minutes to realize what was going on.",["disheartening","devastating","deafening","exploding"],2,"The word 'deafening' means extremely loud, which explains why the speaker 'could hear almost nothing' after the blast.","2011 EC entrance"],["There was a cheerful receptionist at the hotel; she always enjoyed amusing her guests.",["hopeful","mournful","thoughtful","friendly"],3,"A 'cheerful' person is happy, optimistic, and welcoming, which is best matched by the synonym 'friendly' among the options.","2014 EC entrance"],["Teacher: I don't know why but I am feeling very dizzy. Friend: ________ see your doctor immediately. Right now!",["Oh! Perhaps","You had better","It may be good to","You might"],1,"'You had better' is used to give strong advice, especially in urgent situations, and is followed by the bare infinitive 'see'.","2016 EC entrance"],["The teacher told me ____________ to my friends during the exam.",["to not talk","not to talk","stop talking","to don't talk"],1,"The negative reported imperative uses the structure 'not to + infinitive' (e.g., 'not to talk').","2016 EC entrance"],["Whatever delicious food they make turns out to be ___________ to her. It seems she has some deep-seated\nfeeling towards the community.",["appetizing","spicy","disgusting","salty"],2,"Because she holds a deep-seated negative prejudice against the community, even their 'delicious' food turns out to be 'disgusting' to her.","2016 EC entrance"],["I don't have a car, _______, I don't even have a driving license.",["Therefore","By the way","Furthermore","Incidentally"],2,"The transition word 'Furthermore' is used to add extra, supporting information that reinforces the speaker's lack of a car. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["Parents after of you which your take do?",["After which did you take of your parents?","Which of your parents take after you did?","Did you take after which of your parents?","Which of your parents did you take after?"],3,"'Which of your parents did you take after?' is the only grammatically correct and natural rearrangement of the given words, using the phrasal verb 'take after' correctly.","2016 EC entrance"],["Natural Calamity has become a challenge to most nations in developing countries. Mankind can no more ignore\nthe issue.",["Danger","Problem","Drought","disaster"],3,"A 'calamity' is an event causing great and often sudden damage or distress, which is synonymous with 'disaster'.","2008 EC entrance"],["At the meeting, the Chairman allowed ___ of opinions for",["perception","description","instability","diversity"],3,"The phrase 'diversity of opinions' refers to a range of different ideas and viewpoints, which fits perfectly in this context.","2014 EC entrance"],["It is a matter of time. ______ that good thing will come and when it comes, it will be a surprise.",["we can't be certain","There is no doubt","There is no use","I have a doubt"],1,"The phrase 'It is a matter of time' implies that the event will definitely happen eventually, making 'There is no doubt' the most logical continuation.","2013 EC entrance"],["The committee________ the issue thoroughly at the meeting yesterday.",["discussed","is discussed","discusses","was discussed"],0,"The time marker 'yesterday' indicates that the action is completed in the past, requiring the active past simple verb 'discussed'.","2013 EC entrance"],["There are thousands of displaced people in different parts of the country who have no proper shelter, food or\ncloth. Don't you think we ___________ help them?",["might","shall","could","ought to"],3,"'Ought to' is used to express moral obligation or duty, which fits the context of helping displaced people.","2015 EC entrance"],["Shop assistant: What can I help you? Customer: ___________________",["I don't need any help.","You don't have to worry.","Can you give me a jacket?","I am just looking."],3,"'I am just looking' is the standard polite response given by a customer in a store who does not require immediate assistance from a shop assistant.","2007 EC entrance"],["Passenger 1: the weather looks nice, doesn't it? Passenger 2: ___________________",["yeah, but too unpredictable.","would it be the same in Bahir Dar also?","it is like Bahir Dar, where we are going.","it is too hot this time of the year."],0,"Passenger 1 asks for confirmation with a tag question about the weather, and \"yeah, but too unpredictable\" provides a natural, conversational response.","2009 EC entrance"],["Sisay: Have you ever heard that Natan and Dagmawit are getting married? Semegn: Oh, really? What a surprise.\n_____",["Of course, I heard about it","It is not my business","I'm very pleased to hear that","I don't really like her"],2,"Semegn says 'What a surprise', which is a warm reaction to news of a wedding, so the next line continues that pleasure: 'I'm very pleased to hear that', option A. Option B is the trap, because if he had already heard about it the news could not be a surprise. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["I was send you the documents to review them as quickly as you can. They expect our comment early next week.",["Go over","get over","go into","get into"],0,"The phrasal verb 'go over' means to examine, check, or review something carefully.","2008 EC entrance"],["Nearly ____________ of the invited guests appeared for the theatre and the manager was fuming about this. I\nsaid nothing, but chose to keep silent.",["all","some","neither","none"],3,"'Nearly none' fits the context perfectly because the manager's anger ('fuming') indicates that almost no invited guests showed up.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following words is correctly spelt?",["restaurant","vollyball","cafteria","extention"],0,"\"Restaurant\" is the correct spelling, with the \"au\" in the middle and \"ant\" at the end. The other three are all misspelt: extension, cafeteria and volleyball. B is the trap because the ending sounds the same as in \"attention\", but the noun made from \"extend\" keeps the s of the verb, so it is extension.","2005 EC entrance"],["on have finished assignment your working project you?",["Have you finished your assignment project on working?","Have you finished working on your project assignment?","Have you finished working your assignment on project?","Have you finished working on your assignment project?"],1,"Put the scrambled words into the normal order of a yes or no question: auxiliary, subject, then the rest. That gives Have you finished working on your project assignment? B splits the phrasal verb and leaves on project stranded, and C attaches on working to the wrong noun. Note on this copy: option A uses the same words in a slightly different noun order and also reads correctly, so the item does not separate the two cleanly.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an appropriate ending to your letter of complaint to a company?",["All the best,","Many thanks,","Best wishes,","Sincerely,"],3,"A letter of complaint is a formal business communication, making the highly professional sign-off 'Sincerely,' the most appropriate option.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is mentioned as a source of indoor pollutants?",["Industrial exhausts","Particulate matters","Car exhausts","Cosmetics"],3,"Cosmetics (such as sprays, perfumes, and powders) are widely recognized as a significant household source of indoor chemical pollutants.","2014 EC entrance"],["The words below are NOT in the proper order. When put in the right order, they make a correct English sentence.\nChoose the alternative with a correct order. now/books/on/ studying/out/of/is/print/of/the/one/best",["Books on studying out of print is now one of the best.","Now books on studying out of print is one of the best.","One of the best books on studying is now out of print.","Studying on books now is one of the best out of print."],2,"Option A arranges the words into a grammatically correct and coherent declarative sentence: 'One of the best books on studying is now out of print.' (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["When the thief saw the police officers. It is face went as white as a sheet.",["motivated","annoyed","excited","terrified"],3,"\"As white as a sheet\" describes a face that has lost its colour, and blood drains from the face in fear. A thief who has caught sight of police officers is frightened, so terrified is the meaning. B is tempting because any strong feeling can change a face, but excitement usually brings colour to it, and there is nothing pleasant here for the thief.","2005 EC entrance"],["Ararso: What is your opinion about the need for college education? Jirata: ___________________",["What is the requirement to join college?","I feel certain that it's absolutely necessary.","None of my children joined college.","I think I've a good idea about it."],1,"Ararso asks for an opinion on the need for college education, and Jirata directly expresses a strong opinion: 'I feel certain that it's absolutely necessary.'","2017 EC entrance"],["We ______ study in small groups when we were in the secondary school.",["had used","were used to","have used to","used to"],3,"The semi-modal structure 'used to + infinitive' is used to describe past habits or states that no longer occur in the present.","2014 EC entrance"],["I ______ I studied harder in school.",["am wishing","would wish","will wish","wish"],3,"The verb 'wish' is a stative verb used in the simple present tense ('I wish') to express a present regret about a past situation.","2013 EC entrance"],["There appears to be an amendment made to the investment policy. However, we are not sure of who the major\n___________________ is.",["beneficent","Benefit","beneficiary","beneficial"],2,"A 'beneficiary' is a noun referring to a person or group that gains an advantage or profit from something, such as a policy change.","2007 EC entrance"],["As a parent, I have the discretion to determine which TV programs my children may watch.",["alternative","spirit","wealth","right"],3,"Having the 'discretion' to decide something means having the individual authority or 'right' to make that choice.","2013 EC entrance"],["Friend: You: It's Ok. It's enough to live on",["What's your job like?","How much do you earn?","Do you like your job?","is it a good job?"],1,"The response 'It's enough to live on' refers to income or salary, which directly answers the question 'How much do you earn?'.","2007 EC entrance"],["On my way home from office, there was high traffic ________. It took me two hours to get home.",["speed","path way","congestion","freeway"],2,"'Traffic congestion' is the standard collocation used to describe heavy, slow-moving traffic that causes delays.","2017 EC entrance"],["Many more books ___ for the school library next year.",["will buy","are bought","buy","will be bought"],3,"The subject 'Many more books' is passive (books do not buy themselves), and the time indicator 'next year' requires the future passive form 'will be bought'.","2014 EC entrance"],["It ( in par 4) refers to",["a moral lesson","life","situation in life","Aesop’s fable"],3,"'It' is used as a subject pronoun referring to the main subject of the discussion, which is Aesop's fable.","2016 EC entrance"],["Supervisor: _____? There are errors of all kind in your essay. Student: Sorry, I'll proofread it before I hand it in.",["Could you tell me about your writing","Are there errors of any kind in your essay","Do you care about your writing","Am I going to hate your writing"],2,"The supervisor's critical remark about the errors is most logically preceded by asking \"Do you care about your writing?\", prompting the student's apologetic response.","2014 EC entrance"],["Lensa, who is always worried about her weight, eats like a/an ______",["elephant","ant","Bird","pig"],2,"\"To eat like a bird\" means to eat very little, which fits somebody who is always worried about her weight. C is the trap because \"eat like a pig\" is the better known idiom, but it means to eat a lot and greedily, which is the opposite of what the sentence sets up.","2005 EC entrance"],["any to don't us seem more understand they.",["They seem to don't understand us any more.","Any more they don't seem to understand us.","To understand us they don't seem any more.","They don't seem to understand us any more."],3,"Option B follows proper English word order with the negative auxiliary verb preceding the main verb: 'They don't seem to understand us any more.' (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["I didn't ring off until he said he didn't love me. Once i heard that, i forced myself to completely erase him out of\nmy mind.",["Shut down","Hold on","Hang up","Ring up"],2,"The phrasal verb 'ring off' means to end a telephone conversation by putting the receiver down, which is synonymous with 'hang up'.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following words can be synonymous with the word content as used in paragraph 6?",["satisfied","naked","confident","outrageous"],0,"The word 'content' as an adjective is a direct synonym of 'satisfied', which means pleased and easy in mind.","2017 EC entrance"],["A : Do you mind if I ride your bicycle?\nB : __________ It’s broken",["It is not","I can’t judge","No, I don’t","Yes, I do"],3,"Answering 'Yes, I do' to a 'Do you mind' question means 'Yes, I do mind (and would prefer you didn't)', which makes sense here because the bicycle is broken.","2016 EC entrance"],["I understand it is taking them years to________________ the shock of their son's death. I really pity them.",["Get down","Put over","Go over","Get over"],3,"The phrasal verb 'get over' means to recover from a shock, illness, or emotional trauma.","2009 EC entrance"],["Practice has shown us that conflicts __________ occur here and there in the country and unfortunately we lost\nthousands of lives.",["might","ought to","will","would"],2,"The modal 'will' is used to express general truths or predictable characteristic behaviors (things that are known to happen regularly based on practice).","2016 EC entrance"],["We should teach children to _________ when they cross roads. There could be speeding vehicles coming from\neither direction.",["look ahead","look out","look on","look back"],1,"The phrasal verb 'look out' means to watch out or be vigilant, which is crucial when crossing roads to avoid speeding vehicles.","2011 EC entrance"],["____________ need further clarification, give us a call or pay us a visit. We will be happy to assist.",["You may","You will","Would you","Should you"],3,"'Should you' is an inverted conditional structure equivalent to 'If you should', which is used to make formal offers of assistance.","2011 EC entrance"],["Wheel chair user: Could you tell me where the computer center is on this building? You : Oh sure, the 3rd room\nfrom here _______ Wheel chair user : Thank you indeed.",["Leave your wheelchair in my office.","Don't leave your wheelchair in my office.","Oh sure, the 3rd room from here.","Can I help you push the wheelchair?"],3,"Since the interlocutor is a wheelchair user, offering assistance by asking 'Can I help you push the wheelchair?' is polite and matches their grateful response: 'Thank you indeed.'","2014 EC entrance"],["Kosif: I have a job interview after tomorrow. Naftai: ________________",["Job interviews are frustrating.","If you dress smartly, you’ll impress them.","How long have you been jobless?","I know many people looking for a job."],1,"Providing encouraging advice like 'If you dress smartly, you'll impress them' is the most supportive, polite, and natural response to a friend who has an upcoming job interview.","2016 EC entrance"],["I found it difficult ___________the content of the lecturer’s explanation at university.",["to understand","to understanding","understand of","for understanding"],0,"The construction 'find it + adjective' is followed by a 'to-infinitive' ('to understand').","2016 EC entrance"],["Friend: your cousin has just told me he's getting married next week are you very pleased? you: ________, but he\ncould have told me earlier.",["I'm absolutely delighted","no, actually","I'm not","where is the wedding to be held"],0,"The conjunction 'but' introduces a minor complaint, meaning the first clause must answer the friend's question affirmatively with a positive sentiment like 'I'm absolutely delighted'.","2010 EC entrance"],["Teacher: what time do you go to bed? Student: __________________",["At ten o'clock.","After dinner.","very early.","very late."],0,"A direct question asking 'What time...?' expects a specific clock time as the answer, making 'At ten o'clock' the best choice.","2007 EC entrance"],["Adam:__________________ Mary: my pleasure. Just tell me what you want.",["Could you buy me a battery for my watch?","Shall I tell you a secret?","Could you do me a favour, please?","Can I use your camera, please?"],2,"'Could you do me a favour, please?' is the standard request that prompts Mary's willing reply, 'My pleasure. Just tell me what you want.'","2008 EC entrance"],["According to the authors one of those given below is recommended to help deal with climate change.",["expand on urbanization.","modernize agriculture.","prioritizing environmental rehabilitation.","commitment to gender equity."],2,"Prioritizing environmental rehabilitation (such as reforestation and soil conservation) is a primary and highly recommended national strategy to tackle climate change in Ethiopia.","2013 EC entrance"],["Conflicts ________ take place between the pastoralists and farmers in this area every time the dry season\ncomes. The government has to find a means of solving the shortage of water which is the main cause of the\nproblem.",["shall","may","Would","will"],3,"The modal 'will' is used here to express typical or habitual behavior in the present under specific conditions ('every time the dry season comes'). (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["The use of real life situations made the activity so interactive that everyone in the class loved it.",["argumentative","fascinating","distributive","participatory"],3,"An 'interactive' activity involves active participation from everyone, making 'participatory' the most suitable synonym.","2014 EC entrance"],["The words below are NOT in the proper order. When put in the right order, they make a correct English sentence.\nChoose the alternative with a correct order. environment/a/of/affect/can/quality/polluted/our/a",["A polluted quality environment of our life can affect.","A polluted can environment affect our quality of life.","A polluted environment can affect our quality of life.","A polluted affect environment of quality can our life."],2,"Option B forms a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence: 'A polluted environment can affect our quality of life.'","2013 EC entrance"],["Abush: _____________________________________________\nFriend: My dream is actually to visit Japan. The cleanliness attract me.",["Which place in the world do you want to visit?","Which place in the world do you like most?","Which country in the world is attractive you.","Which country are you planning to visit?"],0,"The friend's response refers to a 'dream to visit' a place, which matches the question 'Which place in the world do you want to visit?'","2016 EC entrance"],["The house _______ into last night and they have already reported it to the police. I'll try to follow up the\nprogress.",["was being broken","has broken","was broken","has been broken"],2,"The sentence requires the past simple passive ('was broken') because the action took place at a specific time in the past ('last night') and the focus is on the house receiving the action of the verb.","2015 EC entrance"],["__________ in the town could you find any safe haven. I ask you to leave before it is too late.",["Nothing","Neither","Nowhere","No one"],2,"The negative adverb 'Nowhere' triggers subject-verb inversion ('could you find') when placed at the beginning of a sentence.","2011 EC entrance"],["Bontu: inflation is still on the rise in this country. Don't you think so? Chaltu:___________________",["How about demand-supply balance?","What did you buy these days?","I am afraid, it is not.","Is that still a double digit?"],2,"'Don't you think so?' asks for an opinion or agreement; 'I am afraid, it is not' politely expresses disagreement with the statement that inflation is on the rise.","2007 EC entrance"],["Journalist: Thank you, Wolzero Hirut, for giving me the chance to ask you a few questions about your\norganization. Wolzero Hirut: ____________",["What is it this time? You were here last year, weren't you?","Okay. Go head. What do you want to know?","I have a meeting in an hour. Make it quick, please!","It's my pleasure and thank you for visiting us."],3,"In a formal interview, 'It's my pleasure and thank you for visiting us' is the most polite, professional, and welcoming response to a journalist's thanks.","2016 EC entrance"],["You: Why should they go at this time of the year? Friend: ________, the weather is great now.",["To give you an idea","You may not take it","To be certain","The convincing reason"],0,"'To give you an idea' is used to provide an explanation or context, explaining why going at this time of the year makes sense due to the great weather.","2016 EC entrance"],["We don't want to eat fatty food anymore __________ it is said to be among the diet causing heart problems.",["due to","since","because of","so that"],1,"The conjunction 'since' is used here to introduce a subordinate clause explaining the reason ('because it is said to be...').","2016 EC entrance"],["Doctors_________________ help you unless you tell them what's worng.",["Mustn't","Can't","Shouldn't","Couldn't"],1,"In a real present conditional with 'unless' ('unless you tell them'), the main clause uses 'can't' to express present inability.","2009 EC entrance"],["Teachers should _______ the attitude of honesty and integrity in the minds of their learners.",["cultivate","inflict","consolidate","impart"],0,"One 'cultivates' an attitude or mental quality in others, meaning to foster or grow it over time through teaching and practice. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Being, submissive is usually interpreted very negatively by many people. Others, however, claim that this can\nsometimes make people kind to you.",["alluring","stupid","docile","coward"],2,"The adjective 'docile' means ready to accept control or instruction, making it a direct synonym for 'submissive'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Your room is still _________! Remember, I told you to get your stuff organized when I visited you last time. If I\nfound the same next time, make sure you would be out.",["suffocated","unclean","crowded","untidy"],3,"The request to get 'stuff organized' indicates that the room is currently cluttered or 'untidy'.","2013 EC entrance"],["As the company is new, we will need to produce some kind of ______________ to be distributed to the\ncommunity around.",["leaflet","poster","newspaper","notice"],0,"A 'leaflet' is a printed sheet of paper containing information or advertising that is specifically designed to be distributed to people in a community","2015 EC entrance"],["before were in they a all packed room interrogation tiny started.",["Interrogation were started before they all packed in a tiny room.","Before they were packed started all interrogation in a tiny room.","All packed in a tiny room before they were started interrogation.","They were all packed in a tiny room before interrogation started."],3,"Arranging the words in the order of Option B produces 'They were all packed in a tiny room before interrogation started', which is the only coherent and grammatically correct sentence.","2011 EC entrance"],["I have searched all over and______________could it be found. Someone must have thrown ot out.",["somewhere","anywhere","everywhere","nowhere"],3,"The negative adverb 'nowhere' placed at the front of the clause causes subject-auxiliary inversion ('could it be found').","2006 EC entrance"],["The fundraising project in our kebele has been more successful than ever before. An insider told me\nthey_________ raise 10 million birr in six months.",["were able to","are able to","would be able to","may be able to"],0,"'Were able to' is used to talk about achieving a specific, difficult task on a particular past occasion, which fits the successful completion of the fundraising target.","2013 EC entrance"],["Obang: My computer has suddenly shut down. What has happened to it? Technician: __________________",["Mine has never been like that.","Is that a very old computer?","I hope that wouldn't be a virus.","Were you typing stuff on it?"],2,"A technician would logically speculate on the cause of a sudden shutdown, making 'I hope that wouldn't be a virus' a suitable diagnostic response.","2013 EC entrance"],["The new prime minister seems to have the _________ of a natural leader. But to be successful, he needs the\ncooperation of all the people.",["dynamics","dynamist","dynamicity","dynamism"],3,"'Dynamism' is the noun that describes the quality of being characterized by vigorous activity and progress, which perfectly describes the positive traits of a natural leader. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["He has secured his visa and everything necessary for his travel. They say he_____________move to the USA.",["is going to","May","might","will"],0,"'Is going to' expresses an intention or a plan that has already been arranged and prepared, evidenced by securing the visa and travel necessities.","2007 EC entrance"],["Everybody was unusually punctual. There was, however, someone very important that was still expected the\ndriver. While everyone was eagerly waiting to leave the campus, Samuel's phone range. It was the driver.....This is\ntaken from a piece of writing that is most likely:",["narrative","descriptive","expository","augmentative"],0,"The paragraph tells a story by describing a situation and an unfolding event ('While everyone was eagerly waiting... Samuel's phone rang'), which is the hallmark of narrative writing.","2006 EC entrance"],["_________ prices are still on the rise, we hope they will come down in the near future.",["In contrast to","Nevertheless","Although","Even if"],2,"'Although' is a subordinating conjunction used to introduce a clause of concession, showing contrast between rising prices and the hope that they will come down.","2015 EC entrance"],["You_______ try paying them more money to get the job done.",["were to","should","are to","have to"],1,"The modal verb 'should' is used here to offer a suggestion or advice on how to get the job done.","2013 EC entrance"],["___________________ You come around, i see you making troubles. That is really intolerable.",["Always","Sometimes","All time","Every time"],3,"'Every time' acts as a subordinating conjunction meaning 'whenever', linking the clause 'you come around' to the main clause.","2009 EC entrance"],["Workers in big firms receive a substantial part of their pay in the form of attractive bonuses and overtime.",["distinct","fixed","sensitive","considerable"],3,"The word 'substantial' means of considerable importance, size, or worth.","2013 EC entrance"],["I just heard on the radio that the company is selling goods at a big discount. I___________________ go and\ncheck if there is anything i might need.",["Would","am going to","may","Will"],3,"We use 'will' for spontaneous decisions made at the moment of speaking (upon just hearing the news).","2009 EC entrance"],["I wish that we _______ today. It is really freezing and wet.",["didn't need to work","have not worked","are not working","will not need to work"],0,"To express a regret or wish about a present situation ('today'), the past simple subjunctive ('didn't need to work') is used after 'wish'.","2015 EC entrance"],["Nana: Dad is getting us a new TV set. I am excited. Chala: _____________.",["Many people around do not have a TV set.","How much is he going to pay?","I can't believe that!","Is your dad rich enough?"],2,"Nana shares good news and says she is excited, so the reply should share the feeling. \"I can't believe that!\" is the surprised, pleased reaction news like this expects. B is the trap because it is a question about the family's money, which turns a happy announcement into something uncomfortable.","2005 EC entrance"],["From the excerpts below A-D, identify the one stated in a formal register",["Hi Samson! Are you okay?","Good morning, Mr. Tsegaye. How are you today?","Are you gonna to Friendship Park tomorrow?","Yeah, I am okay. And you?"],1,"Formal register uses a full greeting, a title with the family name, and complete words. D has all three: Good morning, Mr. Tsegaye. How are you today? Hi, Yeah and gonna are marks of informal spoken English, so A, B and C are casual. Rule: Formal writing avoids short forms and slang, and uses titles such as Mr., Mrs. and Dr.","2015 EC entrance"],["My friend took out a ___ from a bank to buy a house, but he could not pay it back in time.",["payment","profit","saving","loan"],3,"To borrow money from a bank to purchase property is to take out a 'loan'.","2014 EC entrance"],["All my friends wanted coffee so I_______________them some.",["make","made","could make","will make"],1,"The sentence describes a completed past action matching the past tense in the first clause ('wanted coffee so I made them some').","2006 EC entrance"],["The interviewee impressed the committee, __________?",["didn't they","did he","did they","didn't he"],3,"For a positive statement in the past simple ('impressed'), the correct question tag is negative and uses the auxiliary 'did' ('didn't he').","2018 EC entrance"],["Nurse: __________________ Patient: Do i have to ?",["Don't disturb, please, be quiet.","Have you taken your medicine?","How do you feel now?","Sleep well. I wish you good dreams."],1,"When asked 'Have you taken your medicine?', a reluctant patient would respond with 'Do I have to [take it]?' to question the necessity of doing so.","2009 EC entrance"],["I am writing to express my disappointment with the Samsung television I purchased from your store on January\n15, 2025 (Receipt #2345). The screen developed dark lines within two weeks of purchase. This letter is most\nlikely a/an:",["Order letter","Application letter","Apology letter","Complaint letter"],2,"The writer names a disappointment, the product, the date of purchase, the receipt number and the fault that appeared. Writing to a shop about a faulty product is a complaint. Option C, an apology letter, would come from the side at fault, and here the writer is the buyer.","2018 EC entrance"],["You don't seem to have ever seen the creature __________ I told you about. It looked nothing like a kangaroo\nexcept in the way it walked.",["one","who","whom","which"],3,"The relative pronoun 'which' (or 'that') is used to refer to non-human entities like 'the creature'.","2015 EC entrance"],["If you don't tell the truth, they __________ keep you jailed forever. Better say that you killed him in defense of\nyourself and you may be paroled.",["will","may","must","would"],0,"This is a First Conditional sentence ('If you don't tell... they will keep...'), where 'will' expresses a certain future consequence of a real possibility.","2016 EC entrance"],["Student: We went to Sodere for the weekend. Teacher________________?",["Where did you go","What for","When did you go","You went where"],1,"The student already stated both the destination ('Sodere') and the time ('the weekend'), so asking 'What for?' is the only logical follow-up to learn the purpose of the trip.","2009 EC entrance"],["If he ___ more carefully, he wouldn't have had the accident.",["would drive","had driven","drove","has driven"],1,"This is a third conditional sentence expressing a hypothetical past situation. The structure requires 'If' + past perfect ('had driven') in the condition clause, and 'would have' + past participle in the consequence clause. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["Many accidents occur_______ drivers are often reckless.",["however","so that","because","despite"],2,"The subordinating conjunction 'because' is used to introduce the clause that gives the reason why many accidents occur.","2013 EC entrance"],["Of all the stuff she bought yesterday, I like the books ______________ she got from the library. I started reading\none of them and the story is really thrilling.",["which","those","whom","whose"],0,"The relative pronoun 'which' is used to refer to things or objects, such as 'the books', in a relative clause. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["a take half it one days to may and cure.",["It may take to cure one and a half days.","It may take one and half days to a cure.","It may take a one and half days to cure.","It may take one and a half days to cure."],3,"The scrambled words are correctly arranged to form the grammatically and semantically sound sentence: 'It may take one and a half days to cure.'","2011 EC entrance"],["Chief: I think we should leave. I didn't like the atmosphere. Yared: ____________ things seem to be changing for\npositive. Let's wait a bit.",["I agree up to a point, but","On the one hand, however","If you think that way","Even though that is the case"],0,"'I agree up to a point, but' is used to politely acknowledge the chief's concern about the atmosphere while presenting a counter-argument to wait.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is NOT implied in what the author states reasons for diversity?",["One's behavioral characteristics","The social origin of the individual","The kind of people one met in life","The kind of family one comes from"],0,"While family, social origin, and personal associations are external factors/reasons that shape diversity (nurture), one's behavioral characteristics are the outcome or expression of that diversity, rather than its cause.","2013 EC entrance"],["my actions and the trouble I have caused...\" this is likely taken from a letter of__________________",["enquiry","complaint","disappointment","apology"],3,"Acknowledging one's own negative actions and expressing regret for the trouble caused is characteristic of a letter of apology.","2008 EC entrance"],["You: i always have trouble with my English. What do you advise me to do? Friend:\n___________________________",["English is an international language.","I wish i could help.","You shouldn't bother about it.","Have you thought about seeing a doctor?"],1,"When unable to provide the requested advice, a speaker politely expresses regret using 'I wish I could help.'","2009 EC entrance"],["Yodit: we're going out for lunch. Would you come? Sara: ________________",["I am afraid, we have no money.","Who is going for lunch now?","I think, she will come?","I would rather do it for dinner."],3,"Sara politely expresses a preference for an alternative time ('I would rather do it for dinner') in response to Yodit's lunch invitation.","2008 EC entrance"],["Children using the swimming pool must be ________ by an adult at all times.",["accorded","accompanied","adapted","accustomed"],1,"'Accompanied by' means to be escorted or joined by someone, which is the standard safety requirement for children at a swimming pool.","2010 EC entrance"],["You ___________ furious I haven't seen you presenting like this before.",["must be","can be","should have been","might be"],0,"'Must be' is used to make a logical deduction based on strong present evidence.","2016 EC entrance"],["Aster: Is he your husband? I haven't met him before. Lidya: Come on, ________ How dare you?",["why do you ask?","my husband is handsome.","what do you mean?","I love my husband."],2,"Lidya's response 'How dare you?' indicates she finds Aster's question or insinuation offensive, and 'what do you mean?' perfectly expresses this indignation.","2016 EC entrance"],["She will have to see the manager __________ she arrives. I heard he is going to send her to the new branch in\nGambella.",["as soon as","on time as","sooner after","very soon"],0,"'As soon as' is a temporal conjunction meaning 'immediately after', which perfectly fits the timeline of her arrival and meeting the manager.","2016 EC entrance"],["The fact is that I didn't know she was in such a serious problem. Now you calm down and I ____________ do\neverything possible. OK?",["will","am going to","may","can"],0,"The modal 'will' is used to express a spontaneous decision or promise made at the moment of speaking, such as offering immediate assistance.","2011 EC entrance"],["Physical labor can exhaust the body; ________. excessive reading can reduce mental power.",["sadly","incidentally","equally","regrettably"],2,"'Equally' is used here as a transition showing a parallel or equivalent effect between physical labor exhausting the body and excessive reading fatiguing the mind.","2010 EC entrance"],["The AU meeting to be held next month is expected to pass resolutions pertaining to the relationship between\nthe two warring parties. We are looking forward to it.",["summit","mediation","cluster","seminar"],0,"An official meeting of heads of state or high-level representatives, such as the African Union (AU) meeting, is called a 'summit'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Samson: How much coffee do you drink? Tewodros:_______________.",["at least five cups","only after lunch","I like coffee","I don't like strong coffee"],0,"The question 'How much coffee do you drink?' asks for a quantity, which is appropriately answered by 'at least five cups'.","2006 EC entrance"],["Committing corruption_______ life imprisonment in several countries in the world.",["impacts","leads to","affects","arises from"],1,"The phrasal verb 'leads to' means 'results in' or 'causes', which fits the context of corruption resulting in imprisonment.","2017 EC entrance"],["I was with her for dinner. She _______________ the car which they claim disappeared around 7 pm.",["won't have stolen","couldn't steal","would have stolen","can probably steal"],2,"The first sentence is an alibi: the speaker was with her at dinner, so she was not able to take the car at the time it disappeared. That denial of ability is \"couldn't\". B is the trap because \"would have stolen\" is also about the past, but it asserts that she did it, which contradicts the alibi the speaker has given.","2005 EC entrance"],["Speaking on the phone, if you press the red button, the call ______.",["ends","ended","would end","is ending"],0,"This is a zero conditional sentence (expressing a general rule or fact), which uses the simple present tense ('ends') in the main clause.","2013 EC entrance"],["Yihun: Poor Lili! She lost all her money.\nJember: ________________________________",["What a pity! How come?","How much money was it?","She is not very poor.","Was she walking around?"],0,"'What a pity! How come?' is a natural response that shows empathy for someone's misfortune and asks for elaboration.","2011 EC entrance"],["Bertukan: My new boyfriend loves me a lot.\nMamitu: ___________________________",["What is his name, please?","Isn't that rather too soon to say?","Did you break up with Temesgen?","He is very handsome, isn't he?"],1,"Since the boyfriend is 'new', Mamitu's skeptical response ('Isn't that rather too soon to say?') is a natural and conversational reaction to the claim that he already loves her a lot.","2011 EC entrance"],["These people are so mean that they hardly give anything to charity. They are different from the other village",["Selfish","unfriendly","Unsociable","Rude"],0,"In British and general English, 'mean' often describes someone who is tight-fisted or unwilling to share or give money to others, closely meaning 'selfish' or ungenerous.","2008 EC entrance"],["Why are you worried about her? I know she is capable . Just leave her alone and you will see how beautifully she \nwould do it.",["bright","clever","competent","diligent"],2,"\"Capable\" means having the ability, fitness, or quality necessary to do something, which is synonymous with \"competent\".","2013 EC entrance"],["The police arrested the man who often has his lunch at this afternoon and makes off .",["leaves in haste","leaves slowly","sleeps","snores"],0,"The phrasal verb 'make off' means to hurry away, especially in order to escape, which corresponds to 'leaves in haste'. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["I __________ this job for the last 35 years and I don't think I would even think of changing it. It is my world and I\nfeel there is no better world for me.",["have done","was doing","had done","am doing"],0,"The present perfect 'have done' is used with 'for the last 35 years' to indicate an activity that began in the past and continues to the present moment. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["Look! The sky is cloudy and __________ to get your T-shirts in.",["I feel","I think","I know","I hope"],3,"The verb 'hope' is grammatically followed by a 'to-infinitive' ('I hope to get your T-shirts in'), whereas 'think', 'feel', and 'know' do not fit this grammatical structure in this context.","2016 EC entrance"],["They had to get together at six in the morning and when we got up at 5:45 a.m, we thought we wouldn't make it. \nHowever, we ________________________ to get there before they left.",["could be able","must be able","are able","were able"],3,"'Were able' is used to express successful performance of a specific action in the past, especially when overcoming difficulties.","2016 EC entrance"],["________ by the speech of the new leader, all the people of the Zone elected him to be Member of Parliament.",["Demotivated","Inspired","Discouraged","Offended"],1,"The fact that the people elected him to the parliament indicates they were positively moved and 'inspired' by his speech.","2017 EC entrance"],["Olonso: Is everything ready? They’re coming this Sunday. Melana: ________________",["Sunday is a day of worship, of course.","I doubt they’ve changed their schedule.","Do you think you’ll be here on Sunday?","Let’s hope they’ll bring us some clothes."],1,"In response to a question about readiness for guests arriving on Sunday, Melana's assurance that she expects them on schedule ('I doubt they’ve changed their schedule') is the most relevant and logical answer. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following can be the best title for the passage?",["Recycling Paper","Paper Pollution","Recyclable and Unrecyclable Things","Paper Manufacturing"],0,"\"Recycling Paper\" is the most suitable title because the text focuses on the environmental impacts of paper production and how recycling helps mitigate them.","2014 EC entrance"],["Heavy shellings in several cities of Syria have turned buildings into rubbles. It would obviously take a lot of\nresource to reconstruct them",["Debris","Rubbish","Desert","Wilderness"],0,"'Rubble' refers to the broken fragments or remains of destroyed buildings, which is synonymous with 'debris'.","2009 EC entrance"],["Customer: I'd like to withdraw 5,000 Birr, please. Cashier: ____________________?",["Could you write your name here, please","How would you like the money","Do you want to make a withdrawal","What is the interest rate on your account"],1,"\"How would you like the money?\" is the standard question a cashier asks a customer who is making a cash withdrawal, referring to the preferred bill denominations.","2014 EC entrance"],["Funny in (par2) means",["Causing laughter","Causing sorrow","belonging to the rich","belonging to the slaves"],0,"'Funny' is defined as causing laughter or amusement.","2016 EC entrance"],["Never lose hope and don't stop your struggle. You will, one day, come out ___________ and put to shame all\nthose who told you would see no success.",["improving","effective","triumphant","reviving"],2,"Coming out 'triumphant' means achieving victory or success, which perfectly contrasts with and puts to shame those who predicted failure. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Despite the provocative comments made by some of her audience, she chose her words very carefully\n__________ not to go out of topic and make the issue personal. I really admired her patience.",["so as","because of","so that","in order that"],0,"The phrase 'so as not to' is the correct negative infinitive of purpose, used to show the intention behind choosing her words carefully.","2011 EC entrance"],["Next time you come to class don't forget to ___ your textbook.",["having brought","bring","bringing","to bring"],1,"The phrase 'don't forget to' is followed by the bare infinitive of the verb, which is 'bring' (since 'to' is already provided in the sentence template). (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["After her long career in several international organizations, she is now engaged in humanitarian service\nintending to give back to the community.",["charitable","obligatory","profitable","professional"],0,"Humanitarian services focus on helping people and improving human welfare, which is synonymous with 'charitable' work.","2016 EC entrance"],["Surafel: They should know that we can't help them because we don't have the time. Tolera:\n______________________",["Besides, we don't have the required resources.","We can find out the information from our friend.","They insist on going out for dinner this evening.","We don't clearly know why he is so interested in the matter."],0,"Surafel explains they cannot help because of a lack of time. Tolera supports this explanation by adding another constraint ('Besides, we don't have the required resources') using the transition word 'besides'. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Ziyad: I hear they provide free lunch here. Mukerem: No! ________________________, nobody will do the public\nworks.",["If there is free lunch","If you have free lunch","In my opinion","Despite lunch is free"],0,"The conditional 'If there is free lunch, nobody will do...' represents a realistic first conditional situation expressing the speaker's concern.","2016 EC entrance"],["'Love is a very powerful force; it conquers barriers of color, race, religion, and culture. It thrives on mutual\nnurturing of each other,' it is very likely that the writing is:",["argumentative","expository","narrative","descriptive"],1,"The excerpt explains and defines the abstract concept of love and its characteristics. Explaining or defining a topic is the primary purpose of expository writing.","2018 EC entrance"],["Mebratu: What are the primary stages of coffee preparation? Rukya: First, we wash, roast and ground coffee\nbeans. ______, we add the coffee powder into the kettle.",["To begin with","The last step","For more clarity","Having done this"],3,"The participle phrase 'Having done this' functions as a transition, meaning 'after washing, roasting, and grinding coffee beans'.","2018 EC entrance"],["II. Language Focus (Questions 33–65)\nYou had better ______ an umbrella. It looks like it will rain.",["took","taking","to take","take"],3,"\"Had better\" is followed by the base form of the verb (infinitive without \"to\"). \"You had better take an umbrella.\" We never use \"to\" after \"had better\" or \"would rather.\"","2018 EC entrance"],["If the police men had not been carrying a gun, he could not have killed the criminal.",["The policeman wasn't carrying a gun and he didn't kill the criminal","The policeman was carrying a gun but he was not able to kill the criminal.","The policeman was not carrying a gun.","The policeman was carrying a gun."],3,"This third conditional sentence (\"If + past perfect..., could have...\") describes a hypothetical scenario that is the opposite of what actually happened. Thus, the implication is that the policeman was carrying a gun and killed the criminal.","2016 EC entrance"],["Apparently there are lots of buildings in Addis Ababa that should be, _________ because of their inferior quality.\nIf left alone, they could be risky to the occupants.",["pulled off","pulled down","pulled away","pulled out"],1,"The phrasal verb 'pulled down' means to demolish a building, which is necessary for structures of inferior quality to prevent them from collapsing on occupants.","2011 EC entrance"],["Robel: It's our friend's wedding this coming Sunday, so I'll have my hair done tomorrow. What about you? Genet:\n________. We should look our best on this great day!",["So will I","Neither will I","Nor should I","I will also"],0,"To agree with a positive future statement ('I'll have my hair done...'), the structure 'So will I' is used. 'Neither' and 'Nor' are used to agree with negative statements.","2016 EC entrance"],["Teacher: Today I'm going to tell you about AI. Student: ________ Teacher: AI, meaning Artificial Intelligence.",["I didn't hold that. Could you repeat that, please?","I didn't catch that. Could you repeat that, please?","I see I got your point.","You're speaking fast, but I can hear you."],1,"The student needs clarification of what 'AI' means. 'I didn't catch that. Could you repeat that, please?' is a standard English idiom used when one fails to hear or understand something.","2016 EC entrance"],["AIDS patients used to be alienated for having HIV in their blood. Today, however, things have changed and they\nare treated like any healthy person.",["involved","disappointed","stigmatized","preserved"],2,"To be 'alienated' or treated as an outcast due to a disease like HIV/AIDS is synonymous with being 'stigmatized'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Many of my friends were in heated argument about which team would win the game last night; in fact, i was\n______________ and simply enjoyed watching the game.",["unfair","Discouraged","Indifferent","Unwise"],2,"'Indifferent' means having no preference or biased interest in the outcome, contrasting with friends engaged in a heated argument.","2009 EC entrance"],["We all contributed what is within our reach ________________ help the needy children in our school. We bought \nthem the stationery they needed for the whole year.",["So that to","because of to","So as to","because to"],2,"The phrase 'so as to' is used to express purpose followed by a bare infinitive ('help').","2013 EC entrance"],["Eldana: it is time we left. It is going to rain later. Friend:________________i_ don 't want to get my hair wet.",["I couldn't agree more.","what do you tell me?","should we really go?","we've been here for long."],0,"\"I couldn't agree more\" expresses strong agreement with Eldana's recommendation to leave before the rain starts. (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["Thomas: Constant use of social media leads to low reading habits. Gebre: ______________.",["I won't say that","I agree with you entirely","I don't have reading habits","I have the right to say that"],1,"The phrase 'I agree with you entirely' is a standard and polite way of expressing total agreement with another person's opinion in a conversation.","2013 EC entrance"],["Ethiopia is working hard towards strengthening its ______ relations with many countries.",["automatic","diplomatic","aromatic","dramatic"],1,"'Diplomatic' relations refers to the formal relations maintained between nations, which fits the context of Ethiopia's international efforts. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["This year, money _________ for the construction of a wider and greener football pitch. The school management\nhas decided to improve the sports field in our school.",["has raised","will be raising","is being raised","is raising"],2,"The noun 'money' is the receiver of the action, so the passive voice is required; 'is being raised' indicates an ongoing action happening 'this year'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Who does ' our ' as used in Paragraph 1 Line 1 refer to?",["Chimps","Friends talking","The writers","Human beings"],3,"The term 'our' refers to human beings, as the passage discusses chimpanzees being our closest living evolutionary relatives, sharing over 98% of our DNA.","2016 EC entrance"],["We were worried that everybody had very little money left. It was even more frustrating that Abdu, our group\nleader, had the __________ compared to the rest of us.",["more little","less","most little","least"],3,"The superlative adjective 'least' is correct because it is preceded by the definite article 'the' and compares Abdu's money to that of everyone else in the group.","2011 EC entrance"],["The smell of fresh 'doro wat' and bread was omnipresent in the neighbourhood during the holidays. We used to\nenjoy it by moving here and there when we were in our country. (omnipresent means)",["very inaccessible","affordable","find everywhere","tests delicious"],0,"The sentence says the smell filled the neighbourhood during the holidays and that people moved about enjoying it. Omnipresent means present in every place. Option C, very inaccessible, would mean hard to reach, which is the opposite of a smell you meet wherever you go.","2018 EC entrance"],["Interviewer: ______ Interviewee: I applied for the position of Business Manager.",["Tell me about yourself.","With which skills are you most comfortable?","What would I give you?","What position are you looking for?"],3,"The interviewee's response directly names the job position they applied for, which answers 'What position are you looking for?'","2018 EC entrance"],["I always believe it is healthy for everyone to repress their emotions.",["throw away","kick out","throw out","hold back"],3,"To 'repress' emotions means to restrain or suppress them, which corresponds directly to the phrasal verb 'hold back'.","2010 EC entrance"],["I don't like people who beat around the bush. I want them to...",["come to an agreement","look for the hidden point","stop blaming others for their own mistakes","stop avoiding the issue"],3,"To beat around the bush is to talk around a subject instead of saying the point. So the speaker wants people to stop avoiding the issue. Option B is tempting because of the word bush, but the idiom blames the speaker for hiding the point, not the listener for hunting it.","2018 EC entrance"],["am / as / think / I / not / I / you / stupid / am / as",["I am not as stupid as you think I am.","As you think I am not stupid as I am.","I am not as I think am stupid as you.","I am not as you think as I am."],0,"This option organizes the words into the grammatically and logically coherent sentence: 'I am not as stupid as you think I am.'","2017 EC entrance"],["often / to quite/I/ dream/ my job.",["I often dream to quit my job.","my job often dream to quit.","I dream often to quit my job.","I quit my job to dream"],0,"The scrambled words are correctly arranged in option D to form the grammatical sentence 'I often dream to quit my job' (correcting the typo 'quite' to 'quit').","2016 EC entrance"],["Student: are we having an exam next week? Teacher:________________",["Your result last time was so good.","How many units have we done?","I am not sure yet, but you might.","In fact, exams are approaching."],2,"The student asks a direct yes/no question about the possibility of an exam, and the teacher appropriately answers with their current state of planning: \"I am not sure yet, but you might.\"","2008 EC entrance"],["Mesele: It seems we are in a difficult time at the moment. Kuma: _______________________",["Please arrive here as early as you can","Where are we?","I believe the situation will improve soon.","We have informed them already."],2,"Kuma's response 'I believe the situation will improve soon' is a logical, reassuring, and cohesive reply to Mesele's observation about being in a difficult time.","2013 EC entrance"],["I was _______ scared to go out in the dark alone. That is why I couldn't join you for dinner.",["absolutely","certainly","surely","definitely"],0,"'Absolutely' is used as an intensifier with adjectives to show a high degree of emotion (e.g., 'absolutely scared'). (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["The teacher asked us to hand in the homework this Friday.",["Admit","Transmit","Transfer","Submit"],3,"The phrasal verb 'hand in' means to give or submit completed work to a person in authority, such as a teacher.","2009 EC entrance"],["On her return from a trip, she got an accident resulting in the amputation on her right leg.",["fitness","scratch","impairment","sickness"],2,"The amputation of a limb results in a permanent physical 'impairment' or disability. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["______________ telephones first appeared they were called talking telegraphs.",["Later on","When","Next","Then"],1,"The subordinating conjunction 'When' is used to introduce the adverbial clause of time in this sentence.","2013 EC entrance"],["In a formal letter the recipient's address will be",["at the bottom of the letter.","in the top right hand corner.","below the sender's address.","below his or her name."],2,"In the standard business letter the sender's own address comes first, then the date, and then the address of the person receiving the letter, on the left. So the recipient's address sits below the sender's address. The top right corner belongs to the sender's address, and nothing about the address goes at the foot of the letter.","2015 EC entrance"],["My friend says that she ______ all her assignments already.",["will be doing","will be done","has done","will do"],2,"The present perfect tense 'has done' is used with 'already' to indicate a completed action reported in the present tense ('says').","2014 EC entrance"],["Ato Bisrat has been ______________chairman of the new committee.",["appointed","applauded","apologized","appreciated"],0,"'Appointed' means officially assigned or chosen for a job or position of responsibility, such as committee chairman.","2006 EC entrance"],["Pen: Write; Rubber: __________",["Erase","Remove","Sweep","Eliminate"],0,"The relationship is tool to function: a pen is used to write, and a rubber (eraser) is used to erase.","2016 EC entrance"],["If a chairperson's argument is nebulous in the meeting, it will confuse the participants.",["precise","apparent","alert","vague"],3,"'Nebulous' means vague, ill-defined, or unclear, which naturally leads to confusion among participants.","2018 EC entrance"],["I know I was______________ in the field, but not exactly where.",["every where","somewhere","nowhere","anywhere"],1,"'Somewhere' is used in affirmative sentences to indicate an unspecified or unknown location, fitting the phrase 'not exactly where'.","2007 EC entrance"],["Kenubish: It is heavily cloudy. Do you think we can go? Kenan: ________________ Let’s make it some other day.",["Rain means green. You should really be happy.","It looks as if it is going to rain.","You know we’ve been in the whole day.","So what? That’s OK."],1,"Kenan's suggestion to postpone ('Let's make it some other day') supports the observation that 'It looks as if it is going to rain' due to the heavy clouds.","2016 EC entrance"],["The man says that he can beat anybody in a fight, but actually he is cowardly bully.",["dishonest","timid","confident","brave"],1,"The word 'cowardly' describes someone who lacks courage, which is synonymous with 'timid'.","2014 EC entrance"],["__________I do not complain much; my friends often take me for a fool.",["Because","Because of","As a result of","In spite of"],0,"The subordinating conjunction 'Because' is used to introduce a clause of reason ('I do not complain much') that explains the main clause.","2017 EC entrance"],["Ethiopia will enjoy a period of peace and ________ in the next few years; this happens if the country ensures\nlaw and gives priority to science, technology and innovation.",["prosperity","nationality","disparity","protest"],0,"The phrase 'peace and prosperity' is a common English collocation that fits the positive future predicted for the country.","2017 EC entrance"],["The organization's new group of trucks has just arrived after ten days' journey from the port.",["crowd","fleet","troop","band"],1,"A 'fleet' is the correct collective noun used to describe a group of vehicles, ships, or trucks operating together. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Your persistent complaints have now started to irritate me. How come that your eyes cannot see anything\npositive of what is going on?",["disgust","annoy","prick","itch"],1,"The verb \"irritate\" means to make someone annoyed, impatient, or angry.","2013 EC entrance"],["Any country needs a strong government in order to limit or eradicate unlawful activities by some elements of\nsociety.",["suspicious","trading","illicit","secretive"],2,"'Illicit' means forbidden by law, rules, or custom, making it the perfect synonym for 'unlawful' activities.","2016 EC entrance"],["\"it is possible to see that parental influence has a significant impact on the academic performance and social\ninteraction of a child.\" Which section of a research report is this most likely taken from?",["introduction","discussion","Conclusion","body"],2,"The phrase 'it is possible to see that parental influence has a significant impact...' summarizes the overarching findings and implications of the study, which belongs in the Conclusion section.","2008 EC entrance"],["As mistake is to eraser so is constitution to ___________________",["Revolution","Draft","Amendment","Concise"],2,"An eraser is used to modify or correct a mistake, just as an amendment is used to modify or alter a constitution.","2009 EC entrance"],["You know! __________ his diligence, you here nobody talking positively of him. I can't understand if the secret\nbehind is luck or lack.",["Because of","Even though","In spite of","Despite of"],2,"'In spite of' is a prepositional phrase followed by a noun phrase ('his diligence'). Option B is incorrect because 'despite' is never followed by 'of', and Option D requires a full clause.","2016 EC entrance"],["My sister is such a little nuisance; she often like to ask too many silly questions.",["Stupid","Exciting","Sad","Annoying"],3,"A 'nuisance' is a person, thing, or circumstance causing irritation or inconvenience, corresponding to 'annoying'.","2009 EC entrance"],["We cannot interfere at the moment. He __________ and all we can do is wait until they finish it and see their\ndecision.",["will have interrogated","was being interrogated","is interrogating","is being interrogated"],3,"The phrase 'at the moment' indicates a present ongoing action, and since the subject 'He' is receiving the action, the present continuous passive 'is being interrogated' is correct.","2016 EC entrance"],["What does the word ' demands ' as used in paragraph 4, line 5 mean?",["opportunities","requirements","orders","requests"],1,"In an academic or institutional context, 'demands' refers to the rigorous standards or 'requirements' that must be met.","2016 EC entrance"],["I often can't stand people who always complain. They get on my nerve.",["take","tell","tolerate","See"],2,"The idiom 'can't stand' means to strongly dislike or be unable to tolerate someone or something.","2007 EC entrance"],["Mekbib: Excuse me, can you lend me a pencil? Zeritu: _________________",["Here you are.","Which one?","Can you borrow?","I've a pen."],0,"'Here you are' is the standard polite phrase used when handing someone an item they have requested to borrow. (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["He asked her to turn round several times before he gave her his opinion of her new dress.",["hold on","display","pose","rotate"],3,"To 'turn round' means to rotate or spin around, allowing someone to view something from all angles.","2017 EC entrance"],["Mamusha: You've got a nice car. It looks great. Yaya: Sure, but _________",["it is not as fast as yours","it is brand new straight from Japan","it is as fast as yours","it is not very good, I'm afraid"],0,"The conjunction 'but' introduces a contrasting limitation about the car, making 'it is not as fast as yours' the most logical option when comparing it to the speaker's car.","2016 EC entrance"],["There is a need to assign an expert to wipe up unnecessary data from computer.",["set up","down load","work out","clean up"],3,"'Wipe up' (often used interchangeably with 'wipe out' or 'clean up' in computing context) means to remove or delete unnecessary data to free up space.","2018 EC entrance"],["Aster: _____does your father do?\nRegasa: He’s a teacher",["Where","who","how","what"],3,"The question 'What does [someone] do?' is the standard way to ask about someone's occupation or job.","2016 EC entrance"],["Alem: The report is not comprehensive. Ululu:____________________",["Sure. The language is really terrible.","I know, it is not easy to understand.","That is true. It has no focus at all.","Certainly. Send it back to her."],3,"Ululu agrees with Alem's evaluation that the report is inadequate (not comprehensive) and offers an appropriate course of action: \"Certainly. Send it back to her.\"","2008 EC entrance"],["Lensa: My spoken English is really horrible; ________________? Zemzem: Practice speaking every day in front\nof your friends.",["what should I do","why you learn English","do you like English","what is yours like"],0,"Zemzem's response is a piece of advice ('Practice speaking every day...'), which directly answers Lensa's question asking for advice, 'what should I do?'. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Abebe: let us contribute to the building of the Renaissance Dam You:____________________",["What is the position of Egypt now?","How much if it has been completed?","I was really proud when I visited it.","Splendid! I can't agree more."],3,"'Splendid! I can't agree more' expresses strong agreement with Abebe's suggestion to contribute to the dam project.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following best replaces the word 'aggravated' in paragraph 2?",["regulated","supplemented","worsened","improved"],2,"The verb 'aggravated' means to make a problem or injury worse, so 'worsened' is the correct synonym.","2017 EC entrance"],["What does the word they (Para. 4) refer to?",["her teachers","her friends","her parents","her siblings"],0,"In her memoirs, she frequently refers to her teachers as her 'saviors' who opened up the world to her, making 'they' refer to her teachers.","2016 EC entrance"],["Breakfast to bread are have going for we.",["We are going to have for breakfast bread.","We are for breakfast going to have bread.","We are going to have bread for breakfast.","We are going for bread to have breakfast."],2,"The standard English word order for this sentence is subject + be going to + verb + direct object + prepositional phrase: \"We are going to have bread for breakfast.\"","2008 EC entrance"],["Their plane is expected to land slightly after 3:00 pm. _______ it gets late, give me a call and I'll see what I can\ndo.",["In case","Unless","Probably","But for"],0,"'In case' is used to talk about things we do in order to be prepared for possible future situations (e.g., calling if the plane gets late).","2015 EC entrance"],["Some students develop a problem of______________________ to the university environment .They should be\nproperly counselled.",["Unadjustment","misadjustment","Inadjustent","Maladjustment"],3,"The correct prefix to denote bad, faulty, or inadequate adjustment is 'mal-', forming the standard psychological and general English noun 'maladjustment'.","2008 EC entrance"],["Son: dad, can you tell me the year I was born? Dad: yes,__________________________",["You're my first child.","you're 10 years old.","February","2007."],3,"The son asks for the year of his birth, and '2007' provides a specific year.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following phrases is similar in meaning to the phrase 'safe and beneficial' in paragraph 4?",["checked and important","treated and relevant","harmless and useful","protected and insignificant"],2,"The phrase 'safe and beneficial' is synonymous with 'harmless and useful' because 'safe' means free from harm and 'beneficial' means producing good results or being useful.","2018 EC entrance"],["The police should heighten the awareness of the community in order to put",["raise","realize","materialize","legalize"],0,"To 'heighten' awareness means to increase or 'raise' it, making 'raise' the best synonym. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["A story written by a person about his/her experience of travelling from one place to another would most likely\nbe________________",["process","narrative","argumentative","descriptive"],1,"A story recounting personal experiences of travelling from one place to another in chronological order is a narrative. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["There was a significant________ in crop production because of the shortage of rain.",["reduction","rise","amount","proportion"],0,"A shortage of rain naturally leads to a decrease or 'reduction' in agricultural crop production.","2013 EC entrance"],["Guest: the kitchen handle has come off. You: don't worry.________",["it has never been like that","it's none of your business","you will buy a replacement","it often does"],3,"Saying 'it often does' reassures the guest that the incident is a common occurrence and not their fault.","2010 EC entrance"],["I can't meet you these days I __________ my semester assignment which is due in two weeks' time.",["would have done","could be doing","will have done","will be doing"],3,"The future continuous 'will be doing' is used to describe an ongoing action that will occupy her time in the near future.","2016 EC entrance"],["Everybody suggested about the major causes of conflict, _____?",["did we","didn't they","weren't they","don't we"],1,"Everybody is picked up by they in a question tag, and the main verb, suggested, is past simple, so the tag is didn't they. Option B uses weren't, which would need a form of be in the main clause, and there is none.","2018 EC entrance"],["For any healthy business, there comes a point when the owners determine to take the _______________ of a\nnew growth strategy.",["immunity","conscience","risk","misunderstanding"],2,"\"Take the risk\" is a standard English collocation that means to do something although you know that something bad could happen, which fits the context of implementing a new growth strategy.","2016 EC entrance"],["You shouldn't let your children ____________ in this pool. The water hasn't been decreased for the past four\nmonths.",["swim","to swim","to swimming","to swam"],0,"The causative verb 'let' is followed by an object and a bare infinitive ('swim' without 'to').","2016 EC entrance"],["were the is stage that it high she time on.",["It is high time that she were on the stage.","It is the stage that she were on high time.","She is on high time that were it the stage.","She is on high time that it were the stage."],0,"The fixed expression is It is high time + subject + past form of the verb, and it means the action is already late. So the sentence is It is high time that she were on the stage. The past form were here is not real past time; it is the unreal past, the same form used after I wish. The other options put she or the stage in the subject position, which breaks the expression. See Grade 12 English, Unit 9, verb patterns with wish.","2015 EC entrance"],["Shumie: If you come from a poor family, you almost always end up poor. Nunu: No! ________________ His\nparents were poor but he’s a millionaire.",["If Mamo works hard, he’ll be OK.","I know somebody like that.","Biru is not in the business industry.","Take, for example, Shola."],3,"Nunu disagrees with Shumie's generalization and introduces Shola as a counterexample: 'Take, for example, Shola. His parents were poor but he’s a millionaire.'","2016 EC entrance"],["Aster: Jim and Jane are marrying next week.\nBeli: _____________________",["I know Jim loves her, but she was going out with someone else.","There are so many weddings to take place next week.","Jane is so beautiful that all the boys around like her.","I don't think they would make a good couple."],3,"Expressing an opinion on whether the couple is well-suited ('I don't think they would make a good couple') is a very common conversational reaction to a wedding announcement. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is most likely an opening to your application for a job?",["Dear Mr. Manager","greetings","Dear Sir","Hello Sir"],2,"\"Dear Sir\" is a traditional and highly appropriate formal salutation used when opening a job application letter when the recipient's name is unknown.","2016 EC entrance"],["There is no point in complaining about his immature behavior; he is always.",["premature","young","childlike","grown-up"],2,"'Immature' behavior in adults is often described as 'childlike' or childish, as it resembles the behavior of a child.","2014 EC entrance"],["Writing a formal letter in English is not difficult, but you should follow certain_______________.",["conventions","conversations","conversion","convictions"],0,"'Conventions' refers to widely accepted rules, norms, or practices, such as the standard format for formal letter writing.","2006 EC entrance"],["Yerom: may I give her my mobile phone? Wirtu:________________",["No way! Are you crazy?","Does she buy a mobile phone?","That is new. Isn't it?","She has lost everything."],0,"'No way! Are you crazy?' is a natural colloquial exclamation expressing strong objection to giving away a valuable personal item like a mobile phone.","2008 EC entrance"],["If you continue practising speaking English like this, you _______ speak it fluently very soon.",["shall","can","will be able to","are able to"],2,"In a first conditional sentence ('If + present simple'), the result clause expresses future ability using 'will be able to'.","2014 EC entrance"],["Same passage\nWhich of the following words is used to suggest disapproval? (paragraph 6)",["contraption","rounds","sniff","stuff"],2,"The phrase 'with a sniff' is used to show disdain or disapproval, indicating that medics look down upon the term or concept of 'cyberchondria'.","2018 EC entrance"],["The lady ___________next to our English teacher is my mother's close friend.",["sitting","sit","sits","sat"],0,"The present participle 'sitting' acts as a reduced relative clause (short for 'who is sitting') describing 'the lady'.","2017 EC entrance"],["Arkato: High school students should get training on note-taking skills. Hagos: ____________. Not now; they can\nhave it when they join university.",["Sure; I agree with you","I don't agree with you","I think you are right","This could save their study time"],1,"Hagos disagrees with Arkato's proposal by saying 'Not now', so 'I don't agree with you' is the correct response.","2018 EC entrance"],["Since its discovery back in 1981 G.C, HIV/AIDS is believed to have remained largely a serious problem among\nthose having many sexual partners.",["uncultured","promiscuous","impolite","prostitute"],1,"The term 'promiscuous' is defined as having many casual or transient sexual relationships or partners.","2016 EC entrance"],["When we were in Gambella, every day after work, we _________________ sit by the river watching fishers\ncaught the big fish called 'gur' and made a lot of money out of it.",["were used to","have used to","are used to","used to"],3,"The phrase 'used to' is used to describe past habits or states that no longer occur, fitting the context of what they did 'every day after work' when they were in Gambella. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["be who stories learn there about are to many couldn't how rich people.",["Stories are there about many rich people who couldn't learn how to be.","Stories about how many people are there who couldn't learn to be rich.","Many rich people are there who couldn't learn about stories.","There are many stories about people who couldn't learn how to be rich."],3,"Option A correctly arranges the words into a natural and grammatically sound English sentence: 'There are many stories about people who couldn't learn how to be rich.'","2015 EC entrance"],["_________ Berhe ________ Umod tampered with this computer. I haven't seen them around and I think they\nwere out of office the whole day.",["Either...or","Neither...nor","Both...and","Not only...but also"],1,"The correlative conjunction 'Neither...nor' is used to join two negative options, which is confirmed by the speaker stating they haven't seen either person all day.","2015 EC entrance"],["Ali:____________________ Almaz: That sounds reasonable.",["Shall we go for coffee?","Is Mimi doing her homework?","Isn't Abera coming this evening?","Did she buy a new purse?"],0,"'That sounds reasonable' is a natural response accepting or approving a proposal or suggestion, such as 'Shall we go for coffee?'.","2007 EC entrance"],["Yoyo: how long does it take to Dire Dawa? Yaya:____________________",["Not more than fifty birr.","It is around 500 kilometres.","Dire Dawa is very far.","it depends on your driving."],3,"'How long does it take?' asks about travel time, and 'It depends on your driving' directly addresses the duration.","2008 EC entrance"],["If he is visually impaired , tell him he should learn how to use braille. Otherwise, things will be hard for him when\nit comes to reading and writing.",["disabled","damaged","weakened","unable"],0,"In this context, \"visually impaired\" refers to a person who has a visual disability, making \"disabled\" the most appropriate synonym.","2013 EC entrance"],["a. They make their home in buildings, gardens, etc. b. Ants are found everywhere in the world. c. In the summer,\nants collect food for the winter season. d. They are very hardworking insects.",["c b a d","d a c b","b d a c","b a c d"],3,"The sequence 'b-a-c-d' is highly logical because 'b' states where ants are found generally, 'a' specifies their local homes, 'c' describes their food-gathering habit, and 'd' concludes that they are hardworking based on that habit.","2014 EC entrance"],["Bubu: Nobody likes me because I’m poor. I’ll leave this school and find another one. Kena: What do you mean? I\ncarry around ________________ you do. Just keep calm.",["very little money than","less money than","considerably little money than","so more little money than"],1,"'Money' is an uncountable noun, so the comparative form 'less money than' is grammatically correct to compare the amounts of money they carry.","2016 EC entrance"],["They still argue that the quality of education is steadily improving. Obviously they are trying to fool us, but we\n____________ the idea.",["either take","never buy","don't expect","neither agree to"],1,"To 'buy' an idea or explanation is an idiom meaning to believe or accept it; thus, 'never buy the idea' means they do not believe the claim.","2011 EC entrance"],["It has been a strongly brutal summer with very hot weather conditions.",["windy","pleasant","harsh","gentle"],2,"'Brutal' when describing weather conditions means severe, unforgiving, or 'harsh'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Most of us are not modest enough to learn from others. We always think we are the best.",["humble","polite","submissive","inferior"],0,"To be 'modest' means to have a humble estimate of one's own merits, so 'humble' is the correct synonym.","2015 EC entrance"],["The most appropriate closing for a business letter is:",["with regards","don't be strange","see you soon safe","stay"],0,"\"With regards\" (or \"Best regards\") is a standard, polite, and formal closing for a professional business letter, unlike the other informal options.","2016 EC entrance"],["The government should take measures on companies that ________ children under 18 by allowing their\nemployment with them. Such practice is globally unaccepdata.",["absorb","entertain","exploit","sympathize"],2,"Employing children under 18 is globally considered child labor, which 'exploits' children rather than protecting them.","2016 EC entrance"],["Rawda: Would you like something to drink? Fatuma: ______________________",["That is exactly what I see.","I need time to determine.","I would like tea if you don't mind.","Interesting to be here with you."],2,"When offered a drink, Option D ('I would like tea if you don't mind') is a polite, natural, and direct way to accept the offer.","2013 EC entrance"],["A father, a mother and children who live together make up a family.",["start","join","form","conserve"],2,"The phrasal verb 'make up' in this context means to form or constitute something.","2014 EC entrance"],["Muse: have you heard that Belete was released? Shoa: _________________",["What good news! When was that?","Is Belete a businessman by profession?","Everybody likes Belete, I suppose.","I know. He severely criticizes the system."],0,"Hearing that someone has been released from detention typically elicits relief and a follow-up question, making 'What good news! When was that?' the most natural response.","2008 EC entrance"],["My friends are _______ all over the country and I don't have an problem wherever I go. I have no worries of\nwhere to stay or what to eat.",["located","scattered","disarrayed","concentrated"],1,"'Scattered' is the standard adjective used to describe friends or people being spread out across different locations in a country. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Alemu: Sounds like you had a boring day. Did anything interesting happen?\nFeyissa: _____________________",["Many things happen in this city.","What's interesting?","Often many things happen, but few may take our attention.","Not really. Don't think so."],3,"To answer the yes/no question 'Did anything interesting happen?' in the context of having a boring day, 'Not really. Don't think so.' is the most natural fit.","2011 EC entrance"],["In a formal letter which of the following could be optional?",["The subject heading","The salutation line","The recipient's address","The date line"],0,"A formal letter must carry the date, the address of the person you are writing to, and a salutation such as Dear Mr. Kebede. Without them the letter cannot be filed or answered. The subject heading, the short line naming the topic, is helpful but not required, so it is the optional part.","2015 EC entrance"],["I ____________ with you, Abel; irregular class attendance isn't the cause of your failure.",["disagreed","have disagreement","am disagreeing","disagree"],3,"'Disagree' is a stative verb used in the simple present tense to state a current opinion or stance.","2011 EC entrance"],["You _______________ speak to him like that. After all, he is your elder brother and deserves some respect.",["will rather not","might not","will not","ought not to"],3,"The modal 'ought not to' is used to express moral obligation or strong advice, which fits the context of respecting an elder brother.","2016 EC entrance"],["Kedija: we've got loads of homework tonight, haven't we? Fayine:________________",["Ok. let's start with maths.","No, they're all easy.","Yes, in three subjects.","Ok. shall we start now?"],2,"'Yes, in three subjects' directly and grammatically answers the confirmation-seeking tag question about having a large amount of homework.","2007 EC entrance"],["Abraham: You should really apologize to your parents. Tizazu:______________________",["It was a crowded classroom.","Mistakes are inevitable.","Why? I don't care what they think!","Yes, my parents apologized."],2,"Option A logically responds to the recommendation to apologize by expressing defiance ('Why? I don't care what they think!'). (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["We do not understand why he always comes so late. If he arrives on time like his friends, he _________ the\nopportunity to meet us and get the necessary assistance.",["ought to have","would have","will have","may be having"],2,"This is a first conditional sentence ('If + simple present, will + base verb'), so 'will have' is the correct form for the main clause.","2013 EC entrance"],["Choose the alternative with a correct spelling.",["optmistic","cooperative","distnguished","comunication"],1,"'Cooperative' is spelled correctly, while the other options contain spelling errors ('optimistic', 'communication', 'distinguished').","2013 EC entrance"],["I couldn't hear what the teacher was saying during the lesson, but I think I ______ him to be louder.",["could ask","would ask","would have asked","could have asked"],3,"'Could have asked' is used to express a past capability or possibility that was not realized.","2014 EC entrance"],["They wasted some time at the beginning and now they are under pressure to",["struggle","strength","tension","fever"],2,"The noun 'pressure' in the phrase 'under pressure' refers to a state of stress or mental/emotional strain, which is closest in meaning to 'tension'.","2014 EC entrance"],["Tourist: What do I need to visit the museum? Guard: ...",["You must get permission from the manager.","You can get permission from the manager.","You have got permission from the manager.","You are sure to get permission from the manager."],0,"What do I need asks about a requirement, and must states a requirement: you must get permission from the manager. Option A, can get permission, says that permission is possible to obtain, which answers a different question, and it leaves the tourist unsure whether it is needed","2018 EC entrance"],["By the year 2020, the cure for both HIV/AIDS and Ebola_________________.",["will be discovered","had been discovered","will Have been discovered","was discovered"],2,"The time marker 'by the year 2020' (viewed from 2007 EC / 2014-2015 GC) requires the future perfect passive form, 'will have been discovered'.","2007 EC entrance"],["a. One of my favourite things to do is wash my car. b. People say they can tell about a person by their shoes. c.\nHere is the thoughtful process I follow to wash my car. d. A clean car says I?m proud and I feel good about my\nself. e. I say that you can tell about a person by how clean his car is.",["b e d a c","a d b e c","c a b d e","e b c d a"],0,"The paragraph builds an idea before it uses it. Sentence b reports what other people say about shoes, e gives the writer's own version about cars, d explains what a clean car says about him, a tells us washing his car is a favourite thing, and c promises the process, which is what a following paragraph would give. That is b e d a c. D is tempting because a sounds like an opening line, but starting there leaves b and e stranded with nothing to lead into.","2005 EC entrance"],["According to the passage, the drought and famine of Wollo demonstrates the relationship between climate\nchange and",["infrastructure.","peasantry.","lack of governance.","overpopulation."],2,"Historically, the Wollo famine is cited as a classic example of how climatic factors interact with political neglect and a lack of governance.","2013 EC entrance"],["A room _______________for you at Hilton Hotel.",["has reserved","has been reserving","reserves","has been reserved"],3,"The subject 'A room' receives the action, requiring the present perfect passive voice 'has been reserved'.","2006 EC entrance"],["we studied together at college, but I________________her ever since.",["didn't see","have seen","won't have seen","Haven't seen"],3,"The time expression 'ever since' refers to a period extending from a specific past point up to the present, which requires the present perfect tense ('haven't seen').","2008 EC entrance"],["In my life, I ______________ had money counted in four digits. Poor me!",["haven't never","am not have","have never","am never"],2,"\"Never\" carries the negative on its own, and the present perfect covers experience from the past up to now: \"In my life, I have never had money counted in four digits.\" B is the trap because it doubles the negative with \"haven't\" and \"never\" together, and standard English uses one negative word for one negative meaning.","2005 EC entrance"],["If what you are telling me is true, then I _______ straight away and register with them. I don't want to miss the\nopportunity.",["must go","am going","will go","am going to go"],2,"This is a first conditional structure expressing a spontaneous decision made at the moment of speaking based on a condition ('If what you are telling me is true'), which requires the future simple 'will go'.","2015 EC entrance"],["I say we should not question the competence of the new team. Each member is ________ those we had in the\nlast round. They may have another problem and that should be studied.",["very experienced as","as experienced as","so experienced","much experienced as"],1,"The comparative construction of equality uses the format 'as + adjective + as', making 'as experienced as' the correct choice.","2013 EC entrance"],["__________ the pilot and his crew recognized the plane had a problem. However, they didn't say anything lest\ndisturbing the passengers.",["All","Together","Either","Both"],3,"The correlative conjunction 'both... and...' is used to connect two subjects ('the pilot' and 'his crew') who performed the same action.","2015 EC entrance"],["Secretary: how do yo do, sir? Vistor:______________",["I am fine. How do you do?","How do you do?","I am fine. How are you?","Very well, how do you do?"],1,"In formal English, the conventional and idiomatic reply to the greeting 'How do you do?' is simply 'How do you do?'.","2007 EC entrance"],["I went home because I...",["felting bored","felt bored","fell bored","am feeling bored"],1,"The main verb went is in the past, so the reason clause has to be in the past too: I felt bored. Feel becomes felt, and the ed ending is not used for it. Option B swaps in the wrong verb, since fell comes from fall, which means to drop down, not to have a feeling.","2018 EC entrance"],["Interviewer: __________________. Jorgie: Actually, my interest is in fashion designing",["Do you like fashion designing?","Could you tell me about your interest?","Did I hear you like fashion designing?","Why are you interested in fashion designing?"],1,"The response specifies what the speaker's interest is, making 'Could you tell me about your interest?' the most logical prompt among the choices.","2015 EC entrance"],["Bulti: The enemy is approaching. We have to evacuate soon. Gebrai:___________________",["who else is evacuating?","I think, they have soldiers in excess of us.","This area is ideal for them.","Perhaps, we might need to do that."],3,"Bulti suggests that they need to evacuate, and Gebrai's reply 'Perhaps, we might need to do that' directly addresses and considers that proposed action. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["Bekalu : How ______ do you watch television?",["relaxed","happy","much","often"],3,"'How often' is the standard question phrase used to ask about the frequency of an activity like watching television.","2014 EC entrance"],["a. You can use it to talk with your friends or family, for example. b. A mobile phone is a very useful device to get\nconnected with others. c. A mobile phone call can be made in so many ways. d. These days, everyone has a\nmobile phone.",["a d b c","c a b d","d c a b","b d a c"],3,"Option A (b-d-a-c) is the most coherent sequence because 'b' introduces the mobile phone, 'd' states its widespread ownership, 'a' gives an example of its use, and 'c' expands on how calls are made. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the paragraphs below emphasizes the need for showing one's own competence in tests?",["Paragraph 3","Paragraph 2","Paragraph 5","Paragraph 4"],3,"Paragraph 4 explains that hiring someone else to do your work is wrong because 'you are not showing your own competence, you are showing someone else's.'","2011 EC entrance"],["You think __________ a child. How do you tell me that nothing will happen if you jump down from this height?",["similar to","like","alike","same with"],1,"The preposition 'like' is used here to mean 'in the same way as' to compare the person's thinking to that of a child. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Customer: Do you have a changing room? Shop assistant: _____",["Certainly, it's over there","No, thank you","The rooms are too narrow","We don't change here"],0,"The customer asks whether the shop has a changing room, so the answer confirms it and shows where it is: 'Certainly, it's over there', option D. Option A is the tempting misreading: a changing room is where you try clothes on, not a place where goods are exchanged.","2017 EC entrance"],["Are those two girls from the same family? They look alike and _____ I see them together, even in odd kind of\nplaces.",["hardly do","infrequently","most of the time","some of the time"],2,"The phrase 'most of the time' functions as an adverbial of frequency that logically connects with 'always see them together' and fits grammatically in the sentence. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Zeru: In my free time, I go swimming in Sheraton Hotel. Molla: ___________________ Zeru: Since 2015. That's\nfor about 9 years now.",["When did you start doing that?","How long ago did you start this hobby?","How long have you been doing it?","How long did you do that?"],2,"The present perfect continuous question 'How long have you been doing it?' is used to ask about the duration of an ongoing habit or hobby, which perfectly matches the response 'Since 2015. That's for about 9 years now.'","2016 EC entrance"],["Mother: Tell me why schools are closed in Kiremt in Ethiopia. Daughter: ___________________________",["I haven't any clue, Mom.","Did you learn year-long yourself?","Nobody likes going to school.","I hate Kiremt, Mom."],0,"When asked why schools are closed, the daughter politely admits she does not know by saying, 'I haven't any clue, Mom.' (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["I __________my homework when you knocked at the door.",["had been","have been doing","have done","was doing"],3,"The past continuous ('was doing') is used for an ongoing past action that was interrupted by another action in the past simple ('knocked').","2017 EC entrance"],["Deboch: national exams should not continue. Teklu: probably, you may be right. Deboch: since we cannot do\naway with exams, regions may need to set their own. Teklu: this may be good idea, but there is the issue of\nstandard. Deboch: the federal ministry may set the basic standards. Teklu: ________",["exams. Set standards.","well, I may agree with you.","I hate exams.","there are ways and methods."],1,"Deboch successfully addresses Teklu's concern about standards, leading Teklu to concede and agree with the proposed solution ('well, I may agree with you').","2010 EC entrance"],["Nardos: I heard you were the only person to get the job. Well done! Girma: ________",["sure, I did","I knew I did well","thank you.","why expected I would not?"],2,"The standard and polite response to congratulations ('Well done!') is 'Thank you.'","2010 EC entrance"],["Can anyone tell me _______ book this is? It has been lying here for months.",["which","of who","whose","what about"],2,"The possessive determiner 'whose' is required to ask about the ownership of the book.","2015 EC entrance"],["By the time you come for your next holiday, they ____________ the construction of the hotel. Surely, you will be\nstaying there.",["will have completed","already completed","would complete","will complete"],0,"The future perfect tense ('will have completed') is required because of the time marker 'By the time', indicating that the construction will be finished before the next holiday.","2011 EC entrance"],["My mother usually wakes up at ______________and goes to her bedroom late at evening.",["night","sunset","dawn","dusk"],2,"'Dawn' refers to the first appearance of light in the sky before sunrise, which fits perfectly as the time one would wake up in the morning.","2016 EC entrance"],["Akalu: What was the party like? Lulu: ______________.",["I think, it was OK.","Do you think people liked it?","About a thousand people were invited.","It started earlier, didn't it?"],0,"The question 'What was the party like?' asks for an evaluation or description of the event, perfectly answered by 'I think, it was OK.'","2006 EC entrance"],["Alemu has been teaching Geography ______________ he was Bale Robe.",["before","since","when","for"],1,"The present perfect continuous tense is used with 'since' to indicate the starting point of an action that continues up to the present.","2016 EC entrance"],["According to the fourth paragraph, nonpoint pollutants come from which one of the following?",["Streams","Ocean","Farming","Lakes"],2,"Nonpoint source pollution comes from diffuse, land-based sources, with agricultural runoff from farming being one of the primary contributors.","2018 EC entrance"],["You: Are you married, Zahara? Zahara:________________",["I'm 30","No, I'm not","Before three years","My husband's name is Jemal"],1,"'Are you married?' is a yes/no question, and 'No, I'm not' provides the direct and grammatically correct short response.","2006 EC entrance"],["You have ___ to do at home this afternoon, so you can't go out.",["something","nothing","anything","not"],0,"The phrase 'so you can't go out' indicates that the person is busy, meaning they have 'something' to do at home.","2014 EC entrance"],["You know this is a literate society.",["Intelligent","Skilled","Informed","educated"],3,"'Literate' refers to the ability to read and write and is closely associated with being 'educated'.","2008 EC entrance"],["Your wife _____________ since 9.00 am but you don't even call and apologize for not being able to arrive until\nnow. What excuse do you have for this?",["would have been waiting","has been waiting","was waiting","is waiting"],1,"The present perfect continuous tense 'has been waiting' is used for an action that started in the past (9:00 am) and is still continuing up to the present.","2016 EC entrance"],["Let me go and check if the car is ready. It _______________________ when I came this morning.",["might be fixed","intended to be fixed","will have to be fixed","was being fixed"],3,"The past continuous passive form 'was being fixed' is used here to describe an action that was in progress in the past when another action occurred ('when I came this morning').","2016 EC entrance"],["Musa: How is your father? I heard he has been hospitalized. Robale: _____ He seems to need further\ninvestigation.",["God knows","Not very well","He is not here","He is very well"],1,"The second half of Robale's line says his father seems to need further investigation, so the report on his health has to be a poor one. \"Not very well\" fits. A is tempting because it is a normal answer to \"How is your father\", but a man who is very well would not need more tests.","2017 EC entrance"],["You I you say to for did want for all us thank.",["I did want you for all for us to say thank you.","I want to say thank you for all you did for us.","you want to say I thank you for all did for us.","you say I want to thank you for all did for us."],1,"Option A forms a grammatically correct and meaningful sentence ('I want to say thank you for all you did for us') using all the given words exactly once.","2009 EC entrance"],["The newly married couple has just gone to Hawassa for the ___.",["lifestyle","tour","honeymoon","visit"],2,"A 'honeymoon' is a holiday taken by a newly married couple, making it the correct term for this context.","2014 EC entrance"],["Conservation of natural resources is one of the key duties of any society.",["protection","afforestation","utilization","renovation"],0,"The 'conservation' of natural resources refers to their preservation and 'protection' from exploitation and destruction.","2016 EC entrance"],["Worldwide, a large number of organizations ______ children who have lost their parents in death.",["offer","foster","sponsor","respect"],2,"Organizations provide financial and material support to orphans, which is best described as 'sponsoring' them.","2014 EC entrance"],["It would be embarrassing________________ the truth. The good thing was that no one told her what had\nhappened.",["had she to find out","Is she to find out","has she to find out","were she to find out"],3,"'Were she to find out' is an inverted second conditional structure functioning as 'if she were to find out', which matches the conditional modal 'would be' in the main clause. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["Customer:______________? Shop assistant: It's 1500 birr.",["Whose is this camera","how much is this camera","it this camera for sale","do you have a camera"],1,"The shop assistant gives the price of an item ('1500 birr'), which corresponds to the question 'How much is this camera?'.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which word is wrongly spelt?",["module","commemoration","commodity","Jiboutian"],3,"The word \"Jiboutian\" is misspelled; the correct spelling of the demonym for someone from Djibouti is \"Djiboutian\" with a silent 'D'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Of the words given below, which one from paragraph 3 can be replaced by 'dislike' ?",["impose","abhor","exploit","prohibit"],1,"'Abhor' means to regard with disgust and hatred, so it is the best synonym for 'dislike' in the given context.","2014 EC entrance"],["As docile is to tamed so is awesome to ________",["fearful","grand","blunt","distasteful"],1,"'Docile' and 'tamed' are synonyms; similarly, 'awesome' and 'grand' share the meaning of being magnificent and inspiring awe.","2010 EC entrance"],["The old systems did not impose additional financial burden on the business community. __________",["So did the new systems","So do the new systems","Neither did the new systems","Neither didn't the new systems"],2,"To show agreement with a negative statement, we use 'Neither + auxiliary verb + subject'. Since the first sentence uses the past simple auxiliary 'did not', the correct addition is 'Neither did the new systems'.","2018 EC entrance"],["The police officers are trying to trace the prisoners that have escaped the prison.",["shoot","locate","penalize","kidnap"],1,"To 'trace' in this context means to track down or discover the location of the escaped prisoners, which is synonymous with 'locate'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Benti: This is the Toyota car we bought last week. Isn't it beautiful? Nani: _______________",["What? Is that really your car?","Oh no! I know you can't afford it.","Who bought it? You?","What a great car! Really exciting!"],3,"Benti invites agreement and admiration with the question 'Isn't it beautiful?', to which an enthusiastic compliment like 'What a great car! Really exciting!' is the most socially appropriate response.","2006 EC entrance"],["Their graduation will be in June. Then, they will do some shopping and tour around probably for three weeks and \nby the end of July, they definitely __________ back.",["would come","will have come","will come","would have come"],1,"The phrase 'by the end of July' is a future time marker that requires the Future Perfect tense ('will have come') to show an action completed before that point.","2016 EC entrance"],["my sister _________________ me a parcel two weeks ago, but I received it only yesterday.",["has sent","had sent","had been sent","Sent"],3,"The definite past time marker 'two weeks ago' requires the simple past tense 'sent'.","2008 EC entrance"],["If you have to go abroad for your education, one of the things you have to be worried about is____________. You \nhave to be sure of where you are going to stay before you leave this country.",["facilities","stipend","provisions","accommodation"],3,"'Accommodation' refers to lodging or a place to live, which directly matches the hint 'where you are going to stay'.","2013 EC entrance"],["You: why did you leave the party early last night? Rahel:__________________",["I left with my husband.","I left at 2 o'clock.","I didn't feel well.","We had a great evening."],2,"The question asks for a reason ('Why...'), and 'I didn't feel well' provides a valid reason for leaving early.","2007 EC entrance"],["Tariku: The personnel manager, without existing evidence, fired Genet from her job. ______ that we will\nreconsider the General Manager's case again because we need further evidence for her dishonesty.",["I doubt","As I see it","I do not think","I am convinced"],3,"'I am convinced that we will reconsider...' makes logical sense in this context as they lack evidence and thus need to reevaluate the case.","2018 EC entrance"],["The price of fertilizer has kept soaring for the last five or six years. Unless they are provided with some form of\n___________, our farmers cannot afford it and will undoubtedly be in a problem.",["manure","finance","subsidy","solution"],2,"A 'subsidy' is a sum of money granted by the state or a public body to help keep the price of a commodity or service low, which fits the context of farmers struggling to afford soaring fertilizer prices.","2016 EC entrance"],["Tomorrow, Sofanit ___ her assignments the whole day.",["would have done","will be doing","does","have been doing"],1,"The phrase 'Tomorrow ... the whole day' indicates an action that will be in progress over a duration of time in the future, which requires the future continuous tense 'will be doing'.","2014 EC entrance"],["Everything they are doing is so rubbish that you would consider firing them. Their former boss told me he had no \nsatisfaction with any one of them.",["contentment","favor","disambiguation","perfection"],0,"The word 'satisfaction' is synonymous with 'contentment', which refers to the state of being happy and satisfied with someone's work.","2016 EC entrance"],["Uncle: when are you going to marry? You:_______________",["I'm going to college next year.","I don't actually live here after marriage.","I'll have only two children.","not until I'm 45."],3,"The question asks 'when', and 'not until I'm 45' specifies the time/age the speaker intends to marry.","2007 EC entrance"],["The purchasers should be accountable for what has happened.____________ piece is faulty.",["All","Neither","Both","Every"],3,"'Every' is used with a singular countable noun ('piece') to indicate that all items in a group share a particular quality.","2008 EC entrance"],["Husband: Where would you like us to go for dinner? Wife: ___________________I like their French toast.",["How about trying Haile Grand Hotel?","I do not care about dinner tonight.","Is your sister going with us?","I do not have enough money for dinner."],0,"The wife suggests a dining location ('How about trying Haile Grand Hotel?') and supports her suggestion by mentioning their French toast, directly answering the husband's question.","2017 EC entrance"],["Applicants should have________ experience in the relevant area to apply for the job.",["access","prior","sector","popular"],1,"Job applications frequently require 'prior' experience, meaning experience gained before applying.","2013 EC entrance"],["____________ it has drastically changed the cultures of many nations and created undisciplined citizens.",["Despite the fact that","In comparison","However","In spite of"],2,"'However' is used as a transition word at the beginning of a sentence to contrast a new point with a previously stated context.","2015 EC entrance"],["I don't get along with most of my classmates.",["meet","play","agree","go"],2,"'Get along with' means to have a harmonious relationship with someone, which is closest in meaning to 'agree' among the provided choices.","2006 EC entrance"],["Aunt: ________ Lojo: sure",["you will give me the bread.","I want the bread.","pass me the bread, will you?","give me the bread."],2,"'Pass me the bread, will you?' is a polite request that can be naturally responded to with 'Sure.'","2010 EC entrance"],["My brother had never expected to get the job. He was really ______________ when he offered it.",["bored","amazed","amazing","boring"],1,"The participial adjective ending in '-ed' ('amazed') is used to describe how a person feels, whereas '-ing' adjectives describe the thing causing the feeling.","2016 EC entrance"],["Although the doctor has warned him several times, he hasn't stopped ___ yet.",["to drink","drinking","to get drunk","drinks"],1,"The verb 'stop' followed by a gerund ('drinking') means to discontinue an activity or habit, which fits the context of ignoring a doctor's warning.","2014 EC entrance"],["If you enjoy ________, you can register with us and trek around the city every Sunday in the afternoon.",["to be walking","to have a walk","walking","to walk"],2,"The verb 'enjoy' is transitively followed by a gerund (-ing form), making 'walking' the correct choice.","2015 EC entrance"],["We are so regretful that we didn't take necessary measures to stop the tyranny that went on in prisons of this\ncountry. No doubt, we would be held responsible.",["gleeful","remorseful","disgraceful","shameful"],1,"The adjective 'regretful' is synonymous with 'remorseful', expressing sorrow or guilt for a past action or failure to act.","2011 EC entrance"],["You will start running__________ the bell rings. Otherwise, you will be disqualified from the competition.",["after","while","till","during"],0,"'After' is the only conjunction that makes chronological sense here, showing that the action of running must follow the ringing of the bell to avoid disqualification.","2017 EC entrance"],["Dessalegn: _____________________ Chaltu: Yes, you are.",["I'm genuine, aren't I?","I'm working to help you, amn't i?","You are trying to help me, aren't you?","There are a number of solutions, aren't there?"],0,"The standard question tag for 'I am' is 'aren't I?'. When the speaker asks 'I'm genuine, aren't I?', the listener correctly responds with 'Yes, you are.'","2009 EC entrance"],["There is a huge increase in the number of newly set up educational institutions during the last thirty years but\nwe need to work on quality as well.",["progressive","bulky","comprehensive","massive"],3,"'Huge' and 'massive' are synonyms used to describe something of exceptionally large size or scale. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["I haven't started my homework yet but I________ it by 4:00 in the afternoon. Submission time is 4:15 p.m.",["am going to do","would have done","will have done","will done"],2,"The prepositional phrase 'by 4:00 in the afternoon' specifies a deadline in the future, which requires the future perfect tense ('will have done').","2013 EC entrance"],["____________________ in the country can you find people free of such bias. Better take it as a norm and live\nwith it.",["Anywhere","Somewhere","Nowhere","Every where"],2,"Negative adverbs of place like 'Nowhere' trigger subject-auxiliary inversion ('can you find') at the beginning of a sentence.","2007 EC entrance"],["Teacher: Alemu has just made a good point on how we can improve education in our country.________ Taye?\nTaye: Yes. We should have well-trained teachers.",["You can't say another opinion","What is another idea you have","Any additional thinking you have","Would you like to add anything"],3,"The teacher is opening the floor to Taye to contribute to the discussion. 'Would you like to add anything' is a polite and common way to invite additional input.","2016 EC entrance"],["I can see your point of argument but _________________ the officials are honest when it comes to denouncing\ncorruption. One of them was caught red-handed by the police a fortnight ago.",["everybody says that","I am not convinced that","I don't doubt that","it is unacceptable"],1,"The speaker contrasts the listener's point of argument with a counterexample, indicating skepticism; 'I am not convinced that' correctly introduces this doubt.","2013 EC entrance"],["I usually get nervous at the beginning of interview sessions but as time goes, I become________ and get back\nto normal.",["settle","stable","calm","healthy"],2,"The adjective 'calm' provides the exact contrast to feeling 'nervous' at the beginning of the interview.","2010 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following has an error in capitalization?",["Lake Tana is the source of the Blue Nile.","I do not go to work on Fridays.","The major religions in Ethiopia are Christianity and Islam.","None of the above"],3,"All three sentences follow the rules: each starts with a capital letter, and the proper nouns Lake Tana, Blue Nile, Fridays, Ethiopia, Christianity and Islam are capitalized. So the answer is None of the above. Option B is the one many readers pick, because days of the week look like ordinary nouns, but English always capitalizes them.","2018 EC entrance"],["Tourist: The roads in the city are dilapidated.\nFriend: ___________________________",["There are more pressing problems, though.","Yeah, they should have at least been patched.","You know, the world economy is in a problem.","They are better in the countryside."],1,"Answering 'Yeah, they should have at least been patched' agrees with the complaint about the dilapidated roads and suggests a minimal corrective action.","2011 EC entrance"],["In got has house all money new the her she.",["she has got all her money in the new house.","All her money she has got in the new house.","she has got her money all in the new house.","she has all here new money got in the house."],0,"The correct syntactic arrangement is 'she has got all her money in the new house', where 'all her money' functions as the direct object of 'has got' followed by the prepositional phrase of location.","2010 EC entrance"],["Once up on a time there was an emperor who loved to spend his money on expensive things. This is most likely\nan introductory part of a writing that is:",["argumentative","expository","narrative","Descriptive"],2,"\"Once upon a time there was an emperor\" is the standard opening of a story, and the past tense sets up events that will follow one after another. Writing that tells a story is narrative. B is tempting because the emperor is being described in the same line, but description is used inside stories all the time, and the opening formula tells you a story is starting.","2005 EC entrance"],["If she________ persistent dry cough and fever, I would have called 8335 but that wasn't the case. It just looked\nlike an ordinary flu.",["did have","would have","had had","has had"],2,"This is a third conditional sentence expressing a hypothetical past situation, which requires 'had had' (past perfect) in the 'if' clause.","2013 EC entrance"],["Stranger: Where is the nearest bank around? You: ____________ that tall building down there.",["You should know","It's on the corner of","The bank is far away from","I don't think it could be"],1,"'It's on the corner of' is a common and grammatically correct prepositional phrase used for giving spatial directions. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["There are wide-spread ________ rumors of exempting students who score over 600 from educational costsharing.",["inspirational","inspiring","inspiration","inspired"],1,"'Inspiring' is the correct participle adjective to describe rumors that give hope and encouragement to the students.","2011 EC entrance"],["Lensa: Lilu loves pizza. She could eat the whole thing herself. Lojo: _____________________",["That's why she is gaining weight","That is why she's cutting down on junk food.","That's why she gets along with her friends very well.","That is why she's very nice."],0,"Eating an entire pizza is high in calories, making 'That's why she is gaining weight' the most logical and coherent reaction.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following words is the closest in meaning to the word unhumanified in Para.1?",["annoying","humiliating","offending","debilitating"],1,"The coined word 'unhumanified' is synonymous with 'dehumanized', which is closest in meaning to 'humiliating' or degrading.","2016 EC entrance"],["Despite their longtime friendship, Biftu and Tola are not in good terms. _______________, they had a problem\nand now they have broken up. I don't know what had happened.",["Anyway, as I was saying","In addition","However, as I understand","Unfortunate it is"],0,"'Anyway, as I was saying' is a conversational filler used to resume a narrative or focus on the main point, which fits the gossip-like, informal tone of the statement.","2013 EC entrance"],["It is now generally accepted that in the future robots will take over many of our tasks, especially the\nmore_____________type of jobs.",["repetition","repeating","repeated","repetitive"],3,"The adjective 'repetitive' appropriately describes tasks or jobs that involve doing the same thing over and over again.","2006 EC entrance"],["It is true, this is time consuming ___________, it brings in a lot of money. You know how much they pay him? A\nmillion birth?",["but on the other hand","however","but in fact","even though then"],0,"The contrastive transition 'but on the other hand' is used to introduce a counter-argument or a positive aspect that balances the negative ('time consuming').","2016 EC entrance"],["Husband: Six people died and three were injured in a car accident today. Wife: __________________ Has the\ncause been known?",["What a terrible news!","Look after yourself on the road.","Never trust a car driver.","I am sorry to say this."],0,"'What a terrible news!' (intended as 'What terrible news!') is a natural exclamation of shock and sympathy upon hearing about a fatal car accident.","2017 EC entrance"],["Son:___________________ Dad: Nice to meet you, Mr. Alemu.",["Dad. This is my teacher, Mr. Alemu.","This is my Dad, Mr. Alemu.","Dad. That one is my teacher, Mr Alemu.","Dad. Mr. Alemu is my teacher."],0,"When introducing one person to another, the standard conversational formula is to address the first person and say, \"This is [name/title].\" Here, the son introduces his teacher to his father using \"Dad. This is my teacher, Mr. Alemu.\"","2008 EC entrance"],["Such/ It/is/ that/ delicious meal/everything/ate/we.",["We ate a delicious meal it is that such everything.","It is that such delicious meal everything we ate.","It is such a delicious meal that we ate everything.","It is everything we ate that such delicious meal."],2,"Option D uses the consecutive 'such... that' structure correctly to say, 'It is such a delicious meal that we ate everything.'","2016 EC entrance"],["_____ they were hungry, Tolla gave them something to eat.",["Thinking","Because of thinking","Thinking of","For thinking"],0,"A participle at the front gives the reason: Thinking they were hungry means because he thought they were hungry, and the subject of both parts is Tolla. Option D fails because because of is followed by a noun, not by a clause with a subject and verb inside it.","2018 EC entrance"],["My English is not good, I __________ advised to study English when I was younger.",["wish I have been","wished I had been","wished I was","wish I had been"],3,"To express a present regret about a past situation, we use 'wish' in the present tense followed by a past perfect verb ('wish I had been').","2017 EC entrance"],["Citizens who are more ________have important role for their country.",["educated","educationally","educating","education"],0,"The adjective 'educated' is required to modify the noun 'Citizens' after the verb 'are'.","2016 EC entrance"],["Friend: _______________I'm almost blind in the dark. You: Don't worry about it.",["I shouldn't have stepped on your foot.","Will you forgive me for stepping on your foot?","Excuse me for stepping on your foot.","Did I step on your foot?"],2,"The speaker apologizes for an accidental action with 'Excuse me for stepping on your foot', which is met with the forgiving response, 'Don't worry about it.'","2017 EC entrance"],["The bad weather ______ our plan to travel to Dire-Dawa this afternoon.",["disturbed","disrupted","dislodged","disappointed"],1,"'Disrupted' is the correct term to use when an event, activity, or process is interrupted or prevented from continuing normally due to an obstacle like bad weather.","2014 EC entrance"],["same passage\nIn the sentence 'Despite these obstacles, the government is committed to addressing these issues and\nimproving the quality of education,' what does 'these' refer to?",["The educational resources","The obstacles in the education system","The students in schools","The issues related to poverty"],1,"'These obstacles' looks back at the problems listed in the sentence before it: overcrowded classrooms, a lack of educational resources, and the gap between urban and rural areas. Those are the obstacles in the education system, which is option A. Option B is tempting because poverty is a real barrier in this passage, but poverty appears later, in paragraph 3, and a pronoun points back, not forward.","2017 EC entrance"],["Our population size has tremendously swelled over the last few decades. Do you know why?",["escaped","jumped","leaped","increased"],3,"The word 'swelled' means to increase in size or number, making 'increased' the closest synonym in this context.","2014 EC entrance"],["Passenger 1: Excuse me; I think those seats facing the front are ours. Passenger 2:________________.",["I'm afraid the seats are not comfortable enough.","Oh, I'm sorry. We know they were reserved.","Oh, I'm sorry. We did not know they were reserved.","Oh, what a shame! I like seats facing the front."],2,"Passenger 2 has taken seats that belong to someone else, so the reply apologises and explains the mistake: \"Oh, I'm sorry. We did not know they were reserved.\" A is the trap because it is one word away from the answer, but \"We know they were reserved\" would be admitting they took the seats on purpose, which no apology can follow.","2005 EC entrance"],["I don't mind the current from the sea but my problem is with the freezing temperature. They even say it is going\nto get worse.",["wave","flow","breeze","roaring"],1,"A 'current' in the sea refers to the continuous, directed movement of sea water, which is synonymous with a water 'flow'.","2016 EC entrance"],["My parents have lived in a rented house for a long time, but they are now having their own house constructed.\nGod willing, the construction _________ in six months' time.",["will complete","will have been completed","has been completed","is being completed"],1,"The phrase 'in six months' time' indicates completion before or by a future point, which requires the future perfect passive ('will have been completed').","2016 EC entrance"],["I didn't find it fascinating. To me it was rather a bit ____________________.",["soothing","boring","bouncing","compelling"],1,"'Boring' provides the direct contrast to 'fascinating' as signaled by the negative sentence and the adverb 'rather'.","2007 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-mathematics","name":"Mathematics","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["If there are many extreme scores in all examinations, the dispersion is",["Large","Normal","Symmetric","Small"],0,"Extreme scores (outliers) lie far away from the center of the data set. Having many such extreme values increases the spread, and thus the dispersion of the data becomes large.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the position vector of the vector with initial point A (1, -1) and terminal point B (2,\n-3)?",["i − 2j","3i − 4j","i − 4j","3i + 4j"],0,"The position vector of the vector from A(1, −1) to B(2, −3) is given by AB = (2 − 1)i + (−3 − (−1))j = i − 2j.","2016 EC entrance"],["Let A and B be two sets such that A = {1, 4, 9} and B = {n ∈ N : 3 < n ≤ 5}. Which of the following sets\nrepresents A × B ?",["{(1, 4), (1, 5), (4, 4), (4, 5), (9, 4), (9, 5)}","{(4, 1), (5, 1), (4, 4), (5, 4), (9, 4), (9, 5)}","{(4, 1), (5, 1), (5, 4), (5, 5), (4, 9), (5, 9)}","{(1, 4), (1, 5), (4, 5), (5, 5), (9, 4), (9, 5)}"],0,"The set B = {n ∈ N : 3 < n ≤ 5} consists of the natural numbers 4 and 5, so B = {4, 5}. The Cartesian product A × B consists of all ordered pairs (a, b) where a ∈ A and b ∈ B , resulting in {(1, 4), (1, 5), (4, 4), (4, 5), (9, 4), (9, 5)}.","2018 EC entrance"],["If P (2, 5, 1) and Q(3, 0, 9) are points on a sphere whose center is on z-axis, then which one of the following\npoint is outside of the sphere?\n​",["(0, 0, 0)","(2, −2, 1)","(−4, 3, 5)","(3, 1, 1)"],3,"Let the center on the z -axis be (0, 0, c). Equating distances to P and Q gives 4 + 5 + (1 − c)2 = 9 + (9 − c)2 , which solves to c = 5 and radius R = 5. The squared distance from (3, 1, 1) to (0, 0, 5) is 32 + 12 + (1 − 5)2 = 26 > 25, so it lies outside the sphere.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following points is the intersection point of the line l : 3x − 2y + 4 = 0 and the circle c :\nx2 + y 2 − 2x − 4y − 5 = 0?",["(2, 5)","(−2, −1)","(4, 8)","(−4, −4)"],0,"Plugging the point (2, 5) into the line gives 3(2) − 2(5) + 4 = 0, and into the circle gives 4 + 25 − 4 − 20 − 5 = 0. Since it satisfies both equations, it is their point of intersection.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the equation of the tangent line to the graph of the function f (x) = ex",["y = x + 1e","y = 1e x + 1e ​ ​","y = ex","y = ex + e at (1, e)? (1) ​"],2,"The derivative of f(x) = e^x is f'(x) = e^x, so the slope at x = 1 is e. The equation of the tangent line is y - e = e(x - 1), which simplifies directly to y = ex.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following functions has a graph that completes one full cycle on −π, 11π\n4 ?\n​\n​",["f (x) = 3 sin(3x + π6 ) ​ ​","f (x) = 3 sin( 43 x + π2 )","f (x) = 2 sin( 23 x − π6 ) ​ ​ ​","f (x) = 2 sin(2x − π6 ) ​ ​"],2,"Assuming the interval is a typo for [−π/4, 11π/4] (which has length 3π ), a function completes one full cycle if its period is 3π . For f (x) = 2 sin( 23 x − π6 ), the period is T = 2π/(2/3) = 3π , which matches the interval length. ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["If f (x) = ln(2tan x ), then what is the value of f ′ ?",["ln 2","1 ​","ln 2 2","−2 ln 2"],0,"Using properties of logarithms, we can rewrite f (x) = ln(2tan x ) = tan x ln 2. Differentiating gives f ′ (x) = sec2 x ln 2, so evaluating at x = 0 yields f ′ (0) = 1 ⋅ ln 2 = ln 2.","2011 EC entrance"],["Consider a rectangle ABCD with base vertices A=(0,3) and B=(4,0) and the other vertices, C and D, in the firstquadrant of the coordinate plane. If its height BC is half of the length of its base, then which of the following\nindicates the coordinates of vertex C?",["(5/2, −2)","(6, 3/2)","(4, 5/2)","(11/2, 2)"],3,"The base vector is AB = (4, −3) with length 5. A perpendicular vector pointing into the first quadrant is (3, 4), and since height BC = 2.5, the displacement vector is BC = 2.5 × (3/5, 4/5) = (1.5, 2), giving C = (4, 0) + (1.5, 2) = (11/2, 2).","2011 EC entrance"],["On the set of Natural numbers N, which one of the following propositions has a truth value True ?",["(∃x)(∃y)(x − y = y − x)","(∀x)(∃y)(x − y = 5)","(∀x)(∀y) (x ≠ y ⟹ x > y)","(∀x)(∃y)(xy < x)"],0,"The statement (∃x)(∃y)(x − y = y − x) is true on N because we can choose x = y = 1, which yields 1 − 1 = 1 − 1 = 0.","2015 EC entrance"],["When the Division Algorithm is applied to the fraction 283\n20 , then which one of the following is the corresponding\nrepresentation?\n​",["283 = 7 × 20 + 143","283 = 1 × 283 + 0","283 = 14 × 20 + 3","283 = 10 × 20 + 83"],2,"The Division Algorithm states a = bq + r, where 0 ≤ r < b. For 283 divided by 20, the quotient q is 14 and the remainder r is 3, yielding 283 = 14 × 20 + 3.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is true about the trigonometric values of 855°?",["tan 855° = 1 2 2 ​ ​","cot 855 = − 2 ​","sin 855∘ = ∘ (1) 3 2 ​ ​","cos 855∘ = −"],3,"The angle 855° is coterminal with 135° (855° - 2 * 360° = 135°), which lies in the second quadrant where cosine is negative. Therefore, cos 855° = cos 135° = -cos 45° = -sqrt(2)/2.","2014 EC entrance"],["A water tank is a rectangular parallelepiped with base length 3 m, width 2 m and height 2.5 m. If water is\nflowing into the tank at the rate of 0.12 m3 /sec, then how fast does the level of water rise up in the tank?",["0.04 m/sec","0.06 m/sec","0.03 m/sec","0.02 m/sec"],3,"The volume of water in the tank is V = L ⋅ W ⋅ h = 6h. Differentiating both sides with respect to time t gives dV dt = dh dV dh 0.12 6 dt . Substituting dt = 0.12 gives dt = 6 = 0.02 m/sec. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\nSuppose Target Population N = 54000 vouchers and sample size n = 6000; following the systematic sampling\napproach if 4th unit is selected as the first unit in the sample then the next unit selected in the sample would\nbe:",["12th","8th","10th","13th"],3,"The sampling interval is k = N /n = 54000/6000 = 9. If the first selected unit is the 4th, the next systematic unit is 4 + 9 = 13th.","2018 EC entrance"],["According to the properties of integration, which of the following is equivalent to ∫ (3f (x) − g(x))dx?",["∫ 3f (x)dx − ∫ g(x)dx","∫ f (x)dx − 3 ∫ g(x)dx","3 ∫ f (x)dx ⋅ ∫ g(x)dx","3(∫ f (x)dx − ∫ g(x)dx)"],0,"By the difference and constant multiple rules of integration, the integral of a difference is the difference of the integrals, making ∫ (3f (x) − g(x))dx equivalent to ∫ 3f (x)dx − ∫ g(x)dx.","2018 EC entrance"],["From the data (marks distribution), if student in the top 8% are to be awarded a certificate. What is the minimum\nmark for a certificate? (Data: class intervals 10-14,15-19,20-29,30-39; frequencies 15,23,46,16)",["30.5","32","34.5","33"],2,"The top 8% correspond to the 92nd percentile (P92 ). With N = 100, the cumulative frequencies show that P92 lies in the interval 30-39 (boundaries 29.5-39.5), and calculating P92 = 29.5 + 92−84 × 10 yields 34.5. 16 ​ ​ ​ ​ (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["If one of the end point of the line segment is (3, 2, -4) and the mid-point is (4, 1, -2), then the coordinate of the\nother end point is:",["(3, 1, 0)","(5, 1, 2)","(5, 0, 0)","(2, 0, 5)"],2,"Using the midpoint formula M = A+B , the other endpoint is B = 2M − A = 2(4, 1, −2) − (3, 2, −4) = (8 − 2 3, 2 − 2, −4 − (−4)) = (5, 0, 0). ​","2008 EC entrance"],["Suppose that a function f has a property that f(x + y)= f(x)f(y) for all x and y and that f = 2, f= 1. Then which\none of the following represents the formula for the derivative f ′ (x)?",["no such function","f ′ (x) = f (x) + 2f ′ (x)","f ′ (x) = f (x) + 2","f (x) = 2f ′ (x) + 1"],0,"For any function satisfying f(x + y) = f(x)f(y), setting x = y = 0 gives f(0) = [f(0)]^2, which requires f(0) to be 0 or 1; it cannot be 2, nor can it take two distinct values at 0. Therefore, no such function exists.","2007 EC entrance"],["If a box with square base open top is made from 1,200cm2 material, what is the largest volume of the box in\ncm3 ?",["15,000","8000","4000","3000"],2,"2 For a box with a square base of side x and height h, the surface area is x2 + 4xh = 1200, giving h = 1200−x . 4x 1 3 ′ 3 2 Maximizing V (x) = 300x − 4 x yields V (x) = 300 − 4 x = 0 ⟹ x = 20 cm, giving a maximum volume of V (20) = 4000 cm3 . ​ ​ ​ 2","2006 EC entrance"],["What is the equation of the tangent line to the graph of f (x) = 2x3 − 3x2 + 1 at x = 2?",["y = 12x − 19","y = 2x + 5","y = 120x − 235","y = 6x − 7"],0,"At x = 2, we have f (2) = 5. The derivative is f ′ (x) = 6x2 − 6x, so the slope at x = 2 is f ′ (2) = 12. The equation of the tangent line is y − 5 = 12(x − 2), which simplifies to y = 12x − 19.","2017 EC entrance"],["Let P be a point in the coordinate space. If P is located 3 units in the direction of the negative x-axis from the\norigin, 1 unit in the direction of the positive y -axis from the origin, and 2 units in the direction of the positive z axis from the origin, which one of the following ordered triple of numbers represents point P ?",["(3, −1, −2)","(3, 1, −2)","(3, −1, 2)","(−3, 1, 2)"],3,"Moving 3 units in the negative x direction gives x = −3, 1 unit in the positive y direction gives y = 1, and 2 units in the positive z direction gives z = 2, yielding (−3, 1, 2).","2016 EC entrance"],["​\nThe probability that an electronic device produced by a company does not function properly is equal to 0.1. If 2\ndevices are bought, then what is the probability that at least one device function properly?",["0.81","0.09","0.18","0.99"],3,"The probability that at least one device functions properly is 1 − P (both fail) = 1 − (0.1)2 = 1 − 0.01 = 0.99.","2009 EC entrance"],["Consider △ABC with right angle at C and m(∠ABC) = 5∘ . If the length of AC is 10 units, then what is the\narea of the triangle? Given tan 35∘ ≈ 0.7 and tan 5∘ ≈ 1.43",["10/149 sq. units","70 sq. units","35 sq. units","5/149 sq. units"],2,"Due to a typo, the angle m(∠ABC) should be 55° (since tan 55° ≈ 1.43). In right △ABC, BC = AC / tan 55° ≈ 10 / 1.43 ≈ 7. Thus, the area is 0.5 * AC * BC ≈ 0.5 * 10 * 7 = 35 sq. units.","2014 EC entrance"],["The Ozone level (in ppb- parts per billion) on a sunny day in metropolitan area is given by formula p(t)= 80 + 12t\n� t2 where t is time in hours and t = 0 corresponds to 9A.M. what is the rate of increase of Ozone level after 3hrs(i.e. at 12 A.M)?",["113 ppb","12 ppb","107 ppb","6 ppb"],3,"The rate of increase is given by the derivative p′ (t) = 12 − 2t. At t = 3 hours, p′ (3) = 12 − 2(3) = 6 ppb.","2007 EC entrance"],["The equation of the line that passes through (2,-1) and perpendicular to the line 3x + 4y = 6 is:",["4x + 3y = 11","-4x + 3y = 5","-4x + 3y = -11","4x - 3y = 5"],2,"The given line 3x + 4y = 6 has slope −3/4, so a perpendicular line has slope 4/3. Using point-slope form with (2, −1) yields y + 1 = 43 (x − 2), which simplifies to −4x + 3y = −11. ​","2008 EC entrance"],["Two dice thrown. Probability sum multiple of 5 or greater than 9?",["11/36","13/36","1/4","5/18"],3,"The sums of two dice that are either multiples of 5 (5, 10) or greater than 9 (10, 11, 12) are 5, 10, 11, and 12. There are 4 ways to get 5, 3 ways to get 10, 2 ways to get 11, and 1 way to get 12, giving a total of 10 favorable outcomes out of 36, which simplifies to 5/18","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the equation of a line that passes through (-2,5) and has a slope 12 ?\n​",["y = 2x + 12","2y + x = 5","2y − x − 12 = 0","y = 12 x + 5 ​"],2,"Using the point-slope formula y − y1 = m(x − x1 ) with (−2, 5) and m = 1/2 gives y − 5 = 12 (x + 2), which simplifies to 2y − x − 12 = 0. ​ ​ ​","2017 EC entrance"],["A frustum of a right circular cone with base radii 3 cm and 4 cm, slant height 6 cm. Total surface area?",["67π cm²","56π cm²","36π cm²","74π cm²"],0,"The total surface area of a frustum of a cone is given by A = π(R^2 + r^2 + (R + r)l). Plugging in R = 4 cm, r = 3 cm, and l = 6 cm, we get A = π(16 + 9 + 7 * 6) = 67π cm². (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Find the median of the grouped data.",["20.865","19.875","21.375","18.685"],2,"The median class is 20-24 since the cumulative frequency reaches N /2 = 10 in this interval. Applying the median N /2−CF ) ⋅ 5 = 19.5 + 1.875 = 21.375. formula yields Median = L + ( f ) ⋅ w = 19.5 + ( 10−7 8 ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["If x and y are composite natural numbers and z is a prime number, then which one of the following is never\ntrue?",["xy = z 2","xz = y","x + y = z","x + y = 2z"],0,"Since z is a prime number, the only factors of z 2 are 1, z, z 2 . If xy = z 2 where x and y are composite, they must both be greater than 1, so the only possibility is x = z and y = z , which contradicts the assumption that z is prime and x, y are composite.","2016 EC entrance"],["A radioactive substance of 1024 grams loses half of its weight per year. What is the weight of the substance that \nwill be left at the end of the ninth year?",["4 grams","12 grams ​","14 grams ​","2 grams"],3,"The weight of the substance at the end of the ninth year is given by 1024 × ( 12 )9 = 210 × 2−9 = 2 grams. ​","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the total surface area of a regular square pyramid with slant height 8cm and base area 25 cm²?",["105 cm2","80 cm2","65 cm2","90 cm2"],0,"Since the base is a square of area 25 cm2 , its side length is 5 cm and perimeter is 20 cm. The total surface area is the sum of the base area and the lateral area, calculated as 25 + 12 (20)(8) = 105 cm2 . ​","2016 EC entrance"],["A particle moves along the x-axis with acceleration a(t)=12t²+6t for t≥0. If v=5 and s=2, then what is\nposition at t=2 sec?",["12 m","22 m","26 m","24 m"],1,"Integrating acceleration a(t) = 12t2 + 6t gives v(t) = 4t3 + 3t2 + C1 . Since v(1) = 5, C1 = −2. Integrating v(t) gives s(t) = t4 + t3 − 2t + C2 , and since s(0) = 2, C2 = 2. Thus, s(2) = 16 + 8 − 4 + 2 = 22 m. ​ ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Shop sells 30 articles for 6600. Plans to sell each for 200. Approximate discount percent?",["9.091%","10%","8%","90.091%"],0,"The current standard price per article is 6600 / 30 = 220. Planning to sell each for 200 represents a discount of (220 200)/220 = 1/11, which is approximately 9.091%.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the conjugate of ∣3 + 4i∣ − 25i ? ?\n3 + 4i",["1 − 3i (1) ​","5 + 3i","1 + 3i","3 − 5i"],2,"25i = 25i(3−4i) First, ∣3 + 4i∣ = 5 and 3+4i = 4 + 3i. The expression is 5 − (4 + 3i) = 1 − 3i, and its complex conjugate 25 is 1 + 3i. ​ ​ π π ) + i 2 sin ( ), then what is the value of z 3 ? 12 12 A. ✓ 2 + 2i B. 2 + 2 i C. 2 2 + 2 2 i D. 3 2 + 3 2 i 2 cos (","2009 EC entrance"],["What is the sixth term in the expanded form of (x + 2y)8 ?",["448x5 y 3","1792x3 y 5","1120x4 y 4","1024xy 7"],1,"8 The sixth term in the expansion of (x + 2y)8 is given by (5)x8−5 (2y)5 = 56 ⋅ 32x3 y 5 = 1792x3 y 5 . ​","2013 EC entrance"],["⎧3 − 22x ,\nLet ⎨ 2x − 5\n⎩\n,\nx+1\ncontain c?\n​\n​\n​\nif x < 0.5\nif x ≥ 0.5\n​\n, if c is a zero of f , that is , f(c) =0, then which one of the following intervals must",["[0, 1]","[1, 2]","[2, 3]","(−∞, 0]"],2,"x −5 For x < 0.5, 3 − 22x > 3 − 21 = 1 > 0, so there is no zero. For x ≥ 0.5, setting 2x+1 = 0 gives 2x = 5, which implies c = log2 5 ≈ 2.32, an element of the interval [2, 3]. ​ ​ (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["The earth's orbit has a semi-major axis a ≈ 149.6 Gm (gigameters) and an eccentricity of e ≈ 0.017. What is\nthe approximate value of the semi-minor axis?",["149.58 Gm","149.06 Gm","145.32 Gm","152.14 Gm"],0,"The relationship between the semi-major axis a, semi-minor axis b, and eccentricity e is b = a 1 − e2 . Calculating with a = 149.6 and e = 0.017, we get b ≈ 149.6 × 0.9998555 ≈ 149.58 Gm. ​","2011 EC entrance"],["If A=[[1,2],[2,3]], B=[[-3,2],[2,-1]], then which is not true?",["AB = BA","A+B = A-B","A+B is symmetric","B-A is a scalar matrix"],1,"If A+B = A-B, then 2B = 0, which implies B must be the zero matrix. Since B is non-zero, this statement is false. The other options are easily verified to be true.","2018 EC entrance"],["A toy rocket is launched. The path is modeled by h(t) = -16t² + 64t. At what time does it reach maximum height?",["64 seconds","4 seconds","2 seconds","10 seconds"],2,"The maximum of a downward-opening parabola h(t) = at2 + bt occurs at the vertex t = −b/(2a). Here, t = −64/(2 ⋅ −16) = 2 seconds.","2018 EC entrance"],["The sequence {a_n} with a₁=2 and a_{n+1}=a_n+4, then ∑_{n=3}^{35} a_n equals:",["2442","2450","2460","2458"],0,"The sequence is an arithmetic progression with first term a_1 = 2 and common difference d = 4, so a_n = 4n - 2. The sum from n=3 to n=35 has 33 terms, with a_3 = 10 and a_35 = 138, giving a sum of 33 * (10 + 138) / 2 = 2442.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the area of the region bounded by the graph of f (x) = x2 − 4 and the x-axis in square units?",["16/3","32","16","32/3"],3,"The x-intercepts of f (x) = x2 − 4 are x = ±2. Since the curve lies below the x-axis in this interval, the area is ∫−2 (4 − x2 )dx = [4x − x3 ] 2 3 ​ 2 ​ ​ −2 = 32 3 . ​","2015 EC entrance"],["If Q₃=50 and Q₁=35, then coefficient of quartile deviation is:",["17/3","5/17","15/2","3/17"],3,"The coefficient of quartile deviation is calculated using the formula (Q₃ - Q₁) / (Q₃ + Q₁). Substituting the given values yields (50 - 35) / (50 + 35) = 15 / 85 = 3/17. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["A taxi service charges a flat fee of Birr 25 and Birr 20 per kilometer. How much does a 10 km ride cost?",["45 birr","270 birr","55 birr","225 birr"],3,"The cost of the taxi ride is modeled by C(x) = 25 + 20x. For a distance of 10 km, the cost is 25 + 20(10) = 225 Birr.","2018 EC entrance"],["If the real part of (z+2)/(z-1) is 4, then the locus of the point representing z in the complex plane is:",["Hyperbola","Circle","Straight line","Parabola"],1,"(x+2)(x−1)+y 2 Letting z = x + iy , the real part of z+2 z−1 is given by (x−1)2 +y 2 2 = 0, which represents a circle in the complex plane. ​ ​ = 4. Rearranging this equation gives x2 − 3x + y 2 + (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Given the grouped data: x 8 - 12 13 - 17 18 - 22 23 - 27 28 - 32 f 3 4 5 6 2 What is the standard deviation of the\ndata?",["37 ​","6","37.5 ​","6.5"],2,"The class midpoints are 10, 15, 20, 25, and 30. The mean is (30 + 60 + 100 + 150 + 60) / 20 = 20. The population variance is the average of the squared deviations weighted by frequency: (3(100) + 4(25) + 5(0) + 6(25) + 2(100)) / 20 = 750 / 20 = 37.5, so the standard deviation is √37.5. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["What does the derivative of a function represent?",["Value of y-intercepts","Slope of the tangent line","Total area under the curve","Average values"],1,"By definition, the derivative of a function at a given point is the limit of the difference quotient, which geometrically represents the slope of the tangent line to the curve at that point.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following interval(s) is the solution set of the quadratic inequality 10x2 − 4x − 6 < 8x2 +\n4x − 12?",["(1, 3)","(3, ∞)","(−∞, 1)","(−∞, 1) ∪ (3, ∞)"],0,"Rearranging the inequality gives 2x2 − 8x + 6 < 0, which simplifies to x2 − 4x + 3 < 0 or (x − 1)(x − 3) < 0. This inequality holds true for values of x strictly between the roots, which is the interval (1, 3).","2015 EC entrance"],["Points P(3,3,2) and Q(2,0,4) on sphere with center on z-axis. Which point is outside?",["(3,1,1)","(-4,3,0)","(0,0,0)","(2,-2,1)"],1,"The center of the sphere is on the z-axis, C(0,0,z). Since P and Q are on the sphere, CP^2 = CQ^2, which yields 18 + (2-z)^2 = 4 + (4-z)^2, solving to z = -1/2. The sphere's equation is x^2 + y^2 + (z + 0.5)^2 = 24.25, and only point A(-4,3,0) gives a squared distance of 25.25 > 24.25, making it lie outside the sphere.","2018 EC entrance"],["Let f (x) = x2 + 2x − 5. What is the meaning of the value f −f ? It is the slope of the tangent line to the\n3−1\ngraph of f at:\n​",["(2.5, f (2.5))","(1, f (1))","(3, f (3))","(2, f (2))"],3,"By the Mean Value Theorem, the average rate of change on [1, 3] equals the instantaneous rate of change at some point c ∈ (1, 3). For a quadratic function, this point is the midpoint c = 2, meaning the value represents the slope of the tangent line at (2, f (2)). (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["If A= (1,-2), B= (-3,2) and v is a position vector such that 2v + AB = o, then v ? is equal to",["(-1, 0)","(2, -2)","(2, 0)","(-2, 2)"],1,"The vector AB = B − A = (−3 − 1, 2 − (−2)) = (−4, 4). Since 2v + AB = 0, 2v = −(−4, 4) = (4, −4), which gives v = (2, −2).","2007 EC entrance"],["Let p, q , and r be propositions. If p is True , q is False , and r is False , which one of the following propositions\nhas truth value True ?",["(q ∧ r) ⇔ (p ∧ ¬r)","(p ∨ q) ⇒ r","(p ∧ ¬q) ⇔ (p ∨ r)","p ⇒ (q ∨ r)"],2,"Substituting the truth values, we have p ∧ ¬q ≡ True ∧ True ≡ True, and p ∨ r ≡ True ∨ False ≡ True. Thus, (p ∧ ¬q) ⇔ (p ∨ r) ≡ True ⇔ True, which is True. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["If the initial point of a vector is A(2,-1,4) and the terminal point is B(4,3,2), what is the position vector AB?",["⟨−2, −4, 2⟩","⟨6, 2, 6⟩","⟨2, 4, −2⟩","⟨8, −3, 8⟩"],2,"The position vector AB is found by subtracting the coordinates of the initial point A from the terminal point B : AB = ⟨4 − 2, 3 − (−1), 2 − 4⟩ = ⟨2, 4, −2⟩. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["​\nAn auditorium has 30 seats in first row, 34 in second, 38 in third. If pattern continues, total seating capacity with\n20 rows?",["1360","3880","106","580"],0,"The seating capacity forms an arithmetic series with a1 = 30, d = 4, and n = 20. The sum of the first 20 terms is S20 = 20 [2(30) + (20 − 1)4] = 10[60 + 76] = 1360. 2 ​ ​ ​ (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["If u = (1, −1) and v = (2, −4) are vectors, then u − v is equal to:",["(1, −3)","(3, −5)","(−3, 5)","(−1, 3)"],3,"To subtract vector v from vector u, we subtract their corresponding components: (1 - 2, -1 - (-4)) = (-1, 3).","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the equation of the tangent line to the circle (x − 2)2 + y 2 = 10 at the point\n(5, 1)?",["3x + y − 16 = 0","−3x + y − 14 = 0","−x + 3y + 14 = 0","x + 3y − 16 = 0"],0,"The center of the circle is (2, 0), so the slope of the radial line to (5, 1) is 1−0 = 13 . Since the tangent line is 5−2 perpendicular to the radial line, its slope is −3, and its equation is y − 1 = −3(x − 5), which simplifies to 3x + y − 16 = 0. ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the sum of all integers between 20 and 201 that are divisible by 2 or 5?",["11,970","16,110","12,970","16,150"],0,"For integers strictly between 20 and 201, the sum of those divisible by 2 or 5 is calculated using inclusion-exclusion: S_2 + S_5 - S_10 = 9990 + 4050 - 2070 = 11,970.","2018 EC entrance"],["If α and β are complementary angles (α + β = 90∘ ), which of the following trigonometric relations is always\ntrue?",["sec(α) = cos(β)","sin(α) = sin(β)","sin(α) = cos(β)","tan(α) = tan(β)"],2,"For any complementary angles where α + β = 90∘ , the cofunction identity states that the sine of an angle is equal to the cosine of its complement, so sin(α) = cos(β) is always true.","2018 EC entrance"],["Assuming that the population of Ethiopia increases at the rate of 3\\% per year and the current population is 102\nmillion, which one of the following is the best approximate of the population of Ethiopia 10 years from now? (If\nyou need, you may take: 1.0310 = 1.344, 1.039 = 1.305, 1.035 = 1.159)",["133 million","141 million","137 million","125 million"],2,"The future population is calculated as P0 (1 + r)t = 102 × (1.03)10 ≈ 102 × 1.344 = 137.088 million, which is approximately 137 million. ​","2013 EC entrance"],["The lower and upper bases of the frustum of a regular pyramid are equilateral triangles of side 3 cm long and 2\ncm long respectively. If its slant height is 4 cm, then what is the lateral surface area of the frustum?",["30 cm²","96 cm²","48 cm²","72 cm²"],0,"The lateral surface area of a regular pyramid frustum is LSA = (1/2) * (P1 + P2) * h_s, where P1 and P2 are the perimeters of the bases (9 cm and 6 cm) and h_s is the slant height (4 cm). This gives LSA = 0.5 * 15 * 4 = 30 cm².","2014 EC entrance"],["​\n​\n​\n​\n⎧2x − y ≤ 3\nThe solution region of the system of inequalities ⎨x > 0\nis found in quadrant _______\n⎩\ny<0\n​",["Three ​","four","One","Two"],1,"The inequalities x > 0 and y < 0 strictly restrict the solution set to the fourth quadrant, and points in this quadrant like (1, −0.5) also satisfy 2x − y ≤ 3.","2016 EC entrance"],["In △ABC m(< B) = 90°, with m(< A) = 30° and BC = 11cm, then what is the length of AC ?",["(1) 22 3 cm 3 ​ ​","22 cm","​ 11 3 cm 3","11 3 cm"],1,"Since m(∠B) = 90∘ , the triangle is right-angled with hypotenuse AC . Using the sine ratio for ∠A, we have 11 sin(30∘ ) = BC , which simplifies to 12 = AC and gives AC = 22 cm. AC ​","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the surface area (in cm2 ) of leather material required to make a spherical shape ball of radius 25cm?",["100π","2500π","1250 sphere","625π"],1,"The surface area A of a sphere of radius r is given by the formula A = 4πr2 . Substituting r = 25 cm yields A = 4π(25)2 = 2500π cm2 .","2017 EC entrance"],["What percent of 15 is equal to 600?",["400","690","90","4000"],3,"Let P be the percentage. We set up the equation (P/100) * 15 = 600, which gives P = 60,000 / 15 = 4000%.","2017 EC entrance"],["A sector of a circle of diameter 8cm is formed by a central angle of 45°. What is the area of the sector?",["2π cm²","π cm²","(2π + 8)cm²","8π cm²"],0,"θ 45 The radius of the circle is r = 4 cm. The area of the sector is given by A = 360 πr2 = 360 π(42 ) = 2π cm2 . ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is true about the signum function, f(x) = sgn x?",["Its range is [0, ∞)","Its domain is the set of real numbers","Its domain is {-1, 0, 1}","Its range is the set of real numbers"],1,"The signum function f(x) = sgn(x) is defined for all real numbers, so its domain is the set of real numbers, which makes option A correct.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an onto function from R onto R?",["f (x) = ∣x − 1∣","f (x) = x2 + 1","f (x) = 2x − 3x2","f (x) = 5x3 + 1 ​"],3,"The cubic function f (x) = 5x3 + 1 has a range of R because it is continuous and goes from −∞ to ∞, making it an onto function from R to R.","2016 EC entrance"],["The following is the distribution of the weight of 40 students in a certain class: Weight (in Kg) 40-48 49-57 5866 67-75 76-84 f 8 18 7 5 2 Then for data given above, what is the median weight in kg?",["54.5","53.8","53","55"],0,"The total number of students is N = 40, so the median lies at the 20th value, which falls in the class interval 49-57. Using the median formula L + ( N /2−cfprev ) w = 48.5 + ( 20−8 ) × 9 = 54.5 Kg. f 18 ​ ​ ​ (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the solution set of the quadratic inequality 3x2 − 3x − 6 < 0?",["(−3, 6)","(−∞, −1) ∪ (2, ∞)","(−∞, −3) ∪ (6, ∞)","(−1, 2)"],3,"Dividing the inequality 3x2 − 3x − 6 < 0 by 3 gives x2 − x − 2 < 0. Factoring the quadratic expression yields (x − 2)(x + 1) < 0, which is satisfied when x lies strictly between the roots −1 and 2, giving the interval (−1, 2). (1) ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Let vector u have an initial point at (1,2)and a terminal point at (-3,6). What are the components of the vector\n−1/2u?",["\\langle 1,-1\\rangle","⟨4, −4⟩","⟨−2, 2⟩","⟨2, −2⟩"],3,"The components of u are ⟨−3 − 1, 6 − 2⟩ = ⟨−4, 4⟩. Multiplying by −1/2 gives − 12 u = ⟨2, −2⟩. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["A certain meeting hall has rows with 27,31,35,39,... seats, last row 107 seats. Total number of seats?",["1327","1427","1307","1407"],3,"The seat counts form an arithmetic sequence starting at 27 with a common difference of 4. First find how many rows there are: 107 = 27 + 4(n − 1) gives 80 = 4(n − 1), so n = 21. The sum of an arithmetic sequence is the number of 27 + 107 terms times the average of the first and last term: S = 21 × = 21 × 67 = 1407. The common trap is the 2 row count. Solving 107 = 27 + 4n instead gives 20 rows and a total of 20 × 67 = 1340, which is not on the list at all, and that missing value is your warning that the count was off by one. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Find the mean of the grouped data.",["19.45","16.95","18.15","21.25"],3,"∑f x The mean of grouped data is calculated as Ni i . Summing the products of the class marks (xi = 12, 17, 22, 27, 32) and their frequencies (fi = 2, 5, 8, 4, 1) gives 24 + 85 + 176 + 108 + 32 = 425, and dividing by N = 20 yields 21.25 . ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["A satellite moves along a hyperbolic curve whose horizontal transverse axis is 24 km and an asymptote y =\n5/12 x + 2. Then, what is the eccentricity of the hyperbola?",["5/13","13/12","15/3","12/13"],3,"A horizontal transverse axis of 24 km means 2a = 24, so a = 12. The asymptotes of such a hyperbola have slopes ± ab , 5 and the given slope is 12 , so b = 5. For a hyperbola c2 = a2 + b2 = 144 + 25 = 169, so c = 13 and the eccentricity is e = ac = 13 . Option B, 12 , is that fraction upside down, and it can be ruled out on sight: the eccentricity of a hyperbola is 12 13 always greater than 1. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["If z = x + yi is a complex number, then ∣z∣2 + 12 (z − zˉ)2 = 1 is equivalent to which one of the following\nequations?\n​",["x2 − y 2 = 1","x2 − 3iy 2 = 1","2x2 − y 2 = 1","x2 − y 2 = 2"],0,"Since ∣z∣2 = x2 + y 2 and z − zˉ = 2iy , we have (z − zˉ)2 = −4y 2 . Substituting these into the equation gives (x2 + y 2 ) + 12 (−4y 2 ) = x2 − y 2 = 1. ​ (1)","2006 EC entrance"],["If sin(α+θ)=12/13 and sin θ = 4/5, then sin α is:",["16/45","56/45","16/65","1/5"],2,"Using the identity sin α = sin((α+θ) - θ) = sin(α+θ) cos θ - cos(α+θ) sin θ. For acute angles, cos θ = 3/5 and cos(α+θ) = 5/13, yielding sin α = (12/13)(3/5) - (5/13)(4/5) = 16/65.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a discrete variable?",["Number of road accidents in Ethiopia.","Profit earned by a company.","The speed of a moving object.","The temperature of an object."],0,"A discrete variable is one that can take on a countable number of values. The number of road accidents in Ethiopia is a countable quantity, unlike temperature, speed, or profit which are continuous variables.","2013 EC entrance"],["Suppose that the equation x2 + y 2 + z 2 + 2x + 8z = 6(y + 1), represents a sphere. Where is the point (1, -1,\n4) located relative to the sphere?",["on the sphere","inside the sphere","at the center of the sphere","outside the sphere"],3,"Rewrite the equation as x2 + 2x + y 2 − 6y + z 2 + 8z = 6, which completes squares to (x + 1)2 + (y − 3)2 + (z + 4)2 = 6 + 1 + 9 + 16 = 32. Substituting the point (1, −1, 4) into the left-hand side gives (1 + 1)2 + (−1 − 3)2 + (4 + 4)2 = 4 + 16 + 64 = 84 > 32, which means the point is outside the sphere. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["If f(x) = 4 + |x+6| for all x, then what is the value of f'(x) at x = -6?",["4","does not exist","-1","1"],1,"The graph of ∣x + 6∣ is a V with its corner at x = −6, and adding 4 lifts the whole V without moving that corner. Approaching from the left the slope is −1, and from the right it is +1. The two one sided slopes disagree, so no single tangent line exists there and the derivative does not exist at x = −6. Option B, 4, mixes up two different values: f (−6) = 4 is the height of the graph at that point, not its slope","2017 EC entrance"],["What is the solution set of the equation 3(x−x ) = 19 ?\n​",["{1, -2}","{-1, 2}","{-1, 0}","{0, 1}"],1,"By writing 1/9 as 3^(-2), we obtain the equation x - x^2 = -2, which simplifies to x^2 - x - 2 = 0. Solving this quadratic equation gives the solution set {-1, 2}.","2014 EC entrance"],["⎧4x − y + z = −5\nWhich one of the following triplets of values of x, y and z contains all solutions for ⎨2x + 2y + 3z = 10 ?\n⎩\n5x − 2y + 6z = 1\n​",["x = 3, y = 2, z = −1","x = 2, y = −1, z = 3 ​","x = 3, y = −1, z = 2","x = −1, y = 3, z = 2"],3,"Substituting the values of Option A (x = −1, y = 3, z = 2) into the system of equations, we get 4(−1) − 3 + 2 = −5, 2(−1) + 2(3) + 3(2) = 10, and 5(−1) − 2(3) + 6(2) = 1, all of which are true. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an arithmetic sequence?",["3, 6, 12, 24, 28, …","1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, …","-3, 6, -9, 12, -15, …","3, 5, 7, 9, 11, …"],3,"An arithmetic sequence has a constant difference between consecutive terms; for 3, 5, 7, 9, 11, the common difference is d = 2.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the equation of an ellipse with centre at (1, 4), vertices at (10, 4) and (1, 2) is :",["2(x − 1)2 + 9(y − 4)2 = 4","(x − 1)2 + 9(y − 4)2 = 4","4(x − 1)2 + 81(y − 4)2 = 324","9(x − 1)2 + 4(y − 4)2 = 1"],2,"The horizontal semi-axis is a = ∣10 − 1∣ = 9 and the vertical semi-axis is b = ∣4 − 2∣ = 2. The standard equation is 2 (x−1)2 + (y−4) = 1, which simplifies to 4(x − 1)2 + 81(y − 4)2 = 324. 81 4 ​","2007 EC entrance"],["Simplify (x²-4)/(x²+3x-10) ÷ (x²+5x+6)/(x²+8x+15).",["(x-2)/(x+3)","(x+2)/(x+5)","((x+2)/(x+5))²","none"],3,"(x−2)(x+2) (x+2)(x+3) x+2 / {−5, −3, −2, 2}). Since 1 is not Factoring the quadratics, we have (x+5)(x−2) ÷ (x+3)(x+5) = x+2 x+5 ÷ x+5 = 1 (for x ∈ in options A, B, or C, the correct choice is 'none'. ​ ​ ​ ​","2017 EC entrance"],["If f (x) =\n1\nex + 1\n​\n, then which one of the following is equal to f −1 (x) for 0 < x < 1?",["ln(1 − x) − ln(x)","1/e−x + 1","e−x + 1","ln(1/x + 1)"],0,"Set y = ex1+1 and make x the subject. Turning both sides upside down gives ex + 1 = y1 , so ex = 1−y . Taking natural y −1 logs, x = ln(1 − y) − ln y , and renaming the letter gives f (x) = ln(1 − x) − ln x. Option C is close to a correct form, but the inside would have to be x1 − 1: the 1 crosses the equals sign, so its sign changes. ​ ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["What is the area of the region bounded by the graph of f (x) = x3 and the x-axis on the interval [−4, 2]?",["120 Square units","60 Square units","136 Square units","68 Square units"],3,"0 The bounded area is found by integrating the absolute value of f (x) = x3 over [−4, 2]. This gives ∫−4 −x3 dx + ​ 4 0 4 2 2 ∫0 x3 dx = [− x4 ] + [ x4 ] = 64 + 4 = 68 square units. −4 0 ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Suppose the following statements are the premises of an argument. �He was lazy or he did not like the\nclassroom. If he was lazy, he could not pass the exam. He passed the exam.� Which one of the following can be\na conclusion that makes the argument valid?",["If he was not lazy, he did like the classroom.","He was not lazy and he did like the classroom.","He did like the classroom.","He did not like the classroom."],3,"Work through the premises in order. He passed the exam, and the second premise says being lazy would have stopped him passing, so he was not lazy. The first premise says he was lazy or he did not like the classroom, and with the first half now ruled out the second half has to be the true one, so he did not like the classroom. Option A states the opposite of that. The premises have already forced laziness out, and it is precisely that which makes the classroom half of the first premise the surviving one.","2005 EC entrance"],["​\n​\nWhat is area of region enclosed between f(x)=x²-4 over [1,5]?",["5/3","65/3","86/3","16/3"],2,"2 5 The function f (x) = x2 − 4 is negative on [1, 2] and positive on [2, 5]. The total area is ∫1 (4 − x2 )dx + ∫2 (x2 − 3 3 4)dx = [4x − x3 ]21 + [ x3 − 4x]52 = 53 + 27 = 86 3 . ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Let a > 0 and a =\n 1. Consider f (x) = ax and g(x) = loga x. Then which one of the following statements is\ntrue about their domains and ranges?\n​",["The domain of f (x) is equal to the domain of g(x).","The range of f (x) is equal to the range of g(x).","The domain of f (x) is equal to the range of g(x).","The domain of f (x) is a subset of the domain of g(x)."],2,"The exponential function f (x) = ax has domain R and range (0, ∞), while the logarithmic function g(x) = loga x has domain (0, ∞) and range R. Thus, the domain of f (x) is equal to the range of g(x). ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Your football has landed at the edge of the roof of your school building. When you are 25 meters away from the\nbase of the building, the angle of elevation to your football is 45°. How high off the ground is your football?",["50/√2 meters","25/√2 meters","50 meters","25 meters"],3,"The relationship between the height h, the horizontal distance, and the angle of elevation is given by tan(45°) = h / 25. Since tan(45°) = 1, the height h is 25 meters.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following conic section is defined by \"the set of points in a plane such that the sum of the\ndistances from two given points is constant\"?",["Hyperbola","Ellipse","Circle","Parabola"],1,"An ellipse is defined geometrically as the set of all points in a plane such that the sum of the distances from two fixed points (foci) is constant.","2016 EC entrance"],["Let P (n, r) be the number of permutations of n objects taking r at a time, and C(n, r) be the number of ways\nof selecting r objects from a set of n objects without considering the order of selection. Which of the following\nis true?",["P (10, 5) = C(10, 5) ⋅ 5!","C(10, 5) = P (10, 5) ⋅ 5!","C(10, 4) = P (10, 4) ⋅ 4!","P (10, 4) = P (10, 4) ⋅ 4!"],0,"The relationship between permutations and combinations is given by P (n, r) = C(n, r) ⋅ r!. Substituting n = 10 and r = 5 yields P (10, 5) = C(10, 5) ⋅ 5!.","2016 EC entrance"],["A parabola with focus (3, -1) has directrix y = 3. Which one of the following is the equation of the parabola?",["(x − 3)2 = 4(y + 1)","(x − 3)2 = −8(y − 1)","(x − 3)2 = 8(y − 1)","(x − 3)2 = −4(y + 1)"],1,"The vertex sits halfway between the focus and the directrix, so it is at (3, 1), and the distance from the vertex to the focus is p = 2. The focus lies below the directrix, so the parabola opens downward and takes the form (x − h)2 = −4p(y − k). With h = 3, k = 1 and p = 2 this gives (x − 3)2 = −8(y − 1). Option A uses −4 where −4p belongs, which would place the focus only one unit from the vertex.","2005 EC entrance"],["Let f (x) = x3 + 2x2 − 3. Which one of the following is true about f ?",["f is decreasing on (−∞, − 43 ). ​","f is decreasing on ( 43 , ∞). ​","f is increasing on (0, ∞).","f is increasing on (− 43 , 0). ​"],2,"The derivative of f (x) = x3 + 2x2 − 3 is f ′ (x) = 3x2 + 4x = x(3x + 4), which is strictly positive on (0, ∞). Therefore, f is increasing on (0, ∞).","2016 EC entrance"],["A group of 100 items have a mean of 62. If the mean of 40 of these items is 55, what is the mean of the\nremaining items?",["69.00","64.55","66.67","65.00"],2,"The sum of all 100 items is 100 × 62 = 6200, and the sum of the first 40 items is 40 × 55 = 2200. The sum of the remaining 60 items is 6200 − 2200 = 4000, giving a mean of 4000/60 = 66.67.","2015 EC entrance"],["If AA is a 3×3 square matrix, which of the following is always true about its transpose AT?",["det(A ) = −det(A)","det(A ) = 1/det(A)","AT = A−1 T (1) T","det(AT ) = det(A)"],3,"A fundamental property of determinants is that the determinant of a matrix is equal to the determinant of its transpose, so det(AT ) = det(A).","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the converse of the conditional statement \"If life in Ethiopia was simpler, then\npeople in Ethiopia would not go to other nations.\"",["If life in Ethiopia was not simpler, then people in Ethiopia would go to other nations.","If people of Ethiopia would not go to other nations, then life in Ethiopia was simpler.","If life in Ethiopia was simpler, then people in Ethiopia would go to other nations.","If people of Ethiopia would go to other nations, then life in the Ethiopia was not simpler."],1,"The converse of a conditional statement P ⟹ Q is Q ⟹ P . Here, P is 'life in Ethiopia was simpler' and Q is 'people in Ethiopia would not go to other nations', so its converse is 'If people of Ethiopia would not go to other nations, then life in Ethiopia was simpler.'","2015 EC entrance"],["The equation of the parabola with vertex V(2, -1) and focus F(-1, -1) is",["(y + 1)2 = −12(x − 2)","(x − 2)2 = −12(y + 1)","(y + 1)2 = 12(x − 2)","(x + 1)2 = −12(y + 1)"],0,"The parabola has a horizontal axis of symmetry since the vertex V (2, −1) and focus F (−1, −1) share the same ycoordinate. The focal distance is p = −1 − 2 = −3, so the equation is (y − k)2 = 4p(x − h) ⇒ (y + 1)2 = −12(x − 2). 2","2015 EC entrance"],["If sin(−53∘ ) = β , then which one of the following is correct?",["sin(307∘ ) = β","sin(37∘ ) = β","sin(−37∘ ) = β","sin(127∘ ) = β"],0,"Since the sine function has a period of 360∘ , we have sin(307∘ ) = sin(307∘ − 360∘ ) = sin(−53∘ ) = β .","2017 EC entrance"],["For a given ellipse, what do you call the ratio of the distance between the two foci to the length of the major\naxis?",["Latus rectum","Eccentricity","Directrix","Length of minor axis"],1,"By definition, the eccentricity (e) of an ellipse is the ratio of the distance between the two foci (2c) to the length of the major axis (2a), which simplifies to c/a.","2013 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the contra positive of the statement: \"If 9 is divisible by 2, then 5 is an even\nnumber\"?",["If 5 is not an even number, then 9 is divisible by 2.","If 5 is an even number, then 9 is divisible by 2.","If 5 is not an even number, then 9 is not divisible by 2.","If 9 is not divisible by 2, then 5 is not an even number."],2,"The contrapositive of the conditional statement P => Q is ~Q => ~P. This translates to: 'If 5 is not an even number, then 9 is not divisible by 2.'","2013 EC entrance"],["Let S, R and T be any three sets. Which one of the following is NOT true about the union of the sets?",["S ∪ T = T","S ∪ S = S","S ∪ R = R ∪ S","(S ∪ R) ∪ T = T ∪ (R ∪ S )"],0,"The statement S ∪ T = T is only true if S is a subset of T , so it is not a general property of set union for any sets S and T.","2016 EC entrance"],["The following is the distribution of the weight of 36 persons.\nWeight in kg\n40 - 49\n50 - 59\nFrequency\n6\n10\nth\nThen, what is the 20 percentile (p20 ) of the measurement?\n60 - 69\n17\n70 - 79\n3\n​",["50.4","51.7","51.4","50.7"],3,"The 20th percentile corresponds to the 0.20 × 36 = 7.2-th value, which lies in the class 50 − 59 (boundaries 49.5 − 59.5). Using the percentile formula P20 = L + ( 7.2−CF ) w = 49.5 + ( 7.2−6 ) 10 = 50.7. f 10 ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Water is running into a canonical tank, which is pointed down at a constant rate of 6π cm³/sec. The cone has a\nheight of 10 cm and a base radius of 5 cm, then how fast is the water level rising when the water reaches 2 cm\ndeep?",["4 cm/sec","6 cm/sec","π4 cm/sec","π6 cm/sec ​ (1) ​"],1,"π 3 π 2 dh By similar triangles, r = h/2, so the volume is V = 12 h . Differentiating gives dV h dt , and substituting dV 6π dt = 4 dt = dh dh ⟹ = and h = 2 yields 6π = π dt 6 cm/sec. dt ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["The volume of the solid generated when the region bounded between graph of y = {\nx2 ,\n4,\n​\n0≤x≤2\nand x2≤x≤3\n​\naxis is rotated about the x-axis:",["32π/5","64π/5","112π/3","112π/5"],3,"The volume is given by V = π ∫_0^2 (x^2)^2 dx + π ∫_2^3 4^2 dx = π [x^5/5]_0^2 + π [16x]_2^3 = π(32/5 + 16) = 112π/5. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["The radian measure of an angle of 120° is equal to:",["2","π ​ 4 ​","​ 4π 3 ​","2π 3 π"],3,"To convert degrees to radians, multiply by π/180∘ , giving 120∘ × π/180∘ = 2π/3 radians.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is qualitative data?",["The time Derartu took to win Atlanta Olympic.","The volume of oil in a container.","Age of President Trump.","The type of Coffee produced in Keffa."],3,"Qualitative data represents categories or attributes rather than numerical measurements. The type of Coffee produced in Keffa is categorical (qualitative), whereas time, age, and volume are all numerical (quantitative) variables. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Mean salary of 10 employees = 6450. New employee gets 7000. New mean?",["6600","6500","6650","6550"],1,"The original sum of the 10 salaries is 10 * 6450 = 64500. Adding the new salary of 7000 gives a total of 71500, which divided by 11 employees yields a new mean of 6500.","2018 EC entrance"],["If angle θ is an acute angle of a right triangle, what is the length of the side adjacent to θ, given the hypotenuse\nhas 6 units length and sec θ = 10/3?",["2 units","18 units","1.8 units","20 units"],2,"hypotenuse hypotenuse 6 Since sec θ = adjacent , we have adjacent = sec θ = 10/3 = 18 10 = 1.8 units. ​ ​ ​ ​","2007 EC entrance"],["Let ABCD is a parallelogram and AC and BD be diagonals, then which one of the following is Not true?",["DC + AD = AC","AB = BC − BD","AB + BC = AC","AB − BC = DC"],3,"In parallelogram ABCD, the opposite sides are represented by equal vectors, so AB = DC . Therefore, AB − BC = DC would imply −BC = 0, which is false.","2016 EC entrance"],["Everyday a person saves 5 cents more than the amount he saved on the previous day. His target is to save the\ntotal amount of 3225 cents by the end of 30 days. How much must be the starting saving to meet the target?",["35 cents","50 cents","25 cents","60 cents"],0,"This is an arithmetic series with d = 5, n = 30, and S30 = 3225. Using the formula Sn = n2 [2a1 + (n − 1)d], we get 3225 = 15[2a1 + 145], which simplifies to 215 = 2a1 + 145, so the starting saving a1 = 35 cents. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is the converse of: \"If wages increase, then inflation decreases.\"?",["If inflation increases, then wages increase","If inflation decreases, then wages increase","If inflation decreases, then wages decrease","If inflation increases, then wages decrease"],1,"The converse of a conditional statement 'If P, then Q' is 'If Q, then P'. Therefore, the converse of 'If wages increase, then inflation decreases' is 'If inflation decreases, then wages increase'.","2014 EC entrance"],["Five English books, 3 of which identical and 3 different Mathematics books are to be arranged in a row. If one\nparticular Mathematics book is to be placed first, in how many ways can this be done?",["6720","5040","240","840"],1,"With one particular Mathematics book fixed in the first position, we need to arrange the remaining 7 books (2 distinct Mathematics books, 2 distinct English books, and 3 identical English books). The number of distinct ways to arrange them 5040 is 7! 3! = 6 = 840. ​ ​ (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the set of all critical numbers of f (x) = 13 x3 − ∣4x − 1∣ ?\n​",["{1/4}","{-2, 1/4, 2}","{1/4, 2}","{-2, 2}"],2,"The function is non-differentiable at x = 1/4. For x > 1/4, f'(x) = x^2 - 4 = 0 gives x = 2 (since -2 is not in this domain), and for x < 1/4, f'(x) = x^2 + 4 = 0 has no real solutions; hence, the critical numbers are {1/4, 2}. (1) π","2006 EC entrance"],["If the truth value of a proposition p is False, then which one of the following compound proposition has a truth\nvalue True?",["p ⇒ ¬p","¬p ⇒ p","¬p ∧ p","¬(¬p ∨ p)"],0,"When p is False, ¬p is True. The conditional statement p ⇒ ¬p has a False hypothesis, which makes the implication vacuously True.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following compound propositions is a tautology?",["p ⇒ (p ∨ ¬q)","(q ∨ ¬q) ⇒ p","p ⇒ (q ∧ ¬q)","p ∨ (q ∧ ¬q)"],0,"By the rule of addition, p implies p ∨ ¬q regardless of the truth values of p and q, making p ⇒ (p ∨ ¬q) a tautology. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["Suppose P and Q are point in space such that the midpoint of PQ is on the negative z-axis and the distance\nbetween P and Q is 6. If P=(2, -1, 0), then what is the coordinate of Q?",["(2, -1, 6)","(-2, 1, 4)","(2, -1, -6)","(-2, 1, -4)"],3,"Let Q = (x, y, z). The midpoint ((2 + x)/2, (-1 + y)/2, z/2) lies on the negative z-axis, so x = -2, y = 1, and z < 0. Using the distance formula, (x - 2)² + (y + 1)² + z² = 16 + 4 + z² = 36 gives z² = 16, so z = -4, yielding Q = (-2, 1, -4).","2006 EC entrance"],["Let f(x) = (1/3)x - |x²-4|. The set of all critical numbers is:",["{-2, -1/6, 2}","{-2, -1/6, 0, 1/6, 2}","{-2, 1/6, 2}","{-2, -1/6, 1/6, 2}"],0,"The critical numbers include x = 2 and x = -2 where the derivative does not exist. For x in (-2, 2), setting the derivative of f(x) = x^2 + x/3 - 4 to zero gives x = -1/6, resulting in the critical set {-2, -1/6, 2}.","2018 EC entrance"],["If f (x) = 2x+4\n. Then, which one of the following points is on the graph of f −1 (x)?\nx−1\n​",["(3, 5)","(2, 8)","(0, −4)","(1, −5)"],3,"A point (a, b) is on the graph of f −1 (x) if and only if (b, a) is on the graph of f (x), meaning f (b) = a. Testing (1, −5) 2(−5)+4 = 1, which confirms that (1, −5) is on the inverse function's graph. gives f (−5) = −5−1 = −6 −6 ​ ​ (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Let p, q and r be propositions. If the truth value of the proposition [(p ⟹ q) ∧ r] ⟹ q is False. Then the\nconverse of which proposition has truth value True?",["p ⟹ ¬q","p ⟹ r","r ⟹ q","q ⟹ ¬p"],2,"For the implication [(p ⟹ q) ∧ r] ⟹ q to be False, its antecedent must be True and its consequent False, which means q = False, r = True, and p ⟹ q is True (so p = False). The converse of option C, r ⟹ q , is q ⟹ r, which has truth value False ⟹ True = True.","2015 EC entrance"],["The equation of an ellipse with center at (1,5) and vertices at (10,5) and (1,2) is:",["9(x − 1)2 + (y − 5)2 = 1","(x − 1)2 + 9(y − 5)2 = 81","9(x − 1)2 + (y − 5)2 = 81","(x − 1)2 + 9(y − 5)2 = 1"],1,"The distance from the center (1, 5) to the horizontal vertex (10, 5) is a = 9, and to the vertical vertex (1, 2) is b = 3. 2 2 The equation of the horizontal ellipse is (x−1) + (y−5) = 1, which simplifies to (x − 1)2 + 9(y − 5)2 = 81. 81 9 ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["A boy and girl are both standing on a sun light. The boy’s height is 1.6m and casts a shadow of 2m. If the girl’s\nheight casts a shadow of 1.8m, then what is the height (in meter) of the girl?",["1.54","1.68","1.44","1.5"],2,"Using the similarity of triangles formed by the objects and their shadows, the ratio of height to shadow length is constant: 1.6/2 = hg /1.8. Solving for the girl's height gives hg = 0.8 × 1.8 = 1.44 meters. ​ ​","2017 EC entrance"],["The volume of spherical balloon is increasing at rate 24 cm³/sec. What is rate of change of surface area when\nradius=8 cm?",["6 cm²/sec","8 cm²/sec","4 cm²/sec","3 cm²/sec"],0,"dV dr 24 3 2 dr 2 For a sphere V = 43 πr3 , so dV dt = 4πr dt . With dt = 24 and r = 8, dt = 4π(64) = 32π . The surface area is S = 4πr , dS dr 3 so dt = 8πr dt = 8π(8) ( 32π ) = 6 cm²/sec. Option D, 3, is what you get by using 4πr in place of 8πr when differentiating 4πr2 . ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Which is the largest interval on which f(x)=-2x³-9x²-12x+1 is increasing?",["(-∞,-2]∪[1,∞)","[-2,∞)","[-2,-1]","(-∞,-2]∪[-1,∞)"],0,"The function is increasing when its derivative is non-negative: f ′ (x) = −6x2 − 18x − 12 ≥ 0. Dividing by −6 reverses the inequality to x2 + 3x + 2 ≤ 0, which factors as (x + 1)(x + 2) ≤ 0, yielding the interval [−2, −1].","2018 EC entrance"],["A group of students, 5 from grade 10, 8 from grade 11 and 2 from grade 12 is to be formed. If a student is chosen\nrandomly from this group, what is the probability that the chosen student is either from grade 10 or grade 12?",["12/15","1/7","7/15","5/15"],2,"The total number of students is 5 + 8 + 2 = 15. The number of students in grade 10 or 12 is 5 + 2 = 7, so the probability of choosing one of them is 7/15.","2015 EC entrance"],["​\n​\n(x + 4)2 , for every x ∈ R?\n​",["g(x) = ∣x∣ + 4","g(x) = x + 4","g(x) = ∣x + 4∣","g(x) = x + 2"],2,"By definition, for any real number u, ​ u2 = ∣u∣. Substituting u = x + 4 gives g(x) = ∣x + 4∣. ​ The center of a circle on the line y = 2x and the line x = 1 is tangent to the circle at (1, 6). How long is the radius of the circle? A. 5 C. 3 (1) B. 4 D. ✓ 2 Answer: D The tangent line x = 1 is vertical, meaning the radius connecting the center (h, 2h) to the tangent point (1, 6) must be horizontal, so 2h = 6 ⟹ h = 3. The radius is the horizontal distance between (3, 6) and (1, 6), which is ∣3 − 1∣ = 2. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["Consider the following data: 6, 11, 4, 15, 26, 11, 4, 10, 2, 9. Which of the following is true about the mode of\nthe given data?",["Unimodal","No mode","Bimodal","Multimodal"],2,"The values 4 and 11 both appear with the highest frequency of 2, meaning the data has two modes and is therefore bimodal.","2018 EC entrance"],["2x2 − 4,\nLet a function, f (x) = { 3\nx − 4x + 1,\nf , at x = −2?\n​\nif x ≥ 1\n. Then what is the equation of the tangent line to the graph of \nif x < 1\n​",["y = −4x + 14","y = 8x + 17","y = −8x − 12","y = 4x − 2"],1,"For x = -2 < 1, we use f(x) = x³ - 4x + 1, where f(-2) = 1 and f'(-2) = 8, yielding the tangent line equation y - 1 = 8(x + 2), or y = 8x + 17.","2018 EC entrance"],["​\n​\nThe sides of an equilateral triangle are increasing at the rate of 2 cm/sec. The rate at which the area increases\nwhen side is 10 cm is:",["10/3 cm²/sec","√3 cm²/sec","10 cm²/sec","10√3 cm²/sec"],1,"3 ds The area of an equilateral triangle is A = 43 s2 . Differentiating with respect to time t gives dA dt = 2 s dt = 3 2 3 cm /sec. 2 (10)(2) = 10 ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the value of ∫ x e +ex dx?\nx +e\ne−1\nx−1\n​",["​ 1 e+1 + ex+1 ) + c e ln(x ​","1e ln(xe + ex+1 ) + c","​ 1 e x+1 )+c e ln((x + 1) + e","1e ln(xe + ex ) + c ​"],3,"Using the substitution u = xe + ex , we have du = (exe−1 + ex )dx = e(xe−1 + ex−1 )dx. Thus, the integral becomes 1 ∫ 1e du ln ∣u∣ + c = 1e ln(xe + ex ) + c. u = e ​ ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["What is the surface area of a sphere with radius 6 cm?",["24π cm²","36π cm²","144π cm²","48π cm²"],2,"The surface area of a sphere is given by 4πr2 . For r = 6 cm, the surface area is 4π(6)2 = 144π cm2 .","2014 EC entrance"],["The corner points of the feasible region determined by the following systems of linear inequalities y ≥ x, x +\n3y ≤ 60, x + y ≥ 10, x ≥ 0, y ≥ 0 are (0, 20), (15, 15)(0, 10) and (5, 5). Let z = 4ax + 2by , where\na, b > 0. Condition on a and b so that the maximum of z occurs at both (15, 15) and (0, 20) is:",["a = 2b","b = 2a","b = 6a","a = 6b"],2,"For the maximum to occur at both (15, 15) and (0, 20), their objective function values must be equal, so 4a(15) + 2b(15) = 4a(0) + 2b(20), which simplifies to 60a + 30b = 40b, or b = 6a.","2016 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-biology","name":"Biology","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["Suppose a couple produced a legitimate child of blood type B, what are the genotypes of the couple?",["AA × BO","AA × BB","AA × AB","AO × BO"],3,"A child of blood type B must inherit at least one I B allele. Among the choices, only the cross AO × BO can yield offspring with the BO genotype, which expresses as blood type B.","1996 EC entrance"],["During culturing micro-organisms, all of the following activities are important, EXCEPT",["adding distilled water to a sterilized agar.","sterilizing the inoculating loops.","transferring target micro-organisms into an agar medium.","tilting the lid of the Petri dish during inoculation."],0,"Adding distilled water to a sterilized agar medium after autoclaving would introduce external microbial contaminants, compromising the sterile culture environment.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is true about the substance represented by the chemical formula C2 H5 NO2 ?\n​",["Amino acid","Fatty acid ​ ​","Simple sugar","Inorganic substance"],0,"The formula C2H5NO2 corresponds to glycine, the simplest amino acid, which contains an amino group (-NH2) and a carboxyl group (-COOH).","2006 EC entrance"],["Secretions of endocrine glands require receptors on cell membrane to be picked by their targets while exocrine\nsecretions do not. This is because",["endocrine glands are ductless.","exocrine glands secrete hormone directly to the blood stream.","endocrine glands are controlled by the nervous system.","endocrine glands produce protein-based hormones."],0,"Because endocrine glands are ductless, they secrete hormones directly into the bloodstream to circulate throughout the body; target cells must express specific receptors to detect and respond to these systemic signals.","2014 EC entrance"],["What happens if the axon is stimulated? Formation of",["positive charge inside the axon","negative charge inside the axon","positive charge outside of the axon","negative charge in both sides of the axon"],0,"When an axon is stimulated, sodium channels open and sodium ions (N a+ ) rush inward, causing depolarization and the generation of a positive charge inside the axon.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is the common idea held by all the creationists?",["Life is eternal.","All life was created in six days.","Life came to earth from elsewhere in the universe.","Life was created by a supernatural being."],3,"While creationists may differ on the timeline and mechanism of creation, the defining belief common to all creationism is that life was created by a supernatural being.","2011 EC entrance"],["Suppose the fibers in the connective tissue of the skin and blood vessels do not form properly and causes\nbleeding gums and poor healing of wounds. This problem is related with deficiency of",["Vitamin A.","Vitamin D.","Vitamin C.","Vitamin B."],2,"Vitamin C is essential for synthesizing collagen. Deficiency leads to scurvy, causing bleeding gums and poor wound healing.","2018 EC entrance"],["70. Which part of plant leaf contain large number of chloroplasts that carry out most of the photosynthetic\nactivity?",["Epidermal cells","Spongy mesophyll","Guard cells","Palisade mesophyll"],3,"The palisade mesophyll consists of column-shaped cells packed with a high concentration of chloroplasts, making it the primary site of light absorption and photosynthesis in a leaf.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which technological products have been made through imitation of termite mound architecture?",["Building technology","Techniques of preserving vaccine","New drone design","Weaving technology"],2,"A termite mound stays close to one temperature all day, because its chimneys and side tunnels let warm air rise out and cool air enter low down. Architects copied that flow of air in buildings such as the Eastgate Centre in Harare, which stays cool with very little air conditioning. New drone design is the tempting answer, but drones copy the flight of birds and insects, not a mound.","2017 EC entrance"],["Grade 9 students identified an organism using dichotomous keys. The organism was poikilothermic, invertebrate\nand had six jointed legs. To which phylum would the students group this organism?",["Mollusca","Arthropoda","Porifera","Cnidaria"],1,"Organisms with a segmented body, jointed appendages (six legs), and an exoskeleton belong to the phylum Arthropoda.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the term that describes plant response towards touch or physical contact?",["Hydrotropism","Chemotropism","Thigmotropism","Phototropism"],2,"Thigmotropism is the directional growth response of a plant in reaction to touch or physical contact with a solid object, such as climbing vines wrapping around a support.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following nucleotide sequences contains four pyrimidine bases?",["GATCAATGC","UAGCGGUAA","Both B and C","GCUAGACAA"],0,"Pyrimidines are cytosine (C), thymine (T), and uracil (U). In GATCAATGC, the pyrimidines are T, C, T, and C, totaling exactly four.","2010 EC entrance"],["Why does photorespiration take place in a hot environment? Because plants close their stomata and face",["O2 accumulation.","CO2 shortage.","O2 shortage ​ ​ (1) ​ ​","H2 O shortage"],1,"Under hot and dry conditions, plants close their stomata to prevent water loss, which blocks carbon dioxide from entering the leaf, leading to a CO2 shortage that triggers photorespiration.","2013 EC entrance"],["All of the following are examples of innate behaviours EXCEPT",["training killer whales at marine parks.","producing tears when dust gets into the eyes.","increasing breathing rate during exercise.","a fly moving its maggot into more humid environment."],0,"Training killer whales at marine parks involves operant conditioning, which is a form of learned behavior rather than an innate behavior.","2015 EC entrance"],["Herpes simplex is a type of",["DNA virus","RNA virus","retrovirus","bacteriophage"],0,"Herpes simplex virus (HSV) is a double-stranded DNA virus belonging to the Herpesviridae family, meaning its genetic material is DNA rather than RNA.","2016 EC entrance"],["Among the following ABO blood group genotype, which one produces two types which one produces two types\nof antigens?",["IB IB","IA IB","IA IO","IB IO"],1,"The genotype IA IB exhibits codominance, meaning both alleles are fully expressed to produce both A and B surface antigens on red blood cells.","2009 EC entrance"],["If someone suddenly removes his/her hand from a very hot object, which of the following types of behavior is\nmanifested?",["Imprinting","Learned behaviour","Sensitization","Reflex action"],3,"The rapid and automatic withdrawal of a hand from a painful hot stimulus is an innate spinal reflex action that protects the body from tissue damage.","2008 EC entrance"],["In Ethiopia, which of the following genera of microorganisms has the potential to be used for single cell protein\nproduction?",["Spirulina","Rhizobium","Agrobacterium","Bacillus"],0,"Spirulina is a genus of blue-green algae (cyanobacteria) that grows abundantly in Ethiopian alkaline lakes (like Lake Chitu) and is widely cultivated as a rich source of single-cell protein (SCP)","1996 EC entrance"],["Which of the following processes explains lactate production during anaerobic respiration in animal cells?",["Reduction of pyruvate","Oxidation of pyruvate","Phosphorylation of pyruvate","Decarboxylation of pyruvate"],0,"Lactate is produced during anaerobic respiration in animal cells by the reduction of pyruvate using electrons from NADH, a reaction catalyzed by lactate dehydrogenase.","2014 EC entrance"],["What does an ethnologist study?",["Animal behavior","Soil types","Fossil fuel","Insect diets"],0,"Although misspelled as 'ethnologist', the question refers to an ethologist, a scientist who studies animal behavior in natural environments.","2007 EC entrance"],["What is the shape of an enzyme molecule?",["Linear","Globular","Pleated","Branched"],1,"Enzymes are tertiary or quaternary proteins that fold into a compact, three-dimensional globular shape.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which drop of iodine solution is added to a solution of a foodstuff and the foodstuff turns dark blue what dose\nthe foodstuff contain",["Glucose","Starch","Disaccharide","Reducing sugar"],1,"Iodine solution reacts specifically with starch to form a characteristic dark blue or blue-black complex.","2009 EC entrance"],["If the protoplasm shrinks away from the cell wall when a plant cell is bathed in a sugar solution, what is the\nconcentration of the solution relative to the protoplasm of the plant cell?",["Hypotonic","Isotonic","Isoosmotic","Hypertonic"],3,"Plasmolysis, where the protoplasm shrinks away from the cell wall, occurs when a plant cell is placed in a hypertonic solution because water leaves the cell by osmosis down its concentration gradient. (1)","1996 EC entrance"],["Which of the following happens during the dark reaction of photosynthesis?",["ATP is produced","Carbon dioxide is fixed","NADPH is produced","Oxygen is split from water"],1,"During the light-independent (dark) reactions or the Calvin cycle, carbon dioxide is fixed into organic molecules using ATP and NADPH produced during the light reactions.","1996 EC entrance"],["If a country has a large number of young people relative to the number of old people, to which category of\ncountries does it belong?",["Industrial","Hunter - gatherer","Post - industrial","Developing"],3,"Developing countries typically have a broad-based population pyramid characterized by a high proportion of young dependents and a low proportion of elderly people due to high birth rates. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["Based on similarity in number of amino acids found in haemoglobin, which one of the following animals has\ncloser phylogenetic relations to human beings?",["Chicken","Horse","Gibbon","Frog"],2,"Gibbons are primates (apes) and share the closest evolutionary relationship to humans among the options, having only a few amino acid differences in their haemoglobin chains compared to humans.","2008 EC entrance"],["Current human concerns such as famine, pestilence, and environmental degradation would be solved through\nthe use of:",["Terracing","Aquaculture","Biological principles","Irrigation"],2,"According to the Ethiopian Grade 11 Biology curriculum, pressing global issues such as famine, pestilence, and environmental degradation can be addressed through the comprehensive application of biological principles.","2010 EC entrance"],["A biome characterized by its frozen soil, cold temperature, dry precipitation and inhabited by lichens and\nmigrating animals?",["Hot Desert","Thorn forest","Boreal forest","Tundra"],3,"The tundra biome is characterized by permafrost (permanently frozen soil), extremely cold and dry conditions, and vegetation dominated by lichens and mosses, with highly migratory animal populations.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following bases are the triplets of codes in the mRNA That cease translation and the ribosome\nfolds the polypeptide into its Final structure?",["CCC, UUA and GUU","ATT, ATCandACT","TAA, TAG and TGA","UAA, UAG and UGA"],3,"UAA, UAG and UGA are the three stop codons. They code for no amino acid, so when the ribosome reaches one of them translation ends and the finished polypeptide is released to fold. Any triplet containing T cannot be an mRNA codon, because RNA uses uracil (U) in place of thymine (T). That removes options B and C, and the triplets in D all code for amino acids.","2012 EC entrance"],["Which type of learnt behavior is developed after a repeated exposure to a stimulus?",["Sensitization","Latent","Habituation","Insight"],2,"Habituation is a simple form of learning where an animal stops or decreases its response to a stimulus after repeated exposure to it, provided the stimulus is neither beneficial nor harmful.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is not an industrial use of bacteria?",["Genetic engineering","Food processing","Waste water treatment","Recycling of minerals through ecosystems"],3,"The recycling of minerals through ecosystems is a natural biogeochemical process, not an industrial or commercial application of bacteria.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following biomes supports the highest diversity of plant and animal life?",["Tropical rain forest","African savannah","Deciduous forest","Grassland"],0,"Tropical rain forests support the highest biodiversity of any terrestrial biome due to year-round warm temperatures, ample sunlight, and high precipitation.","2009 EC entrance"],["A student made a collection of plants having flowers and seeds from his locality and compared their embryo,\nleaves and stems using hand lens. He found that all his collections contain a single seed leaf embryo, long and\nthin with parallel veins of leaves and stem contains scattered vascular bundles. Which option contains plants\nthat can be categorized under his collection?",["Grasses, orchids, teff and roses","Grasses, orchids, teff and beans","Grasses, sunflowers, teff and maize","Grasses, orchids, teff and maize"],3,"One seed leaf (cotyledon), long narrow leaves with parallel veins and scattered vascular bundles in the stem are the marks of monocot plants. Grasses, orchids, teff and maize are all monocots, so option D fits the whole collection. The other options fail because roses, beans and sunflowers are dicots: they have two seed leaves, net shaped veins and vascular bundles arranged in a ring.","2017 EC entrance"],["If the average diameter of the human red blood cell is 0.000007 m, which one is its correct diameter when\nexpressed in a smaller unit?",["0.007 μm","7000 nm","7 mm","0.00007μm"],1,"The value 0.000007 m is equal to 7 × 10−6 m or 7μm. To convert this to nanometers, multiply by 103 , yielding 7000 nm.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which of the following parts of the flower did Mendel remove from young flowers to prevent self-population ?",["Petals","Sepals","Stamens","Ovaries"],2,"Mendel removed the immature stamens (the male reproductive organs containing pollen) from pea flowers to prevent self-pollination during his hybridization experiments.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following enzymes is responsible to catalyze the joining of two molecules by hydrolysis of\nATP?",["Ligases","Transferases","Isomerases","Lyases"],0,"Ligases are enzymes that catalyze the joining (ligation) of two large molecules by forming a new chemical bond, a process usually powered by the hydrolysis of ATP. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following practices is a part of a responsible HIV/AIDS engagement in the fight against it?",["Avoiding circumcision","Washing hands after shaking HIV positive individuals","Sharing needles only with close friends","Maintaining a monogamous relationship"],3,"Maintaining a monogamous relationship prevents the transmission of HIV, whereas sharing needles (even with friends) is highly risky, and washing hands is unnecessary as HIV is not transmitted via casual skin contact. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["If an F1 round yellow pea of Rr Yy genotype is selfed, which class of pea is the most frequent in the F2\ngeneration?\n​\n​\n​",["Round yellow","Round green","Wrinkled green","Wrinkled yellow ​"],0,"In a dihybrid cross of a selfed Rr Yy heterozygote, the expected phenotypic ratio in the F2 generation is 9:3:3:1, where the double dominant phenotype (Round yellow) is the most frequent at 9/16. ​ ​ ​","1996 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following characteristic is UNNECESSARY for an object to be considered a living thing?",["Ability to respond to stimuli","Ability to grow","Ability to move","Ability to reproduce"],2,"Locomotion (the ability to move from place to place) is not a universal characteristic of life, as plants and many fungi and sessile animals do not possess it.","2006 EC entrance"],["which of the following is an inorganic molecule?",["C6 H22 O11 (1) ​ ​","CH4 ​","C18 H36 O2 ​ ​ ​","CaCo3 ​ ​"],3,"Calcium carbonate (CaCO3) is classified as an inorganic compound; carbonates, oxides of carbon, and cyanides are standard exceptions to carbon-containing organic molecules.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which one is the viral symmetry refers to the shape with 20 triangular faces and 12 corners?",["Icosahedral","Cylindrical","Helical","Complex"],2,"An icosahedron is a solid with 20 triangular faces and 12 corners, and many viruses build their protein coat in that shape because identical protein units can pack into it neatly. Helical symmetry is the tempting answer, but that gives a rod or a spiral, as in the tobacco mosaic virus.","2017 EC entrance"],["What is the important role played by microorganism such as bacteria and fungi in the ecosystem?",["Forming organic substance","?Antibiotic production","Supplying energy to the ecosystem","Recycling of nutrients"],0,"Bacteria and fungi are the decomposers. They break down dead bodies, fallen leaves and waste, and in doing so they release the carbon, nitrogen and minerals locked in that material back into the soil and the air where plants can take them up again. Without them the nutrients would stay trapped in dead matter and the cycle would stop. Forming organic substances is the tempting answer, but building organic matter from simple raw materials is the work of green plants and other producers. (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following organs serves as a coordinating system in a reflex action?",["Nerve cells","Dehydrogenase","Oxidoreductase","Spinal cord"],3,"In a simple reflex arc, the spinal cord acts as the central coordinating/integrating organ that receives sensory input and directly sends motor output, bypassing the conscious brain.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following diseases increases the likelihood of contracting HIV?",["Gonorrhoea","Tuberculosis","Syphilis","Chancroid"],2,"Syphilis is a sexually transmitted infection that causes genital ulcers, which break the skin barrier and greatly facilitate the transmission and contraction of HIV.","2014 EC entrance"],["To which category of behavior does the human behavior that involves the strengthening of existing responses or \nthe formation of new responses to existing stimuli that occur because of practice or repetition belong?",["Learned behavior","Innate behavior","Instinctive behavior","Inborn behavior"],0,"Behavior that is modified, strengthened, or acquired through practice, experience, or repetition is classified as learned behavior.","2009 EC entrance"],["The ultimate source of genetic variation is:",["Selection","Genetic drift","Migration","Mutation"],3,"Mutation is the ultimate source of all genetic variation because it introduces completely new alleles into a gene pool.","2010 EC entrance"],["What is one of the main uses of biotechnology in food production?",["Genetic engineering of crops","Developing biological weapons","Reducing biodiversity loss","Creating synthetic chemicals"],0,"Genetic engineering of crops is the main use of biotechnology in food production. Genes are added to give pest resistance, tolerance of drought or salt, longer shelf life or better nutrient content, as in vitamin A enriched rice. Option B tempts because industry does make chemicals, but making synthetic chemicals is an industrial chemical process and does not involve living systems. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following Ethiopian biological research institutes is known for housing a major gene bank in\nAfrica?",["Addis Ababa University Biology Department","Akiliu Lemma Institute of Pathobiology","Institute of Biodiversity Conservation","Armauer Hansen Research Institute"],2,"The Institute of Biodiversity Conservation (today called the Ethiopian Biodiversity Institute) keeps one of the largest gene banks in Africa. A gene bank stores seeds and other genetic material so that Ethiopia's crop varieties and wild species are not lost. The other choices are a university department and medical research institutes; storing genetic resources is not their job.","2017 EC entrance"],["The sheep 'dolly' is an example of which biotechnological manipulation of animals by human?",["Transgenic animal","Cloned animal","Genetically engineered animal","Hybrid animal"],2,"Dolly was made by somatic cell nuclear transfer. The nucleus of a body cell taken from one adult sheep was placed into an egg cell whose own nucleus had been removed, and the embryo that grew carried the same nuclear DNA as that adult, so Dolly was a clone. Genetically engineered animal is the tempting answer because the work was done in a laboratory, but no gene was cut, changed or inserted: the whole existing set of genes was copied as it was.","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is a product of the Krebs cycle?",["Oxygen","NADH, FADH2, ATP, and CO2","Glucose","Pyruvate"],3,"Each turn of the Krebs cycle in the mitochondrial matrix strips hydrogen from the intermediates onto carriers, giving 3 NADH and 1 FADH2 , makes 1 ATP through GTP by substrate level phosphorylation, and releases 2 molecules of CO2 . Pyruvate is the tempting option, but pyruvate comes out of glycolysis and is the input that feeds the cycle, not a product of it. ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["In a metabolic pathway(A-->B-->C-->D) where each step is catalyzed by a separate enzyme which substance\nin the pathway serves as an allosteric regulator?",["Substance A","Substance B","Substance D","Substance C"],2,"In feedback inhibition of metabolic pathways, the end-product (Substance D) acts as an allosteric regulator (inhibitor) by binding to an allosteric site on the first enzyme.","2010 EC entrance"],["Hummus & chimpanzees, both evolved from a common ancestor that lived about",["15 Million years ago","20 million years ago","6 million years ago","10 million years ago"],2,"Genetic and fossil evidence show that humans (misspelled as 'Hummus' in the stem) and chimpanzees diverged from a common ancestor approximately 6 million years ago.","2016 EC entrance"],["In an HIV/AIDS community screening, students were asked to take part in voluntary testing. The following\ndiscussion presents the views of four grade 12 students named A, B, C and D towards HIV testing. Student A: I\nshould not take the testing; it is simply boring. Student B: We should take the testing, since we are educated;\nwe should be exemplary. Student C: If we get tested and got positive, what should we do? So, let us not get\ntested. Student D: You know, this HIVIAIDS testing is simply a business. We should not be cheated. Which\nstudent do you think is correct?",["Student C","Student B","Student A","Student D"],1,"Student B shows a responsible and educated attitude towards HIV testing, recognizing the importance of being tested to set a positive example for the community.","2013 EC entrance"],["If certain food stuff gave a positive result with benedicts test only after it was hydrolysed with hydrochloric acid,\nwhich of the following substances could it be?",["Lipid","Nucleic acid","Proteins","Non-reducing sugar"],3,"Non-reducing sugars, such as sucrose, do not reduce Benedict's reagent directly; they yield a positive result only after being hydrolysed by an acid (such as HCl) into their constituent reducing monosaccharides.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which part of the cell makes necessary changes packages and secretes proteins?",["Cell wall","Endoplasmic �reticulum","Golgi apparatus","Mitochondria"],2,"The Golgi apparatus modifies (e.g., glycosylation), sorts, packages, and directs proteins received from the rough endoplasmic reticulum for secretion or delivery to other organelles.","2010 EC entrance"],["Which of the following groups probably ate more of a herbivorous diet?",["Cromagnon humans","Australopithecus afarensis","Homo habilis","Homo erectus"],1,"Australopithecus afarensis lived earlier and possessed dental adaptations (such as thick enamel and large molars) suited for grinding fibrous plant materials, eating a much higher proportion of vegetation than later Homo species. (1)","1996 EC entrance"],["Baby ostriches tend to follow the first moving object that they see as they hatch out of the eggs. What kind of\nanimal behaviour does this demonstrate?",["Positive kinesis","Learned behavior","Positive taxis","Innate behavior"],1,"This phenomenon describes imprinting, which is classified in the Ethiopian curriculum as a form of learned behavior that occurs during a critical, sensitive period early in an animal's life. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following classes of molecule CANNOT pass easily across the cell membrane by simple diffusion?",["Non-polar molecules","Lipid soluble molecules","Small non-polar molecules","polar molecules"],3,"The hydrophobic core of the lipid bilayer acts as a barrier to polar molecules, preventing them from easily crossing the membrane by simple diffusion.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following forms of nitrogen are readily utilization by green plants?",["Nitrate","Nitrite","Atmospheric nitrogen","Ammonium ion"],0,"Although plants can absorb ammonium, nitrate (NO3-) is the primary, most abundant, and readily absorbed form of inorganic nitrogen utilized by green plants from the soil.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is responsible for the bending of a young plant towards a unidirectional source of light?",["Increased rate of cell division on the light side","Faster growth rate on the dark side","Reduced auxin concentration on dark side","Reduced photosynthesis on dark side"],1,"Phototropism is caused by auxins migrating to the shaded (dark) side of the shoot, stimulating cell elongation and resulting in a faster growth rate on the dark side, which bends the shoot toward the light.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following expression is more related to the phase \"survival of the fittest\"?",["Natural selection","Gene mutation","Inheritance of acquired characteristics","Mendelian inheritance"],0,"Herbert Spencer coined the phrase 'survival of the fittest,' which Charles Darwin later used interchangeably with his concept of natural selection.","2007 EC entrance"],["Biological tool that is used to separate components of different molecular weight is known as;",["Centrifuge","GPS","Transect","Quadra"],0,"A centrifuge is a laboratory device used to separate components of a mixture based on their size, shape, density, and molecular weight by spinning them at high speeds.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following paired organelle are membrane-bound?",["Chloroplasts and ribosomes","Ribosomes and peroxisomes","chloroplasts and mitochondria","Mitochondria and ribosome"],2,"Chloroplasts and mitochondria are each wrapped in a double membrane, and both also carry folded membranes inside, the thylakoids and the cristae, where their energy reactions take place. Ribosomes have no membrane at all: they are two blocks of RNA and protein, which is why every option pairing a ribosome with something else fails. Option A is the tempting one because a peroxisome is genuinely membrane bound, but its partner in that pair is the ribosome, so the pair as a whole is wrong. (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following processes has a decreasing effect on the concentration of atmospheric carbon\ndioxide?",["Photosynthesis","Decomposition of dead organism","Combustion of fossil fuels","Cellular respiration"],0,"Photosynthesis removes carbon dioxide from the atmosphere to produce organic compounds, while respiration, combustion, and decomposition all release carbon dioxide into the atmosphere. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["Identify learned behavior from the following.",["Honey bee making honey.","Dog trained to hunt.","Child withdraws hand from hot things.","Ants making nest."],1,"A dog trained to hunt represents a learned behavior because it is acquired through training and experience, unlike the innate behaviors listed in the other options.","2013 EC entrance"],["During which stage of aerobic respiration dose oxidative phosphorylatuion occur?",["Link reaction","Glycolysis","Chemiosmosis","Krebs cycle"],2,"Oxidative phosphorylation occurs via chemiosmosis, where ATP synthase utilizes the proton gradient established by the electron transport chain to phosphorylate ADP to ATP.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which class of enzymes joins to molecule together by formation of new bonds?",["Hydrolase","Lyase","Ligase","Isomerase"],2,"Ligases are the class of enzymes that catalyze the joining (ligation) of two molecules accompanied by the hydrolysis of a high-energy phosphate bond (such as ATP).","2008 EC entrance"],["Which group of organic compound includes the enzymes?",["Lipids","Starches","Carbohydrates","Proteins"],3,"Enzymes are biological catalysts that are almost exclusively globular proteins.","2006 EC entrance"],["Into which of the following organic compound can lipase maltase and sucrase be grouped?",["Nucleic acids","Enzymes","Hormones","Carbohydrates"],1,"Lipase, maltase, and sucrase are all enzymes, typically recognizable by the suffix '-ase', that catalyze the breakdown of lipids, maltose, and sucrose, respectively. (1)","2006 EC entrance"],["From evolutionary point of view, which of the following animals is expected to have haemoglobin proteins that\nare least similar to that of human?",["Cow","Ape","Frog","Chicken"],2,"Frogs are amphibians, which diverged earliest from the evolutionary lineage leading to mammals, meaning their hemoglobin sequence has accumulated the most differences compared to humans.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following processes in the phosphate cycle DOES NOT return phosphate ions to the soil?",["Decomposition of dead animals","Weathering of rocks","Use of fertilizers","Cellular respiration"],3,"Cellular respiration is a process that releases carbon dioxide and water into the environment, playing a key role in the carbon and water cycles. It does not release or return phosphate ions to the soil, unlike weathering, fertilizer use, and decomposition.","2013 EC entrance"],["Among the following scientists who contributed to the cell theory, identify the one who stated that a cell can\narise only from another cell like it.",["Rudolf virchow","Theodor Schwann","Robert Hooke","Matthias Schleiden"],0,"Rudolf Virchow added the third tenet to the cell theory with his principle 'Omnis cellula e cellula', stating that cells arise only from pre-existing cells.","2007 EC entrance"],["What is the best term that expresses the movement of substances in cells against their concentration gradient?",["Passive transport","Water","Active transport","Osmosis"],2,"Active transport moves molecules or ions across a cell membrane against their concentration gradient using energy, typically in the form of ATP.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which part of the digestive system is responsible for producing enzymes that digest carbohydrates, proteins,\nand fats?",["Stomach","Liver","Pancreas","Small intestine"],3,"Pancreatic juice is the one secretion that carries all three enzyme classes at once: amylase for starch, trypsin and other proteases for protein, and lipase for fat. It empties into the duodenum through the pancreatic duct. The small intestine tempts because its lining does make enzymes such as maltase and peptidases, but those finish the job on small molecules rather than supply the full set.","2018 EC entrance"],["Glycolysis occurs in the",["Cytoplasm","Chloroplast","Nucleus","Mitochondrion"],0,"Glycolysis takes place entirely within the cytoplasm (cytosol) of the cell and does not require membrane-bound organelles like mitochondria.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following importance of water is directly related with its ideal viscosity?",["Habitat for aquatic animals","Reactant in photosynthesis","Reaction medium","Transport medium"],3,"Water has a relatively low viscosity, allowing it to flow easily through narrow tubes like blood vessels and xylem, making it an ideal transport medium.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following molecules can serve as a raw material for industries that produce glucose?",["Nucleic acids","Proteins","Lipids","Starch"],3,"Starch is a polysaccharide composed of glucose monomers; industrial hydrolysis of starch yields glucose syrups.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following resources is needed by an ecosystem from outside in order to sustain itself",["Producers","Sunlight","Micronutrients","Macronutrients"],1,"Unlike chemical nutrients, which cycle within ecosystems, energy cannot be recycled and must continuously enter the ecosystem from an external source, most commonly sunlight.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following stage of photosynthesis can take place in the dark?",["Photolysis of water","Photosystem I","Calvin cycle","Photosystem II"],2,"The Calvin cycle represents the light-independent reactions of photosynthesis, utilizing ATP and NADPH to fix carbon dioxide without the direct requirement of light.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which group of archaebacterial are called salt loving bacteria?",["Halophiles","Thermophiles","Methanogens","Acidophilus"],0,"Halophiles are specialized extremophilic archaebacteria that thrive in environments with very high salt concentrations.","2016 EC entrance"],["Ammonium compounds are oxidized to nitrate by",["ammonifying bacteria","denitrifying bacteria","nitrogen fixing bacteria","nitrifying bacteria"],3,"Nitrifying bacteria, such as Nitrosomonas and Nitrobacter, oxidize ammonia and ammonium compounds first to nitrites and then to nitrates during the nitrogen cycle.","2016 EC entrance"],["What does an evolutionary selective pressure that acts around the mean do?",["It converges","It disrupts","It stabilizes","It terminates"],2,"Natural selection that acts to favor the average phenotype and selects against extremes is known as stabilizing selection, so it stabilizes the population around the mean.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which two groups of organisms does the fossil animal known as Archeopteryx link?",["Reptiles and birds","Mammals and reptiles","Amphibians and fishes","Reptiles and amphibians"],0,"Archaeopteryx is a famous transitional fossil displaying a mix of reptilian features (such as teeth and a long bony tail) and avian features (such as feathers and wings), linking reptiles and birds.","1996 EC entrance"],["From the following alternatives select the common features that are found both in animal and plant cells.",["Cell membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, chloroplast and Golgi apparatus","Cell membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, lysosome and Golgi apparatus","Cell membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, large vacuole and Golgi apparatus","Cell membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, mitochondria and endoplasmic reticulum"],3,"Animal and plant cells are both eukaryotic, so they share the cell membrane, nucleus, cytoplasm, mitochondria and endoplasmic reticulum. The wrong options each smuggle in a structure that belongs to only one cell type: chloroplasts and the single large vacuole are found in plant cells, while lysosomes are typical of animal cells.","2017 EC entrance"],["In which of the following are flowers and fruits found?",["monocots and dicots","Ferns and relative","Gymnosperms and ferns","Mosses and conifers"],0,"Flowers and fruits are the defining features of the angiosperms, the flowering plants, and monocots and dicots are the two groups the angiosperms are divided into. The flower is the reproductive structure and the fruit is the ripened ovary that protects and spreads the seeds. Gymnosperms are the tempting answer because they also make seeds, but their seeds sit exposed on the scales of a cone, with no true flower and no fruit around them.","2005 EC entrance"],["If your body cannot make enough red blood cells, which one of the following mineral rich foods can correct this\nproblem?",["Sodium-rich food","Calcium-rich food","Iron-rich food","Iodine-rich food"],2,"Red blood cells carry oxygen using haemoglobin, and iron is the mineral at the centre of every haemoglobin molecule. When the body lacks iron it cannot make enough healthy red blood cells, a condition called anaemia, so iron rich foods correct the problem. Iodine is needed by the thyroid gland, calcium builds bones and teeth, and sodium balances body fluids; none of them builds red blood cells.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is different from the rest with regard to conservation of vegetation?",["Replanting of land with endemic species","Large scale introduction of exotic plants","Replanting indigenous tree species","Using local practices for conservation"],1,"The large-scale introduction of exotic plants often threatens native biodiversity and ecosystems, unlike the other options which promote the conservation of native and endemic vegetation.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following tools is used by a biologist to study the internal anatomy of experimental animals?",["Dissecting kit","Microscope","Hand lens","Petri dish"],0,"A dissecting kit contains instruments such as scalpels, scissors, and forceps, which are essential for opening and exposing the internal anatomical structures of experimental animals.","2010 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following events is an example of a sex influenced trait?",["Pattern baldness","Ritinitis pigmentosa","Lactation","Undescended testicles"],0,"Pattern baldness is a classic sex-influenced trait because its expression is dependent on hormone levels; the allele acts as a dominant trait in males but as a recessive trait in females.","2015 EC entrance"],["If organisms share very similar molecules such as DNA, then they must be closely related evolutionarily. Which\nevidence of evolution supports the above information?",["Comparative physiology","Comparative biochemistry","Comparative anatomy","Comparative embryology"],1,"Comparing molecular structures, such as DNA, RNA, and proteins, to determine evolutionary relationships among different organisms falls under the field of comparative biochemistry.","2013 EC entrance"],["A plant cell is placed in a solution which has lower solute concentration than its contents. After a few minutes\nthe cell will become",["plasmolysed.","burst.","turgid.","flaccid."],2,"When a plant cell is placed in a hypotonic solution (lower solute concentration than the cell contents), water enters the cell by osmosis, causing the vacuole to swell and push against the rigid cell wall, making the cell turgid.","2015 EC entrance"],["In which organ of the human body are more bacteria found?",["Large intestine","Lungs","Stomach","Small intestine"],0,"The human large intestine (colon) harbors the highest concentration and absolute number of bacteria of any organ in the body, forming the gut microbiota.","2010 EC entrance"],["In Gram staining, if some bacteria retain the crystal violet after counter staining, then the bacteria is",["Gram intermediate.","Gram negative.","Gram positive.","Gram variable."],2,"Gram-positive bacteria have a thick peptidoglycan cell wall that successfully retains the crystal violet-iodine complex, even after alcohol decolorization and counterstaining, appearing purple.","2015 EC entrance"],["Bacteria can cause diseases in all of the following mechanisms EXCEPT",["releasing toxins as they multiply.","entering living cells and disrupting metabolic systems.","invading and growing on the tissues of organs.","changing the genetic structure of host cells."],3,"Changing the genetic structure of host cells is characteristic of viruses (like retroviruses), whereas bacteria cause disease by tissue invasion and releasing toxins, not by altering host DNA.","2013 EC entrance"],["Among the following, which one had the cranial capacity of about the same size as that Of Homo sapiens?",["Homo habilis","Homo erectus","Lucy","The Neanderthal man"],3,"The Neanderthal man had a cranial capacity of approximately 1400 to 1600 cc, which is highly comparable to, and sometimes slightly larger than, that of modern Homo sapiens (averaging ~1350-1400 cc).","2011 EC entrance"],["All are correct about genetic fingerprinting except:",["It is unique to individuals except identical twins","It is based on RNA analysis","It is made by gel electrophoresis in the PCR machine","It is used for crime investigation"],1,"Genetic fingerprinting compares DNA. Repeated sequences that vary from person to person are copied by PCR, cut, and separated by gel electrophoresis into a banding pattern that is unique except in identical twins. So the statement that it is based on RNA analysis is the false one. Option C is tempting because its wording is loose, but PCR and gel electrophoresis really are the tools used.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which groups of lipids are bipolar due to the presence of hydrophilic and hydrophobic regions?",["Waxes","Steroids","Phospholipids","Triglycerides"],2,"Phospholipids are amphipathic (bipolar) molecules consisting of a hydrophilic (polar) phosphate head and two hydrophobic (non-polar) fatty acid tails.","2016 EC entrance"],["If one base in the six triplets of the gene coding for one of the four polypeptides in the haemoglobin molecule\nalters the triplet from GAG to GTG, which one of the following biological terms best describes the above\nphenomenon?",["Cloning","Transcription","Translation","Mutation"],3,"A change in a single base pair of a DNA sequence (such as GAG to GTG in the beta-globin gene, which causes sickle-cell anemia) is defined as a point mutation.","2013 EC entrance"],["If a sample fruit juice and some drops of Benedict’s solution obtain a brick – red precipitate up on warming the\nmixture, what does the juice contain?",["Reducing sugar","Sucrose","Starch","Protein"],0,"Benedict's solution is a chemical reagent used to detect the presence of reducing sugars; a change to a brick-red precipitate upon heating indicates a high concentration of reducing sugars.","2016 EC entrance"],["Aggregation of a large number of penguins staying close to each other to conserve heat can be an example of a",["mating behavior","social behavior","courtship behavior","defense behavior"],1,"The cooperative huddling of penguins to conserve heat is a group interaction that enhances survival, which is a classic example of social behavior.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following bacteria produces ammonium ion by forming a symbiotic association with peas and\nbeans?",["Klebsiella","Azotobacter","Rhizobium","Psuedomonas"],2,"Rhizobium is a symbiotic, nitrogen-fixing bacterium that inhabits the root nodules of legumes (such as peas and beans) and converts atmospheric nitrogen into ammonium ions.","2015 EC entrance"],["This item is based on the following course of human evolution.\n1.Use of fire and other tools\n2.Increase in brain size\n3.Emergence of Homo sapiens\n4.Bipedal walking and arboreal life\nWhich of the following is the correct order of the above evolutionary time line markers?",["4, 2, 1, 3","3, 2, 4, 1","2, 1, 3, 4","1, 3, 4, 2"],0,"Walking upright on two legs (bipedalism) appeared first in human evolution, in early ancestors that were leaving arboreal (tree) life. Brain size then increased gradually over millions of years. With bigger brains, species such as Homo erectus began using fire and better tools. The emergence of our own species, Homo sapiens, came last. So the timeline is 4, 2, 1, 3.","2017 EC entrance"],["The allele for baldness is found on somatic chromosomes. But it is more expressed in males than females.\nConsequently, it is taken as",["sex-linked","sex-restricted","sex-limited","sex-influenced"],3,"Sex-influenced traits are determined by autosomal genes but are expressed differently in males and females due to hormonal differences, such as male pattern baldness being dominant in males but recessive in females.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the ultimate source of renege for all organism living on the earth?",["Oxygen","Nitrogen","Water","The sun"],3,"The sun is the ultimate source of energy for life on Earth, captured by autotrophs via photosynthesis and passed through food webs.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which genus of bacteria oxidize hydrogen sulphide to sulphate and make sulphate ions available to be taken by\nplant roots from the soil?",["Desulfovibrio","Thiobacillus","Azotobacter","Klebsiella"],1,"Thiobacillus species are chemolithotrophic bacteria that obtain energy by oxidizing sulfur and hydrogen sulfide into sulfate, making it available for uptake by plant roots.","2014 EC entrance"],["This item is based on the following choices of feeding habit employed by organisms.\nI. Using nutrients dissolved in the surrounding medium\nII. Manufacturing own nutrients by photosynthesis\nIII. Depending on other plants or animals for food\nWhich method/s the protozoan used to get their nutrition? They employed",["I only.","II and III only","I and II only.","I, II and III."],3,"Protozoa as a group use all three feeding methods. Saprozoic protozoa absorb nutrients dissolved in the water around them (I). Plant like protozoa such as Euglena carry chloroplasts and make food by photosynthesis (II). Holozoic and parasitic protozoa, such as Amoeba and Plasmodium, feed on other organisms (III). Because different members use different methods, the full answer is I, II and III.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following chromosomal errors creates a cell with an extra chromosome?",["Deletion","Non-disjunction","Duplication","Inversion"],1,"Non-disjunction is the failure of homologous chromosomes or sister chromatids to separate properly during cell division, resulting in daughter cells with an abnormal number of chromosomes (such as an extra chromosome).","2011 EC entrance"],["What triggers fermentation during exercise?",["Over activity of respiratory enzymes","Presence of excess glucose","Shortage of oxygen","Production of ATP beyond the cells demand"],2,"During strenuous exercise, oxygen supply to muscle tissues cannot keep up with the high demand, leading to a shortage of oxygen and triggering lactic acid fermentation to regenerate NAD+ and sustain glycolysis.","2014 EC entrance"],["The most complex structure of proteins is called",["Primary structure","Quaternary structure","Tertiary structure","Secondary structure"],1,"Quaternary structure is the highest and most complex level of protein organization, formed when two or more polypeptide chains interact to form a functional multimeric protein.","2007 EC entrance"],["In all the following condition diffusion is faster except;",["With higher concentration difference","At high temperature","For smaller molecules","Over long distance"],3,"The rate of diffusion is inversely proportional to the distance; thus, diffusion is extremely slow over long distances, which is why multicellular organisms require circulatory systems.","2016 EC entrance"],["Regarding human evolution, which hominid was unable to run faster and had small brain size as compared to\nthe others?",["Homo habilis","Home neanderthalensis","Homo sapiens","Home erectus"],0,"Homo habilis is the earliest and most primitive species of the genus Homo listed; it possessed a significantly smaller brain size (around 600-700 cc) and lacked the anatomical adaptations for endurance running found in Homo erectus.","2016 EC entrance"],["An organic molecule which is an important part of structure of chromosome is",["amylose.","amino acid.","triglyceride.","glycogen."],1,"Chromosomes are made of DNA coiled around histone proteins. Proteins are polymers composed of amino acid monomers, making amino acids a vital structural component of chromosomes.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which type of animal behavior happens with out learning?",["Insight","Conditioned","Latent","Innate"],3,"Innate behavior is genetically programmed and inherited, allowing an animal to perform it correctly the first time without prior experience or learning.","2009 EC entrance"],["The molecule of which pigment is located at the reaction center of a photosystem?",["Carotenoid","Chlorophyll a","Chlorophyll b","Accessory pigments"],1,"The reaction center of a photosystem contains a specialized pair of chlorophyll a molecules that donate energized electrons to the primary electron acceptor.","2006 EC entrance"],["Both photosynthesis and respiration are involved in:",["Phosphorous Cycle","Nitrogen Cycle","Water Cycle","Carbon Cycle"],3,"Photosynthesis removes carbon dioxide from the atmosphere to make organic compounds, while respiration breaks these compounds down to release carbon dioxide back, making both vital to the carbon cycle.","2011 EC entrance"],["The behavior which trainers look, if modified, could lead to the desired behavior and reward such a behavior is",["instinct.","reflex.","innate.","operant."],3,"An operant is a behavior that is actively emitted by an organism and operates on the environment; in training, operant behaviors are reinforced with rewards to shape the desired outcome.","2013 EC entrance"],["Which process produced mRNA during protein synthesis?",["Replication","Translation","Transcription","Mutation"],2,"Transcription is the process by which a specific segment of DNA is copied into messenger RNA (mRNA) by RNA polymerase.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following organelles settles out last when homogenized cells are centrifuged?",["Nucleus","Ribosome","Mitochondria","Chloroplast"],1,"In differential centrifugation, the largest and densest components (nuclei) pellet first at low speeds, while the smallest components like ribosomes require the highest speeds and pellet last.","2010 EC entrance"],["The evolution of species which is based upon the sum total adaptation changes could be preserved by:",["Speciation","Human conservation","Isolation","Natural selection"],3,"Natural selection acts to preserve favorable adaptive variations in a population across generations while weeding out disadvantageous traits.","2010 EC entrance"],["In an experiment to study photosynthesis, a plant was provided with radioactive carbon dioxide as a metabolic\ntracer and the radioactive carbon was incorporated first into oxaloacetate. Which one of the following would\nbest characterize this plant?",["C3 plant","C4 plant","CAM plant","Heterotrophic plant"],1,"C4 plants use the enzyme PEP carboxylase to initially fix carbon dioxide into a 4-carbon compound, oxaloacetate, in the mesophyll cells.","2011 EC entrance"],["How many fatty acids would a cell need to form a molecule of triglyceride",["Two","Five","Four","Three"],3,"A triglyceride (triacylglycerol) is synthesized by esterifying three fatty acid chains to a single molecule of glycerol.","2008 EC entrance"],["A chimpanzee concentrates to reach at a bunch of grapes hanging above its head. What kind of behavior is this?",["Associative learning","Sensitization learning","Insight learning","Latent learning"],2,"Insight learning involves solving a problem rapidly by understanding the relationships between various parts of the problem without trial-and-error, as famously demonstrated by primates solving tasks to reach food.","1996 EC entrance"],["Consider the following chemical reaction below. RH2 + A E R + AH2 Based on the above chemical\nreaction, in which classes of enzymes can enzyme \"E\" be grouped?\n​",["Transferases","Oxidoreductases","Isomerases ​","Hydrolyases"],1,"The chemical equation depicts a redox (oxidation-reduction) reaction in which hydrogen is transferred, which is catalyzed by enzymes belonging to the class oxidoreductases.","2013 EC entrance"],["Some amino acids are synthesized using transamination process in the cell. This activity more describes the\ncell's",["energy production.","anabolism.","replication.","catabolism."],1,"Anabolism refers to metabolic pathways that construct molecules from smaller units, requiring energy; the biosynthesis of amino acids through transamination is an anabolic process.","2013 EC entrance"],["The total amount of living tissue within a given trophic level is called:",["Biomass","Energy mass","Trophic mass","Organic mass"],0,"Biomass is defined as the total mass of living organic matter within a specific trophic level or given ecosystem.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following groups of viruses copy their RNA to DNA?",["Retroviruses","Bacteriphages","RNA viruses","DNA viruses"],0,"Retroviruses possess an RNA genome and use the enzyme reverse transcriptase to transcribe their RNA into DNA inside the host cell.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following laboratory glassware is used for culturing bacteria?",["Petri-dish","Filter paper","Measuring cylinder","Test tube"],0,"A Petri dish containing nutrient agar is the standard laboratory equipment used for culturing microorganisms such as bacteria and fungi.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is NOT the correct characteristics of tropical rainforests?",["trees of different heights","Low biodiversity","High temperature","Heavy precipitation"],1,"Tropical rainforests are recognized as having the highest terrestrial biodiversity on Earth, so possessing low biodiversity is incorrect.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is an example of anthropogenic driving factor that contributes to species extinction?",["Outbreak of wild-fire","Expansions of agriculture","Volcanic eruption","Earth quake"],2,"Anthropogenic means caused by human beings. Expanding farmland is a human activity that clears forests and grasslands, destroying the habitats that species need, so it is an anthropogenic driver of extinction. Earthquakes, volcanic eruptions and natural wildfires happen without human action, so they are natural drivers.","2017 EC entrance"],["For a biological detergent to effectively remove oily and greasy dirt, which of the following enzymes should it\ncontain?",["Lipase","Protease","Cellulase","Amylase"],0,"Lipases are enzymes that catalyze the hydrolysis of fats and oils (lipids), making them ideal for removing greasy stains in biological detergents.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is not practice that affects reproductive health?",["Early marriage","Gender-based violence","Kidnapping or abduction","Spacing and timing of births"],0,"The question asks which practice does not damage reproductive health. Planning the gap between births lets the mother recover and improves the health of both mother and child, so it protects health rather than harming it. Early marriage is the tempting distractor because it is common, but it exposes a girl to pregnancy before her body is ready and raises the risk of obstructed labour and fistula.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which organic molecules are formed when two fatty acid molecules are bounded to the glycerol and the place\nof the third is taken by a phosphate group?",["Triglycerides","Phospholipids","Glycolipids","Waxes"],1,"Phospholipids are lipids containing a glycerol backbone bound to two fatty acids and a phosphate group, forming a hydrophilic head and hydrophobic tails.","2013 EC entrance"],["All of the following features define a chromosome EXCEPT",["made up of DNA and protein.","exists in pairs in diploid organisms.","functional unit of inheritance.","contains hundreds to thousands of genes."],2,"The functional unit of inheritance is the gene, not the chromosome. A chromosome is a much larger structure made of DNA wound around proteins, it carries hundreds to thousands of genes, and in diploid organisms chromosomes come in homologous pairs. So statements A, B and C describe a chromosome, while D describes a gene.","2017 EC entrance"],["When two species are compared ,which of the following sources of evidence is least informative about the\ndegree of relationships between the species?",["DNA-DNA hybridization","Amino acid sequence of proteins","Gluscose sequence of polysaccharides","Nucleotide sequence of DNAs"],1,"A polysaccharide such as starch or cellulose is the same sugar, glucose, repeated over and over. Because the units do not vary, there is no sequence to compare between two species, so the molecule carries almost no information about how closely they are related. The amino acid sequence of proteins is the tempting answer because it is also a comparison of building blocks, but there are twenty different amino acids, so their order differs between species and the number of differences measures how far apart the species are.","2005 EC entrance"],["Organelles in the cytoplasm that are known as 'power house' of the cell are:",["ribosome","cellulose","chloroplast","mitochondria"],3,"Mitochondria are known as the powerhouses of the cell because they generate most of the cell's supply of adenosine triphosphate (ATP) through aerobic respiration.","2011 EC entrance"],["Currently, natural resources are being depleted at increasing rate and waste materials are accumulated and\ndischarged freely into water bodies. What is the best strategy to overcome these problems?",["Decomposition","Fossilization","Recycling","Succession"],2,"Recycling reduces the demand for raw natural resource extraction and diverts waste materials from landfill and water body dumping back into productive use.","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the method of conservation in which animals are kept in captivity and plants are grown in botanical\ngardens?",["Complementary in-situ and ex-situ conservation","Zoo conservation","Ex-situ conservation","In-situ conservation"],2,"Ex-situ conservation refers to the preservation of components of biological diversity outside their natural habitats, such as in zoos, botanical gardens, and seed banks.","1996 EC entrance"],["Which filed studies the way in which individual traits of organisms are transmitted from one generation to the\nnext?",["Genetics","Evolution","Ecology","Morphology"],0,"Genetics is the branch of biology that deals with heredity, specifically how traits are passed down from parents to offspring across generations. (1)","2006 EC entrance"],["What is the main function of the cell membrane? It controls",["reproduction of cells.","transport of molecules.","synthesis of lipids.","protein synthesis."],1,"The cell membrane is selectively permeable, so its primary function is to control the transport of molecules into and out of the cell. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Suppose a hypothetical cube- shaped cell has sides of 10 micrometers, what is the surface area to volume ratio\nof this cell?",["6:10","10:10","3:6","4:8"],0,"For a cube of side s = 10 μm, the total surface area is 6 × s^2 = 600 μm^2 and the volume is s^3 = 1000 μm^3. The ratio of surface area to volume is 600:1000, which simplifies to 6:10.","2006 EC entrance"],["A biologist is organizing a museum exhibit and wants to categorize four research scientists based on the\nspecific groups of organisms they study. Scientist A: Studies the structure, function of animals. Scientist B:\nFocuses on the scientific study of plants, their physiology and genetics. Scientist C: Investigates the complex\nworld of insects. Based on these descriptions, Scientists A, B, C can be classified under which biology subfields, respectively?",["Zoology, Entomology, Ornithology","Entomology, Zoology, Botany","Zoology, Botany, Entomology","Botany, Zoology, Entomology"],2,"The sub-fields are named after what they study. Zoology is the study of animals, botany is the study of plants, and entomology is the study of insects. Scientist A studies animals, B studies plants and C studies insects, so the order is zoology, botany, entomology. Option B is tempting because it holds the same three words, but it puts botany with the animal researcher and zoology with the plant researcher.","2018 EC entrance"],["The process in which individuals with a particular heritable trait survive better than the other is",["adaptation.","natural selection,","evolution.","selective breeding."],1,"Natural selection is the process by which individuals with favorable, heritable traits are more likely to survive and reproduce, passing those advantageous traits on to the next generation.","2013 EC entrance"],["Who conducted the famous experiment in 1953 that simulated early Earth conditions to test the origins of life?",["Charles Darwin","Stanley Miller","Louis Pasteur","Alexander Oparin"],1,"In 1953 Stanley Miller, working with Harold Urey, sealed methane, ammonia, hydrogen and water vapour in glassware and passed electric sparks through the mixture to imitate lightning on the early Earth. Amino acids appeared within days, which showed that the building blocks of life can form from simple gases with no living thing involved. Option B is the closest trap, because Oparin proposed the chemical origin hypothesis in the 1920s, but he did not run this experiment.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following behavioral biologists is known for his study about imprinting behavior in animals?",["Konrad Lorenz","Ivan pavlov","B.F.Skinner","W. Kohler"],0,"Konrad Lorenz is renowned for his ethological studies demonstrating imprinting behavior in newly hatched greylag geese.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following structures is NOT present in animal cells?",["Cell wall","Protoplasm","Nucleus","Nucleic acid"],0,"Animal cells are surrounded only by a flexible plasma membrane and lack a rigid cell wall, which is characteristic of plants, fungi, and bacteria.","2006 EC entrance"],["\"Skinner box\" is used for experiments in:",["taxis","classical conditioning","migration","operant conditioning"],3,"The Skinner box, or operant conditioning chamber, is used to study animal behavior by training them to perform actions (like pressing a lever) in response to rewards or punishments.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which molecule in the cell is the constituent of the gene?",["Protein","Lipid","Carbohydrate","Nucleic acid"],3,"Genes are specific functional segments of DNA (deoxyribonucleic acid), which is a type of nucleic acid.","2006 EC entrance"],["The organelle of the cell which is concerned with the synthesis of lipids in addition to being associated with\ncarbohydrate metabolism and detoxification is:",["Rough endoplasmic reticulum","Thylakoid membrane","Smooth endoplasmic reticulum","Golgi body/apparatus"],2,"The smooth endoplasmic reticulum (SER) is specialized for lipid and steroid synthesis, carbohydrate metabolism, calcium storage, and the detoxification of drugs and poisons.","2010 EC entrance"],["Ethiopian Biological research center which is involved in mechanized farming is:",["EIAR","ALIPB","AHRI","IBC"],0,"EIAR is the Ethiopian Institute of Agricultural Research. It works on crops, livestock, soils and farm machinery, which is why mechanized farming falls under it. IBC is the tempting answer because it also deals with plants, but its job is conserving genetic resources and ecosystems, not farm technology.","2017 EC entrance"],["If a phagocytic white blood cell is unable to digest bacteria that have been engulfed, which organelles could be\nfailed to do this function?",["Endoplasmic reticulum","Ribosomes","Lysosomes","Golgi body"],2,"Lysosomes contain hydrolytic enzymes that fuse with phagosomes to digest engulfed pathogens; if lysosomes fail to function, the phagocytic cell cannot digest the bacteria.","2016 EC entrance"],["In which area of enzyme application is invertase injected to sucrose paste in order to produce liquid chocolates?",["Food processing industry","Pharmaceutical industry","Detergent making industry","pulp and paper industry"],0,"Invertase hydrolyzes sucrose into glucose and fructose, creating a soft or liquid centre in chocolates, which is a major application in the food processing industry. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["If radioactive substance that weighs one kilogram has a half-life of 100 years what would be the percentage of\nthe substance left after 300 years?",["25","50","12.5","30"],2,"With a half-life of 100 years, 300 years corresponds to 3 half-lives. The remaining fraction is (1/2)^3 = 1/8, which equals 12.5% of the original substance.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following protozoan disease causes blindness, mental retardation & multi system organ familiarity?",["Toxoplasmosis","Leishmaniasis","Trypanosomes","Malaria"],0,"Toxoplasmosis, caused by the protozoan parasite Toxoplasma gondii, can cause congenital infections leading to severe issues like blindness, mental retardation, and systemic organ damage.","2016 EC entrance"],["Mutations become more serious and threatening if they occur on genes that regulate",["fatty acid metabolism","cell division","lactose metabolism","hair growth"],1,"Mutations in genes that regulate cell division (such as proto-oncogenes and tumor suppressor genes) can lead to uncontrolled cell division and cancer, making them highly life-threatening.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is a key threat of biodiversity in Ethiopia?",["Large scale reforestation attempt","Climate change and desertification","Abundant protected areas","Strict conservation policies"],1,"Climate change and desertification present major environmental challenges and significant threats to the rich biodiversity of Ethiopia.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which class of HIV anti-retroviral drugs binds to T-cells in order to inhibit joining of the virus with its receptor?",["Non-nucleotide reverse transcriptase inhibitors","Nucleotide reverse transcriptase inhibitors","Entry inhibitors","Protease inhibitors"],2,"Entry inhibitors (such as CCR5 antagonists) block HIV from entering host T-cells by binding to receptors on the T-cell surface, thereby preventing the viral envelope from attaching to its target.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is an ecosystem",["The African continent","The non-living components of an environment","All the organisms in a given area","A Tropical Rain forest"],3,"An ecosystem is all the living things in an area together with the non living surroundings they depend on, and the flow of energy and nutrients between the two. A tropical rain forest fits this: it has its plants and animals plus the soil, water, air and sunlight they live in. Option C is the tempting answer, but all the organisms in an area with the physical surroundings left out is a community, which is only one half of an ecosystem.","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following external factors influence the turnover rate of enzymes by completely damaging their\ntertiary structure?",["Competitive inhibitors","Reversible inhibitors","Temperature and pH","Substrate concentration"],2,"Extremes in temperature and pH cause the denaturation of enzymes by disrupting the non-covalent bonds (such as hydrogen and ionic bonds) that maintain their tertiary structure, permanently destroying their activity.","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the processes called when two bacteria directly contact cell to cell and exchange their genetic\ninformation?",["transduction","Conjugation","Co-transformation","Transformation"],1,"Bacterial conjugation involves direct cell-to-cell contact through a sex pilus to transfer genetic material (such as a plasmid) from a donor to a recipient bacterium.","2007 EC entrance"],["To which of the following groups do those bacterio phages that integrate their DNA in to the chromosome of\ntheir bacterial host belong?",["Non-parasitic viruses","Lysogenic viruses","Lytic viruses","Virulent viruses"],2,"A lysogenic phage does not destroy its host at once. It inserts its DNA into the bacterial chromosome as a prophage, which is then copied along with the host DNA every time the bacterium divides, and only later may it leave and start destroying cells. Lytic viruses are the tempting answer because they are the other half of the same story, but a lytic phage copies itself straight away and bursts the cell without ever joining the host chromosome. (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["The structure of specimens can be studied after they are freshly collected using a",["theodolite","field microscope","data logger","flow meter"],1,"A field microscope is a portable microscope designed for use outdoors, allowing biologists to examine the microscopic structure of freshly collected specimens directly at the field site.","2016 EC entrance"],["If a homogenate of eukaryotic cells is spun in a centrifuge, which of the cellular organelles settles out first?",["Chloroplast","Mitochondria","Nucleus","Ribosome"],2,"The nucleus is the largest and densest organelle in eukaryotic cells; therefore, it precipitates out first at the lowest centrifugal speeds during differential centrifugation. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["One of the following renowned Ethiopian biologists has developed a vaccine for the rinderpest disease.",["Professor Beyene Petros","Professor Yalemtsehay Mekonnen","Professor Sebsebe Demissew","Professor Tilahun Yilma"],3,"Professor Tilahun Yilma is a highly distinguished Ethiopian virologist who successfully developed a recombinant vaccine against rinderpest, a devastating viral disease of cattle.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which theory proposes the origin of life to be from resistant spores landing on Earth from outer space?",["Spontaneous generation","Eternity of life","Cosmozoan","Biochemical"],2,"The Cosmozoan theory (also known as the Panspermia theory) proposes that life on Earth originated from resistant spores or microorganisms that arrived from outer space.","2016 EC entrance"],["Suppose sites A,B,C and D have Simpson's Index of Diversity (d) values of 20,8,16,and 3, respectively, which site\nis dominated by one or just a few species?",["Site D","Site A","Site B","Site C"],0,"In Simpson's reciprocal index of diversity, higher values indicate high species richness and evenness, whereas low values (the minimum being 1) indicate a community dominated by only one or a few species; Site D has the lowest index (3).","2006 EC entrance"],["The word science comes from the Latin word 'Scientia' meaning what ?",["Study","Experiment","Knowledge","Life"],2,"The word science is derived from the Latin noun 'scientia', which means 'knowledge'.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is classified as a mechanical measure of soil and water conservation?",["The Green Legacy initiative","Planting tree seedlings on farmlands","Constructing check dams and terraces","Enclosing degraded land from animals"],0,"Mechanical, or physical, conservation measures are structures that are built on the land to slow water down and hold soil in place. Check dams across gullies and terraces across a slope both do that, so they are mechanical measures. Planting tree seedlings is the tempting answer because it also protects soil, but living cover is a biological measure, and the Green Legacy initiative and area enclosure fall in the same biological group.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is correct if a molecule is transported across the plasma membrane using active\ntransport involving a carrier protein? The molecule is",["non - charged","lipid soluble","polar","small size"],2,"Polar and charged molecules are hydrophilic and cannot easily pass through the hydrophobic lipid bilayer by simple diffusion; hence, they require carrier proteins for active transport against their concentration gradient. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following terms refers to the failure of sister chromatids to separate from one another during\nanaphase?",["Deletion","Non-disjunction","Double inversion","Replication"],1,"Non-disjunction is the failure of homologous chromosomes or sister chromatids to separate properly during cell division, leading to daughter cells with abnormal numbers of chromosomes.","2008 EC entrance"],["One of the following sources of evidence provides a more direct support to the process of Charles Darwin's\ntheory of evolution.",["Physiology","Genetics","Geographical distribution","Anatomy"],2,"The study of the geographical distribution of organisms (biogeography) was one of the most compelling and direct fields of evidence that led Charles Darwin to formulate his theory of evolution.","2011 EC entrance"],["Gardener brings an ornamental plant from other country and plant it in urban parks. This species through time\nmoved into conservation area and caused a loss for many other plant species. This is a loss of biodiversity due to",["invasive species.","overexploitation.","climate change.","deforestation."],0,"When a non-native species is introduced and outcompetes native species, it is classified as an invasive species, causing biodiversity loss.","2018 EC entrance"],["from among the following choice the field which is a branch or a part of biotechnology.",["parasitology","Genetic engineering","Immunology","Phycology"],1,"Genetic engineering is the core branch and tool of modern biotechnology, involving direct manipulation of an organism's genes.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following processes involved in the water cycle is carried out by green plants?",["Precipitation","Evaporation","Transpiration","Condensation"],2,"Transpiration is the process by which moisture is carried through plants from roots to small pores on leaves, where it changes to vapor and is released to the atmosphere.","2008 EC entrance"],["The amount of energy required to raise the temperature of one gram of water by one degree Celsius is",["cohesion force.","surface tension.","specific heat capacity.","latent heat of vaporization."],2,"Specific heat capacity is defined as the energy required to raise the temperature of 1 gram of a substance by 1°C. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["The scientific name of a house fly is:",["Felis domesticus","Canis familiaris","Zea mays","Musca domestica"],3,"The scientific binomial name of the common house fly is Musca domestica.","2016 EC entrance"],["In which industrial products is pyruvate fermentation by yeast practically applied?",["Swiss cheese making","Brewing beer","Production of vinegar","Yoghurt making"],1,"Brewing beer utilizes alcoholic fermentation by yeast (Saccharomyces cerevisiae) to convert sugars into ethanol and carbon dioxide.","2007 EC entrance"],["The terrestrial biome characterized by cold temperature, dry precipitation, frozen soil and inhabited by migrating\nbirds is",["boreal forests.","tropical montane forests.","tundra.","deserts"],2,"The tundra biome is characterized by very cold and dry conditions, permanently frozen soil (permafrost), and serves as a summer nesting ground for many migratory birds. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is adaptation mechanism of animal in cold climate?",["Active in the early morning","Blubber","More sweat","Large, thin ears"],1,"Blubber is a thick layer of fat under the skin. Fat conducts heat poorly, so it holds body heat inside the animal and keeps it warm in cold water or cold air. Large thin ears is the opposite adaptation. A wide, thin ear carries a lot of blood close to the air and loses heat, which suits a desert animal such as a fox, not a polar one.","2017 EC entrance"],["Grade 12 students went to a field and collected plant specimens for identification in the laboratory. They wanted\nto preserve the plant parts for some times and specimens can be analyzed later. Which one of the following\nbiological tool is used for their activities?",["Quadrat","Theodolite","Plant press","Pitfall traps"],2,"A plant press is a biological tool used to flatten, dry, and preserve plant specimens collected in the field for long-term laboratory identification and study. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Which of the following diseases is transmitted by mosquitoes?",["Kaposi's cancer","Rabies","Diabetes mellitus","Malaria"],3,"Malaria is a vector-borne infectious disease caused by Plasmodium parasites transmitted to humans via the bites of infected female Anopheles mosquitoes. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["At which stage of the population growth curve is the rate of natality and the rate of mortality expected to be\nequal?",["Lag phase","Log phase","Decline phase","Stationary phase"],3,"In the stationary phase of a population growth curve, the carrying capacity is reached, and the rate of natality (births) equals the rate of mortality (deaths), resulting in a stable population size.","2014 EC entrance"],["78. Which of the following involve extracting and obtaining energy from their environment by enzyme mediated\nchemical reaction?",["living things","Soil","Water","Sunlight"],0,"Metabolism, which involves extracting and obtaining energy from the environment through enzyme-mediated chemical reactions, is a defining characteristic of all living things.","2016 EC entrance"],["Consider the following reaction: Reactant A + Reactant B → Enzyme → Intermediate → Product AB + Enzyme? At \nwhich point are the chemical bonds weakened?",["intermediate","reactant A","reactant B","product AB"],0,"During an enzyme-catalyzed reaction, the chemical bonds of the substrates are weakened and strained while in the intermediate enzyme-substrate complex, reducing the activation energy required for the reaction.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which physiological response helps conserve heat when the core body temperature drops?",["Vasodilation","Vasoconstriction","Sweating","Panting"],0,"When the core cools, the arterioles supplying the skin narrow. Less warm blood reaches the surface, so less heat is radiated away and the core is protected. Vasodilation is the tempting opposite: it widens those vessels, floods the skin with blood and increases heat loss, which is what the body does when it is too hot.","2018 EC entrance"],["Why do we get tired and fatigued during heavy exercise such as long distance running? It is due to",["high rate of aerobic respiration.","accumulation of lactic acid.","shortage of glucose. ​","accumulation of CO2 ."],1,"During intense exercise, oxygen supply to muscles is limited, causing them to undergo anaerobic respiration. This leads to the accumulation of lactic acid, which causes muscle fatigue and soreness.","2013 EC entrance"],["Which property of water is useful for life that it continues in relatively warm water underneath through the cold\nweather?",["High density in its solid form than its liquid form","High latent heat of vaporization","High specific heat capacity","High surface tension"],2,"High specific heat capacity allows water to resist rapid temperature changes, keeping the water underneath relatively warm and stable for aquatic life during cold weather. Option B is factually incorrect because solid water (ice) is actually less dense than liquid water, which is why it floats.","2013 EC entrance"],["From which of the following do scientists usually formulate a hypothesis?",["Observation","Experiment","Theory","Prediction"],0,"The scientific method typically starts with observations, from which scientists formulate a testable hypothesis to explain those observations.","1996 EC entrance"],["Which of the following enzymes has its optimum pH within low pH range?",["Pancreatic lipase","Salivary amylase","Catalase","Pepsin"],3,"Pepsin is an enzyme found in the stomach that functions best in a highly acidic environment, with an optimum pH of about 1.5 to 2.0.","1996 EC entrance"],["Which part of the human elementary canal contains digestive enzymes that function at acidic pH?",["Stomach","Small intestine","Mouth","Esophagus"],0,"The stomach secretes hydrochloric acid along with pepsinogen, creating an acidic environment (pH ~1.5–2) necessary for pepsin to digest proteins effectively. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["Which element is found in nucleic acids?",["Calcium","Magnesium","phosphorus","Iron"],2,"Nucleic acids (DNA and RNA) are composed of nucleotides, which contain a nitrogenous base, a pentose sugar, and a phosphate group containing phosphorus.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the basic characteristic of mutation? It is",["spontaneous.","planned.","expected.","regular."],0,"Mutations are primary sources of genetic variation and are characterized as spontaneous, random, and unpredictable changes in the genome.","2013 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following cellular forms did Robert Hooke observe under his crude microscope?",["Bacteria","Empty cell wall","Yeast","Protozoa"],1,"In 1665, Robert Hooke examined thin slices of non-living bottle cork and observed small, box-like compartments that were actually the empty cell walls of dead plant cells.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following parts of plant roots is harboring nitrogen fixing bacteria",["Root cap","Root hair","Root nodule","Root tip"],2,"Root nodules, found primarily on the roots of leguminous plants, house symbiotic nitrogen-fixing bacteria such as Rhizobium.","2006 EC entrance"],["Among the vertebrate found In ethiopia, which class has the highest percentage of endemic species?",["Amphibians","Mammals","Reptiles","Birds"],0,"Amphibians have the highest rate of endemism among Ethiopian vertebrates, with around 40–50% of known species being endemic to the country.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following laboratory tools is LEAST accurate to measure 1 ml of liquid?",["Measuring cylinder","Beaker","Pipette","Burett"],1,"Beakers have wide diameters and approximate graduations, making them the least accurate laboratory glassware for measuring small volumes such as 1 ml. (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following techniques is employed in the transfer of human insulin gene to bacteria inorder to\nproduce human insulin in the bacteria?",["Cross pollination technique","DNA finger printing technique","Recombinant DNA technique","Protoplast fusion technique"],2,"Recombinant DNA technique is used to splice the human insulin gene into bacterial plasmids, allowing the genetically modified bacteria to synthesize human insulin. (1)","1996 EC entrance"],["In the case of enzymatic chemical reactions, what do you call the substance that is acted up on by an enzyme?",["Vitamin","Substrate","Polypeptide","Coenzyme"],1,"The reactant or chemical substance upon which an enzyme acts and binds at its active site is called the substrate.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following cell types can be rich in lysosomes?",["Red blood cells","Nerve cells","Phagocytic cells","Muscle cells"],1,"Phagocytic white blood cells swallow bacteria and cell debris into a vesicle, and lysosomes then fuse with that vesicle and empty their digestive enzymes onto the contents. A cell that does this all day needs a large stock of lysosomes ready to use. Nerve cells are the tempting answer because they are large and busy, but their work is carrying electrical signals, so they have no reason to hold a store of digestive enzymes.","2005 EC entrance"],["Traditional fermentation products such as 'Tella' and 'Injera', and modern industrial products such as detergents\nand textiles generally would not have been possible without the use of",["metallic cofactors","organic acids","enzymes","inorganic catalysts"],2,"Both traditional fermentation (using yeasts and bacteria) and modern industrial processes like textile and detergent manufacturing rely on enzymes to catalyze chemical reactions.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the natural process that allows continuity of supply of nutrients to organisms in an ecosystem?",["Recycling","Respiration","Photosynthesis","Sedimentation"],0,"Nutrient recycling (biogeochemical cycling) ensures that essential elements like carbon, nitrogen, and phosphorus are continuously cycled through the ecosystem, maintaining a constant supply for living organisms.","2016 EC entrance"],["The evolutionary process that allows survival of well adapted and successfully reproducing individuals is called",["differentiation","natural selection","co-evolution","random selection"],1,"Natural selection is the evolutionary mechanism where individuals with favorable, heritable traits are more likely to survive, reproduce, and pass those adaptive traits to the next generation.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the result of the similarity observed between the wings of a bird and a\npterodactyl?",["Divergent evolution","Convergent evolution","Stabilizing selection","Directional selection"],1,"The wings of birds and pterodactyls are analogous structures that arose independently through convergent evolution to serve the function of flight.","2009 EC entrance"],["During alcohol fermentation pyruvic acid in the presence of pyruvate decarboxylase is first converted to .",["Glucose","Lactic acid","Acetaldehyde","Lactose"],2,"In alcoholic fermentation, pyruvate decarboxylase first removes a carboxyl group from pyruvic acid to form acetaldehyde and carbon dioxide, which is then reduced to ethanol.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which kind of enzyme inhibitors bind to enzyme only weakly and the bond that hold them breaks easily\nreleasing the inhibitor to allow the enzyme to become active again?",["Reversible inhibitor","Inhibitors that permanently alter enzyme structure","Inhibitors that bind strongly to enzymes","Irreversible inhibitors"],0,"Reversible inhibitors bind to enzymes through non-covalent, weak interactions that can readily dissociate, allowing the enzyme to regain activity.","2010 EC entrance"],["Which of the following mechanism moves digested amino acids and glucose across the plasma membrane of\nthe cell lining the wall of the small intestine?",["Osmosis","Active transport","Simple diffusion","Facilitated diffusion"],1,"Absorption of glucose and amino acids from the intestinal lumen into the epithelial cells occurs via active transport, primarily using sodium-dependent cotransporters.","2006 EC entrance"],["69. Which of the following absorb different wavelength of light?",["Minerals","Enzymes","Nutrients","Pigments"],3,"Photosynthetic pigments, such as chlorophyll a, chlorophyll b, and carotenoids, are specialized molecules that absorb specific wavelengths of light to drive the process of photosynthesis.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is NOT usually true as an ecological succession progresses to advanced seral stages ?",["Species become more diverse","The depth of the soil increase","Less population is supported","More ecological niches are formed"],2,"As succession advances the habitat gets richer, not poorer. Soil deepens, more kinds of plants and animals arrive, more niches open up and the amount of life the area can support goes up, so saying less population is supported is the statement that is not true. Deeper soil is the tempting answer if the question is read too fast, but soil building is exactly what the earlier stages do for the later ones, so that statement is true and is not what the question asks for.","2005 EC entrance"],["Homologus structures are evidence of evolution produced from:",["comparative anatomy","Paleontology","Comparative embryology","Comparative biochemstry"],0,"Homologous structures share a common evolutionary origin but have different functions, which is key evidence for evolution studied under comparative anatomy.","2016 EC entrance"],["74. In the calvin cycle which of the following compound is produced in C3 plants first?\n​",["Glucose -6-phosphate","Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate","Glucose, 1, 6 bisphosphate","Fructose 6 phosphate"],1,"In C3 plants, the first stable product of carbon fixation is 3-phosphoglycerate (PGA), which is subsequently reduced to Glyceraldehyde-3-phosphate (G3P) during the Calvin cycle. Since PGA is not listed, G3P represents the most immediate Calvin cycle product among the options. (1)","2016 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-chemistry","name":"Chemistry","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["Which of the following process involves preventing the growth of bacteria, fungi and reducing the oxidation of\nfats?",["Food preservation","Tanning","Contact","Haber-Bosch"],0,"Food preservation involves methods that inhibit microbial growth (bacteria, fungi) and retard the oxidation of fats to prevent spoilage and maintain food quality.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is used in the reaction called saponification?",["Nickel","Strong base","Strong acid","Hydrogen"],1,"Saponification is the alkaline hydrolysis of fats and oils using a strong base such as NaOH or KOH to produce soap and glycerol.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which substance is used to lower the melting point of aluminum oxide ore in the electrolytic extraction of\naluminum?",["Hematite","Magnetite","Bauxite","Cryolite"],3,"Cryolite (Na₃AlF₆) is added to alumina (Al₂O₃) to lower its melting point from about 2050°C to around 950°C, making the electrolytic extraction of aluminum energy-efficient.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following fertilizers supplies the highest percentage of nitrogen to plants?",["Monoammonium Phosphate (NH₄H₂PO₄)","Diammonium Phosphate (NH₄)₂HPO₄","Urea Ammonium Nitrate (CO(NH₂)₂ + NH₄NO₃)","Urea (CO(NH₂)₂)"],3,"Urea, CO(NH2)2, has a molar mass of 60 g/mol and contains 28 g/mol of nitrogen, translating to approximately 46.7% nitrogen, which is the highest among the choices.","2018 EC entrance"],["All of the following compounds contain ionic and covalent bonds except:",["NH3BF3","NH4Cl","CaCO3","Na3PO4"],2,"In N H4 Cl, CaCO3 and N a3 P O4 a polyatomic ion is held together inside by covalent bonds, and that ion is held to its partner ion by an ionic bond, so each has both bond types. In H3 N -BF3 the nitrogen donates its lone pair to boron, which is a dative covalent bond, and no ions are formed at all. A is tempting because ammonium looks like a molecule, but N H4+ and Cl− are separate ions. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["The shift in the position of equilibrium caused by the addition of an ion already involved in the reaction is known\nas _________.",["buffer-ion effect","titration-effect","hydrolysis-effect","common-ion effect"],3,"The common-ion effect is the reduction in solubility or shift in equilibrium when an ionic compound containing an ion already present in the solution is added.","2016 EC entrance"],["The species that being reduced and causes oxidation is a/an",["Reduction","Oxidizing agent","Oxidation","Reducing agent"],1,"An oxidizing agent is the reactant that oxidizes another substance by gaining electrons, meaning the oxidizing agent itself is reduced in the process.","2016 EC entrance"],["What property of an ionic compound can be investigated by heating it in a crucible?",["Malleability","Crystallization point","Solubility","Melting point"],3,"Heating an ionic compound in a crucible allows one to observe the temperature at which it transitions from a solid to a liquid, which determines its melting point.","2017 EC entrance"],["The process of vulcanization of rubber makes it",["Less elastic","More soluble in solvents","Soft","Hard"],3,"Vulcanization involves cross-linking polymer chains of rubber with sulfur, which makes the rubber harder, stiffer, and more resistant to heat and wear.","2010 EC entrance"],["A student added 25 mL of AgNO 3 solution to a beaker and weighed the mass of the beaker and its content as\nm 1 . He/she added 50 mL of a saturated solution of NaCl into the second beaker and weighed the mass of the\nbeaker and its content as m 2 . Finally, he/she mixed the two solutions and weighed the mass of the resulting\nsolution with the two beakers and recorded as m 3 . If he/she found that m 1 = m 2 , which one of the following\nlaws is investigated by this trial?",["Law of conservation of mass","Law of multiple proportions","Law of definite composition","Law of conservation of energy"],0,"Comparing the total mass of reactants before a reaction and the total mass of products after the reaction is the classic experimental method to demonstrate the Law of Conservation of Mass.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following has the same number of significant figures as the number 1.00310?",["1 × 106","199.791","5.119","100"],1,"The number 1.00310 has 6 significant figures. Among the choices, 199.791 also contains exactly 6 significant figures, while option A and B have 1, and option D has 4.","2011 EC entrance"],["​\n​\nThe general formula for saturated monocarboxylic acids is",["RCOR","RCOOH","ROR","RCHO ​ ​"],1,"Saturated monocarboxylic acids (also known as alkanoic acids) contain one carboxyl group (-COOH) attached to an alkyl group, represented by the general formula RCOOH.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the four colligative properties arises in systems where there is an equilibrium between a liquid solution\nphase and a second liquid phase?",["Freezing point depression","Vapour pressure lowering","Osmotic pressure","Boiling point elevation"],2,"Osmotic pressure involves an equilibrium established between two liquid phases (the pure solvent and the solution) across a semipermeable membrane.","2011 EC entrance"],["Aluminum reacts with a certain nonmetallic element, X to form a compound with the general formula AlX.\nElement X is a diatomic gas at room temperature. Element X must be",["fluorine","Bromine","sulfur","Nitrogen"],3,"Aluminum has a +3 oxidation state, so for the neutral 1:1 compound AlX, X must have a -3 oxidation state. Nitrogen (N) is a diatomic gas (N2) at room temperature and typically forms a -3 nitride ion, yielding AlN.","2018 EC entrance"],["A chemical bond that results from the attractive force between shared electrons and nonmetal nucleus is called\n_____.",["covalent bond","hydrogen bond","metallic bond","ionic bond"],0,"A covalent bond is formed by the electrostatic attraction between the shared pair of electrons and the positively charged nuclei of the nonmetal atoms. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["A system does 15 J of work and no other changes take place. Which of the following function has fallen by 15\nJ?",["Entropy","Internal energy","Specific heat","Enthalpy"],1,"According to the First Law of Thermodynamics (delta U = q + w), if a system does 15 J of work (w = -15 J) and no heat is exchanged (q = 0), its internal energy falls by 15 J.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following postulates of Dalton's atomic theory was modified by the modern atomic theory?",["Atoms are neither created nor destroyed in chemical reactions","Atoms are indivisible and indestructible","Atoms are the smallest particles of all elements","Compounds are formed when atoms of more than one element combine"],1,"Dalton's postulate that atoms are indivisible and indestructible was modified by modern atomic theory following the discovery of subatomic particles (protons, neutrons, and electrons).","2014 EC entrance"],["Given the following unbalanced equation KMnO4 + KI + H2 SO4 → K2 SO4 + MnSO4 + I2 + H2 O\nHow many grams of KMnO4 are needed to make 250 mL of 0.20 N solution?\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​\n​",["3.95 g","3.16 g","2.98 g","1.58 g"],3,"In acidic media, KM nO4 undergoes a 5-electron reduction (M n7+ → M n2+ ), so its equivalent mass is Molar Mass/5 = 158.0/5 = 31.6 g/eq. Thus, the mass required is Normality × Volume (L) × Equivalent Mass = 0.20 eq/L × 0.250 L × 31.6 g/eq = 1.58 g. − + +","2011 EC entrance"],["An element X has two naturally occurring isotopes. The information about these isotopes is given in the table\nbelow. Isotope X-40 (Atomic Mass 40 u, Natural Abundance 80%) and Isotope X-44 (Atomic Mass 44 u, Natural\nAbundance 20%). What is the average atomic mass of element X?",["42.0 u","40.0 u","40.8 u","41.5 u"],2,"Average atomic mass is the weighted average over the isotopes, so multiply each mass by its abundance and add. 0.80 × 40 + 0.20 × 44 = 32 + 8.8 = 40.8 u. C is tempting because 40 is the mass of the common isotope, but the heavier isotope still pulls the average above 40. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["The heat change at constant pressure that results when 1 mole of a compound is formed from its elements in\ntheir standard states is",["standard enthalpy of reaction","standard reduction potential","standard entropy of reaction","standard enthalpy of formation"],3,"The standard enthalpy of formation is defined as the change in enthalpy (heat change at constant pressure) when one mole of a compound is synthesized directly from its constituent elements in their standard states.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an essential nutrient of plants?",["Lead","Aluminum","Sodium","Potassium"],3,"Potassium (K) is one of the three primary macronutrients (along with nitrogen and phosphorus) essential for healthy plant growth and development. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following types of energy change occurs from the combustion of carbon in oxygen?",["solar energy","light energy","electrical energy","heat energy"],3,"The combustion of carbon in oxygen is a highly exothermic chemical reaction that releases energy primarily in the form of heat energy.","2014 EC entrance"],["Fats and oils are:",["Acids","Alcohols","Alkenes","Esters"],3,"Fats and oils are triglycerides, which are triesters formed from glycerol and three fatty acid molecules.","2010 EC entrance"],["What is the relationship between frequency (V), wavelength ( λ) and the speed of light (c)?",["hc/λ = v","λ/v = c","vc = λ","c = vλ"],3,"The speed of light (c) is directly proportional to the product of frequency (v) and wavelength (λ), giving the wave equation c = vλ.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following substances are added to natural rubber to toughen it?",["Sulfur","Nitrogen","Calcium","Carbon"],0,"Sulfur is added to natural rubber in a heating process called vulcanization, which introduces cross-links between polymer chains to significantly increase its toughness and elasticity.","2012 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is NOT both a Bronsted-Lowry acid and a Bronsted-Lowry base?",["HS−","OH−","HSO− 4 ​ ​","HCO− 3"],3,"− An amphiprotic species can both donate and accept a proton. HS− , HCO− 3 , and HSO4 can all act as both Bronsted− Lowry acids and bases, whereas OH acts exclusively as a base in aqueous solutions. ​ ​","2010 EC entrance"],["The stage in which the shredded sugarcane travels on the conveyor belt through a series of heavy-duty rollers,\nwhich extract juice from the pulp in sugar manufacturing, is called_____.",["Clarifying","Juicing","Collecting the Harvest","Cleansing and Grinding"],1,"The process of extracting juice from sugarcane pulp using a series of heavy-duty rollers is referred to as 'Juicing' (or extraction) in the sugar manufacturing process.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following compounds reacts with basic oxide to form salt and water?",["Acid","Acidic oxide","Neutral oxide","Base"],0,"An acid (such as HCl) reacts with a basic oxide (such as CuO) to form a salt and water through a neutralization-like reaction.","2015 EC entrance"],["In which of the following order of a reaction, a plot of In [A]t versus time is a straight line whose slope is - k?\n​",["Second","Zero","Third","First"],3,"The integrated rate law for a first-order reaction is ln[A]t = -kt + ln[A]0, which represents a straight-line equation (y = mx + c) where a plot of ln[A]t vs. time has a slope of -k. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["The average mass of the atoms in an element is known to be",["isotopic mass","molar mass","equivalent mass","atomic mass"],3,"The average mass of the atoms in a naturally occurring element, taking into account the abundance of its isotopes, is known as its atomic mass.","2016 EC entrance"],["The molecular geometry of H3 O+ ion is\n​",["Linear","Tetrahedral","Bent","Trigonal pyramidal"],3,"The hydronium ion (H3O+) has 3 bonding pairs and 1 lone pair on the oxygen atom, giving it a trigonal pyramidal molecular geometry.","2007 EC entrance"],["The half-life for the first order decomposition of nitromethane, CH3 NO2 , at 500k is 650 seconds. If the initial\nconcentration of CH3 NO2 is 0.500M, what will its concentration be (M) after 1300 seconds have elapsed?\n​\n​",["0.425","0.125","0.140","0.250 ​ (1) ​"],1,"The elapsed time of 1300 seconds represents exactly two half-lives (2 × 650 s). After two half-lives, the concentration decreases to 0.500 M/4 = 0.125 M.","2006 EC entrance"],["When the molecular equation: CaCl2 (aq) + Na2 CO3 (aq) → CaCO3(s) + 2NaCl(aq) Is written in terms of \nionic equation, which one of the following pairs will be the spectator ions?\n​\n​",["Na2− 3 and Cl ​","Na+ and Cl− −","Ca2+ and CO2− 3 ​ ​","Ca2+ and Cl−"],1,"In the reaction between CaCl₂ and Na₂CO₃, Ca²⁺ and CO₃²⁻ precipitate as CaCO₃(s), while Na⁺ and Cl⁻ remain dissolved in aqueous solution unchanged as spectator ions.","2009 EC entrance"],["What is the first step of the scientific method?",["Performing an experiment","Making observations","Predicting the result of an experiment","Forming a hypothesis"],1,"The scientific method traditionally begins with making observations about a phenomenon, which then leads to asking a question and formulating a hypothesis.","2008 EC entrance"],["In thermodynamics: solutions in a beaker, a gas in a cylinder, a reaction vessel, a biological cell are examples of\na",["path function","state function","thermodynamic system","thermodynamic variables"],2,"A thermodynamic system is any specific portion of the universe under study, such as a solution in a beaker, a gas in a cylinder, or a cell.","2015 EC entrance"],["How many kilo joules of heat are absorbed when 20 g of NaCl(s) is decomposed in to Na(s) and Cl2 (g) at\nconstant pressure according to the following reaction?\n​\n2Na(s) + Cl2 (g) → 2NaCl(s)\n​",["-281.0","-140.5","+140.5 (1) ΔH = −821.8 kl","+281.0"],1,"The equation as written makes 2 mol of NaCl and gives out 821.8 kJ, so forming 1 mol releases 410.9 kJ and breaking 1 mol back apart takes the same 410.9 kJ in. The sample is 20/58.5 = 0.342 mol of NaCl. Heat absorbed = 0.342 × 410.9 = 140.5 kJ, and heat taken in is positive, so the answer is +140.5. Option B has the right size but the wrong sign, because decomposition is the reverse of the reaction printed.","2005 EC entrance"],["The simplest formula for a compound containing Mn4+ and O2− is",["MnO","MnO2","Mn2 O4","Mn4 O2 ​ ​ ​ ​"],1,"To form an electrically neutral compound from Mn^4+ and O^2-, two oxide ions are required for each manganese ion, giving the empirical formula MnO2.","2006 EC entrance"],["In which one of the following numbers are all of the zeros significant?",["0.14329","0.1","0.003002","100.09009"],3,"In 100.09009, all zeros are captive (located between non-zero digits), making every zero significant. In the other options, leading zeros are not significant.","2007 EC entrance"],["For lithium, enthalpy of sublimation = +161 kJ/mol, first IE = +520 kJ/mol. Dissociation energy of F2 = +154\nkJ/mol, electron affinity of F = -328 kJ/mol. Lattice energy of LiF = -1047 kJ/mol. The overall enthalpy of\nformation for LiF is:",["-694 kJ/mol","2066 kJ/mol","-617 kJ/mol","2134 kJ/mol"],2,"Using the Born-Haber cycle, the enthalpy of formation is calculated as: H_f = H_sub(Li) + IE(Li) + 0.5 * D(F2) + EA(F) + U_L(LiF) = 161 + 520 + 77 - 328 - 1047 = -617 kJ/mol.","2012 EC entrance"],["Which of the following electron transitions requires the highest energy to be absorbed by the hydrogen atom?",["from n = 3 to n = 4","from n = 4 to n = 5","from n = 2 to n = 3","from n = 1 to n = 2"],3,"The energy levels of a hydrogen atom are spaced such that the transition from n = 1 to n = 2 has the largest energy gap, meaning it requires the absorption of the highest energy photon.","2016 EC entrance"],["For the four quantum numbers needed to describe an electron, which of these combinations are not possible?",["(2, 1, 1, -1/2)","(1, 0, 0, +1/2)","(3, 2, -2, -1/2)","(1, 0, -1, +1/2)"],3,"The quantum numbers are tied to each other. For n = 1 the only allowed value of l is 0, and when l = 0 the only allowed value of ml is 0. The set (1, 0, −1, +1/2) breaks that rule, because ml cannot be −1 when l is 0. C looks risky because of its negative values, but with l = 2 the allowed ml values run from −2 to +2, so it is fine. ​ ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following isomers differs in the arrangement of carbon atoms in the longest continuous carbon\nchain?",["Structural","Geometric","Position","Cis-trans"],0,"Chain isomers, which differ in the arrangement of carbon atoms in the main chain, are a subcategory of structural (or constitutional) isomers.","2015 EC entrance"],["If different processes are used to bring about the same change the enthalpy changes during these processes\nare the same, this is the statement of",["Standard Enthalpy","2nd law thermodynamics","Hess's law","1st law thermodynamics"],2,"Hess's law states that the total enthalpy change for a chemical reaction is the same regardless of whether the reaction takes place in one step or in several steps.","2012 EC entrance"],["Which principle emphasizes maximizing the desired product and minimizing by-products?",["Less hazardous chemical synthesis","Design for energy efficiency","Atom economy","Use of renewable feedstock"],2,"Atom economy asks how much of the mass of the reactants finishes up in the wanted product. A high atom economy means most atoms end up in the product and few are thrown away as by-products, which is exactly what the question describes. C is tempting, but less hazardous synthesis is about how harmful the substances used and made are, not about how much of them reaches the product.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the wavelength associated with an electron of mass, m = 9.11 × 10−28 g, travelling at 40% of the\nvelocity of light?",["6.06 × 10−15 m","6.06 × 10−12 m","2.42 × 10−15","2.42 × 10−11 m"],1,"Use de Broglie's relation, λ = h/mv . First put the mass into kilograms, 9.11 × 10−28 g = 9.11 × 10−31 kg, and find the 6.626 × 10−34 speed, 0.40 × 3.0 × 108 = 1.2 × 108 m/s. Then λ = = 6.06 × 10−12 m. Option A has 9.11 × 10−31 × 1.2 × 108 the same digits but a different power of ten, which is what comes out if the mass is left in grams. ​ (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following molecules has a trigonal bi pyramidal structure?",["IF5","PCl5","ICl− 4","BrF5 ​ (1) ​ ​ ​"],1,"In PCl5 the phosphorus atom is surrounded by five bonding pairs and no lone pair. Five regions of electron density with none of them lone gives the trigonal bipyramid: three bonds spread in a plane at 120 degrees, and two more at right angles above and below. IF5 tempts because it also has five bonds, but iodine keeps a lone pair as well, and six regions with one lone pair make a square pyramid. ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["The branch of chemistry that is involved in separation, identifying and determining the relative amounts of\ncomponents in a sample of material is known as",["analytical chemistry","inorganic chemistry","physical chemistry","biochemistry"],0,"Analytical chemistry is the branch of chemistry focused on the separation, identification, and quantification of the chemical components of natural and artificial materials.","2013 EC entrance"],["How can a project of establishing an industry that consumes coal affect the environment?",["Rise in global temperature","By changing the pH of water","Increment in concentration of nitric oxide","Production of high level of lead in the atmosphere"],0,"Coal-consuming industries burn massive quantities of coal, releasing carbon dioxide (CO2 ), which is a greenhouse gas that traps heat in the atmosphere and leads to a rise in global temperature. ​","2014 EC entrance"],["A solution of NH4 Cl made by dissolving 3.16g NH4 Cl in 30.14g H2 O has a density of 1.0272g cm−3 . What is\nthe mole fraction of NH4 Cl?\n​\n​\n​\n​",["0.0341","0.21","0.65","0.9659"],0,"Moles of NH4 Cl = 3.16 g/53.5 g/mol ≈ 0.0591 mol and moles of H2 O = 30.14 g/18.02 g/mol ≈ 1.673 mol. The mole fraction is X = 0.0591/(0.0591 + 1.673) ≈ 0.0341. ​ ​","2010 EC entrance"],["The value of E° for the reaction Zn(s) + Cu^2+(aq) → Cu(s) + Zn^2+(aq) is 1.10 V. What is the value of Ecell when\nthe concentrations of Cu^2+ and Zn^2+ are equal to 0.025 M?",["0.80 V","1.15 V","1.10 V","0.95 V"],2,"Using the Nernst equation, Ecell = E°cell - (0.0592 / n) * log([Zn2+]/[Cu2+]). Since the concentrations of both ions are equal, the reaction quotient Q = 1, and log(1) = 0, meaning Ecell = E°cell = 1.10 V.","2012 EC entrance"],["For the following hypothetical equation, in aqueous solution, what is the correct representation of the cell\nnotation?\nA(s) + B2+ (aq) _ A2+ (aq) + B(s)",["A(s)∣A2+ (aq)∣∣B2+ (aq)∣B(s)","B2+ (aq)∣B(s)∣∣A2+ (aq)∣A(s)","A2+ (aq)(s)∣A(s)∣∣B(s)∣B2+ (aq)","B(s)∣B2+ (aq)∣∣A2+ (aq)∣A(s)"],0,"In cell notation the anode is written on the left, the cathode on the right, and the double bar in the middle stands for the salt bridge. In this reaction A(s) loses electrons and becomes A2+ , so A is the anode, while B2+ gains electrons and becomes B(s), so B is the cathode. That gives A(s)∣A2+ (aq)∣∣B2+ (aq)∣B(s). Option D is the same cell written back to front, which would describe the reverse reaction, the one that does not happen on its own","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following ionic compounds is formed from the reaction between magnesium and nitrogen?",["MgN2","Mg2 N2 ​ ​","Mg2 N3 ​ ​ (1) ​ ​","Mg3 N2 ​"],3,"Magnesium is in group IIA and loses two electrons to give Mg2+ . Nitrogen gains three electrons to give N3− . The compound must be electrically neutral, so three Mg2+ ions carrying +6 pair with two N3− ions carrying −6, which gives Mg3 N2 . Option A tempts if you copy the 2 from the N2 gas, but the subscripts in an ionic formula come from the charges. ​","2005 EC entrance"],["What is the density of methane (CH4 ) at a pressure of 900 torr and a temperature of 25°C? (R = 0.082 atm.\nL/mol. K, 1 atm = 760 torr)\n​",["9.2","0.92","0.78","1.25"],2,"First convert pressure to atmospheres: 900/760 = 1.184 atm. Using the density formula for an ideal gas, d = PM /RT = (1.184 × 16)/(0.082 × 298.15) ≈ 0.78 g/L.","2017 EC entrance"],["The decomposition of hydrogen iodide on gold surface is zero - order in HI. The rate constant for the reaction is\n0.050 M/s. If the initial concentration of HI is 0.50 M, what is the half - life of this reaction?",["5.0 s","0.1 s","1.0 s","0.5 s"],0,"For a zero-order reaction, the half-life is calculated using the formula t_1/2 = [A]_0 / (2k). Substituting the given values yields t_1/2 = 0.50 M / (2 * 0.050 M/s) = 5.0 s.","2016 EC entrance"],["In the production of NH3 by the Haber process according to the equation N 2 (g)+3H 2 (g) ⇌ 2NH 3 (g)\nΔH=-92KJ mol -1 What are the favorable conditions for the production of high yield of NH 3 ?",["Low pressure and high temperature","High pressure and low temperature","Low pressure and low temperature","High pressure and high temperature"],1,"This is a duplicate of Question 42. High pressure and low temperature are thermodynamically favorable for maximizing the yield of NH₃ because the forward reaction is exothermic and results in a decrease in the number of moles of gas. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Which of the following molecules does not obey the octet rule?",["NCl3","ClO2","CCl4","CO2"],1,"Count the valence electrons in ClO2 : 7 + 2 × 6 = 19, an odd number. An odd total cannot be shared out to give every atom a complete octet, so one electron is left unpaired and the octet rule is broken. C is tempting because CO2 has double bonds, but carbon and both oxygens still finish with eight electrons each, so it obeys the rule. ​ ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Among the following acids, which has the lowest PKa value?\n​",["(CH3 )2CHCOOH","CH3 COOH ​ ​ ​","HCOOH","CH3 CH2 COOH"],2,"Formic acid (HCOOH) is the strongest acid among the given carboxylic acids because it lacks an electron-donating alkyl group, giving it the lowest pKa (around 3.75).","2009 EC entrance"],["The conversion of nitrogen gas into useful nitrogen compounds is known as",["Respiration","Photosynthesis","Oxidation","Fixation"],3,"Nitrogen fixation is the chemical process by which atmospheric nitrogen (N2) is converted into ammonia or other organic nitrogen compounds, making it usable by organisms.","2013 EC entrance"],["What is the [OH − ] of a solution with a pH of 4?",["104","1010","10−10","10−4"],2,"Since pH + pOH = 14 at 25∘ C, a solution with a pH of 4 has a pOH of 10, meaning the hydroxide ion concentration [OH − ] = 10−pOH = 10−10 M.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one is the correct order of increasing Cl-A-Cl bond angle in the following species where A is central\natom: I. BCl3, II. SiCl4, III. SCl2, IV. PCl3?",["III < IV < II < I","I < II < III < IV","II < III < I < IV","IV < I < II < III"],0,"According to VSEPR theory, bond angles decrease as the number of lone pairs on the central atom increases. Thus, SCl2 (bent, 2 lone pairs) has a smaller angle than PCl3 (trigonal pyramidal, 1 lone pair), which is smaller than SiCl4 (tetrahedral, 109.5°), and BCl3 (trigonal planar, 120°) has the largest angle, leading to the order III < IV < II < I. (1)","2012 EC entrance"],["What is the most common Ore used for the extraction of copper?",["CuFeS2 ​","CuSO4 ​ ​","CuO","CuCO3"],0,"Chalcopyrite (CuFeS2), also known as copper pyrites, is the most common and principal ore from which copper is commercially extracted.","2008 EC entrance"],["\"At a given temperature and pressure, equal volumes of different gases contain equal number of molecules\", this\nis known as _______",["Boyle's law","Charle's law","Avogadro's law","Gay Lussac's law"],2,"Avogadro's law states that equal volumes of all gases, at the same temperature and pressure, have the same number of molecules.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following synthetic polymers is used to make squeeze bottles, plastic wrapping and electrical\ninsulation?",["Polyvinylchloride","Polyethylene","Polypropylene","Polymethyl methacrylate"],1,"Polyethylene, especially low-density polyethylene (LDPE), is highly flexible and chemically inert, making it ideal for squeeze bottles, plastic wraps, and electrical wire insulation.","2016 EC entrance"],["When 5.0 g of magnesium reacts with 20.0 g of oxygen gas according to the reaction: Mg(s) + O₂(g) → MgO(s),\nWhat is the mass of MgO that can be formed?",["8.3 g","16.7 g","20.0 g","10.0 g"],0,"The balanced equation is 2Mg + O2 -> 2MgO. Magnesium is the limiting reactant (5.0 g / 24.3 g/mol = 0.206 mol), which yields 0.206 mol of MgO (0.206 mol * 40.3 g/mol = 8.3 g).","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the freezing point of a solution of 250 g of CaCl₂ in 1.0 kg of water? ( Kf for H₂O = 1.86 kg/mol)\n​",["- 1.3 °C","- 6.5 °C","- 9.0 °C","- 13 °C"],3,"Calcium chloride dissociates into three ions (i = 3). The molality of the solution is 250 g/111 g/mol/1.0 kg = 2.25 m, giving a freezing point depression of ΔTf = i ⋅ Kf ⋅ m = 3 × 1.86 × 2.25 ≈ 12.6∘ C, which corresponds to a freezing point of −13∘ C. ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["An equation that defines the experimentally determined relation between the concentrations of reactants and\nrate of that reaction is known as _____.",["order of reaction","rate constant","rate law","mechanism reaction"],2,"The rate law (or rate equation) is the experimentally determined expression that relates the rate of a chemical reaction to the concentrations of its reactants.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the cause of unusual high boiling points of HF, H2 O and NH3 ?\n​",["Induced dipole forces","Dipole-Dipole forces","Hydrogen bonding","Ion-dipole forces ​"],2,"HF, H2O, and NH3 exhibit unusually high boiling points because of hydrogen bonding, which is a strong type of intermolecular attraction that occurs when hydrogen is bonded to highly electronegative atoms (F, O, N). (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["A type of chemical bonding that results from the mutual attraction between positively charged metal nuclei and\nthe surrounding freely moving sea of electrons is named as:",["Dative","Ionic","Metallic","Covalent"],2,"Metallic bonding is defined as the electrostatic attraction between positively charged metal ions and the delocalized 'sea' of freely moving electrons.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is the most important source for the extraction of iron?",["Hematite","Bauxite","Sphalerite","Chalcopyrite"],0,"Hematite (Fe2O3) is the most abundant and commercially important ore used for the industrial extraction of iron in blast furnaces","2006 EC entrance"],["The correct balanced chemical equation for the reaction: Phosphorus + oxygen → phosphorus(V) oxide is:",["P₅ + O₂ → P₂O₅","P₄ + 5O₂ → P₄O₁₀","5P + O₂ → P₅O₂","2P + O₂ → 2PO"],1,"Phosphorus exists elementally as P₄ molecules, and phosphorus(V) oxide has the molecular formula P₄O₁₀. The correctly balanced equation is P₄ + 5O₂ → P₄O₁₀.","2018 EC entrance"],["The molecule of BF3 has both bonding and lone pair of electrons. Based upon these electrons, which one is the\nCORRECT molecular geometry of the molecule of BF3 ?\n​\n​",["Trigonal planar","Square planar","Trigonal bipyramidal","Square pyramidal"],0,"Boron trifluoride (BF3) has three bonding pairs of electrons on the central boron atom and zero lone pairs, giving it a trigonal planar molecular geometry according to VSEPR theory.","2017 EC entrance"],["Carbon forms two stable compounds with oxygen, namely, carbon monoxide and carbon dioxide. For a fixed\nmass of carbon, the ratio of oxygen in carbon monoxide to oxygen in carbon dioxide is 1:2. This result is\nconsistent with the law of",["conservation of mass.","multiple proportion.","definite proportion.","constant composition."],1,"The law of multiple proportions states that when two elements combine to form more than one compound, the masses of one element that combine with a fixed mass of the other are in a ratio of small whole numbers (1:2 for CO and CO2).","2015 EC entrance"],["The following reaction can be used for the synthesis of CH₃CH=CHCH₃ as a desired product: CH₃CH₂CHBrCH₃ +\nCH₃S⁻ → CH₃CH=CHCH₃ + CH₃SH + Br⁻. What is the atom economy for the above reaction?",["30.4%","48%","56%","80%"],0,"Atom economy is calculated as (molar mass of desired product / sum of molar masses of reactants) x 100%. For this reaction, it is (56 g/mol of C’H“ / 184 g/mol of reactants) x 100% = 30.4%","2018 EC entrance"],["When a saturated solution of sodium chloride is heated, it becomes",["Remains saturated","Supersaturated","Unsaturated","Attains equilibrium conditions"],2,"Since the dissolution of sodium chloride is an endothermic process, its solubility increases with increasing temperature. Heating a saturated solution increases its solubility limit, making the solution unsaturated if no more solute is added.","2011 EC entrance"],["In which region of the Periodic Table would the element with the electronic structure below be located?\n1s2 2s2 2p6 3s2 3p6 3d10 4s2 4p6 4d6 5s2",["S block","Noble gases","D block","Group 6"],2,"The valence shell configuration ends in 4d⁶ 5s², indicating that the differentiating electron enters the d subshell, placing this element (ruthenium) in the d-block.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a colorless, flammable volatile liquid and miscible with non-polar solvents?",["Methanol","Benzene","Methane","Ethanol"],1,"Benzene is a colorless, volatile, and flammable liquid. Being non-polar, it is immiscible with polar solvents like water but highly miscible with non-polar organic solvents.","2015 EC entrance"],["Two electrolytic cells were placed in series, one of AgNO3 and the other of CuSO4 . If 1.273g Ag is deposited,\nhow much Cu was deposited, how much Cu was deposited at the same time?\n​",["0.0118","0.954","0.748 ​","0.374"],3,"According to Faraday's second law, mass ratio is (m_Cu / m_Ag) = (M_Cu / z_Cu) / (M_Ag / z_Ag) = (63.55 / 2) / (107.9 / 1) ≈ 0.2945. Therefore, m_Cu = 1.273 g × 0.2945 ≈ 0.374 g","2010 EC entrance"],["At 75°C, the vapor pressure of pure water is 39 kPa. Which one of the vapor pressure of a solution obtained by\ndissolving 34.2 g sucrose in 180 mL of water? (Assume that the density of water is 1.000 g/mL)",["41.1 kPa","44.5 kPa","38.6 kPa","31.2 kPa"],2,"180/18 The mole fraction of water is Xwater = 180/18+34.2/342.9 ≈ 0.9901. Using Raoult's Law, the vapor pressure of the solution is P = Xwater ⋅ P ∘ = 0.9901 × 39 kPa ≈ 38.6 kPa. ​ ​ ​","2014 EC entrance"],["​\n​\nWhich of the following molecules represents a non-polar covalent bond?",["C-Cl","B-Cl","Mg-Cl","Cl-Cl"],0,"A bond is non-polar when both atoms pull on the shared pair with the same strength. Two chlorine atoms have identical electronegativity, so the difference is zero and the electron pair sits in the middle. C-Cl is the tempting choice because carbon and chlorine are both non-metals, but their electronegativities differ by about 0.5, so that bond is polar covalent. (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["Any discharge of a solid, liquid or gaseous substance or radiation (energy) into an environment that causes\nunwanted changes is said to be:",["Contaminates","Pollution","Slug","Corrosion"],1,"Pollution is the release of any solid, liquid, gas or energy into the environment in a form or amount that causes unwanted change. That is what the sentence describes. C is tempting because a contaminant is closely related, but a contaminant is the substance itself, while the question describes the act of discharging it and the harm that follows.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following compound does NOT follow the octet rule?",["CS2","PBr3 ​","BrF5 ​","IBr ​"],2,"In BrF5, bromine has 5 single bonds and 1 lone pair, expanding its valence shell to 12 electrons and thus violating the octet rule.","2007 EC entrance"],["What is the pH of a 0.10 M solution of NH₃, a weak base, whose Kb = 1.8 × 10−5 ?\n​",["4.76","11.11","2.89","9.24"],1,"For a weak base, [OH− ] = Kb × Cb = 1.8 × 10−5 × 0.10 ≈ 1.34 × 10−3 M. This gives a pOH ≈ 2.87 and a pH = 14 − pOH ≈ 11.13, which is closest to option D (11.11). ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["Which of the following particle was discovered by the cathode rays experiment?",["Neutron","Nucleus","Electron","Proton"],2,"Cathode rays were shown by J.J. Thomson in 1897 to consist of negatively charged particles, leading to the discovery of the electron.","2009 EC entrance"],["What are the two principal polysaccharide forms of starch?",["Sucrose and lactose.","Amylose and amylopectin.","Aldohexose and ketopentose.","Maltose and cellobiose."],3,"Starch is not one substance but a mixture of two glucose polymers. Amylose is the long unbranched chain that coils into a helix, and amylopectin is the branched one, and the two together make up the starch grain. Option C tempts because maltose and cellobiose are also built from glucose, but those are disaccharides, two units long, so they are not polysaccharide forms of starch.","2005 EC entrance"],["In the electroplating of nickel from a solution containing N i2+ ion, what will be the weight of the metal\ndeposited on the cathode by a current of 8 A flowing for 500 minutes?",["117.4 g","145 g","73 g","103 g"],2,"Using Faraday's laws of electrolysis, Q = I * t = 8 A * 30000 s = 240,000 C. The moles of electrons is 240,000 / 96500 = 2.487 mol, yielding 1.2435 mol of Ni (since Ni2+ + 2e- -> Ni), which corresponds to 1.2435 * 58.69 g/mol = 73 g.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following chemicals is used to disinfect water?",["Nitrogen","Oxygen","Fluorine","Chlorine"],3,"Chlorine is widely used as a disinfectant in water treatment to kill bacteria, viruses, and other harmful microorganisms.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an ionic compound?",["CaCl2 ​ ​","PCl3 ​ ​","CO2","H2 O2 ​"],0,"CaCl2 is an ionic compound formed by the transfer of electrons from a metal (calcium) to a non-metal (chlorine), resulting in ionic bonding, whereas the other options are molecular compounds with covalent bonds.","2015 EC entrance"],["The partial pressure of acetylene, C₂H₂, in a container is 10 atm at 25°C. What is the solubility in molarity of C₂H₂, \nassume that C₂H₂ obeys Henry's law? (KH = 1.04 mol/L atm)\n​",["9.62","104","10.4","0.104"],2,"According to Henry's law, the solubility of a gas is directly proportional to its partial pressure: C = KH * P. Here, C = 1.04 mol/L atm * 10 atm = 10.4 M.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following pairs of substances are miscible?",["Water and gasoline","Water and oxygen","Water and ethanol","Water and salt"],2,"Miscibility refers to the ability of two liquids to mix in all proportions to form a homogeneous solution; water and ethanol form hydrogen bonds and are completely miscible.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the CORRECT description of uncertainty in measurements? It is used that exact\nnumber is",["whose values are known exactly","whose values known inexactly","accurate number","certain number"],0,"Exact numbers are those whose values are known exactly, such as counted values (e.g., 12 eggs in a dozen) or defined quantities, and they have zero uncertainty.","2016 EC entrance"],["For the reaction, N₂ + 3H₂ → 2NH₃, the rate of disappearance of H₂ is 0.01 mol L−1 min−1 . What is the rate of\nappearance of NH₃?",["0.007 mol L−1 min−1","0.02 mol L−1 min−1","0.01 mol L−1 min−1","0.002 mol L−1 min−1"],0,"From the stoichiometry of the reaction, the rate of appearance of NH₃ is equal to two-thirds of the rate of disappearance of H₂, which is 2/3 × 0.01 ≈ 0.007 mol L−1 min−1 .","2011 EC entrance"],["The solubility of NaCl in water at 200 C is 36g in 100g of water. A solution that contains 18g of NaCl in 50g of\nwater at 200 C is",["Supersaturated","Dilute","Saturated","Unsaturated"],2,"At 20 °C, 18 g of NaCl in 50 g of water corresponds to 36 g of NaCl per 100 g of water, which exactly equals its solubility limit, meaning the solution is saturated.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which type of glass is made by heating a mixture of silica, sodium carbonate and limestone?",["Borosilicate","Pyrex","Soda-lime","Quartz"],2,"Soda-lime glass, the most common type of glass, is manufactured by melting a mixture of silica (sand), sodium carbonate (soda), and calcium carbonate (limestone).","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is a monomer of natural rubber?",["Isoprene","Hexamethylene diamine","Styrene","Ethylene terephthalate"],0,"Natural rubber is a polymer of the organic compound isoprene (2-methyl-1,3-butadiene), which is its repeating monomer unit.","2016 EC entrance"],["The dye bromothymol blue (HBb) is a weak acid whose ionization can be represented as follows: HBb(aq) ⇌\nH⁺(aq) + Bb⁻(aq). Which way will the equilibrium shift when NaOH is added?",["Initially to the right finally to left","to the right","To the left","Initially to the left, finally to right"],1,"Adding NaOH introduces hydroxide ions (OH-) which neutralize hydrogen ions (H+). According to Le Chatelier's principle, the equilibrium shifts to the right to replenish the consumed H+ ions.","2018 EC entrance"],["\"Both the position and the momentum of an electron in atom cannot be determined at the same time\", this is the \nstatement of the:",["Heisenberg's uncertainty principle","Planck's theory","de-Broglie's statement","Bohr's theory"],0,"Heisenberg's uncertainty principle states that it is fundamentally impossible to determine simultaneously both the exact position and momentum of a subatomic particle like an electron.","2016 EC entrance"],["The equilibrium constant K p for the reaction 2SO 2 (g) ⇌ 2SO 3 (g) + O 2 (g) is 3.8 × 10 -3 K p at 227 °C. What is\nthe value of K c for the reaction at the same temperature?",["9.1 × 10 -4 mol m -3","2.3 × 10 -4 mol m -3","1.8 × 10 -3 mol m -3","4.6 × 10 -4 mol m -3"],0,"For the reaction 2SO3(g) ⇌ 2SO2(g) + O2(g), the change in moles of gas is Δn = 1. Using Kc = Kp / (RT) with T = 500 K and R = 0.08206 L atm/(mol K) yields approximately 9.1 * 10^-5 mol/L (often misprinted with different exponents or units as 9.1 * 10^-4 mol m^-3).","2013 EC entrance"],["The statement 'The properties of the elements are periodic functions of their atomic masses' is the",["Mendeleev's periodic law","Law of mass action","Modern periodic law","Law of definite proportion"],2,"Mendeleev lined the elements up by increasing atomic mass and saw their properties repeat at regular intervals. That is his periodic law. C is the tempting answer, but the modern periodic law makes properties a function of atomic number, not atomic mass, and that change is what fixed the places where Mendeleev's order broke down.","2018 EC entrance"],["What mass of aluminum is deposited electrolytically in 10 minutes by a current of 40 A? (I F = 96500 C/mol)",["0.24 g","2.25 g","0.67 g","6.71 g"],1,"The total charge passed is Q = I × t = 40 A × 600 s = 24, 000 C. Using Faraday's law, the mass of aluminum = 24,000×27 deposited is m = Q×M 2.24 g, which matches option A (2.25 g). n×F 3×96,500 ≈ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following types of rays combine to form atoms of Helium?",["X-rays","Gamma (γ ) rays","Beta (β )","Alpha (α)"],3,"Alpha particles are doubly ionized helium nuclei (He²⁺). When alpha particles capture two electrons, they become neutral helium atoms.","2008 EC entrance"],["A 0.2M solution of a weak acid HA is 1% ionized at 250 C Ka for the acid is equal to:",["0.198 0.01 × 0.01 ​ ​ (1) ​ ​ ​","0.01 × 0.01","0.002 × 0.002","0.02 × 0.02 0.19 0.18 0.19"],2,"At 1% ionization, [H+] = [A-] = 0.2 M × 0.01 = 0.002 M, and the un-ionized acid concentration is [HA] = 0.2 - 0.002 = 0.198 M. Thus, Ka = [H+][A-]/[HA] = (0.002 × 0.002) / 0.198.","2010 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following type of bonding exists between atoms with very different electro-negativities?",["Ionic bonding","Network covalent bonding","Metallic bonding","Hydrogen bonding"],0,"Ionic bonding occurs when there is a transfer of electrons between atoms with very different electronegativities, usually between a metal and a nonmetal.","2011 EC entrance"],["Among the following compounds which one is a by-product in Solvay process during the production of\nN a2 CO3 ?\n​\n​",["N H3 ​","CaCl2","CaCO3 ​ ​","CO2 ​"],1,"Calcium chloride (CaCl2) is formed as a major by-product of the Solvay process when ammonium chloride is treated with calcium hydroxide to regenerate the ammonia.","2016 EC entrance"],["In the following reaction:\n+\n3+\n3Cl− (aq) + 4CrO2−\n4 (aq) + 23H (aq) → 3HClO2 (aq) + 4Cr (aq) + 10H2 O(l) What is the behaviour\nCl− (aq)?\n​\n​\n​",["An oxidizing agent","A reducing agent","An acid","A base"],1,"The oxidation state of chlorine increases from -1 in Cl-(aq) to +3 in HClO2(aq); since it undergoes oxidation, Cl-(aq) acts as a reducing agent.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following compound is a Bronsted-Lowry base?",["\\ceN H3","\\ceBF 3","\\ceH2S","\\ceHCl"],0,"A Brønsted-Lowry base is defined as a proton (H + ) acceptor. Ammonia (\\ceN H3) has a lone pair of electrons on the nitrogen atom that can readily accept a proton to form the ammonium ion (\\ceN H4+).","2017 EC entrance"],["To 0.2 M solution of a weak monoprotic acid, HA, enough quantity of its sodium salt, NaA, was dissolved to give\na concentration of 0.2 M of the salt. What will be the acid concentration, [H3 O+ ], in the final solutions? (Ka of\nHA = 1.80 × 10−5 )\n​",["1.80 × 10−5 M","1.00 × 10−5 M","1.90 × 10−3 M (1) ​","3.60 × 10−6 M"],0,"This mixture is a buffer, with the weak acid and its salt at the same concentration. Write the expression Ka = [H3 O+ ][A− ] ; since [A− ] = [HA] = 0.2 M those two cancel, leaving [H3 O+ ] = Ka = 1.80 × 10−5 M. Option D [HA] tempts if you treat the acid as though it were alone in water and use Ka × 0.2 = 1.9 × 10−3 , but the added salt pushes the ionisation back and keeps the acidity down. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["In three different experiments the following results were obtained for the reaction A → products: [A]ₒ = 1.00 M,\nt₁/₂ = 50 min; [A]ₒ = 2.00 M, t₁/₂ = 25 min; [A]ₒ = 0.50 M, t₁/₂ = 100 min. What is the value of the rate constant\nfor this reaction?",["0.010 L mol−1 min−1","0.030 L mol−1 min−1","0.040 L mol−1 min−1","0.020 L mol−1 min−1"],3,"The half-life is inversely proportional to the initial concentration, which is characteristic of a second-order reaction. Using the second-order half-life formula, t1/2 = 1/(k[A]0 ), we get k = 1/(50 min × 1.00 M) = 0.020 L mol−1 min−1 . ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["For the determination of the density of a new ceramic, a student measured the mass of a piece on an analytical\nbalance and obtained 3.8056 gram and its volume 2.5 mL by displacement of water in a graduated cylinder. The\ncorrect reported density of the ceramic should be",["1.5224 g/mL","3.5 g/mL","1.5 g/mL","1.5222 g/mL"],2,"The volume measurement (2.5 mL) has two significant figures, so the calculated density (3.8056 g / 2.5 mL = 1.52224 g/mL) must be rounded to two significant figures, which is 1.5 g/mL.","2013 EC entrance"],["Which of the following methods is used for the preparation of saturated monocarboxylic acids? Oxidation of",["secondary alcohols","primary alcohols","tertiary alcohols","quaternary alcohols"],1,"Saturated monocarboxylic acids are prepared by the complete oxidation of primary alcohols, typically using a strong oxidizing agent like acidified potassium dichromate. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the equivalence point pH of the solution formed by the titration of 50 mL of 0.15 M CH3COOH using 25\nmL of 0.3 M NaOH? [Use log 7.5 = 0.87, Kb of acetate ion = 5.6×10^{-10}]",["8.44","6.22","8.87","7.44"],2,"At the equivalence point, the moles of acetate ion formed equal 0.0075 mol in a total volume of 75 mL, giving [CH3 COO− ] = 0.1 M. Using the base dissociation constant Kb = 5.6 × 10−10 , the [OH− ] concentration is calculated as 5.6 × 10−11 ≈ 7.5 × 10−6 M, yielding a pOH of 5.13 and a pH of 14 − 5.13 = 8.87. ​ ​ ​","2012 EC entrance"],["\"Reactant molecules are first transformed into an intermediate activated complex that is unstable and breaks\ninto the products\", this is called",["transition state theory","reaction theory","activation theory","collision theory"],0,"According to transition state theory, reactants must pass through a high-energy, unstable intermediate state called the transition state or activated complex before forming products.","2016 EC entrance"],["180 g of calcium carbonate (CaCO3 ) is allowed to react with 156 gram of hydrochloric acid (HCI), according to the \nfollowing reaction. Which of the following substances is the limiting reagent? (Atomic masses; Ca=40, Cl 35.5,\nO=16, C=12, H=1) CaCO 3 + 2 HCl → CaCl 2 + CO 2 + H 2 O\n​",["CO2","HCl","H2 O ​","CaCO3 ​ ​"],3,"Molar mass of CaCO3 is 100 g/mol, giving 1.8 moles. Molar mass of HCl is 36.5 g/mol, giving 4.27 moles. Since the stoichiometry requires 2 moles of HCl per mole of CaCO3, 1.8 moles of CaCO3 would require 3.6 moles of HCl, leaving HCl in excess and making CaCO3 the limiting reagent.","2015 EC entrance"],["The maximum amount of a solute that dissolves in a given quantity of solvent at a given temperature is said to\nbe _____.",["solubility","molality","molarity","normality"],0,"Solubility is defined as the maximum concentration of a solute that can dissolve in a solvent at a given temperature and pressure to establish an equilibrium.","2016 EC entrance"],["When electrons fall down from the higher energy level to the first excited state, the spectral lines correspond to:",["Paschen series","Lyman series","Pfund series","Balmer series"],3,"The ground state of hydrogen is n = 1, so the first excited state is n = 2. Spectral lines resulting from transitions down to n = 2 belong to the Balmer series.","2012 EC entrance"],["The wave number of an electromagnetic radiation is 1 × 105 cm−1 . The frequency of the radiation would be",["3 × 1010 s−1","3 × 108 s−1","3 × 106 s−1","3 × 1015 s−1"],3,"Frequency is related to wave number by ν = c ⋅ νˉ. Using c = 3 × 1010 cm/s, ν = (3 × 1010 cm/s) × (1 × 105 cm−1 ) = 3 × 1015 s−1 .","2007 EC entrance"],["4 L of 0.02 M of aqueous solution of NaCl is diluted with 1 L of water. What is the molarity of the solution?",["0.016","0.012","0.004","0.008"],0,"Using the dilution equation M1 V1 = M2 V2 with V1 = 4 L, M1 = 0.02 M, and V2 = 4 L + 1 L = 5 L, we get M2 = (0.02 × 4)/5 = 0.016 M. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["What is the process that converts liquid vegetable oils to solid fats?",["Hydration","Saponification","Hydrogenation","Hydrolysis"],3,"Vegetable oils stay liquid because their fatty acid chains carry C = C double bonds that put a kink in the chain and keep the molecules apart. Passing hydrogen over the oil with a nickel catalyst adds H2 across those double bonds, the chains straighten, they pack closely and the product is solid at room temperature. Hydrolysis tempts because it also attacks fats, but hydrolysis breaks the ester links and gives glycerol and fatty acids instead of a solid fat. ​","2005 EC entrance"],["A chemical reaction that releases heat energy to the surrounding is known as _____.",["decomposition reaction","combination reaction","exothermic reaction","endothermic reaction"],2,"An exothermic reaction is a chemical reaction that releases energy to its surroundings, usually in the form of heat.","2016 EC entrance"],["Phosphorus (Z=15) has the electronic configuration 1s²2s²2p⁶3s²3p³, what kind of hybridization does phosphorus\nundergo in the formation of phosphorus pentachloride (PCl5)?",["sp³d","sp²","sp³","sp"],0,"In PCl₅, the central phosphorus atom forms 5 single bonds with no lone pairs, requiring 5 hybrid orbitals, which is achieved through sp³d hybridization.","2013 EC entrance"],["The maximum kinetic energy of a photoelectron emitted from a metal is 1.03 × 10−19 J when light that has a\n656 nm wavelength shines on the surface. What is the threshold frequency for this metal?",["4.57 × 10−14 s−1","3.02 × 10−14 s−1","4.57 × 1014 s−1","3.02 × 1014 s−1"],3,"The photon energy of the incident light is E = hc/λ = 3.03 × 10−19 J. Using the photoelectric equation, the work function is Φ = E − KEmax = 3.03 × 10−19 − 1.03 × 10−19 = 2.00 × 10−19 J, giving a threshold frequency ν0 = Φ/h = (2.00 × 10−19 )/(6.626 × 10−34 ) ≈ 3.02 × 1014 s−1 . ​ ​","2010 EC entrance"],["Which of the following conduct electricity without undergoing any chemical change?",["Molten magnesium chloride","Copper metal","Hydrochloric acid solution","Potassium chloride solution"],1,"Copper metal is a metallic conductor, which conducts electricity through the movement of free electrons without undergoing any chemical alteration, whereas electrolytic conductors (like solutions or molten salts) conduct via ions and undergo chemical changes at the electrodes.","2018 EC entrance"],["Consider the following reaction between nitrogen (N 2 ) and oxygen (O 2 ): N 2 (g) + O 2 (g) → 2NO(g) If the rate\nof disappearance of N 2 is 2.5 x 10 -6 M/s, what is the rate of reaction for the formation of NO?",["5.0 x 10 -6 M/s","2.50 x 10 -3 M/s","1.25 x 10 -3 M/s","2.50 x 10 -6 M/s"],0,"According to the stoichiometry of the reaction, 2 moles of NO are formed for every 1 mole of N2 consumed; therefore, the rate of formation of NO is twice the rate of disappearance of N2, which is 2 * (2.5 x 10^-6 M/s) = 5.0 x 10^-6 M/s.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which compound is an ester?",["CH3 OC2 H5","CH3 COOH","HCOOCH3 ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","C2 H5 CHO"],2,"HCOOCH3 (methyl formate or methyl methanoate) contains the ester functional group (-COO-).","2006 EC entrance"],["The sanitizer in wide use for protection against Covid-19 is labelled 83% alcohol. How can one scientifically\ncheck the concentration?",["collection of data","experimentation","forming hypothesis","making observation"],1,"To scientifically verify the concentration of a substance like alcohol in a solution, one must perform laboratory experimentation, such as density measurements, distillation, or gas chromatography. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Consider the mechanism for the decomposition of N 2 O 5 to NO 2 : First step: 2N 2 O 5 (g) = 4NO 2 (g) Second\nstep: N 4 O 10 (g) → NO 3 (g) + 2 NO 2 (g) + O 3 (g) Third step: N 2 O 5 (g) + O 3 (g) → 2 NO 2 (g) + O 2 (g) Overall:\n2N 2 O 5 (g) → 4 NO 2 (g) + O 2 (g) Which step is the rate-determining step?",["Second step","The overall step","First step","Third step"],0,"The second step is the slow step of the mechanism, which determines the overall rate of the chemical reaction and is known as the rate-determining step.","2016 EC entrance"],["Bakelite is obtained from phenol by reacting with",["HCHO","(CH2 OH)2","CH3 CHO","CH3 COCH3 ​ ​ ​ ​ ​"],0,"Bakelite is a thermosetting phenol-formaldehyde polymer prepared by the condensation reaction of phenol with formaldehyde (HCHO).","2007 EC entrance"],["What are the bond angles in NO₃⁻?",["90º","90º and 120º","109.5º","120º"],2,"The nitrogen in NO− 3 is surrounded by three oxygen atoms and carries no lone pair, so there are three regions of electron density. They repel each other into the widest flat arrangement, a trigonal planar shape, and a full turn shared between three directions gives 360/3 = 120 degrees. Option B, 109.5 degrees, is the tetrahedral angle, which would need four regions around the nitrogen. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["A nuclear breakdown in which particles or electromagnetic radiation is emitted is _______________.",["Radioactivity","Radio wave","Radioactive decay","Radioactive isotopes"],2,"Radioactive decay is the spontaneous process in which an unstable atomic nucleus undergoes breakdown and emits radiation (particles or electromagnetic waves) to achieve stability. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the standard free energy change, ΔG°, for the complete combustion of methane? CH₄(g) + 2O₂(g) →\nCO₂(g) + 2H₂O(l) Given: The standard free energies of formation: - CH₄(g) = -51 kJ/mol - CO₂(g) = -394 kJ/mol H₂O(l) = -237 kJ/mol",["-817 kJ/mol","-631 kJ/mol","-632 kJ/mol","-838 kJ/mol"],0,"The free energy change is calculated as ΔG∘rxn = [ΔG∘f (CO2 ) + 2ΔG∘f (H2 O)] − [ΔG∘f (CH4 ) + 2ΔG∘f (O2 )] = [−394 + 2(−237)] − [−51 + 0] = −817 kJ/mol. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is not a form of chemical bonding?",["Metallic bonding","Covalent bonding","Ionic bonding","Hydrogen bonding"],3,"Ionic, covalent, and metallic bonds are primary intramolecular chemical bonds, whereas hydrogen bonding is an intermolecular force.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following statement is true about oxide?",["Oxides are ternary compounds","All basic oxides are metallic oxides","All non-metallic oxides are acidic oxides","Amphoteric oxides are basic oxides"],1,"All basic oxides are metallic oxides, because non-metals do not form basic oxides (only acidic or neutral ones). (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following methods is used to reduce land pollution?",["Reducing CO₂ emission","Removal of lead compounds from gasoline","Replacing CFCs by less harmful alternatives","Recycling plastics"],3,"Recycling plastics directly reduces the accumulation of non-biodegradable waste in landfills, thereby mitigating land pollution, while the other options primary target air pollution.","2016 EC entrance"],["What skill is a scientist using when he/she listens to the sounds that animals make?",["Drawing conclusions","Interpreting data","Making a hypothesis","Making observations"],3,"Making observations involves using any of the five senses, including hearing, to gather information about natural phenomena.","2010 EC entrance"],["Alcohol that yield ketones on oxidation are classified as;",["Dihydric alcohol","Trihydric alcohol","Secondary alcohol","Primary alcohol"],2,"Secondary alcohols contain a hydroxyl group bonded to a carbon that is attached to two other carbons; upon oxidation, they lose hydrogen to form ketones.","2016 EC entrance"],["Commercially, liquid vegetable oils are converted to solid fats such as margarine by:",["Hydrogenation","Oxidation","Saponification","Hydration"],0,"Catalytic hydrogenation adds hydrogen across carbon-carbon double bonds in unsaturated liquid vegetable oils, raising their melting point to produce semi-solid or solid fats like margarine.","2006 EC entrance"],["Compounds that contain the carboxyl (carbonyl and hydroxyl) group are said to be:",["Esters","Ketones","Aldehydes","Organic acids"],3,"The carboxyl functional group (-COOH) consists of a carbonyl group bonded to a hydroxyl group, which characterizes carboxylic acids (organic acids). (1)","2010 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following quantum numbers determines the orientation of atomic orbitals?",["Principal quantum number","Spin quantum number","Azimuthal (angular) quantum number","Magnetic quantum number"],3,"The magnetic quantum number (m_l) determines the orientation of atomic orbitals in space, whereas the principal (n) determines size/energy and the azimuthal (l) determines the shape.","2016 EC entrance"],["Consider the following reaction of zinc carbonate, ZnCO 3 : ZnCO 3 (s) → ZnO(s) + CO 2 (g) The chemical reaction \nthat takes place during the conversion of ZnCO 3 is classified as",["single displacement reaction","decomposition reaction","double displacement reaction","combination reaction"],1,"The reaction shows a single reactant, zinc carbonate (ZnCO3), breaking down into two simpler substances, zinc oxide (ZnO) and carbon dioxide (CO2), which defines a decomposition reaction.","2016 EC entrance"],["The point in a titration at which the number of moles of OH− ions added to a solution is equal to the number of\nmoles of H+ ions originally present is",["Zero point","Equivalence point","Triple point","End point"],1,"The equivalence point in an acid-base titration is the theoretical point at which the quantity of added titrant is stoichiometrically equal to the quantity of analyte originally present (i.e., moles of OH- added equals moles of H+ originally present). (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["A sample of solid ammonium carbamate is heated in a closed container at 298 K and allowed to reach\nequilibrium.\nNH₄CO₂NH₂ (s) ⇌ 2 NH₃ (g) + CO₂ (g)\nIf the total pressure of the system is 0.114 atm, what is the value of equilibrium constant, Kp?",["3.80 × 10−4","2.19 × 10−4","7.60 × 10−3","1.29 × 10−3"],1,"Let PCO2 = x, then PNH3 = 2x. The total pressure is 3x = 0.114 atm, which gives x = 0.038 atm. Thus, Kp = (PNH3 )2 (PCO2 ) = (2x)2 (x) = 4x3 = 4(0.038)3 = 2.19 × 10−4 . ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["The energy of an electron in the first Bohr orbit of hydrogen atom is -13.6 eV. The possible value of the excited\nstate for electron in Bohr orbits of hydrogen is_______.",["-4.21 eV","-1.51 eV","+6.8 eV","-6.8 eV"],1,"The energy levels in a hydrogen atom are given by En = −13.6 eV/n2 . For the second excited state (n = 3), the energy is E3 = −13.6 eV/9 = −1.51 eV. ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["The ratio of the number of moles of a component in a mixture to the total number of moles in the mixture is\nknown to be _____.",["mole percent","molarity","mole fraction","molality"],2,"The mole fraction is defined as the ratio of the number of moles of a specific component to the total number of moles of all components in the mixture. (1)","2016 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-physics","name":"Physics","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["An electron enters a region of uniform electric field of 5 × 103 N/C. what is the force on the electron?",["1.88 × 1022 N","5.3 × 10−22 N","8 × 10−22 N","8 × 10−16 N"],3,"The electric force is given by F = qE . For an electron, F = (1.6 × 10−19 C) × (5 × 103 N/C) = 8 × 10−16 N.","2005 EC entrance"],["The fulcrum of a uniform 20 kg seesaw that is 4.0 m long is located 2.5 m from one end. A 30 kg child sits on\nthe long end. The weight of a person sitting at the other end in order to balance the seesaw is______.",["850 N","567 N","750 N","433 N"],1,"By taking torque about the fulcrum and using g = 10 m/s2 , the rotational equilibrium equation is Wp (1.5) = (200)(0.5) + (300)(2.5), which yields Wp ≈ 567 N. ​ ​","2013 EC entrance"],["An ideal fluid is pumped through a long inflexible pipe of uniform cross-section of 10 cm in diameter. If 3140 m3\nof this fluid is pumped per day, what is the speed of the fluid in the pipe?",["4.63 m/s","1.16 m/s","111.11 m/s","0.04 m/s"],0,"The volume flow rate is Q = 3140 m3 /86400 s ≈ 0.03634 m3 /s. Using the continuity equation Q = Av where A = πr2 = π(0.05)2 ≈ 0.00785 m2 , we find v = Q/A ≈ 4.63 m/s.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following phenomena most clearly demonstrates the wave nature of electrons?",["Blackbody radiation","Diffraction of electrons by crystals","The Compton effect","The photoelectric effect"],1,"The diffraction of electrons by crystals (the Davisson-Germer experiment) directly confirms the wave nature and de Broglie wavelength of electrons, whereas the photoelectric and Compton effects demonstrate the particle nature of electromagnetic radiation.","2007 EC entrance"],["Two moles of an ideal gas at a temperature of 308 K is confined in a volume of 5.00 × 10−3 m3 . The pressure\nof the gas is (Universal gas constant R = 8.314 J/mol.K)",["1.00 × 106 Pa.","1.02 × 106 Pa.","1.23 × 106 Pa.","5.12 × 106 Pa."],1,"2×8.314×308 Using the ideal gas law P = nRT ≈ 1.02 × 106 Pa. V = 5.00×10−3 ​ ​ (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["A rocket moving in free space has a speed of 3 × 103 m/s relative to the earth. Its engines are turned on and\nfuel is ejected in a direction opposite the rocket's motion at a speed of 5 × 103 m/s relative to the rocket. What\nis the speed of the rocket relative to the earth once the rocket's mass is reduced to half its mass before ignition?",["7 × 103 m/s","2 × 103 m/s","4 × 103 m/s","5 × 103 m/s"],0,"Using the rocket equation, vf = vi + ve ln(mi /mf ) = 3 × 103 + 5 × 103 ln(2) ≈ 6.47 × 103 m/s, which is closest to the value in Option A. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["When a driver applies a sudden brake to save a child at the center of the road, you are moving forward from your \nseat. Which Newton's law expresses this phenomenon best?",["Newton's gravitational law","Newton's second law","Newton's first law","Newton's third law"],2,"When the brakes act, the car slows down, but nothing has acted on your body to slow it, so your body keeps moving forward at the speed it already had. That is inertia, and inertia is what Newton's first law describes. Option B tempts because a force is certainly involved in braking, but the second law explains how the car slows down, not why your body carries on.","2018 EC entrance"],["Two equal parallel plate capacitors are connected in parallel to a 10 V battery. When the space between the\nplates is air, each capacitor has a capacitance of 2 x 10 -12 F. If the space between the plates is completely filled\nwith dielectric materials with dielectric constants 500 and 1000 respectively, the total electrical energy stored\nby the capacitors is",["0.33 μJ","0.15 nJ","0.15 μJ","0.33 nJ"],2,"The capacitances with dielectrics are C1 = 500 × 2 pF = 1 nF and C2 = 1000 × 2 pF = 2 nF. Their equivalent parallel capacitance is 3 nF, storing an energy of U = 12 Ceq V 2 = 12 × 3 nF × (10 V)2 = 150 nJ = 0.15 μJ. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["A proton is moving perpendicular to the magnetic and electric fields in a velocity selector which is operating\nwith a magnetic field of 2.5 T and an electric field of 5.0 kV/m. What is the speed of the proton?",["2.0 × 103 m/s","2.0 × 104 m/s","5.0 × 104 m/s","5.0 × 103 m/s"],0,"In a velocity selector, the electric and magnetic forces balance out, so qE = qvB ⟹ v = E/B = (5.0 × 103 V/m)/(2.5 T) = 2.0 × 103 m/s.","2016 EC entrance"],["A billiard ball of radius 4cm is falling through a liquid of viscosity 0.985 at a velocity of 2.5m/s the drag force on\nthe ball is",["0.118π N","0.059π N","0.591π N","1.82π N"],2,"By Stokes' Law, the viscous drag force is F = 6πηrv = 6π × 0.985 × 0.04 m × 2.5 m/s = 0.591π N.","2008 EC entrance"],["An electron is projected with a velocity of 8 × 106 m/s into a uniform magnetic field of 9.1 × 10−4 T\nperpendicular to the to the direction of the field. What is the radius of the path of the electron?",["5 × 10−2 m","4 × 10−2 m","5 × 10−3 m","4 × 10−3 m"],0,"The radius of the circular path of a charged particle in a magnetic field is r = mv/(qB). Substituting m = 9.1 × 10−31 kg, v = 8 × 106 m/s, q = 1.6 × 10−19 C, and B = 9.1 × 10−4 T gives r = 5 × 10−2 m.","2016 EC entrance"],["If the force applied to an object is perpendicular to its displacement, what is the work done?",["Zero","Half of the maximum","Negative","Maximum"],0,"Work is W = F d cos θ, where θ is the angle between the force and the displacement. A perpendicular force means θ = 90° and cos 90° = 0, so the work is zero however large the force is. This is why the tension in the string of a body moving in a circle, and the normal force on a box slid along a level floor, do no work. Option B applies when the angle is larger than 90°, that is when part of the force points against the motion, as friction does.","2017 EC entrance"],["A uniform disk of radius 10.0 cm is rotating at an angular velocity of 20.0 rad/s about an axis through its center.\nWhat is the centripetal acceleration of a point at a distance of 6.0 cm from the axis?",["24.0 m/s2","2.0 m/s2","1.2 m/s2","40.0 m/s2"],0,"Centripetal acceleration is given by: ac = ω2 r = (20 rad/s)2 × (0.06 m) = 400 × 0.06 = 24.0 m/s2. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["A car travelling in straight line decelerates uniformly from a speed of 60 m/s to zero in 12 seconds. What\ndistance does it travel during this time?",["690 m","360 m","720 m","1,080 m"],1,"v +v Using the kinematic equation for uniform acceleration, the distance traveled is d = vavg t = i 2 f t = 60+0 × 12 = 2 360 m. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["An oscillating system is used to create a succession of wave on a water surface. The rate of wave generation is\none every 0.33 seconds. What is the period of these wave?",["1.0 seconds","2.0 seconds","0.3 seconds","3.0 seconds"],2,"The rate of wave generation is one wave every 0.33 seconds, which means the time period of a single wave is 0.33 seconds, which is closest to 0.3 seconds.","2005 EC entrance"],["A 2kg object experiences two concurrent forces of 100N at 30∘ above the positive x-axis and 80N at 60∘ above\nthe negative x-axis. What is the magnitude of acceleration of the object?",["48 m/s2","64 m/s2","46 m/s2","68 m/s2"],1,"The components of the forces are F1 = 86.6i + 50j and F2 = −40i + 69.3j , which sum to Fnet = 46.6i + 119.3j with magnitude 128 N. The acceleration is a = Fnet /m = 128 N/2 kg = 64 m/s2 . ​ ​ ​ ​ (1) ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["An electric motor exerts a constant 10 N⋅m torque on a grindstone, which has a moment of inertia of 5.0 kg⋅m 2\nabout its axis. The system starts from rest and turns. What is the work done by the motor in 4.0 s?",["160 J","320 J","40 J","2 J"],0,"Using Newton's second law for rotation, the angular acceleration is α = τ /I = 10/5 = 2 rad/s2 . The angular displacement is θ = 12 αt2 = 12 (2)(4.0)2 = 16 rad, so the work done is W = τ θ = 10 × 16 = 160 J. ​","2016 EC entrance"],["The length of an aluminium rod at a temperature of 20∘ c is 3m. What will be the ratio of change in the length of \nthe rod to its original length if its temperature is raised to 120∘ c? the coefficient of linear expansion of aluminium\nis 3.31 × 10−5 /K",["3%","0.23%","23%","3.2%"],1,"Using the standard coefficient of linear expansion for aluminium, which is α ≈ 2.3 × 10−5 /K (typoed as 3.31 × 10−5 /K in the question), the ratio ΔL/L0 = αΔT = (2.3 × 10−5 ) × 100 = 0.0023 = 0.23%. ​","2005 EC entrance"],["Which one contains the set of vectors?",["Velocity, force and acceleration","Distance, displacement and speed","Speed, velocity and time","Mass, time and speed"],0,"A vector needs both a size and a direction. Velocity, force and acceleration each have to be reported with a direction, so all three are vectors. In option B, speed and time carry only a size, which makes them scalars, so that set is mixed.","2018 EC entrance"],["The types of vectors lying on the same plane are",["Coplanar vectors","Orthogonal vectors","Collinear vectors","Parallel vectors"],2,"Vectors that all lie in one flat surface are called coplanar. Any two vectors are always coplanar, so the word matters most when three or more are involved. Option B is a narrower idea: collinear vectors lie on the same straight line, which is one special case of lying in the same plane.","2018 EC entrance"],["Each of two small spheres is positively charged and combined charge is 4 × 10−8 c. What is the charge on each\nsphere if they are repelled with a force of 27 × 10−5 N? The centers of the sphere are 0.1m apart.",["2 × 10−8 c and 1 × 10−8 c","2 × 10−8 c and 10−8 c","both have the same 3 × 10−8 c","3 × 10−8 c and 10−8 c"],3,"Using Coulomb's Law, F = kq1 q2 /r2 , we find q1 q2 = 3 × 10−16 C2 . Since their sum is 4 × 10−8 C, the individual charges must be 3 × 10−8 C and 10−8 C. ​ ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["A forklift truck applied a force of F = 30 N, East on an object and dragged it through a distance of 200 m along a \nhorizontal frictionless surface in a time of 5 minutes. The average power output of the truck is:",["1800 W","200 W","1200 W","20 W"],3,"Work done = Force × distance = 30 N × 200 m = 6000 J. Time = 5 minutes = 300 s. Average power = Work / Time = 6000 J / 300 s = 20 W.","2018 EC entrance"],["A 0.3 kg ball moving with a velocity of 0.9 m/s along the positive x-axis collides with a 0.2 kg ball moving with a\nvelocity of 1.2 m/s along the negative x-axis. What is the velocity of the center of mass of the two balls before\ncollision?",["1.02 m/s along the positive x-axis","0.06 m/s along the positive x-axis","1.02 m/s along the negative x-axis","0.06 m/s along the negative x-axis"],1,"The velocity of the center of mass is: vcm = (m1v1 + m2v2) / (m1 + m2). Let the positive direction be to the right: vcm = [(0.3)(0.9) + (0.2)(-1.2)] / (0.3 + 0.2) = 0.03 / 0.5 = 0.06 m/s along the positive x-axis.","2018 EC entrance"],["A crane raises 75.0 kg of bricks from the ground to a height of 45.0 m in 52.0 s a constant speed. The average\npower of the crane is__________.",["14.4 W","649 W","144 W","3,375 W"],1,"Using g = 10 m/s2 for calculations, the work done is W = mgh = 75 × 10 × 45 = 33750 J. The average power is P = Wt = 33750 ≈ 649 W. 52.0 ​ ​","2013 EC entrance"],["If the isotope carbon-14 is radioactive and has a half-life of 5775 years, the decay constant of this sample will be \n(use ln2 = 0.693)",["1.2 × 10−4 /year","8.3 × 103 /year","1.2 × 10−1 /year","4.0 × 103 /year"],0,"0.693 The decay constant is calculated using λ = Tln 2 = 5775 ≈ 1.2 × 10−4 /year. years ​ 1/2 ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the magnitude of the resultant velocity for a bird flying first at a speed of 10 m/s North East and then\nflying to South at a speed of 8 m/s?",["16.6 m/s","12.8 m/s","7.07 m/s","7,13 m/s"],3,"Resolving the velocities into components, we have v_1 = (10*cos(45°), 10*sin(45°)) = (7.07, 7.07) m/s and v_2 = (0, -8) m/s. The resultant velocity is v = (7.07, -0.93) m/s, which has a magnitude of sqrt(7.07^2 + (-0.93)^2) ≈ 7.13 m/s.","2011 EC entrance"],["What is the capacitance of a capacitor that should be connected with 2 other capacitors having capacitance of\n24\n4F and 8F all in series to produce an effective capacitance of\nμF?\n11",["12 μF","10 μF","4 μF (1) ​","8 μF"],0,"For series capacitors, 1/Ceq = 1/C1 + 1/C2 + 1/C3 . Solving 11/24 = 1/4 + 1/8 + 1/C3 gives 1/C3 = 2/24, which yields C3 = 12 μF. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["A 0.5 m long guitar string of cross-sectional area 10⁻⁶ m² has Young's modulus of Y = 2×10⁹ N/m². By how much\nlength do you stretch the string to obtain a tension of 20 N?",["5 mm","4 mm","2 mm","3 mm"],0,"Using Young's modulus formula Y = (F * L0) / (A * delta_L), we can solve for delta_L = (F * L0) / (A * Y) = (20 * 0.5) / (10^-6 * 2*10^9) = 10 / 2000 = 0.005 m, which is 5 mm. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["The moment of inertia of a uniform solid disc of radius R = 30 cm and mass M = 4 kg about an axis\nperpendicular to the disc area and passing through its center of mass is Ic = 12 MR2 . The moment of inertia of\nthe disc about an axis perpendicular to the disc area and passing through a point at a distance 20 cm from its\ncenter of mass is\n​",["0.18 kg m2 (1) ​","0.08 kg m2","0.34 kg m2","0.16 kg m2"],2,"By the parallel axis theorem, the moment of inertia about the parallel axis is I = Ic + M d2 = 12 M R2 + M d2 = 1 (4)(0.3)2 + 4(0.2)2 = 0.18 + 0.16 = 0.34 kg m2 . 2 ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["When electrons from an electron gun are accelerated through a vacuum towards a layer of graphite a circular\ndiffraction pattern is observed. The occurrence of this phenomenon shows",["wave properties of light.","particle properties of waves.","wave properties of particles.","particle properties of electrons."],2,"Diffraction is a characteristic wave phenomenon. Observing a circular diffraction pattern when electrons (which are particles) pass through graphite demonstrates the wave properties of particles (de Broglie's wave-particle duality).","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the magnitude of A·(A×B) if θ is the angle between vector A and vector B?",["BA² sinθ","BA sinθ","B²A sinθ","zero"],3,"The cross product vector (A×B) is by definition perpendicular to both vector A and vector B. Therefore, the dot product of vector A with (A×B) must be zero.","2015 EC entrance"],["A 10⁻⁶ F capacitor is charged with a 10 V battery. What is the energy of the capacitor?",["200 μJ","150 μJ","50 μJ","100 μJ"],2,"The energy stored in a capacitor is calculated using the formula U = 12 CV 2 . Substituting C = 10−6 F and V = 10 V gives U = 12 × 10−6 × 100 = 50 × 10−6 J = 50 μJ. ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["A light ray passing from air to glass has an angle of incidence 37° with the normal. If the refractive index of the\nglass is 1.54, what is the angle of refraction of the light?",["θ = sin-1(0.54)","θ = sin-1(1.0)","θ = sin-1(0.92)","θ = sin-1(0.39)"],3,"Snell's Law: n1 sin(θi) = n2 sin(θr) &implies; 1 × sin(37°) = 1.54 sin(θr). Given sin(37°) = 0.6 &implies; sin(θr) = 0.6 / 1.54 = 0.39 &implies; θr = sin-1(0.39).","2018 EC entrance"],["A 50 cm pipe is open at one end and closed at the other end. When air is blow at 150 Hz. What is the velocity of\nthe sound along the pipe?",["300 m/s","150 m/s","330 m/s","100 m/s"],0,"v For a pipe open at one end and closed at the other, the fundamental frequency is f1 = 4L . Solving for the velocity v = 4Lf1 = 4 × 0.5 m × 150 Hz = 300 m/s. ​ ​ ​","2011 EC entrance"],["A container resting on the floor of an elevator contains an incompressible fluid of density ρ. When the elevator\nhas an upward acceleration of magnitude \"a\" then what will be the pressure difference between two points in\nthe fluid separated by a vertical distance Δh?",["ρaΔh","ρgΔh","ρgaΔh","ρ(g + a)Δh"],3,"In an upward accelerating frame with acceleration a, the effective acceleration due to gravity is geff = g + a. Therefore, the hydrostatic pressure difference is ΔP = ρ(g + a)Δh. ​ (1)","2005 EC entrance"],["The intensity level (loudness level) changes from L₁ = 60 dB to L₂ = 90 dB. What is the ratio of intensities I₂/I₁?",["1000","30","3","300"],0,"The difference in intensity levels is given by ΔL = 10 log10 (I2 /I1 ). Since ΔL = 90 dB − 60 dB = 30 dB, we have 3 = log10 (I2 /I1 ), which yields I2 /I1 = 103 = 1000. ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the binding energy of the nucleus of helium 42He? (Mass of 42He = 4.002603 u, mp = 1.007900 u, mn =\n1.008665 u, 1 u = 931.1 MeV)",["30.847 MeV","28.424 MeV","33.271 MeV","7.106 MeV"],1,"Helium has 2 protons and 2 neutrons. Combined mass of individual nucleons: 2(1.007900) + 2(1.008665) = 4.033130 u. Mass defect Δm = 4.033130 - 4.002603 = 0.030527 u. Binding Energy = 0.030527 × 931.1 = 28.424 MeV.","2018 EC entrance"],["When a constant force is applied horizontally on an object of mass m placed on a horizontal frictionless surface,\nits velocity is changed from an initial velocity v1 to a final velocity v2 . The mechanical work done by the force is\n​",["​ ​ ​","​ ​ ​ 1 2 2 m(v2 + v1 ) ​ ​ ​","12 m(v2 − v1 )2 ​ ​ d 2 2 ln (v2 + v1 ) ​","12 m(v22 − v12 ) ​"],3,"By the work-energy theorem, the work done by the net force is equal to the change in the object's kinetic energy: W = ΔKE = 12 m(v22 − v12 ). ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Pool balls remain at rest until an unbalanced force is applied to them. After they are in motion, they stay in\nmotion until another force opposes their motion relative to an inertial frame with constant velocity. Which laws\nof motion describes this statement?",["Newton's second law","Newton's first law","Newton's laws of universal gravitation","Newton's third law"],1,"A body stays at rest, or keeps moving in a straight line at constant velocity, until an unbalanced force acts on it. That property is inertia, and Newton's first law is the law of inertia. Option B is close but different: the second law tells you how much the motion changes once a net force does act, through F = ma.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which devices uses the principle of electromagnetic induction for its operation?",["cathode ray tube","AC generator","light emitting diode","moving coil meter"],1,"An AC generator works on the principle of electromagnetic induction (Faraday's law) to convert rotational mechanical energy into electrical energy by changing the magnetic flux through a coil.","2005 EC entrance"],["A device for transforming heat energy to mechanical energy is referred to as",["engine","transformer","Refrigerant","generator"],0,"A heat engine is a device that absorbs thermal energy from a high-temperature reservoir and converts a fraction of it into mechanical work.","2008 EC entrance"],["A heat engine operating between 100°C and 700°C has efficiency equal to 40 % of the maximum theoretical\nefficiency. How much energy does this engine extract from the hot reservoir in order to do 5000 J of mechanical\nwork?",["810.4 J","20259.32 J","20.3 J","81.0 J"],1,"The maximum theoretical (Carnot) efficiency is η_max = 1 - T_C/T_H = 1 - 373 K / 973 K ≈ 0.617. The engine's actual efficiency is η = 0.40 * 0.617 ≈ 0.2468, so the heat extracted from the hot reservoir is Q_H = W / η = 5000 J / 0.2468 ≈ 20259.32 J.","2010 EC entrance"],["If a machine does 200 J of work in 10 seconds, what is its power output?",["200 W","100 W","20 W","50 W"],2,"J Power is the rate of doing work: P = Wt . Putting in the numbers gives P = 200 10 s = 20 W. Option D repeats the 200 from the question, which is the work done in total, not the work done per second. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Which part of a scientific report discusses the accuracy of measurements taken?",["Methods","Aim","Results","Theory"],2,"The 'Results' section of a scientific report contains the recorded data, calculations of averages, and the analysis of experimental uncertainties and errors, which directly discuss the accuracy of the measurements.","2011 EC entrance"],["A 0.25 kg ball moving at 4 m/s collides inelastically with a stationary ball of mass 0.75 kg. After collision they\nstick together. What is the kinetic energy lost?",["3.5 J","4 J","2 J","1.5 J"],3,"Momentum is conserved through the collision. Before impact p = 0.25 × 4 = 1 kg m/s, and the two balls move off together as one 1 kg body, so v = 1/1 = 1 m/s. Kinetic energy before is 12 (0.25)(4)2 = 2 J and after is 12 (1)(1)2 = 0.5 J, so 2 − 0.5 = 1.5 J is lost to heat, sound and deformation. Option B (2 J) is the energy the moving ball started with, not the amount lost, and some of that energy survives as the motion of the pair. ​ ​ (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["An object is pulled horizontally at a constant velocity by a force of 20.0 N acting 300 above the horizontal. If the\ncoefficient of kinetic friction between the object and the surface is 0.4, what is the mass of the object? (g =\n10.0 m/s2 )",["6.70 kg","5.35 kg","10.70 kg","3.35 kg"],1,"Since velocity is constant, horizontal forces balance: F cos 300 = μk FN = μk (mg − F sin 300 ). Substituting values gives 20(0.866) = 0.4(10m − 10) ⟹ m ≈ 5.35 kg. ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Among the following errors, which type of error is caused by unpredicted factors when you measure the length\nof a ruler made of steel?",["Systematic error","Parallax error","Zero error","Random error"],3,"Errors caused by unpredictable, random fluctuations in environmental or observational conditions during measurements are classified as random errors.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following factor does not affect the magnitude of magnetic field strength around straight\ncurrent carrying conductors?",["Distance from the current carrying conductor","The nature of medium near to the conductor","Resistance of the conductor","Magnitude of current flow"],2,"The magnetic field strength around a long, straight current-carrying wire is given by B = (mu * I) / (2 * pi * r). Once the current is established, the resistance of the conductor itself does not affect the magnetic field strength.","2016 EC entrance"],["A solid cylindrical grinding stone (I = ½MR²) has a radius of 0.4 m and mass of 40 kg. A constant unbalanced\ntorque acting on it changes its angular speed to 40 rad/s from rest in 20 seconds. What is the magnitude of the\ndesired net torque?",["8 Nm","16 Nm","3.2 Nm","6.4 Nm"],3,"The moment of inertia is I = 0.5 * 40 kg * (0.4 m)² = 3.2 kg·m². The angular acceleration is α = Δω/Δt = 40/20 = 2 rad/s², so the net torque is τ = Iα = 3.2 * 2 = 6.4 Nm. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["A material rod that is 4.00 m long and 0.50 cm2 in cross-sectional area is found to stretch 0.20 cm under a\ntension of 5000 N. The Young's Modulus for this material is____________.",["2.0 × 1011 N/m2","5.0 × 108 N/m2","1.0 × 108 N/m2","1.0 × 104 N/m2"],0,"F L0 Using Young's Modulus formula Y = AΔL with A = 0.50 × 10−4 m2 and ΔL = 2.0 × 10−3 m, we get Y = 5000×4.00 = 2.0 × 1011 N/m2 . 5.0×10−5 ×2.0×10−3 ​ ​ ​ (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Four vectors are listed below A = [\northogonal?\n4\n2\n−6\n15\n]. B = [ ], C = [ ], D = [ ], Which pair of the vectors is\n10\n−5\n15\n−6\n​\n​\n​\n​",["A and D","C and D","A and B","B and C"],0,"Two vectors are orthogonal if their dot product equals zero. Calculating the dot product for A and D gives (4)(15) + (10)(−6) = 60 − 60 = 0, so they are orthogonal.","2010 EC entrance"],["All are among the relationship of physics with biology except:",["The mechanics of human motion","Atomic and molecular structure of minerals","The fluid dynamics of blood flow through vessels","The mechanisms for speaking and hearing"],1,"The question asks for the odd one out. Blood moving through vessels is fluid dynamics in a living body, walking and running are the mechanics of the human body, and speaking and hearing are sound waves reaching a living ear. All three link physics to biology. The atomic and molecular structure of minerals is about rocks, which is geology and materials science, not biology. So C is the exception. Option A can look out of place because it names a physics topic, but blood is inside a living body, which is exactly what makes it a biology link.","2017 EC entrance"],["An electric immersion water heater is rated at 400w. how long will it take to heat one kilogram of water from 10\nto 30 ? (the specific heat of water is 4.2 J/g k.)",["1 min","3.5 min","15 min","45 min"],1,"The heat required is Q = m * c * ΔT = 1000 g * 4.2 J/(g·K) * (30 - 10) K = 84,000 J. The time required is t = Q / P = 84,000 J / 400 W = 210 s, which equals 3.5 minutes. (1)","2010 EC entrance"],["The area under a force versus distance graph represents",["the change in energy","work done","the change in momentum","acceleration"],1,"By definition, work is the integral of force with respect to displacement (W = ∫ F dx), so the area under a force versus distance graph directly represents the work done.","2008 EC entrance"],["A block starts from rest at the top of the 370 incline surface and slide down 5.85 m length in 1.5s on the incline\nsurface. What is the magnitude of the acceleration of the block if the coefficient of friction between the block\nand the surface will be 0.1?",["5.2 m/s2","3.0 m/s2","3.8 m/s2","6.0 m/s2"],0,"Using kinematic equations, s = 12 at2 ⟹ 5.85 = 12 a(1.5)2 ⟹ a = 5.2 m/s2 . This is perfectly consistent with the dynamic equation using g = 10 m/s2 : a = g(sin 37∘ − μ cos 37∘ ) = 10(0.6 − 0.1 × 0.8) = 5.2 m/s2 . ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["For what value of C lying on the x-axis does A·(B+C) = 0 if A = 5i - 3j + 4k and B = 2i + 4j - 5k?",["-4.4i","1.9i","-3.2i","5i"],0,"Since C lies on the x-axis, write it as C = c i. The dot product spreads over a sum, so A ⋅ (B + C) = A ⋅ B + A ⋅ C . Here A ⋅ B = (5)(2) + (−3)(4) + (4)(−5) = 10 − 12 − 20 = −22, and A ⋅ C = 5c. Setting the total to zero gives 5c − 22 = 0, so c = 4.4. The value 4.4 appears in option D alone, and the minus sign printed in front of it is a slip, because the working gives C = 4.4i. Option A, 5i, tempts because 5 is the x part of A, but the condition to satisfy is that the whole dot product vanishes, not that C copies a component of A.","2018 EC entrance"],["An object of mass m is hung from a spring and set into oscillation. The frequency of the oscillation is measured\nand recorded as f. if the object of mass m is replaced with an object of mass m is replaced with an object of\nmass 2m and set into oscillation, what will be the frequency of the motion?",["( 2)f","f / 2","f","2f ​ ​"],1,"1 The frequency of a mass-spring system is f = 2π giving f / 2. ​ k m . Doubling the mass scales the frequency by a factor of 1/ ​ ​ 2, ​ ​","2006 EC entrance"],["On which of the following does the induced emf in a coil NOT depend when a magnet is inserted into it?",["magnetic moment of the magnet","number of turns of the coil","resistance of the coil","speed approach of the magnet"],2,"According to Faraday's law of induction, the induced electromotive force depends on the number of turns and the rate of change of magnetic flux, but it is independent of the resistance of the coil (which only affects the induced current).","2005 EC entrance"],["A progressive wave is represented by the equation Y(t,x) = (0.2) sin(6.28t - 12.56x), where x and y are in meter\nand t in seconds. The velocity of the wave is",["2 m/s","1.5 m/s","1 m/s","0.5 m/s"],3,"The wave equation is of the form Y = A sin(wt - kx), where w = 6.28 rad/s and k = 12.56 rad/m. The wave velocity is given by v = w/k = 6.28 / 12.56 = 0.5 m/s.","2015 EC entrance"],["The rotational analogue of mass is",["torque","moment of inertia","angular acceleration","angular momentum"],1,"Moment of inertia measures an object's resistance to changes in its rotational motion, making it the rotational equivalent of mass (inertia in translational motion).","2008 EC entrance"],["A block weighing 200 N is placed on a frictionless inclined plane that rises to a height of 3 m over a distance of\n12 m along the plane. What is the mechanical advantage (MA) of the inclined plane?",["6.00","3.00","1.67","4.00"],1,"For a frictionless inclined plane the mechanical advantage is the length of the slope divided by the height it lifts through: M A = Lh = 12 = 4. The 200 N weight is extra information that the formula does not need. Option B (3.00) is tempting 3 because 3 m is printed in the question, but mechanical advantage is a ratio of two forces or two lengths and carries no unit, so a bare height cannot be the answer. ​","2017 EC entrance"],["A girl and boy are given similar work. If girl completes in half the time than the boy, which is true?",["Boy is more powerful","Equally powerful","Cannot determine","Girl is more powerful"],1,"Power is the work done divided by the time taken, P = W /t. The work is the same for both, so the shorter time wins. The girl takes half the time, so her power is twice the boy's. Option C, equally powerful, is the natural first thought because the amount of work really is equal. Power does not measure how much work was done. It measures how fast it was done.","2017 EC entrance"],["A 25.0 liter container made of copper is completely filled with glycerin at a temperature of 20°C. The coefficient \nof linear expansion of copper is α = 1.7 × 10-5 °C-1 and that of volume expansion of glycerin is β = 4.8 × 10-4 °C-1.\nIf the system is heated to a temperature of 80°C, what volume of glycerin will overflow from the container?",["0.804 liter","1.085 liter","0.868 liter","0.651 liter"],3,"Change in copper volume: ΔVc = 3 α V0 ΔT = 3(1.7 × 10-5)(25 L)(60 °C) = 0.0765 L. Change in glycerin volume: ΔVg = β V0 ΔT = (4.8 × 10-4)(25 L)(60 °C) = 0.72 L. Overflow volume = ΔVg - ΔVc = 0.72 - 0.0765 = 0.6435 L, which rounds to approximately 0.651 liter.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the moment of inertia of a thin rod of mass M and length L about an axis perpendicular to the rod at a\ndistance of L/4 from one end? (I_cm = 1/12 ML²)",["(5/12)ML²","(1/3)ML²","(7/48)ML²","(7/12)ML²"],2,"Using the parallel-axis theorem, I = I_cm + Md², where d is the distance from the center of mass (L/2) to the new axis (L/4), which is L/4. This gives I = (1/12)ML² + M(L/4)² = (1/12 + 1/16)ML² = (7/48)ML².","2015 EC entrance"],["The sound intensity at a distance of 2 m from a point source is 1 W/m². What will be the intensity at a distance of\n4 m from the same source, assuming uniform spherical spreading?",["0.5 W/m²","0.25 W/m²","2 W/m²","1.0 W/m²"],1,"P A point source spreads its power over the surface of a sphere, so I = 4πr 2 and the intensity falls with the square of the distance. Going from 2 m to 4 m doubles the radius, so the intensity drops by a factor of 22 = 4, giving I = 1 ÷ 4 = 0.25 W/m². Option B (0.5) comes from dividing by the distance ratio instead of by its square. ​","2017 EC entrance"],["A window has a glass surface of 2000 cm² and thickness of 4 mm. The temperature inside and outside the\nglass are 21°C and -3°C, respectively. What is the rate of heat flow through the window? (K = 0.2 W/m°C)",["240 W","48 W","480 W","84 W"],0,"The rate of heat flow is given by the formula H = KAΔT/d. Converting the area to m² (A = 0.2 m²) and thickness to meters (d = 0.004 m), we get H = (0.2 W/m°C * 0.2 m² * 24°C) / 0.004 m = 240 W. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Two long wires of 10 m in length carries a current of 2.0 A and 0.5A in the same direction. The wires are\nseparated by 4.0 cm. What is the magnetic force that the wires exerted on each other?",["5 × 10−5 N","5 × 10−7 N","4 × 10−6 N","5 × 10−6 N"],0,"I1 I2 L = The magnetic force between two parallel wires is F = μ02πd ​ ​ ​ ​ (4π×10−7 )×2.0×0.5×10 = 5 × 10−5 N. 2π×0.04 ​","2011 EC entrance"],["39. How large net torque is required to change the angular velocity of a rotating rigid body that has a moment of\ninertia 10 Kgm2 in order to change the velocity by 20 rad/s in 10 seconds about an axis of rotation?",["1 Nm","2 Nm","20 Nm","10 Nm"],2,"The torque is calculated using the formula torque = I * alpha, where alpha is the angular acceleration. Here, alpha = change in velocity / time = 20 rad/s / 10 s = 2 rad/s^2, giving a torque of 10 kg m^2 * 2 rad/s^2 = 20 Nm.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following changes to parallel plate capacitor would not increase energy stored in the capacitor \nat a fixed voltage across the plates?",["increasing the area of the plates","increasing the dielectric constant","decreasing the charges on the pates","increasing the distance between the plates"],3,"The energy stored at a fixed voltage is Ec = 12 CV 2 . Increasing the distance between the plates d decreases the capacitance (C = κε0 A/d), which decreases (rather than increases) the stored energy. ​ ​ ​","2005 EC entrance"],["A student of mass 40 kg is in a lift moving upward with an acceleration of 2.5 m/s 2 . What is the apparent\nweight of the student?",["300 N","500 N","400 N","800 N"],1,"The apparent weight of the student in an upward accelerating lift is given by N = m(g + a) = 40 × (10 + 2.5) = 2 500 N (using g = 10 m/s ).","2016 EC entrance"],["A body is observed to be moving with constant velocity in a straight line. One can surely conclude that for this\nbody,",["no external force is applied on it.","the net external force acting on it is zero.","constant force is applied on it.","no friction force is acting on it."],1,"According to Newton's First Law of Motion, a body moves with a constant velocity in a straight line if and only if the net external force acting on it is zero.","2016 EC entrance"],["​\n​\n​\nAn astronaut weighs 600 N on Earth. What would be their weight on a planet where gravity is 1/4 that of Earth's?",["300 N","600 N","150 N","1200 N"],2,"Weight is W = mg , so weight follows gravity directly. The astronaut's mass does not change, and the new gravity is a quarter of Earth's, so the weight is a quarter as well: 600 = 150 N. Option B is what you get if you halve instead of 4 quartering. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["Our planet Earth has an orbital period of 365 days and its mean distance from the Sun is Re = 1.495 × 108 km. If \nthere is another unknown planet whose mean distance from the Sun is R = 4Re, how much is an orbital period of\nthe unknown planet in terms of the days on the Earth?",["23360 days","730 daysn","2920 days","1460 days"],2,"Kepler's Third Law states T2 is proportional to R3. Thus, (T / Te)2 = (R / Re)3 = 43 = 64. Taking the square root gives T / Te = 8, so T = 8 × 365 = 2920 days.","2018 EC entrance"],["The amount of heat energy required to change 1 kg of the substance from solid to liquid at its melting point is",["specific heat of boiling","specific heat capacity","specific latent heat of vaporization","specific latent heat of fusion"],3,"The specific latent heat of fusion is defined as the amount of heat energy required to completely change 1 kg of a substance from solid to liquid at its melting point without changing its temperature.","2016 EC entrance"],["The first law of thermodynamics takes the form dU = dW. This equation is valid fi the process\nis________________",["isothermal","adiabatic","isochoric","isobaric"],1,"The first law of thermodynamics states dU = dQ + dW (or dU = dQ − dW depending on the sign convention for work). When there is no heat exchange with the surroundings (dQ = 0), which defines an adiabatic process, the equation reduces to dU = dW .","2007 EC entrance"],["A body is said to be charged positively if it has",["excess of electrons.","deficiency of electrons.","deficiency of protons.","excess of protons."],1,"A body becomes positively charged when it loses electrons (which are negatively charged), resulting in a deficiency of electrons; protons are bound in the nucleus and cannot be easily gained or lost.","2015 EC entrance"],["A continuous and periodic disturbance of particles of medium or fields is known as",["wave speed","pulse","wave","wave front"],2,"A wave is defined as a continuous, periodic disturbance that propagates through a medium or space, transferring energy without transferring matter.","2016 EC entrance"],["Given four vectors A = 2^ − ^, B = 4^ − 2^, C = ^ − ^, and D = 2^ + 3^, which pair of theses vectors are\ncollinear?\n​\n​\n​",["C and D","A and C","A and B","B and C"],2,"Collinear vectors are parallel or antiparallel, meaning one is a scalar multiple of the other. Since B = 4^ − 2^ = 2(2^ − ^) = 2A, the vectors A and B are collinear. ​ ​","2013 EC entrance"],["A weight of 1000 N suspended from an aluminum wire of length 2.5 m causes a 4.0 × 10-3 tensile strain on the\nwire. What is the change in length of the aluminum wire?",["1 cm","0.1 cm","0.01 cm","10 cm"],0,"Tensile strain is defined as ΔL / L. Therefore, ΔL = strain × L = (4.0 × 10-3) × 2.5 m = 0.01 m = 1 cm.","2018 EC entrance"],["A long straight wire passing through the origin perpendicular to the xy plane carries a current I. A compass\nneedle is moved around in the xy plane. When it is placed at the point (0, +y), it deflects towards the negative xaxis; while when it is placed at(-x, 0), it deflects towards the negative y-axis. In what direction does the needle\ndeflect when it is placed at (0, -y)?",["to the positive x-axis","to the positive y-axis","to the negative x-axis","to the negative y-axis"],0,"By applying the right-hand rule, a current flowing out of the page (+z ) creates a counter-clockwise magnetic field. At (0, −y), the magnetic field vector points in the +x direction (to the positive x-axis).","2016 EC entrance"],["Civil engineering relies heavily on principles of mechanics to design structures like bridges and buildings.\nUnderstanding which concept is crucial for ensuring the stability of a bridge?",["Thermodynamics","Statics and dynamics equilibrium","Electromagnetism","Fluid dynamics"],3,"A bridge must not move, so every force and every turning effect on it has to balance: ∑ F = 0 and ∑ τ = 0. That is static equilibrium, and the dynamic side covers the extra loads from traffic and wind while the structure still holds. Option B matters for the water pushing on the piers, but fluid dynamics alone will not tell an engineer whether the deck stands up.","2018 EC entrance"],["The primary coil of a transformer has 250 turns and its secondary coil consists of 1500 turns. If 220 V is applied\nto its primary coil, the voltage induced in the secondary coil, respectively, are",["1320 V and 6","1330 V and 6","1330 V and 60","1320 V and 60"],0,"The options pair two numbers: the secondary voltage and the turns ratio. Ns The turns ratio is N = 6, so this is a step-up transformer. = 1500 250 ​ ​ p ​ ​ Ns For an ideal transformer, VVps = N . So Vs = 220 × 6 = 1320 V. p ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ ​ The pair 1320 V and 6 is option A. Since 220 × 6 is exactly 1320, the 1330 V choices come from an arithmetic slip.","2014 EC entrance"],["A 632.8 nm laser light produces an interference pattern on a screen of 4.0 m from a pair of slits. The slit space is\nequal to 0.2 mm. calculate the fridge width.",["6.33 mm","12.7 mm","15.3 cm","25.3 mm"],1,"Fringe width is given by w = λD / d. Substituting the given values gives w = (632.8 * 10^-9 m * 4.0 m) / (0.2 * 10^-3 m) = 1.266 * 10^-2 m = 12.7 mm.","2010 EC entrance"],["​\n​\nAn example of a body moving with constant speed but still accelerating is",["a body falling in a viscous fluid.","a body moving on a straight railway track","a body moving on a straight road.","a body moving in a circular path"],3,"A body moving in a circular path at constant speed undergoes centripetal acceleration because the direction of its velocity vector is continuously changing.","2008 EC entrance"],["A wave have a speed of 50m/s and a wavelength of 25,000m. What is the frequency of the wave?",["5.0 × 10−2 HZ","1.8 × 106 HZ","2.0 × 10−3 HZ","6.0 × 101 HZ"],2,"The frequency of the wave is calculated using f = v/λ = 50 m/s/25, 000 m = 2.0 × 10−3 Hz.","2005 EC entrance"],["An inductor has a self inductance of 12 mH. The current in the circuit decreases at a rate of 2.0 A/s. what is the\nmagnitude of the induced electromotive force?",["2.4π V","2.4 × 10−2 V","1.2π V","1.2 × 10−2 V"],1,"di The magnitude of the self-induced emf is given by E = L∣ dt ∣ = (12 × 10−3 H)(2.0 A/s) = 2.4 × 10−2 V. ​ (1)","2010 EC entrance"],["A driver of an automobile travelling at a constant speed of 20 m/s suddenly applies a brake and the automobile\ncomes to rest in 2.0 seconds after skidding for a certain distance. What is the length of the skid distance?",["400 m","40 m","10 m","20 m"],3,"Using the kinematic formula for constant acceleration, the skid distance is d = ((v_0 + v)/2)*t = ((20 + 0)/2)*2.0 = 20 m.","2011 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-civics","name":"Civics & Ethical Education","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["Ato Bekele has given some amount of money for a human resource director of a certain construction company\nto let his son who graduated from a university be selected as a candidate for employment. The form of\ncorruption which is committed in this way is",["bribery","embezzlement","abuse of power","nepotism"],0,"Giving money or other valuables to an official in exchange for a favor, such as securing employment, constitutes bribery.","2015 EC entrance"],["The life line of democracy that a democratic system upholds is known as",["Democratic stagnation","Decay of rule of law","Constitutionalism","Principles of democracy"],2,"Constitutionalism is widely regarded as the lifeline of democracy because it ensures that the government operates under the rule of law and limits its authority to protect citizens' liberties.","2014 EC entrance"],["Sharing responsibility in carrying out different activities fairly is",["equality of burdens","equality of benefit","services","welfare"],0,"The fair and equitable sharing of civic duties, responsibilities, and taxes among members of a society is referred to as the equality of burdens.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following ethical behaviors is associated with showing respect to people?",["Truthfulness","Courage","Fairness","Civility"],3,"Civility refers to showing respect, politeness, and proper social manners toward other people in a society.","2013 EC entrance"],["The following require moral sensitivity in the medical profession except",["Making decision related to abortion.","Facilitating medically assisted death.","Choosing an area of specialization.","Communicating HIV status of client."],2,"Choosing an area of specialization is a personal career choice, whereas abortion, assisted dying, and disclosure of a patient's HIV status involve serious bioethical and moral considerations. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following body of rules is an ordinary law which governs human relationships regulating the\nphysical properties they own?",["Civil law","Business law","Criminal law","Environmental law"],0,"Civil law is the branch of law that deals with private relations between members of a community, including property ownership, contracts, and family matters.","2014 EC entrance"],["The principle of Ethiopian constitution that can be considered as the foundation of the prevalence of the rule of\nlaw is",["the sovereignty of the people.","the separation of state and religion.","the supremacy of the constitution.","the respect of human and democratic rights."],2,"The supremacy of the constitution (Article 9 of the FDRE Constitution) ensures that all other laws and decisions must conform to it, serving as the ultimate foundation for the rule of law.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the reason behind the world's recognition of Ethiopia as the symbol of\nindependence and anti-colonial struggle in Africa?",["The establishment of regional organizations.","The membership to the League of Nations.","The foundation of the Organization of African Unity.","The Victory of Adwa"],3,"The Victory of Adwa in 1896, where Ethiopia defeated an invading European colonial power, established the nation as a global symbol of black sovereignty, dignity, and anti-colonial resistance.","2016 EC entrance"],["Who was the leader of the black civil rights' movement killed in April 1968 after addressing his last speech?",["Allan john","Mohandas Gandhi","Martin Luther king","Rose parks"],2,"Martin Luther King Jr., the prominent leader of the American Civil Rights Movement, was assassinated on April 4, 1968, in Memphis, Tennessee, shortly after delivering his famous 'I've Been to the Mountaintop' speech.","2007 EC entrance"],["An international economic principle which is taken from the market economy principle that countries should\nproduce those products which bear a minimum cost and should not produce those products which cost more is",["sustainable development","global welfare","distributive justice","comparative advantage"],3,"The principle of comparative advantage states that countries should specialize in producing goods and services that they can produce at a lower relative cost, leading to mutually beneficial trade.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is countries is a good example of a constitutional monarchy and parliamentary\ndemocracy?",["The Republic of Sudan.","The United Kingdom.","The Republic of China.","The United States of America."],1,"The United Kingdom is a classic model of a constitutional monarchy (where the monarch serves as the ceremonial head of state) combined with a parliamentary democracy (where the executive is drawn from and accountable to parliament).","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following traits is expected from judges for justice for justices to prevail?",["impartiality","kindness","sympathy","Compassion"],0,"Impartiality is essential for judges to decide cases purely based on evidence and law without bias, prejudice, or personal favor.","2006 EC entrance"],["The quality of a self-reliant person that involves the process of evaluating one's own achievements and\nweaknesses in a fair way is",["dependability","civility","open-mindedness","self-Criticism"],3,"Self-criticism is the personal quality that allows a self-reliant individual to honestly and fairly evaluate their own accomplishments, strengths, and limitations for continuous self-improvement.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following refers to a crime that involves the examination of ethnic, religious or other corporate\ngroups?",["Fascism","Racism","Homicide","Genocide"],3,"Genocide refers to acts committed with intent to destroy or exterminate (misprinted as 'examination' in the exam paper), in whole or in part, a national, ethnic, racial, or religious group.","2010 EC entrance"],["The governments set up by Adolf Hitler in Germany and Benito Mussolini in Italy were examples of:",["anarchist government","individualist government","totalitarian government","limited government"],2,"The fascist regimes of Adolf Hitler in Germany and Benito Mussolini in Italy are classic historical examples of totalitarian governments, which seek total control over public and private life.","2011 EC entrance"],["Among the basic principle of the Ethiopian constitution, the one which vests power on nations, nationalities and\npeople of Ethiopia is",["the supremacy of the government","separation of state and religion","accountability of the government","the sovereignty of the people"],3,"Article 8 of the FDRE Constitution establishes the sovereignty of the people, declaring that all sovereign power resides in the Nations, Nationalities, and Peoples of Ethiopia.","2014 EC entrance"],["The people of Konso in South western Ethiopia protected the beautiful Konso land scape from environmental\ndamage for centuries. Preservation of the environment in this way contributes to",["carbon emission","deforestation","eco-tourism","global warming"],2,"The traditional stone-walled terraces and landscape of Konso represent highly sustainable environmental preservation, which attracts visitors and directly supports eco-tourism.","2014 EC entrance"],["Among the following rights, which one is a democratic right?",["The right to life","Right of nationality","Right of privacy","The right to liberty"],1,"In the FDRE Constitution, Chapter Three is divided into Human Rights (such as life, liberty, and privacy) and Democratic Rights (such as the right of nationality, voting, and assembly). (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["A type of democracy which is practiced through a referendum democracy is",["representative democracy","indirect democracy","direct democracy","revolutionary democracy"],2,"A referendum allows citizens to vote directly on specific laws or public issues, representing a key tool of direct democracy.","2013 EC entrance"],["Whose appointment should be approved by the parliament of FDRE?",["Ethiopian Ambassadors and envoys","Chairperson of the House of federation","President of a regional state council","President of the Federal supreme court"],3,"The Prime Minister recommends the president and vice president of the Federal Supreme Court, and the House of Peoples' Representatives approves the appointment. That approval is what the question is asking about. Ambassadors and envoys are tempting because they are senior federal posts, but they are appointed within the executive and do not go to the House for approval.","2005 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following social groups is the most disadvantaged group in Ethiopia?",["persons with Disabilities","Artisans","women","children"],0,"In the Civics and Ethical Education curriculum, persons with disabilities are highlighted as the most disadvantaged group due to pervasive social stigma, economic marginalization, and severe lack of accessible infrastructure.","2006 EC entrance"],["Tsion is a high school student who strongly believes that students can make a difference by joining the different\nclubs in the school. Hence, he often argues that parents should play a great role in promoting this right of\nstudents. According to the above stated case which democratic right is voiced byTsion?",["Freedom of Association","Freedom of Nationality","freedom of expression","Freedom of Movement"],0,"Joining clubs, organizations, or interest groups of one's choice is a direct exercise of the constitutional right to freedom of association.","2016 EC entrance"],["Who was the American civil right activists sent to prison for refusing to give up her seat in a bus for a white\nman?",["Patricia Goldman","clara zeitkin","Rose park","Rose Luxemburg"],2,"Rosa Parks (rendered as 'Rose park') was the American civil rights activist arrested in Montgomery, Alabama, for refusing to surrender her bus seat to a white passenger in 1955.","2006 EC entrance"],["In which economic system an individual can produce and sell the goods and services that earn him/her a good\nreward?",["Free market economic system","Mixed economic system","Command economic system","Planned economic system"],0,"In a free market economic system, individuals have the economic freedom to produce and sell goods and services based on market demand to earn profits.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a constructive contribution of responsible citizens in the operation of justice?",["Letting justice go unchecked","Opposing injustice only when it comes against one's own self","Being submissive to all acts of injustice","Abiding by the laws of one's nation"],3,"Abiding by the laws of one's nation is a fundamental duty of every responsible citizen and directly contributes to the smooth operation of justice and maintaining social order.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one is a cardinal element of due process of law?",["Right to look for a political alternative.","Right to assembly","Right to demonstration","Right to counsel"],3,"The right to counsel is a fundamental, constitutional component of the due process of law, ensuring a fair trial and legal representation for the accused.","2013 EC entrance"],["What form of democracy has recently been adopted by the Ethiopian government?",["Liberal democracy","developmental democracy","Neo-liberalism","Social democracy"],1,"The Ethiopian government under the EPRDF officially embraced the ideology of 'developmental democracy' (the democratic developmental state model) to drive state-led economic transformation.","2007 EC entrance"],["Which of the following gives ultimate decisions according to the Ethiopian law?",["The federal high court","the state supreme court","the state high court","The Federal supreme court"],3,"Under Article 80 of the FDRE Constitution, the Federal Supreme Court possesses the highest and final judicial authority, and its Cassation Division gives final and binding decisions on fundamental errors of law.","2006 EC entrance"],["The corresponding expectations from the citizen with the rights provided by the constitution are termed as:",["Expectations","Penalties","Obligations","Burdens"],2,"Rights and obligations are reciprocal; the duties and responsibilities that citizens are expected to perform in return for enjoying their constitutional rights are termed obligations.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a strategy devised by the Ethiopian government to enhance the economic\ndevelopment of the country?",["Dependency on goods from other countries","Creation of consumer society","Agricultural Development Led Industrialization","Promoting industrialization before agriculture"],2,"Agricultural Development Led Industrialization (ADLI) was the long-standing economic strategy adopted by the Ethiopian government to use agriculture as the engine for industrial growth.","2014 EC entrance"],["The non-consequential theory in that an action that determines the decision but whether the action itself is\nperceived to be right, is",["utilitarianism","ethical egoism","Kantian ethics","ethical relativism"],2,"Kantian ethics is a major non-consequentialist (deontological) moral theory which holds that the morality of an action is based on the action's adherence to rules or duty, rather than its consequences.","2015 EC entrance"],["What does the separation of state and religion make Ethiopia?",["a secular state","a unitary state","a federal state","a democratic state"],0,"A secular state is defined by the strict separation of state affairs from religious institutions, as affirmed under Article 11 of the FDRE Constitution.","2010 EC entrance"],["What form of government best represents the commonness of extra-constitutional power by those who assume\nstate power?",["Oligarchy","dictatorship","Aristocracy","Democracy"],1,"A dictatorship is a form of government where rulers wield unchecked, extra-constitutional power without being bound by legal or constitutional limits. (1)","2007 EC entrance"],["Which one of following is NOT the reward of a sound economic system?",["Healthy market conditions","reduction of debt burden","Skyrocketing prices","Overall economic development"],2,"Skyrocketing prices (high inflation) indicate economic instability and failure, which is not a result or reward of a healthy and sound economic system.","2013 EC entrance"],["During the Ethiopian Students’ Movement of the 1960s and 1970s, the main slogan of the students was:",["“Church and State Should be Separated”","“Cultural Equality of Nations and Nationalities”","“Land to the Tiller”","“One United Ethiopia or Death”"],2,"\"Land to the Tiller\" (Meret Larashu) was the primary and most famous slogan of the Ethiopian Students' Movement during the 1960s and 1970s, aimed at agrarian reform. (1)","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following contributes to living within the limits of one's income?",["Planning","Using public property appropriately","Spending beyond the limits of one's resources","Extravagance"],0,"Planning (or budgeting) is essential to managing one's finances effectively and living within the limits of one's income.","2014 EC entrance"],["Constitutionalism is the feature of",["limited government","fascist rule","unlimited government","totalitarian rule"],0,"Constitutionalism is the political principle that government authority is limited by a system of fundamental laws (a constitution), which is a key characteristic of limited government.","2014 EC entrance"],["The right of an individual or a group to be treated the same way as the others is termed as:",["Fairness","Equality","Transparency","Honesty"],1,"Equality is the democratic principle that ensures every individual or group is treated the same way, with the same rights, opportunities, and status under the law.","2011 EC entrance"],["All activities that we do that are subjected to taxation are known as",["tariffs and duties","business profit tax","tax rate","tax base"],3,"The tax base refers to the total amount of assets, income, transactions, or economic activities that a government is legally permitted to tax. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["The author of the declaration of independence is :",["George Washington","Abraham Lincoln.","John F. Kennedy","Thomas Jefferson"],3,"Thomas Jefferson was the principal author of the American Declaration of Independence, adopted on July 4, 1776.","2008 EC entrance"],["Identified the type of tax that is categorized under an indirect type of tax.",["Value Added Tax","Business Profit Tax","Income Tax","Rental Tax"],0,"Value Added Tax (VAT) is an indirect tax because it is collected by intermediaries (merchants) but ultimately paid by the final consumers as part of the purchase price of goods and services.","2014 EC entrance"],["Mr. Mohammed is a licensed accountant and auditor in firm X. He found an imbalance of income and expenses.\nFurthermore, there were cases of tax fraud committed by the firm. This case demonstrates form of corruption\nwhich is potentially committed by the firm namely",["Embezzlement","Nepotism","Bribery","Favoritism"],0,"Embezzlement involves the theft or misappropriation of funds placed in one's trust, which often manifests as discrepancies in financial records and fraudulent tax practices to hide the missing assets.","2015 EC entrance"],["One among the following choices is an international organization in which Ethiopia has made a significant\ncontribution in the global peace and stability.",["New Partnership for Africa's Development (NEPAD).","United Nations (UN).","Intergovernmental Authority on Development (IGAD).","Organization of African Unity (OAU)."],1,"Ethiopia is a founding member of the United Nations (UN) and has historically been, and remains, one of the largest contributors of peacekeeping forces to secure global peace and stability.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which action contributes to increase the role of individuals in the fight against corruption?",["Applying divide and rule between those who govern and the governed","Imposing restriction on office holders","Encouraging whistle-blowers","Frequently changing government officials"],2,"Encouraging whistle-blowers directly empowers individual citizens to report corrupt activities, thereby increasing their active role in fighting corruption.","2014 EC entrance"],["The right not to be discriminated because of one's age, race, sex, ability , political view or any other status is\ntermed as,",["diversity","freedom","Unity","equality"],3,"Equality entails that all persons are entitled to equal protection without any discrimination based on race, sex, age, ability, or other status.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following ideas refers to an attempt to exterminate a clan, family or people?",["Drug trafficking","corruption","Genocide","aggression"],2,"Genocide is defined as the deliberate and systematic destruction, in whole or in part, of an ethnic, national, racial, or religious group.","2007 EC entrance"],["In the history of Ethiopian peoples' struggle against oppression, a movement that strongly challenged the feudal\nsystem and compelled the declaration of \"Land to the Tiller\" is",["the Bale Peasant Rebellion.","Ethiopian Students' Movement.","the First Woyane Movement.","the Gojam Peasant Rebellion."],1,"The Ethiopian Students' Movement of the 1960s and 1970s famously adopted the slogan 'Land to the Tiller' to challenge the exploitative feudal land tenure system of the imperial regime.","2016 EC entrance"],["The millennium development goals include all of the following except?",["Eradicating gender inequality in education","Reducing infant mortality by ninety percent","Making the poor rich","Providing primary education for all children of the world."],2,"The Millennium Development Goals set measurable targets such as primary schooling for every child, lower child and maternal deaths and an end to the gender gap in education. Making poor people rich was never one of them; the goals aimed at extreme poverty, health and schooling. The infant mortality option is tempting because the figure in it is wrong, but cutting child deaths was a real goal, while making the poor rich never appeared on the list at all.","2005 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a principle or opinion that expresses more than what a single fact can express?",["Analysis","Abstraction","Generalization","Conceptualization"],2,"A generalization is defined as a broad statement, principle, or opinion that is derived from multiple facts and expresses more than any single fact. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["Outside the continent of Africa, where did Ethiopia send peace-keeping troops?",["The Southern Europe.","The Far East.","The Middle East.","The Caribbean."],1,"Ethiopia has a long history of participating in UN peacekeeping missions, including sending the Kagnew Battalion to Korea (which is in the Far East) during the Korean War in the 1950s.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which of the following country is considered as a model parliamentary democracy?",["South Korea.","United States of America.","United Kingdom.","Russia Federation."],2,"The United Kingdom, home of the Westminster system, is historically regarded as the classic model and 'mother' of parliamentary democracy.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is correct about the permanent tendency to lead one's life on outside support?",["Dependency syndrome","Dependency fatigue","Relative dependency","Donor fatigue"],0,"Dependency syndrome is a state of mind where individuals or communities develop a permanent reliance on external aid or support rather than striving for self-reliance.","2015 EC entrance"],["The appointment of judges for the Federal Supreme Courts in Ethiopia is made by",["the House of Peoples' Representatives","the President of the Supreme Court","the President of the nation","the Prime Minister of the nation"],0,"According to the Ethiopian (FDRE) Constitution, judges of the Federal Supreme Court are formally appointed by the House of Peoples' Representatives upon recommendation.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following term refers to an unscientific stories that people would like to tell and believe?",["Traditions.","Myth.","Culture.","Faith."],1,"A myth is defined in civic epistemology as an unscientific, traditional story or belief accepted without scientific evidence or empirical verification.","2010 EC entrance"],["Civic minded citizens serve their community wholeheartedly mainly to get",["Monetary reward","Fame and recognition","Appointment to public office","Personal satisfaction."],3,"Civic-minded citizens engage in voluntary service not for money, status, or public office, but out of a sense of moral duty and the personal satisfaction of helping their community.","2006 EC entrance"],["Which of the following African country is associated to a fairly recent phenomenon of genocide?",["Burundi","democratic Republic of Congo","Rwanda","South Africa"],2,"The 1994 Rwandan genocide against the Tutsi is one of the most prominent and tragic modern genocides in African history.","2006 EC entrance"],["The belief that one's culture is superior to others is",["ethnocentrism","multilateralism","multiculturalism","pluralism"],0,"Ethnocentrism is the biased belief that one's own culture or ethnic group is superior to all others.","2013 EC entrance"],["The author of the declaration of independence of USA was,",["Thomas Jefferson","George Washington","Franklin Roosevelt","Abraham Lincoln"],0,"Thomas Jefferson was the principal author of the United States Declaration of Independence, adopted by the Continental Congress in 1776.","2009 EC entrance"],["The democratic system in which the Prime Minister is a Member of Parliament and head of the Executive Branch \nis:",["Constitutional Democracy.","Parliamentary Democracy.","Presidential Democracy.","Republican Democracy."],1,"In a Parliamentary Democracy, the Prime Minister is elected from among the members of parliament and serves as the head of the executive branch.","2011 EC entrance"],["The skill to care and consider issues related to right and wrong decisions and actions is known as",["self-awareness","self-assertiveness","independence","moral sensitivity"],3,"Moral sensitivity is the ability to recognize, care about, and interpret ethical situations and understand how one's actions and decisions affect others in terms of right and wrong.","2015 EC entrance"],["When people learn to protect natural vegetation and engage in re-afforestation, this shows an awareness of\npeople with their",["environment.","political interest.","social independence.","economic benefits."],0,"Protecting natural vegetation and undertaking re-afforestation activities reflect a strong awareness and care for the environment. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is an international multilateral organization founded after the Second World War to assist\nthe reconstruction of Europe?",["world Health Organization","World Bank","International Monetary Fund","world Trade organization"],1,"The World Bank, originally founded as the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development (IBRD) at the 1944 Bretton Woods Conference, was established to aid in the post-WWII reconstruction of Europe. (1)","2010 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is one of the key institutions that fashioned globalization?",["International Labor organization","International monetary Fund","Transparency international","Amnesty international"],1,"The International Monetary Fund (IMF), along with the World Bank and the WTO, is a premier global financial institution instrumental in driving economic globalization.","2006 EC entrance"],["An individual who is charismatic, attractive, appealing, charming and influential is said to possess the personal\nquality of a leader, which is",["a motivator","realistic","engaging","versatile"],2,"In leadership studies within Civics, an 'engaging' leader is defined as one who is charismatic, appealing, charming, and influential, thereby easily drawing others to their vision.","2015 EC entrance"],["Among the work ethics, the one which requires workers to obey rules and guidelines of the work place is termed \nas:",["Improving professional skills","Punctuality","Harmony and cooperation","Labor discipline"],3,"Labor discipline is the professional work ethic that requires employees to respect, follow, and adhere to workplace regulations and administrative guidelines.","2011 EC entrance"],["A grade 12 Civic and Ethical Education teacher assigned his students to gather data and write a research paper\nin group on women's participation in their Irrredas. However, almost all the papers presented to him were done\nby some group members, but the result that was given to all was the same. As a result, students who were\nactively involved in the assignment felt angry. What is the basic thing that is omitted in the evaluation of the\nteacher that has caused this feeling of anger?",["The notion of equality","The distribution of benefits and burdens.","The principle of affirmative action","The idea of the group discrimination"],1,"This scenario represents an injustice in the distribution of benefits and burdens, where some members bore the entire burden of the work while everyone shared the benefit of the high grade equally. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is incorrect about the behavior of aggressive person?",["Standing rigidly and invading person boundaries.","Speaking too loudly and string at others.","Having an open and polite expression.","Forwarding treating expressions and looking down others."],2,"Having an open and polite expression is a hallmark of assertiveness or politeness, not aggressive behavior, which is typically marked by intimidation and hostility. (1)","2008 EC entrance"],["What is the mechanism through which responsible citizens can influence the political decisions of government\nofficials?",["Giving money as bribe","Removal from the positions","intimidation using force","demonstration"],3,"Peaceful demonstration is a constitutional, legal, and democratic method through which citizens can voice grievances and influence public policy.","2010 EC entrance"],["An international principle of taxation that says people earning the same amount of income should pay the same\namount of tax is termed as:",["Ability to pay","Vertical equity","Value added","Horizontal equity"],3,"Horizontal equity is an economic and taxation principle stating that taxpayers who are in the same financial situation or earn the same income should pay the same amount of tax.","2011 EC entrance"],["What is meant by treating others the way you want to be treated as well as impartial treatment of people?",["courage","truthfulness","Fairness","honest"],2,"Fairness is defined as impartial and just treatment without favoritism or discrimination, often embodied in the Golden Rule of treating others as one wishes to be treated.","2007 EC entrance"],["The process of thought that helps make objective judgment is termed as:",["Knowledge","Reasoning","Wisdom","Rationality"],1,"In civic education, reasoning is defined as the mental process of thought that helps individuals make objective, logical, and fair judgments.","2011 EC entrance"],["A feature of democratic system which can mainly be characterized by the respect of others' view points and\nsharing ideas in a polite way is known as",["tolerance.","liberty.","transparency.","accountability."],0,"Tolerance is a core democratic value characterized by showing respect for the opinions, beliefs, and viewpoints of others, and engaging in civil, polite dialogue even when there is disagreement.","2016 EC entrance"],["Secondary sources of history include:",["Ancient buildings.","History books.","Diaries and coins.","Inscription and monuments."],1,"History books are secondary sources because they analyze, synthesize, and interpret primary sources such as diaries, inscriptions, monuments, and coins.","2008 EC entrance"],["The major role of court in the administration of justice is",["to protect the authority of the rulers","interpreting the law","to make sure the government is legitimate","implementing the law"],1,"The primary role of the judiciary (courts) in the administration of justice and system of checks and balances is interpreting the law.","2014 EC entrance"],["In the FDRE ,interprating law is the responsibility of the judiciary organ ,whereas interprating the constituation is\nthe responsiblity of:",["The executive organ","The house of people Representative","The Legislative organ","The house of Federation"],3,"Under Article 62(1) and Article 83(1) of the FDRE Constitution, the power to interpret the Constitution is vested in the House of Federation, assisted by the Council of Constitutional Inquiry.","2006 EC entrance"],["One of the following is a means of reversing dependency.",["Eradicating poverty","Conducting a socialist revolution","Negotiating with developed countries to end unequal relationship","Increasing imports from developed countries"],0,"Eradicating poverty is essential to overcoming dependency, as it enables a country to be self-reliant and reduce its reliance on foreign aid and loans.","2013 EC entrance"],["The process of sufficiently reducing uncertainty about alternatives to make a reasonable choice refers to:",["self awareness","self reliance","decision making","assertiveness"],2,"Decision making is the cognitive process of evaluating different options and reducing uncertainty to make a reasonable and informed choice.","2011 EC entrance"],["A belief in the superiority of one's cultural groups refers to.",["Prejudice","cultural relativism","Ethnocentrism","cultural universalism"],2,"Ethnocentrism is defined as the belief in the inherent superiority of one's own cultural or ethnic group and evaluating other cultures by its standards.","2008 EC entrance"],["Respecting the conducts and disciplines of working environment, keeping the confidentiality of clients and\nexerting maximum effort to employ one's expertise knowledge for the common good is known as",["collective duties and responsibilities.","personal duties and responsibilities.","professional duties and responsibilities.","official duties and responsibilities."],2,"The duty to respect the conducts of a workplace, maintain client confidentiality, and use specialized knowledge for the public benefit defines professional duties and responsibilities.","2016 EC entrance"],["An international climate change convention adopted in 2015 is:",["The Vienna agreement","the Paris agreement","The Olso protocol","the Beijing declaration"],1,"The Paris Agreement was adopted by consensus on 12 December 2015 at COP21 to address global climate change and reduce greenhouse gas emissions.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is the name of the corruption in which Richard Nixon, the 37th president of America was\ninvolved?",["The Washington scandal.","The Watergate scandal.","The Monica scandal.","The white house scandal."],1,"The Watergate scandal was a major political scandal in the United States involving the administration of President Richard Nixon from 1972 to 1974, which ultimately led to his resignation.","2010 EC entrance"],["During the period of Emperor Haile Selassie the Emperor claimed to acquire his power from:",["all nationalities of the people","the people","popularly elected assembly","supernatural force"],3,"Emperor Haile Selassie claimed his power through divine right (the grace of God/supernatural force), tracing his lineage back to the Solomonic dynasty.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following was the most negative experience in the period of the derg?",["\"Meserete Timihrt\"","\"Ideget Behibret\"","\"Meret Le arashu\"","\"Qey Shibir\""],3,"\"Qey Shibir\" (the Red Terror) was a state-sponsored campaign of violence and mass killings during the Derg regime, representing its most catastrophic and negative legacy. (1)","2006 EC entrance"],["An international organization established after the second world war to assist the reconstruction of Europe is:",["Intergovernmental development authority.","World Bank.","World trade organization.","International monetary fund."],1,"The World Bank (initially the International Bank for Reconstruction and Development, IBRD) was created in 1944 primarily to fund the post-WWII reconstruction of European nations.","2008 EC entrance"],["What is the consequence of dependency on national development?",["Economic growth and poverty reduction","Economic and social disparity","Development of democratic culture","Scientific and technological advancement"],1,"Dependency on foreign aid and external decision-making weakens local capacity and self-reliance, leading to stunted local growth, poverty, and severe economic and social disparity.","2015 EC entrance"],["An economic system in which individuals decide what to produce and how it is distributed in line with priorities\nset by the government",["Free Market Economic System","Planned Economic System","Mixed Economic System","Command Economic System"],2,"A mixed economic system combines market-driven decision making by individuals with government planning, regulation, and priority-setting to guide overall development.","2015 EC entrance"],["Mohammad is a business entrepreneur working in Addis Ababa for the past 5 years. Recently, he changed his\nbusiness venture to a sector that is favored by the government in which those who invest are charged less tax.\nAccording to the case stated above, Mohammad's act is",["fraud.","tax evasion.","contraband.","tax avoidance."],3,"Tax avoidance is the legal minimizing of tax liabilities by exploiting options and incentives provided in the tax laws, such as moving investments into government-favored, lower-tax sectors.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is a manifestation for the absence of the rule of law?",["Existence of supreme power.","Consolidation of state authority.","General feeling of security.","The prevalence of anarchy."],3,"The absence of the rule of law leads to lawlessness, disorder, and the prevalence of anarchy, as there are no enforceable rules to govern societal behavior.","2011 EC entrance"],["The type of crime that involves a deliberate act of endangering the lives of people or property, or denying the\nfreedom of a person or group of persons is known as",["terrorism","corruption","drug trafficking","treason"],0,"Terrorism is defined as the deliberate use or threat of violence to endanger lives, damage property, or restrict freedom, usually to instill fear or achieve political, ideological, or religious objectives","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following reasons justifies affirmative action for women?",["Non-discrimination","Reverse discrimination","Assimilation","Discrimination"],3,"Affirmative action is justified to remedy and compensate for historical and systemic discrimination against marginalized groups, such as women. (1)","2013 EC entrance"],["The most vocal opposition to the regime of Haile Sellassie I, particularly during its last stage came from",["Industrial workers and teachers","General officers in the army","Students and the educated elite","Dissatisfied ordinary peasants"],2,"In the last years of Haile Selassie's reign the university and secondary school students led the open opposition, with demands such as land to the tiller and with questions about famine, poverty and inequality. Their strikes, pamphlets and demonstrations set the political mood that carried into 1974. Army officers are tempting because soldiers finally took power, but the army moved late, after the students and the educated elite had already put the questions in public.","2005 EC entrance"],["For nations like Ethiopia, diversity is one of the values as well as challenges of national unity. When people\naspire to develop their own cultures, maintaining equality and recognition of languages, religions, and other\ncultural traits contributes to national unity. But against this norm, there are individuals or groups who have a\ntendency to consider their own identities are good and superior to others. Furthermore, such tendencies may\nlead into assumption that others are inferior and enemies. Such tendency is known as",["eurocentrism","ethnocentrism","multiculturalism","accommodative"],1,"Ethnocentrism is the biased attitude of viewing one's own ethnic group or culture as superior to others, often leading to prejudice against other groups.","2014 EC entrance"],["A tendency to value the cultures of others based on one's own cultural values and conceptions known as",["cultural Relativism.","absolutism","ethnocentrism.","multiculturalism."],2,"Ethnocentrism is the cognitive bias or tendency of judging and evaluating other cultures according to the standards and values of one's own culture, often viewing one's own as superior.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following explains best the formulation of the 1995 FDRE's constitution?",["the House of Federation","the constitutional commission","Nations and Nationalities","the parliament"],1,"The 1995 FDRE Constitution was drafted and formulated by the Constitutional Commission, which was established during the transitional period to prepare the draft charter.","2014 EC entrance"],["The act of chasing away the community from the normal distribution of goods is",["rent seeking.","market competition.","retail sale.","whole sale."],0,"In civic education, actions like hoarding, artificial price manipulation, or excluding citizens from the fair distribution of goods to secure unearned benefits are classic examples of rent-seeking behavior.","2015 EC entrance"],["At the main gate of Keble 'X' in 'Y' national regional state of Ethiopia a big chart with details about the budget\nallocated for the kebele and the plan of various activates is posted for the public to see. This action of kebele 'X'\nimplies which principle of FDRE constitution?",["Conduct and accountability of government.","The respect of human and democratic rights.","The sovereignty of people.","The supremacy of constitution."],0,"Article 12 of the FDRE Constitution establishes the principle of conduct and accountability of government, stating that government activities and finances must be transparent to the public. (1)","2009 EC entrance"],["In Ethiopia, the progressive taxation system follows a principle in which people who earn different amounts\nshould be taxed differently. This principle of taxation is known as",["Vertical Equity.","Horizontal Equity.","ability to Pay.","evasion of tax."],0,"Vertical Equity is the taxation principle which states that individuals with different tax-paying abilities (i.e., different income levels) should be taxed differently, which is the basis of progressive taxation.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following actions helps to minimize extravagant practices?",["Fixing a budget before shopping","Avoiding buying things","Buying things for no reason","Avoiding any social ceremonies which require money"],0,"Fixing a budget before shopping helps to avoid impulsive purchases and ensures that spending is kept within one's financial means, thus reducing extravagance.","2014 EC entrance"],["A body which is set up by a mutual agreement of states to deal with foreign relations to maintain constant\nofficial contacts and to facilitate inter relationships among states referred to as",["Diplomatic aggression","Diplomatic manipulation.","Diplomatic Mission.","Diplomatic arbitration."],2,"A diplomatic mission is an official group of representatives sent by one state to another to facilitate formal communication, negotiations, and maintain ongoing relationships.","2015 EC entrance"],["The basic principle of the Ethiopian Constitution includes:",["the sovereignty of the state.","the supremacy of Regional Constitutions.","the respect of Parliamentarians.","the separation of State and Religion."],3,"The separation of state and religion is one of the five basic principles of the FDRE Constitution, as outlined in Article 11.","2011 EC entrance"],["In order to avail capital for investment, get an interest and place money in a safe environment, people must\ndeposit their money in",["Banks","Their own houses","Equb stores","Iddir centers"],0,"Banks provide a secure environment, pay interest on savings, and mobilize those savings as capital for investments in the economy.","2013 EC entrance"],["Ato Kassa is an engineer who believes that he has a responsibility to be honest and truthful in every course of\nhis life. This responsibility of Ato Kassa arises from his",["custom and tradition","occupation","law","moral principles"],3,"Being honest and truthful across all aspects of one's life is a fundamental moral duty that stems from an individual's personal ethical and moral principles rather than professional or legal requirements alone.","2015 EC entrance"],["A person born to Ethiopian parents abroad acquires Ethiopian citizenship by",["jus soil","jus sanguinis","naturalization","adoption"],1,"Citizenship acquired through parentage or descent, regardless of the country of birth, is known as jus sanguinis (right of blood). (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["In most countries the term \"government benefits\" are related to,",["Payment of wages.","Protection of public properties.","Collection of taxes.","Social welfare provisions."],3,"Government benefits typically refer to public assistance and social welfare provisions such as healthcare, education, social security, and subsidies intended to improve the well-being of citizens.","2008 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is important characteristics for effective civic participation?",["Home base political organization and political agenda.","Competition and profit orientation.","Commitment and dedication.","Focus on individual talent and competence."],2,"Commitment and dedication to public welfare are core civic virtues that ensure meaningful and sustained civic participation.","2009 EC entrance"],["Which of the following countries is unique example in the world that does not have a written constitution?",["France","Netherlands","England","China"],2,"England (the United Kingdom) is the classic global example of a nation with an unwritten (uncodified) constitution, relying instead on statutes, common law, and conventions.","2006 EC entrance"],["Ato Kinde is a resident in Addis Ababa who is engaged in a retail business sector. He complained to the Wereda\nIncome and Revenue Authority that he is requested to pay more amount of tax than those who have the same\namount of earning with him. Accordingly, which principle of taxation is violated by the Wereda Income and\nRevenue Authority in this case?",["Tax avoidance","Vertical Equity","Ability to pay","Horizontal equity"],3,"Horizontal equity is a principle of taxation which states that taxpayers with the same income or wealth should pay the same amount of tax. In this case, requesting Ato Kinde to pay more than others with the same earnings directly violates this principle.","2015 EC entrance"],["An individual who has claimed the right to refuse to perform active military service on the grounds of freedom of \nthought, conscience, or religion is referred to as",["Treason","conscientious objector","Arbitrary Rule","whistle blower"],1,"A conscientious objector is an individual who refuses to engage in military service or combat due to deeply held moral, ethical, or religious beliefs.","2015 EC entrance"],["According to the current Constitution of FDRE elected officials are given their power by the citizen of the\ncountry. Which of the following basic principles of the Constitution is reflected by this practice?",["Sovereignty of the people.","Respect of human and democratic rights.","Conduct and accountability of government.","The supremacy of the Constitution."],0,"The constitutional principle where elected officials derive their mandate and authority from the citizens reflects the sovereignty of the people, as stated in Article 8 of the FDRE Constitution.","2011 EC entrance"],["A lawful gathering of people to protest ,support or create awareness on a certain issue implies ;",["Peaceful demonstration","Political freedom","Popular participation","Civic campaign"],2,"A demonstration is people assembling in public to show support, to protest or to draw attention to an issue, and doing it within the law makes it peaceful. Article 30 of the FDRE Constitution protects that right. Popular participation is tempting because a demonstration is one form of it, but popular participation is the wide term covering voting, meetings and civic work, while the gathering described has its own name.","2005 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is NOT an indicator of poverty?",["Existence of a high infant mortality rate in a country.","A high average life expectancy and a high literacy rate.","Prevalence of a very low income level.","Failure of people to satisfy their basic needs."],1,"A high average life expectancy and a high literacy rate are key indicators of human development and high quality of life, which are opposite to the indicators of poverty.","2011 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-economics","name":"Economics","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["Short-run equilibrium of the monopolist is a point where",["revenues are minimized.","profits are minimized.","profits are maximized.","losses are maximized."],2,"A monopolist, like any rational profit-maximizing firm, achieves short-run equilibrium at the output level where total profits are maximized (where MR = MC).","2018 EC entrance"],["If the Real GDP of country \"A\" in the year 2023 is 19,550,000 dollar and in the year 2022 it was 18,600,000\ndollar, then the real GDP growth in 2023 as compared to the previous year will be equal to",["6.55%","3.39%","4.86%","5.11%"],3,"The real GDP growth rate is calculated as [(Real GDP in 2023 - Real GDP in 2022) / Real GDP in 2022] * 100 = [(19,550,000 - 18,600,000) / 18,600,000] * 100 = 5.11%.","2018 EC entrance"],["What was the goal of sustainable development and poverty reduction program (SDPRP) assigned by Ethiopian\nPeoples’ Revolutionary Democratic Front?",["Building all-inclusive implementation capacity","A massive push to accelerate economic growth","Unleashing the potentials of Ethiopia's women","Capacity building in the public and private sector"],3,"The Sustainable Development and Poverty Reduction Programme ran from 2002/03 to 2004/05 and was built on five goals: Agricultural Development Led Industrialisation, food security, decentralisation and empowerment, capacity building in the public and private sector, and reform of the justice system and civil service. Capacity building in the public and private sector is on that list, so it is the answer. The other three options are strategic goals of the next plan, PASDEP, which covered 2005/06 to 2009/10.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following terms explains an economy characterized by low carbon usage, resource efficiency\nand socially inclusive?",["Green economy","Green growth","Developed economy","Developing economy"],0,"According to the United Nations Environment Programme (UNEP), a green economy is defined as one that is low carbon, resource efficient, and socially inclusive.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a measure of inequality which is often expressed by the ratio of the area between\nthe Lorenz curve and a 45 0 line and the total area under the 45 0 line?",["Per capita income","Gini Coefficient","Kuznets ratio","Human Development Index"],1,"The Gini Coefficient is a standard measure of inequality, calculated as the ratio of the area between the Lorenz curve and the 45-degree line of perfect equality to the total area under the 45-degree line.","2018 EC entrance"],["Compared to other African countries, Ethiopia is more successful in terms of",["Road transport.","Metro transport services.","Air transport and Civil Aviation.","Railways transport."],2,"Ethiopia's clearest transport success is air transport and civil aviation. Ethiopian Airlines flies to more destinations than any other African carrier, runs a large cargo business and has made Addis Ababa the main air hub of the continent. Road density is still low by African standards, the railway network is short and new, and the light rail is a single city service, so none of the other three can be described as a lead over other African countries. (1)","2012 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is separately categorized under the Sustainable Development Goals?",["Achieve universal primary education","Reduce child mortality","Combat HIV/AIDS, malaria and other diseases","Responsible consumption and production"],3,"Responsible consumption and production is SDG Goal 12, whereas reducing child mortality, combating major diseases, and achieving universal primary education were distinct goals under the predecessor MDG framework.","2018 EC entrance"],["In a hypothetical country, (K) the number of employed labor is 25 million and the number of unemployed labors\nis 5 million. Moreover, the total adult population of the country is given as 80 million. How much is the labor\nforce participation rate?",["25%","37.5%","31.3%","25.1"],1,"The labor force consists of both the employed and unemployed (25 + 5 = 30 million). The labor force participation rate is (Labor Force / Adult Population) * 100 = (30 million / 80 million) * 100 = 37.5%","2018 EC entrance"],["Suppose an Ethiopian importer is importing commodities by taking a full advantage of the deductions or\nincentives approved in the tax schedule by the government to reduce its tax obligation. Which one of the\nfollowing terms reflects such kind of a tax non-compliance problem?",["Tax advantage","Tax avoidance","Tax evasion","Tax reduction"],1,"Tax avoidance involves utilizing legal methods, such as approved deductions and government tax incentives, to minimize the amount of tax owed.","2018 EC entrance"],["In macroeconomics, the current consumption expenditure is likely to increase due to",["increase in income tax","expectation of higher future income","expectation of lower price in the future","increase in interest rate"],1,"An expectation of higher future income shifts current consumption upwards as households feel wealthier and increase their current spending in anticipation of their future gains.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is correct about the key strategic pillars of the ten-year development plan after\nreform?",["Public sector-led economic growth","Gender and social exclusion","Building regional monopoly power and economy","Quality economic growth and shared prosperity"],3,"The ten year development plan for 2021 to 2030 lists ten strategic pillars, and the first one is quality economic growth and shared prosperity. The other pillars include productivity and competitiveness, private sector led growth, a resilient green economy and gender and social inclusion. Choice D is the trap: the real pillar is gender and social inclusion, and the option prints exclusion, which is the problem the plan sets out to remove. Choice C also reverses a pillar, since the plan calls for private sector led growth.","2017 EC entrance"],["When an insurance company provides fringe benefits on the basis of an average rate over a set of employees\nand guarantees them to participate in the program, then this can be seen as a solution for which one of the\nfollowing problem?",["Signalling","Screening","Moral hazard","Adverse selection"],3,"Adverse selection occurs when high-risk individuals are more likely to buy insurance. Group coverage with mandatory participation solves this by averaging risk across all employees, preventing low-risk individuals from opting out.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which type of tax is imposed and payable on luxury items according to the Ethiopian tax policy?",["Value added tax","Turnover tax","Surtax","Excise tax"],3,"Excise taxes are selective taxes levied on specific luxury items, such as expensive cars and perfumes, as well as socially harmful products like tobacco and alcohol. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["The unemployment rate for an economy is 4%. The labor force is estimated to be 55 million. What is the number\nof unemployed people in millions?",["2.2 million","22 million","20 million","220 million"],0,"The unemployment rate is the number of unemployed people divided by the labour force, times 100. Rearranged, the number of unemployed equals the rate times the labour force. Write the rate as a decimal: 4 percent is 0.04. Unemployed = 0.04 × 55 million = 2.2 million A quick check: 4 percent is a small share, so the answer must be far smaller than the 55 million labour force. That rules out choices B, C and D at once.","2017 EC entrance"],["What is the role of the National Bank of Ethiopia?",["Provision of loans to the individual farmers","Taxing the private sector","Regulation of the financial sector","Collecting interest income"],2,"The National Bank of Ethiopia is the country's central bank. It issues currency, holds foreign reserves, sets monetary policy and licenses and supervises banks, insurers and microfinance institutions, which is the regulation of the financial sector. Lending to individual farmers is the work of commercial banks and microfinance institutions, and collecting taxes is the job of the revenue authority, so A, B and C belong to other bodies.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the key priority area that is considered to be the basis for the locally developed\neconomic reform program recently?",["Sustainable rural development","Inclusive financial sector development","Widening the demographic dividend","Uni - polar source of growth"],1,"Inclusive financial sector development is a key priority under the macroeconomic pillar of Ethiopia's Home-Grown Economic Reform (HGER) program, aiming to expand access to finance and savings mobilization.","2016 EC entrance"],["In Ethiopia, which of the following has got particular attention in the past yet characterized as the lowest\nproductive in its performance?",["Mining sector","Tourism sector","Agricultural sector","Trade sector"],2,"The agricultural sector has historically received substantial policy focus in Ethiopia (such as through the ADLI strategy), yet it remains characterized by very low productivity due to traditional farming practices and reliance on rainfed systems.","2016 EC entrance"],["One of the following is considered to be fiscal policy tool. Which one is it?",["Grants in aid","Investment","Transfer payments","Taxation"],3,"Taxation is a primary tool of fiscal policy, alongside government spending, used by the government to manage economic activity and aggregate demand. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["A firm produces 10 units of output at a total cost of 500 birr. When output increases to 11 units, total cost rises\nto 540 birr. The marginal cost of the 11th unit is:",["45 birr","50 birr","60 birr","40 birr"],3,"Marginal cost (MC) = change in total cost / change in quantity = (540 - 500) / (11 - 10) = 40 / 1 = 40 birr. MC is the additional cost of producing one more unit. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Which theory provides a more realistic explanation of consumer choice?",["Cardinal Utility Theory","Ordinal Utility Theory","Production theory","Supply and demand theory"],1,"Ordinal utility theory is considered more realistic because it only requires consumers to rank preferences (prefer A over B) rather than assign numerical utility values. This avoids the unrealistic assumption that utility is measurable cardinally. Indifference curve analysis is based on ordinal utility.","2018 EC entrance"],["Among the followings, which one is the objective of the Home Grown Economic Reform?",["Creating inadequate job opportunities","Transition from private to public sector-led growth","Maintaining macroeconomic stability","Encouraging debt vulnerabilities."],2,"The Home Grown Economic Reform was launched with three central objectives: sustaining rapid growth, keeping a stable macroeconomic environment by reducing debt vulnerabilities, and creating enough lasting jobs. Maintaining macroeconomic stability is therefore an objective. Choices A and B state harmful outcomes, and choice C runs the reform backwards, because it aims to move gradually from public to private sector led growth.","2017 EC entrance"],["If the economy is facing deficient demand, which one of the following fiscal policy should be applied?",["Increasing the tax rate","Increasing government expenditure","Increasing the discount rate","Increasing required reserve ratio"],1,"To combat deficient aggregate demand (recession), expansionary fiscal policy should be implemented, which involves increasing government expenditure or decreasing taxes.","2018 EC entrance"],["The greatest contribution to Ethiopia's agricultural GDP comes from the",["nomadic/pastoral system","livestock sub-sector","crop-production sub-sector","forestry and fishery sub-sector"],2,"Ethiopian agriculture is made up of crop production, livestock, and forestry with fishery. The largest share of agricultural GDP comes from the crop production sub sector, where smallholder farmers grow cereals, pulses, oilseeds and cash crops such as coffee. Livestock is second and matters a lot for exports and household income, but it is still smaller than crops. Forestry and fishery contribute the least, and pastoral farming is a farming system, not a sub sector.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following indicates the direct health dimension of the impacts of climate change?",["Expansion of desertification","Malaria","Water shortages","Drought"],1,"Malaria represents a direct health dimension of climate change, as rising temperatures and changing rainfall patterns expand the geographic range and transmission seasons of vector-borne diseases.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following institutions plays a major role in implementing fiscal decentralization in Ethiopia?",["Regional state governments","World Bank","International Monetary Fund","Private commercial banks"],0,"Fiscal decentralization in Ethiopia transfers revenue-raising and expenditure responsibilities to regional and woreda (district) governments. Regional state governments collect regional taxes, receive federal block grants, and manage local public services (education, health, agriculture) under the constitution.","2018 EC entrance"],["In Ethiopia, which one of the following institution is responsible to collect tax on behalf of the government?",["The Ministry of Finance","The Central Bank","The Commercial bank","The Ministry of Revenue"],3,"The Ministry of Revenues is the federal institution in Ethiopia officially mandated to administer and collect federal taxes and custom duties.","2016 EC entrance"],["Gemechu owns a sole proprietorship type of business and incurred a loss. Which one of the following could\nresult in the sale of his private house if his business assets are not enough to cover the business liabilities?",["Not suitable for large scale operations","Non-transferability of shares","Limited managerial expertise","Unlimited liability"],3,"In a sole proprietorship, the owner has unlimited liability, meaning their personal assets (such as a private home) can be seized and sold to settle any unpaid debts of the business.","2018 EC entrance"],["Among the following, which one is a macroeconomic issue?",["Actions of an individual agent within an economy","Resource allocation or price determination as central problem","The economic activities of a consumer, a producer or industry","Structure and performance of the economy as a whole"],3,"While microeconomics deals with individual economic units (consumers, firms, and industries), macroeconomics focuses on aggregates and the structure and performance of the economy as a whole.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following principles of taxation states that the tax system should be able to yield enough\nrevenue so that it should not be forced to resort to deficit financing?",["Principle of maximum revenue","Principle of economy","Principle of tax equity","Principle of fiscal adequacy"],3,"The principle of fiscal adequacy states that the government's tax revenue should be sufficient to cover its necessary public expenditures so that it does not need to rely heavily on deficit financing.","2018 EC entrance"],["A tight monetary policy is applied in circumstances where there is",["high economic growth.","high inflation.","slow economic growth.","high unemployment."],1,"A tight (contractionary) monetary policy is implemented by the central bank to decrease the money supply and raise interest rates, aiming to reduce aggregate demand and curb high inflation.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the major role of non-banking financial institutions?",["Serving as intermediary between borrowers and lenders","Mobilizing savings from depositors","Facilitating bank-related financial services","Providing loan to borrowers"],2,"Non-bank financial institutions (NBFIs) complement commercial banks by facilitating bank-related financial services such as investment, risk pooling, and contractual savings.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is among the key strategic pillars of the ten-year development plan in the homegrown economic reform period?",["Managing risk and volatility","Strengthen human resource development","Quality economic growth and shared prosperity","A massive push to accelerate economic growth"],2,"The Ten-Year Development Plan (2021-2030) of Ethiopia, formulated during the homegrown economic reform period, identifies 'Quality economic growth and shared prosperity' as its first strategic pillar.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is duly emphasized in one of the home-grown economic reform called sectoral\nreform?",["Internal trade","External Trade","Tourism","Service sectors"],2,"The sectoral reform pillar of the HGER targets five key sectors to drive economic growth: Agriculture, Manufacturing, Mining, ICT, and Tourism.","2016 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-geography","name":"Geography","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["As compared to others, which climatic region of Africa shows lower seasonality?",["The Mediterranean","The Tropical continental","The Tropical desert","The Equatorial"],3,"The Equatorial climate region is characterized by high temperatures and abundant rainfall throughout the year, resulting in very low seasonal variation (seasonality) compared to other climates.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which kind of town serves as a center of financial services?",["Mining towns","Industrial town","Commercial town","Market town"],2,"Commercial towns function as central hubs for business, trading, banking, and diverse financial services that support regional or national economies.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following river is known for having the largest waterfall in Africa?",["The Congo River","The Zambezi River","The Nile River","The Volta River"],1,"The Zambezi River is home to Victoria Falls, which is recognized as the largest waterfall in Africa and one of the most spectacular in the world.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which environmental movement prioritizes the consumption of local and organic products than conventionally\nimported products as a means of environmental protection?",["Free market environmentalism.","Conservation environmentalism.","Light green environmentalism.","Popular environmentalism."],2,"Light green environmentalism emphasizes personal responsibility and lifestyle choices, promoting green consumerism such as purchasing local and organic products to minimize environmental footprints.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which wind type is dominantly affecting the tropical climate of Africa?",["Polar easterlies","Westerly winds","Trade winds","Guinea Monsoon"],2,"The Trade Winds (Northeast and Southeast trade winds) converge at the ITCZ and are the dominant wind systems controlling the tropical climate and seasonal rainfall patterns over most of Africa.","2015 EC entrance"],["A hypothetical town is located along the beach where its temperature is modified by the local wind. Which type\nof wind does this town commonly experiences during the daytime?",["Valley breeze","Sea breeze","Land breeze","Mountain breeze"],1,"During the day, land heats up faster than the adjacent body of water, creating lower pressure over land and drawing cooler air from the water toward the coast as a sea breeze. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Which branch of human geography is concerned with the dynamic nature of places over time?",["Political geography","Cultural geography","Urban geography","Historical geography"],3,"Historical geography is the branch of human geography that investigates how geographic patterns, landscapes, and spatial organizations evolve over time.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following served as the foundation for Ancient Greeks' climate classification?",["The Earth-Sun relationship.","Distribution of natural vegetation.","Cloud cover and winds.","Seasonality of temperature and precipitation."],0,"The Ancient Greeks classified climate zones (Torrid, Temperate, Frigid) based on the Earth-Sun relationship (latitudinal variation in the angle of incoming solar radiation).","2018 EC entrance"],["Among the following, which one is a cause for the formation of barchans?",["Wind","Sea wave","Moving ice","Running water"],0,"Barchans are crescent-shaped sand dunes formed by wind action in arid regions where wind blows predominantly from one direction over a limited supply of sand.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which branch of physical geography is concerned with the study of distribution of landforms and forces that\nchange them?",["Oceanography","Climatology","Biogeography","Geomorphology"],3,"Geomorphology is the sub-discipline of physical geography that studies the origin, evolution, and spatial distribution of Earth's landforms and the processes acting on them.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which geologic process mainly involves the breaking of rocks into pieces and formation of new substances?",["Weathering","Deposition","Orogenesis","Sedimentation"],0,"Weathering includes mechanical weathering, which breaks rocks into smaller fragments, and chemical weathering, which alters minerals to form new chemical substances.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following practices lead to habitat destruction?",["Underutilization of resources.","Landscape modification.","Increased reliance on organic fertilizers.","Decreasing population pressure."],1,"Landscape modification, such as converting forests into agricultural land or urban areas, physically alters ecosystems and is the primary driver of habitat destruction.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one is a good practice to minimize the effects of drought?",["Fallowing","Reducing overgrazing","Water harvesting","Intercropping"],2,"Water harvesting involves collecting and storing rainwater during wet periods, which is a highly effective measure to mitigate the direct impacts of water scarcity during droughts. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following country is the leading in fish processing industry in Africa?",["Morocco","Nigeria","South Africa","Egypt"],0,"Morocco is the leading fishing and fish-processing nation in Africa, particularly renowned globally as a leading producer and exporter of canned sardines.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which country currently stands as the leading exporter of agricultural products within intra-African trade?",["Uganda","Egypt","South Africa","Ethiopia"],2,"South Africa is the leading exporter of agricultural products in intra-African trade, exporting maize, wine, citrus fruits, and other processed goods to neighboring countries (Botswana, Namibia, Zimbabwe, Mozambique) and beyond, due to its advanced agricultural sector and infrastructure.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following region has the longest population doubling time?",["Africa","South America","Asia","Europe"],3,"Europe has the lowest population growth rate (and in some cases, population decline), which translates into the longest population doubling time of any continent.","2016 EC entrance"],["Where is the highest mean annual temperature recorded?",["The Baro lowlands","The Elkeri plains","The Dallol depression","The Ghlbe lowlands"],2,"The Dallol depression, located in the Danakil Depression of Afar, holds the record for the highest average annual temperature for an inhabited place on Earth.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following Era is responsible for the formation of the present surface configuration of the African\ncontinent?",["Precambrian Era","Paleozoic Era","Cenozoic Era","Mesozoic Era"],2,"Tectonic activities of the Cenozoic Era, such as faulting, rifting, and massive volcanic eruptions, were primarily responsible for shaping the current surface features of the African continent.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a reddish-brown toxic gas that causes air pollution?",["Carbon monoxide","Methane","Sulphur dioxide","Nitrogen dioxide"],3,"Nitrogen dioxide (NO2) is a prominent, pungent, reddish-brown toxic gas produced primarily by high-temperature fuel combustion in vehicles and power plants.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is a non-renewable natural resource?",["Minerals","Air","Water","Soil"],0,"Minerals are exhaustible, non-renewable resources formed over millions of years that cannot be naturally regenerated on a human timescale. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Which continent is included in the Eurasian plate?",["Australia","Part of South America","North Africa","Part of Asia"],0,"The Eurasian tectonic plate covers most of the landmass of Europe and Asia, so parts of Asia are located on this plate, whereas Australia, South America, and Africa belong to their own respective plates.","2016 EC entrance"],["In which categories of settlement pattern do you categorize the towns that are found along the main highway\nfrom Addis Ababa to Gondar?",["Nucleated settlement","Dispersed settlement","Compacted settlement","Linear settlement"],3,"Settlements that develop along transport routes such as main highways are characterized by a linear settlement pattern.","2016 EC entrance"],["What landform is created by the deposition of sediment at a river's mouth?",["Gorge","Escarpment","Delta","Canyon"],2,"A delta is a depositional landform created at the mouth of a river where the river's velocity decreases as it enters a standing body of water, depositing its sediment load.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which African country has the highest number of major languages?",["Kenya.","Tanzania.","Nigeria.","South Africa."],2,"Nigeria is Africa's most linguistically diverse nation, with more than 500 distinct languages spoken across its various ethnic groups.","2018 EC entrance"],["If you travel from Addis Ababa to the northeastern lowlands of Ethiopia in summer, you can recognize a high\nvariation in the rainfall. This variation is mainly caused by",["mountain barriers.","distance from the sea.","revolution of the earth.","latitude."],0,"The dramatic variation in rainfall between the highlands and the northeastern lowlands is mainly caused by the rainshadow effect of the mountain barriers (the Ethiopian escarpment) which block rain-bearing winds.","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the trend of world population growth in the second stage of the demographic transitional model?",["Low birth rate.","Rapid natural increase.","Slow growth rate.","Stable death rate."],1,"In Stage 2 of the Demographic Transition Model, the death rate drops rapidly due to improvements in food supply and sanitation while the birth rate remains high, resulting in a rapid natural increase in population. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["The population pyramid which is wider at the base and narrow at the apex is mostly the characteristic of:",["Developed countries","Advanced countries","North America countries","Developing countries"],3,"A population pyramid with a broad base and a narrow apex is characteristic of developing countries, indicating high birth rates (broad base) and high death rates or lower life expectancy (narrow apex).","2016 EC entrance"],["Which soil type is mainly located in the tropical monsoon climatic region of Africa?",["Lixisols","Luvisols","Calcisols","Acrisols"],3,"Acrisols are highly weathered, acidic soils characterized by an accumulation of low-activity clays in the subsoil, commonly found in humid tropical and tropical monsoon regions of Africa.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which area of the world is sparsely populated mainly due to physical factor?",["Peninsular Europe","South Asia","Central Africa","East Asia"],2,"Central Africa, particularly the Congo Basin, is sparsely populated due to physical constraints such as dense tropical rainforests, high humidity, and poor soils, unlike the highly populated regions of Europe and Asia. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which element of research presents what is already known about the research topic by other studies?",["Research questions","Sampling procedure","Objectives of the research","Literature review"],3,"A literature review provides a comprehensive synthesis of existing knowledge, theories, and previous research findings relevant to the topic being investigated.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which approach is often utilized to enhance community-based resource management?",["Collaborative management","Exclusive decision-making","Resource privatization","Government-controlled initiatives"],0,"Collaborative management (or co-management) brings together local communities and government authorities to sustainably manage and protect natural resources.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which structure of the atmosphere is known by containing the lowest percentage of atmospheric mass?",["Troposphere","Stratosphere","Mesosphere","Thermosphere"],3,"Because atmospheric pressure and density decrease exponentially with altitude, the thermosphere is extremely rarified and contains less than 0.001% of the atmosphere's total mass.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following directly indicates the presence of a developed health sector in a certain country?",["Growth of capital expenditure.","High life expectancy.","Few people below poverty line.","High female literacy."],1,"High life expectancy is a primary health outcome indicator that directly reflects the accessibility, quality, and effectiveness of a country's health care sector. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Which measure of soil conservation should be widely used against soil erosion in arid and semi-arid areas of the\nHorn?",["Intercropping","Terracing","Shelter belts","Check dams"],2,"Shelter belts (or windbreaks) consist of rows of trees and shrubs planted to reduce wind velocity and are the most effective method against wind-driven soil erosion in arid and semi-arid environments.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following types of erosion results in the formation of deeper and wider ditches?",["gully erosion","dip erosion","sheet erosion","Rill erosion"],0,"Gully erosion is an advanced stage of water erosion where deep and wide channels or ditches (gullies) are carved into the landscape, which cannot be obliterated by normal cultivation.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the disadvantage of migration to the receiving countries?",["An increase in the number of skilled workers","Communication barrier","A reduction in social and racial tension","A reduction in pressure on jobs"],1,"In the receiving country, newcomers often speak a different language and follow different customs, so a communication barrier grows between migrants and their hosts. That barrier makes work, schooling and health services harder to deliver. Option A is a benefit of migration, not a disadvantage, and options B and C state the reverse of what happens: migration usually increases competition for jobs and can raise social and racial tension rather than reduce it.","2012 EC entrance"],["Which type of environmental movement recommends promotion of property rights as a tool for conserving the\nenvironment?",["Free market environmentalism","Dark greens environmentalism","Preservation environmentalism","Population environmentalism"],0,"Free-market environmentalism advocates that clearly defined, legally enforced private property rights provide the best incentives for conservation and sustainable resource management.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is a challenge to environmental sustainability?",["Rapid urbanization","Environmental movements","Slow growth of population","Use of renewable energy"],0,"Rapid urbanization is a major threat to environmental sustainability as it leads to deforestation, increased pollution, habitat fragmentation, and excessive consumption of resources.","2016 EC entrance"],["Where in Africa does the highest income inequality prevail?",["Mali","Mauritania","Liberia","South Africa"],3,"South Africa has the highest income inequality not only in Africa but globally, consistently recording the highest Gini coefficient due to historical and structural disparities.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is correct about the size of landmasses over the globe?",["Africa is the third largest continent.","Asia is the largest continent.","Europe is the smallest continent.","Antarctica is the second smallest continent."],1,"Asia is the largest continent in terms of both land area and population, while Australia is the smallest continent and Africa is the second largest.","2018 EC entrance"],["What term describes the point where two rivers meet?",["Confluence","Estuary","Tributary","Distributary"],0,"The point where two or more rivers meet and merge into a single channel is called a confluence.","2016 EC entrance"],["What type of wind might a visitor to one of the coastal areas in Africa observe?",["Planetary winds","Mountain breezes","Sea breezes","Monsoon winds"],2,"Due to the differential heating of land and water, coastal regions experience localized winds, such as sea breezes during the day when the land heats up faster than the ocean.","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the type of corruption that involves the diversion of community funds from their intended use to\nindividuals' pockets?",["Kick-backs","Nepotism","Bribery","Theft of public assets"],3,"Theft of public assets (or embezzlement) involves public officials unlawfully misappropriating, diverting, or stealing public or community funds for private gain.","2017 EC entrance"],["Among the following major types of rock, which one is formed as a result of compaction and cementation?",["Igneous","Sedimentary","Volcanic","Metamorphic"],1,"Sedimentary rocks are formed through the lithification process, which involves the accumulation, compaction, and cementation of mineral and organic particles over time.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following continent was part of Laurasia?",["South America.","Europe.","Africa.","Antarctica."],1,"Laurasia was the ancient northern supercontinent that split to form North America, Europe, and Asia (excluding the Indian subcontinent), whereas Gondwana formed the southern continents.","2018 EC entrance"],["The Zambezi, Wabishebelle and Juba rivers are the major basins in:",["The Indian Ocean Drainage System","The Closed Drainage System","The Atlantic Ocean Drainage System","The Mediterranean Sea Drainage System"],0,"The Zambezi, Juba, and Wabi Shebelle rivers are all major rivers of East/Southern Africa that flow into the Indian Ocean drainage system. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is considered as the turning point in the development of Geographic Information\nSystems (GIS)?",["The integration of GIS in many disciplines","The advancement of quantitative geography","The increasing demand of GIS from different users","The advancement of computer technology"],3,"The advancement of computer technology in the mid-to-late 20th century was the key turning point that allowed geographic data to be processed, analyzed, and visualized digitally, leading to modern GIS. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the implication of the low level of urbanization in Africa?",["Low rate of rural to urban migration","Low cost of urban transport facilities","Low living standard of urban population","Low rate of urban to urban migration"],3,"A low level of urbanization indicates that the majority of the population lives in rural areas with few urban centers, which naturally results in a low rate of urban-to-urban migration. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the type of land feature cut off from the sea by sand banks?",["Lagoon","Spit","Tombolo","Beach"],0,"A lagoon is a shallow body of coastal water that is partially or completely separated from the deep ocean by barrier islands, reefs, or sand banks. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following National Regional State of Ethiopia has the lowest percentage urban from the\nregional total population?",["Afar","SNNP","Somali","Tigray"],1,"The Southern Nations, Nationalities, and Peoples' Region (SNNPR) has historically had one of the lowest proportions of urban residents (around 8-10%) relative to its total population in Ethiopia.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following plays a decisive role to govern natural resources sustainably?",["Giving exclusive rights to the government in managing resources","Encouraging indigenous resource management systems","Prioritizing the participation of males in resource management","Fostering top-down decision making in resource management"],1,"Integrating and encouraging indigenous resource management systems plays a decisive role in achieving sustainable, community-supported resource governance.","2016 EC entrance"],["Among the most common woods of Ethiopia, which one has been traditionally used for making water pipes and\nbaskets?",["Kerero","Zigba","Bamboo","Olea"],2,"Bamboo stems are hollow and flexible, traditionally making them ideal in Ethiopia for manufacturing water transport pipes, baskets, mats, and household utensils.","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the main cause of conflict over natural resources such as the River Nile?",["Political","Social","Administrative","Legal"],0,"Conflicts over transboundary natural resources like the River Nile are primarily political and geopolitical, involving disagreements over water rights, sovereignty, and historical treaties.","2016 EC entrance"],["Among the following landforms, which one is formed when magma solidifies in a vertical or near vertical crack?",["Batholith","Laccolith","Sill","Dike"],3,"A dike (or dyke) is a discordant, sheet-like body of intrusive igneous rock formed when magma intrudes and solidifies in vertical or steeply inclined fractures.","2017 EC entrance"],["Closed contour with elongated shape and the value increasing towards the center without specific tips\nrepresents:",["Mountain","Plateau","Depression","Re- intrant"],1,"A plateau is represented by elongated, closed contour lines where values increase towards the center but lack a specific peak, indicating a flat-topped elevated landform.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is the most extensive land form in Africa?",["Plateaus","Plains","Hills","Mountains"],0,"Africa is frequently referred to as the 'plateau continent' because plateaus are the most dominant and extensive landform, covering the majority of its land area. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which land feature of Ethiopia separates the southeast highlands from the northern and southwestern\nhighlands?",["Eastern lowlands","Rift valley","Western lowlands","Central highlands"],1,"The Ethiopian Rift Valley runs diagonally across the country from northeast to southwest, clearly dividing the highlands into the northwestern and southeastern blocks.","2017 EC entrance"],["Sustainable development involved in the needs of the present without making a deal of:",["Past generation","Future generation","Present generation","Population"],1,"According to the Brundtland Report, sustainable development meets the needs of the present without compromising the ability of future generations to meet theirs.","2016 EC entrance"],["In which major African landform are the majority of the continent's famous national wildlife parks located?",["Sahel region","Tropical rain forest region","Sahara Desert","Savanna region"],3,"Most famous African wildlife parks (Serengeti, Maasai Mara, Kruger, Ngorongoro, Okavango) are in savanna regions, characterized by grasslands with scattered trees, abundant herbivores (zebra, wildebeest, elephant, giraffe), and predators (lion, leopard, hyena). The open vegetation allows wildlife viewing.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following countries lies in the Pacific Ring of Fire?",["Sweden","Botswana","Australia","Japan"],3,"Japan is located along the Pacific Ring of Fire, a major area in the basin of the Pacific Ocean where many earthquakes and volcanic eruptions occur due to plate subduction.","2017 EC entrance"],["What is the soil conservation measure that involves resting of arable land for a limited period of time called?",["Intercropping","Check dams","Fallowing","Limiting grazing"],2,"Fallowing is the traditional soil conservation technique where a field is left uncultivated (resting) for one or more growing seasons to allow the soil to naturally regain its nutrients and fertility.","2014 EC entrance"],["Despite many efforts, wild life resources of Africa are deteriorating from time to time. If you are asked to\nprioritize and implement conservation measures, which one is the most important one?",["Raising awareness of the community","Regulating the practice of illegal hunting","Establishing national parks and game reserves","Preserving the natural vegetation"],3,"Habitat loss is the primary driver of wildlife decline in Africa; therefore, preserving the natural vegetation (wildlife habitats) is the most critical and foundational conservation measure.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following distinguishes the regions of Africa?",["Central Africa is the most sparsely populated.","Northern Africa has the highest number of countries.","Eastern Africa is the smallest in terms of area.","Western Africa has the highest urban population."],0,"Central Africa is the most sparsely populated region of the continent due to extensive tropical rainforest environments, swampy terrains, and historically low density. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the type of corruption committed by a public official to make decisions by receiving money?",["Bribery","Theft","Burglary","Stealing"],0,"Bribery is the specific form of corruption where a public official accepts or solicits financial or other benefits to influence their official decisions or actions. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following Ethiopian lakes is classified as the Rift Valley Lake?",["Lake Hashenge","Lake Abaya","Lake Haik","Lake Tana"],1,"Lake Abaya is a major Rift Valley lake located in the southern main Ethiopian rift, whereas Lakes Tana, Haik, and Hashenge are highland lakes located outside the Rift Valley. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following refers to how energy from the sun is transmitted to the Surface of the earth?",["Radiation","Convection","Advection","Conduction"],0,"Solar energy travels through the vacuum of space to Earth in the form of electromagnetic waves, a process known as radiation.","2015 EC entrance"],["What kind of geological event occurred during the Precambrian Era in the Horn of Africa?",["Transgression and regression of sea","Denudation and peneplanation","Formation of the Rift Valley","Intensive volcanic activities"],1,"During the Precambrian Era, intense folding and mountain building occurred, which was followed by a long period of denudation and peneplanation that leveled the landscape into a flat tableland.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which factor is used to classify urban and rural land uses?",["Types of economic activities","relief","interests of the residences","types of soil"],0,"Urban and rural land uses are primarily classified based on the types of economic activities dominant in those areas, with rural areas focusing on primary activities (like agriculture) and urban areas on secondary and tertiary activities.","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the main reason that makes intra-continental trade to be low in Africa?",["Absence of common currency","Lack of political willingness","Limited access to sea transport","The diverse nature of the economy"],1,"Despite various treaties, a lack of political willingness to implement regional agreements, open borders, and reduce tariff barriers remains a primary obstacle to intra-continental trade in Africa.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which of the following was NOT used by Alfred Wegener as primary evidence to support his theory of\ncontinental drift?",["Fossil distribution across continents","Rock type and structural similarities","Paleomagnetic data from ocean floors","Coastline similarity (Jig-Saw-Fit)"],2,"Wegener (1912) used coastline fit, fossil evidence (Mesosaurus, Glossopteris), glacial deposits, and matching rock sequences across continents. Paleomagnetic data from ocean floors became available later (1950s-60s) and provided key evidence for seafloor spreading and plate tectonics, not Wegener's original work.","2018 EC entrance"],["What type of drought occurs when a soil moisture deficit happens consistently?",["Agricultural drought","Hydrological drought","Intermittent drought","Meteorological drought"],0,"Agricultural drought is specifically characterized by a deficit in soil moisture that is insufficient to meet crop water requirements, distinguishing it from meteorological (precipitation deficit) and hydrological (surface/subsurface water shortage) droughts.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which of the following statements is NOT a true reflection of the challenges faced by landlocked countries?",["Their commercial activities rarely face customs delays or transit interruptions","They depend on negotiated agreements for unrestricted passage through neighboring transit states","They are generally required to pay high transit fees to access coastal seaports","They lack direct territorial access to the sea for export-import trade"],0,"Landlocked countries face significant trade challenges including lack of sea access, high transit fees, and dependence on neighboring states for passage. The statement that their commercial activities rarely face customs delays or transit interruptions is false; in reality, they frequently experience bureaucratic delays, corruption, and infrastructure bottlenecks at border crossings and ports.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the major cause of Africa being unable to exploit its potential resources?",["Inadequate revenue from resources","Unfavorable climate","Inappropriate allocation of resources","Political instability"],3,"Political instability, along with a lack of capital and technology, is one of the most significant barriers preventing many African nations from safely, efficiently, and consistently exploiting their natural resource potential.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following country is found in the 'ring of fire' zone?",["United Kingdom","Peru","Norway","Brazil"],1,"Peru is situated along the western coast of South America, which directly borders the Pacific Plate and forms part of the highly seismically and volcanically active 'Pacific Ring of Fire'. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["During which geological era did the Pangea break into the Laurasia and the Gondwanaland?",["The Paleozoic Era","The Precambrian Era","The Cenozoic Era","The Mesozoic Era"],3,"The supercontinent Pangea began to break apart into Laurasia and Gondwanaland during the Mesozoic Era, specifically during the Triassic period.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is an environmental implication of population growth?",["Rapid depletion of natural resources","Improvement in the provision of transport services","Deterioration of social values","Increase in the number of unemployed people"],0,"The rapid depletion of natural resources is a direct environmental consequence of population growth, while poverty and unemployment are socio-economic implications.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which region of Africa lies both in the northern and southern hemispheres?",["Eastern Africa","Northern Africa","Southern Africa","Western Africa"],0,"The Equator crosses Eastern Africa (passing directly through Uganda, Kenya, and Somalia), dividing the region across both the Northern and Southern hemispheres.","2015 EC entrance"],["Globally which region is highly affected by HIV/AIDS?",["Latin America","Sub-Saharan Africa","Southeast Asia","Oceania"],1,"Sub-Saharan Africa remains the region most severely affected by HIV/AIDS, accounting for the vast majority of all global infections and related deaths.","2017 EC entrance"],["What is the effect of latitude on the climate of areas closer to the equator in the world? It causes them to have",["less intense insolation.","short daylight in summer.","high solar declination.","little seasonal change."],3,"Areas close to the equator experience high, near-vertical solar angles year-round, resulting in constant warm temperatures and very little seasonal change.","2018 EC entrance"],["Total population\nNumber of live birth in the year\nNumber of deaths below age of 1 year\nNumber of Immigrants\nNumber of Emigrants\nTotal death\nMale population\nWhat is the Net Migration Rate (NMR) of the region?",["7.6/1000","2.8/1000","4.8/1000 67,400,000 2,300,000 78,000 509,100 323,100 392,200 33,983,200","5.6/1000"],1,"Net Migration Rate = ((Immigrants - Emigrants) / Total Population) × 1000 = ((509,100 - 323,100) / 67,400,000) × 1000 = (186,000 / 67,400,000) × 1000 ≈ 2.76 per 1,000, which rounds to 2.8/1000.","2017 EC entrance"],["One of the following doesn’t explain the formation of a river capture?",["The pirate river has a steeper course and erodes its course as a result","Heavy erosion occurring on the pirate river’s side of the watershed","The rock on the sides of the victim river is soft","The victim river drain or erode the hard rock other side of pirate stream"],2,"If the rock on the sides of the victim river is soft, it would erode rapidly and deepen its own valley, making it harder for a pirate river to capture it. (1)","2016 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-history","name":"History","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["Which one of the following Nigerian City -States served as a major supplier of Slaves",["Gobir","Zamfira","Kano","Zazzau"],3,"Among the Hausa city-states, Zazzau (modern-day Zaria) was located in the southernmost region and served as the major supplier of slaves by raiding neighboring non-Hausa populations.","2016 EC entrance"],["All of the following are characterized by the strong hold of Shiism except;",["Lebanon","Saudi","Iran","India"],1,"Saudi Arabia is a staunchly Sunni nation governed by Wahhabi Islamic law and is not characterized by any strong hold of Shiism.","2016 EC entrance"],["What was the main goal of the Soviet Union during the Cold War period?",["To spread communist ideology.","To strengthen ties with the Capitalist countries.","To prevent the expansion of War.","To unite the two separated German states."],0,"The Soviet Union's primary goal during the Cold War was to spread communist ideology globally, expand its sphere of influence, and counter US-led capitalism. Strengthening ties with capitalists was opposite. Uniting Germany was not a main goal. Preventing war was secondary to ideological expansion. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["The Byzantine empire reached at its peak under the reign of",["Augustus Caesar","Justinian I","Remus","Romulus"],1,"The Byzantine Empire reached its golden age and peak territorial extent during the reign of Justinian I (527–565 AD), famous for his military conquests and his legal code (Corpus Juris Civilis).","2016 EC entrance"],["In which of the following anti-colonial movements was forced cotton production the major issue?",["The Mahdist Movement","The Urabi Pasha Rebellion","The Maji Maji Rebellion","The Mau Mau Movement"],2,"The Maji Maji Rebellion (1905–1907) in German East Africa was primarily triggered by colonial policies that forced the indigenous population to cultivate cotton for export under harsh conditions.","2014 EC entrance"],["Ethiopian state formation was begun around 1000 B.C. During the civilization of;",["Damot","Addi Seglemeni","Hawelti Melazo","Yeha"],0,"The earliest known state in the region of Ethiopia and Eritrea was D'mt (often written as Damot or Da'amat in textbooks), which emerged around 1000 B.C.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following was signed in 1941 by Roosevelt and Churchill that outlined the establishment of the\nUN?",["The Versailles Treaty","The Atlantic Charter","The Monroe Doctrine","The Sevres Treaty"],1,"The Atlantic Charter was signed in August 1941 by US President Franklin D. Roosevelt and British Prime Minister Winston Churchill. It outlined post-WWII goals, including the establishment of the United Nations (UN). The Sevres and Versailles treaties ended WWI. Monroe Doctrine (1823) was US foreign policy. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["On July 1871, Emperor Takla Giorgis was defeated by Kssa Mircha at the battle of;",["Segele","Chalanqo","Sarwuha","Asem"],3,"Emperor Takla Giorgis (Wagshum Gobeze) was defeated and captured by Kassa Mircha (later Emperor Yohannes IV) at the Battle of Assam (Asem) near Adwa in July 1871.","2016 EC entrance"],["What was the most important innovation that made the Industrial Revolution possible?",["Wind power","Hydro power","The massive production of coal","Steam power"],3,"Steam power was the innovation that made the Industrial Revolution possible. James Watt improved the steam engine in the 1780s, which freed factories from rivers and wind and later drove steamboats, steamships and railway locomotives. Coal is the tempting answer, but coal mattered because it fed the steam engines: it is the fuel, not the invention that changed production.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which of the following pair of European countries pioneered overseas expansion?",["Portugal and England","Spain and Portugal","Holland and Spain","Holland and England"],1,"Spain and Portugal led the voyages of the 15th and 16th centuries. Prince Henry the Navigator of Portugal and Queen Isabella of Spain paid for them, Vasco da Gama reached India in 1498 and Columbus reached America in 1492. Holland, Britain and France followed the two pioneers later, so any pair that names them is wrong.","2011 EC entrance"],["What economic measure was taken by Prussia as a major facilitator for unification by removing internal trade\nbarriers and creating economic unity?",["The Zollverein","The Austria-Prussian agreement","The Vienna agreement","The Continental System"],0,"The Zollverein was a German customs union established under Prussian leadership in 1834, eliminating internal tariffs and creating a single economic market. It laid the economic foundation for German political unification under Prussia by excluding Austria and fostering economic interdependence. Option D is correct. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["Among the French colonies of West Africa which of the following became independent in 1958 by voting 'No' to\ncontinued association with France?",["Mali","Senegal","Cameroon","Guinea"],3,"In the 1958 constitutional referendum, Guinea, led by Ahmed Sékou Touré, was the only French colony in West Africa to vote 'No' to joining the French Community, resulting in its immediate and complete independence.","2014 EC entrance"],["One of the following is believed to be the earliest state in the Horn of Africa region?",["Damat","Punt","Aksum","Meroe"],1,"The Land of Punt, recorded in ancient Egyptian expedition logs starting from the 3rd millennium BC, is recognized as the earliest documented state-like entity in the Horn of Africa region.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which Organ of the United Nation is responsible to assign an ad-hoc committees for a special mission?",["General Assembly","Trusteeship Council","Security Council","The Secretariat"],0,"Under the United Nations Charter, the General Assembly is empowered to establish various subsidiary organs, including ad-hoc committees, to study and report on specific international issues.","2018 EC entrance"],["What was the important principle approved at The Berlin Conference that was designed to facilitate the process\nof colonization in Africa?",["The principle of equitable distribution of colonies","The principle of peaceful occupation of colonies","The principle of effective occupation","The principle of the The White Man's Burden"],2,"The Berlin Conference of 1884 to 1885 set the principle of effective occupation. Article 35 of the Final Act said a power could claim African land only if it really held it: treaties with local rulers, its flag flying there, and an administration on the ground. Option A tempts you because the conference did try to keep the Europeans from fighting each other, but the rule written into the Act was effective occupation.","2013 EC entrance"],["Identify the battle that marked an end to the Napoleonic era in Europe;",["Waterloo","Trafalgar","Leipzig","Valmy"],0,"The Battle of Waterloo in 1815 marked the final defeat of Napoleon Bonaparte, ending his rule as Emperor of the French and bringing the Napoleonic era to a close.","2016 EC entrance"],["Identify the country which has achieved or attained its independence ahead of any other Balkan Nations.",["Greece","Montenegro","Bulgaria","Romania"],0,"Greece was the first nation in the Balkans to win its independence from the Ottoman Empire, which was formally recognized by the international community in 1830. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["What was the long-term effect of conflicts between the Christian and Adal sultanate from 1529-1543?",["The Christian highland kingdom expanded its territory.","Intermixing of ethnic and religious groups.","It completely abolished the trade of the region.","The highlands remained culturally isolated."],1,"The long-term effect of the Ethiopian-Adal War (under Ahmad Gragn) and subsequent Oromo migrations was significant intermixing of ethnic and religious groups in the Horn of Africa. The wars weakened both Christian and Muslim states, allowing Oromo populations to expand and integrate, leading to cultural and political realignment.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following countries believe in the\" Mandate of Heaven\"",["France","China","Greece","Britain"],1,"The 'Mandate of Heaven' is an ancient Chinese political and religious doctrine used to justify the rule of the Emperor of China, asserting that heaven bestows the right to rule on a just leader.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is referred as the birth place of Western civilization",["France","Germany","Bulgaria","Greece"],3,"Ancient Greece is widely recognized as the birthplace of Western civilization because of its foundational contributions to democracy, philosophy, science, literature, and art. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following southern states exercised extensive influence in areas south of the Abbay before the\n14th century?",["Damot","Enarea","Bizamo","Hadiya"],0,"Damot was the strong kingdom south of the Abay before the 14th century. Its best known ruler, Motalami, was powerful enough to press on the Christian kingdom in the 13th century, and Damot was later converted and reduced by the Solomonic kings. Option D fails on dates: Enarya became important later, and it was the Limmu Oromo takeover about 1710 that turned it into Limmu Enarya.","2015 EC entrance"],["The availability of one of the following is irreplaceable or a mandatory requirement in academic history. Which\none?",["Quantitative data","Written sources","Correct evidence","Oral traditions"],2,"Academic history stands on evidence that has been checked. The steps of writing history are collecting evidence, criticising the source, interpreting it and writing objectively. Written records, figures and oral tradition are only types of source. A history can be written without any one of them, but not without correct evidence.","2012 EC entrance"],["Identify the one that has achieved its independence as a result of the Balkan wars of 1912-13.",["Serbia","Montenegro","Greece","Albania"],3,"Albania declared its independence in 1912 during the First Balkan War, and this independence was recognized by the great powers in the 1913 Treaty of London.","2016 EC entrance"],["In which of the following aspects of French and European life did Napoleon influence as a model mark?",["Legal system","Bureaucratic system","Election system","Education system"],0,"Napoleon's lasting mark was the Civil Code of 1804. It put the law in one clear written book, secured equality before the law and property rights, and was carried into Italy, the Low Countries, Germany and beyond, where it shaped legal systems long after his fall. Option C is real but smaller. He did rebuild the French bureaucracy with prefects and a state bank, yet it is the code that other countries copied.","2017 EC entrance"],["Of the following, which event facilitated the partition of Africa in 1884-1885?",["The Vienna Congress","The Versailles Treaty","The Durban Conference","The Berlin Conference"],3,"The Berlin Conference (1884-1885), convened by Otto von Bismarck, established the rules for the partition (scramble) of Africa among European powers, including the principle of 'effective occupation.' The Treaty of Versailles (1919) ended WWI. Vienna Congress (1815) reorganized Europe after Napoleon. Durban Conference (2001) addressed racism.","2018 EC entrance"],["In which part of Africa was the civilization of the Shona people located?",["Eastern Africa","Northern Africa","Southern Africa","Western Africa"],2,"The Shona civilization, renowned for constructing the impressive stone-walled complex of Great Zimbabwe and establishing the Mutapa Empire, was located in Southern Africa.","2014 EC entrance"],["Where was the political and religious center of the Oromo people before they began their movement?",["Oda Bultum","Mada Walabu","Oda Bisil","Oda Malabu"],0,"Madda Walabu, on the Bale and Sidama borderlands, was the political and religious centre of the Oromo before the movement of the 16th century. The Abba Muda, the father of anointment, sat there, and delegates from all branches came to it as the central chaffe. The Oda names in the other options are real assembly sites, but they were set up later by particular branches after the movement had begun, such as Oda Nabee for the Tulama and Oda Bultum in Hararghe.","2017 EC entrance"],["18. Identify merchants of the long-distance trade of the 19th century who dominated the Northern Ethiopian\ntrade as far as the Red Sea",["the Safare","the Afkala","Argobba","the Jabarti"],3,"The Jabarti were northern Ethiopian Muslim merchants who dominated the trade routes leading to the Red Sea ports during the 19th century.","2016 EC entrance"],["All of the following served as a mobile courts from 1270-1636 until the emergence of Gondar as a permanent\ncapital city except;",["Chelenqo and Babile","wachacha and Bulga","Tegulet and Haiq","Menagesha and Furi"],0,"Chelenqo and Babile are located in eastern Ethiopia and were never mobile courts (temporary capitals) of the medieval Christian kingdom, unlike Tegulet, Bulga, Wachacha, and Menagesha. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["The flight of prophet Mohammed from Mecca to Medina was happened in the ;",["the 7th century A.D","10th century A.D","8th century A.D","11th century A.D"],0,"The Hijra, which was the migration of the Prophet Muhammad from Mecca to Medina, occurred in 622 A.D., falling in the 7th century A.D.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is introduced federal system of approach or governance in the history of the\ncountry?",["Emperor Yohannes IV","Emperor Menelik II","Emperor Teklegiorgis II","Emperor Tewodros II"],0,"Emperor Yohannes IV followed a decentralized or federal-like approach to governance, allowing regional rulers like Menelik of Shewa and Adal Tesema of Gojjam to maintain their local autonomy and titles in exchange for recognition of his imperial suzerainty.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following events was directly related to the immediate outbreak of the WWI?",["The British declaration of war against Germany","The German invasion against neutral Belgium","The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand","The Russian support for Serbia against Austro-Hungary"],2,"The assassination of Archduke Franz Ferdinand of Austria-Hungary by a Serbian nationalist in Sarajevo on June 28, 1914, was the immediate spark that triggered the diplomatic crisis leading to World War I.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following institutions in Ethiopia was rebuilt with the help of the US in the post-liberation\nperiod?",["The Imperial Board of Telecommunications.","The Parliament.","The Imperial Highway Authority.","The Imperial Body Guard."],2,"The Imperial Highway Authority was set up in 1951 to rebuild and extend the country's roads, and Americans directed it until it got its first Ethiopian manager in 1962. It belongs to what the textbook calls the American era, along with Ethiopian Air Lines and the Point Four programme. Option D is the trap: the Imperial Bodyguard was reorganised after 1941 with Swedish assistance, not American. Option C also received substantial American help, so read the question as asking which body the Americans actually ran.","2015 EC entrance"],["Of the following, which revolution was considered as a result of the First World War?",["the Russian Revolution","the English Revolution","the American Revolution","the French Revolution"],0,"The Russian Revolution (1917) occurred during WWI as a direct result of war-induced hardships: military defeats, food shortages, economic collapse, and Tsar Nicholas II's incompetence. The French (1789), English (17th century), and American (1776) revolutions occurred long before WWI.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which continents were connected to each other in the Triangular Trade?",["Asia, Europe and Africa","The Americas, Asia and Europe","Africa, Europe and the Americas","The Americas, Africa and Asia"],2,"The triangular trade linked Africa, Europe and the Americas across the Atlantic Ocean. Ships carried guns, cloth and spirits from Europe to Africa, enslaved Africans from Africa to the plantations of the Americas, and sugar, cotton and tobacco from the Americas back to Europe. Every option that names Asia fails, because Asia was not one of the three corners of this Atlantic circuit.","2011 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following Ethiopian states had an old tradition of digging trenches and ditches to defend itself\nfrom its enemy",["Enarya","Damot","Kaffa","Bizamo"],2,"The Kingdom of Kaffa had a highly developed defensive system that included digging deep trenches and ditches along its borders, secured by guarded gates known as kella.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following sources is categorized under Primary Sources?",["Biographies","travel documents","books and text books","Articles"],1,"Travel documents or travelogues written by contemporary travelers are primary sources because they provide first-hand, eyewitness evidence of the events and societies of the period.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which of the following people was partly assimilated into the Mecha Oromo and partly moved to Gojjam?",["Bizamo","Wajj","Ganz","Ennarya"],0,"The kingdom of Bizamo, located south of the Blue Nile (Abay), was heavily impacted by the Oromo population movements; its people were partly integrated into the Mecha Oromo and partly fled across the river into Gojjam. (1)","2018 EC entrance"]]},{"id":"g12-aptitude","name":"Scholastic Aptitude","group":"g12","college":"Grade 12 Entrance (ESSLCE)","q":[["She showed a blatant disregard for the rules.",["rebellious","respectful","obvious","hidden"],2,"A 'blatant' disregard refers to actions that are completely obvious, conspicuous, or flagrant, showing no attempt at concealment.","2014 EC entrance"],["Abraham Lincoln was the 16th American President who championed the _____ of the slave trade during the Civil \nwar against the separatist southern states.",["adoption","abolition","expansion","endorsement"],1,"'Abolition' means the formal act of ending or putting a stop to an institution, correctly describing Abraham Lincoln's efforts against slavery.","2017 EC entrance"],["GRAMMAR is to LANGUAGE as Culture is to:",["Fact","Society","Knowledge","Philosophy"],1,"Grammar represents the system of rules that structures a language, while culture represents the system of customs and values that structures a society.","2018 EC entrance"],["In how many different ways can the letters of the word 'CORPORATION' be arranged, so that vowels always\ncome together?",["50400","1440","810","2880"],0,"CORPORATION has 11 letters: the consonants C, R, P, R, T, N with R twice, and the vowels O, O, A, I, O with O three times. Tie the five vowels into one block, so 7 items are being arranged, and the repeated R divides the count: 7! 2520. Inside 2! = the block the five vowels arrange in 5! 20 ways. The two choices happen together, so the total is 2520 × 20 = 50400 = 3! . Option C is the trap for anyone who counts one of the two steps and stops there. ​ ​","2017 EC entrance"],["In September 2000, Ahmed was more than eleven times as old as his son Mustafa and in September 2009,\nAhmed was seven more than three times as old as Mustafa. How old was Mustafa in September 2000?",["12 years old","9 years old","7 years old","3 years old"],3,"Let A and M be their ages in 2000. In 2009, A + 9 = 3(M + 9) + 7, which simplifies to A = 3M + 25. Given A > 11M, we have 3M + 25 > 11M, leading to M < 3.125. The only option less than 3.125 is 3 years old (Option D).","2014 EC entrance"],["A large square pizza has 49 pieces (square pieces). Ali, Alemu and Abebe ate all the pieces in the ratio 4:2:1,\nrespectively. How many pieces did Alemu eat?",["10 Pieces","18 pieces","14 pieces","12 pieces"],2,"The total ratio parts are 4 + 2 + 1 = 7. Alemu ate 2/7 of the 49 pieces, which is equal to 14 pieces.","2014 EC entrance"],["What is the height of a building in meters, if the angle of elevation of the top of the building from a point 10\nmeters away from the ground floor of the building is 60°?",["5 ​ ​","5 3 ​ ​","10 3","10 3 3"],2,"Using the trigonometric tangent ratio for the right triangle formed by the building, the ground, and the line of sight, tan(60∘ ) = height . Since tan(60∘ ) = 3, the height of the building is 10 3 meters. 10 ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["What does “…change color according to their background” mean in the passage?",["evolutionary","camouflage","visibility","variation"],1,"The ability of an animal to blend into its environment by changing color is the definition of camouflage.","2018 EC entrance"],["TREES is to FOREST as Tower is to:",["City","Countryside","Landscape","Scenery"],0,"This is a part-to-whole analogy: many trees make up a forest, just as many buildings and towers make up a city.","2018 EC entrance"],["EMBARRASSED is to HUMILIATED as FRIGHTENED is to",["Terrified","Reckless","Courageous","Agitated"],0,"Humiliated is an extreme degree of being embarrassed, just as terrified is an extreme degree of being frightened.","2014 EC entrance"],["According to paragraph one, which of the following is not directly related to climate change?",["Protracted droughts","Displacement of people","Deteriorating health conditions","Fuel energy"],3,"Droughts, displacement, and deteriorating health are direct impacts (effects) of climate change mentioned in the introductory paragraph, whereas fuel energy is a cause, not a direct impact of climate change. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["CALF : COW :: LAMB : ?",["Horse","Goat","Deer","Sheep"],3,"A calf is the young offspring of a cow, just as a lamb is the young offspring of a sheep.","2018 EC entrance"],["She contracted COVID 19 easily because she was obese and had other preexisting diseases. The doctor said\nthat if she ___________________ obese, her chances of getting the disease would have been slim.",["Had been","were","had not been","were not"],2,"This is a third conditional sentence referring to a past hypothetical scenario; the conditional clause must use the past perfect tense (\"had not been\"). (1)","2012 EC entrance"],["Everyone respects the manager for his __________.",["integrity","elegance","strength","charisma"],0,"'Integrity' refers to the quality of being honest and having strong moral principles, which is the most universally respected attribute for a leader or manager in a professional environment.","2016 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the domain of g(x) = ln(1 − x) + ln x?",["(0, ∞)","R ∖ {−1, 0}","(1, ∞)","(0, 1)"],3,"For the function g(x) = ln(1 − x) + ln x to be defined, both arguments must be positive: 1 − x > 0 ⟹ x < 1 and x > 0. The intersection of these intervals is (0, 1). y","2017 EC entrance"],["Which word means the same as “counterfeit?”",["copy","match","robbery","fake"],3,"To be 'counterfeit' means to be made in imitation of something else with intent to deceive; 'fake' is a direct synonym.","2012 EC entrance"],["Town A: below = 36%, above = 64%. Below M:F = 4:5; above M:F = 2:3.\nIf the male students below standard level line for town A is 3000, then what is the students of females above\nstandard level of line in that town?",["6400","6200","7200","6800"],2,"Below the line the male to female ratio is 4 to 5, so the 3000 males are 49 of that group, making it 3000 × 94 = 6750 students. That group is 36 percent of the town, so the town holds 6750 ÷ 0.36 = 18750 students. Above the line sits the other 64 percent, which is 12000, and there the ratio is 2 to 3, so the females are 35 × 12000 = 7200. It is tempting to reach 12000 and halve it, but the above-line split is 2 to 3, so the females take three parts out of five. ​ ​ ​ (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is equal to the ratio 36 km/hr to 30 m/s?",["3 : 1","5 : 6","1 : 3","6 : 5"],2,"Converting 36 km/hr to m/s gives 36 × 1000 = 10 m/s. Thus, the ratio of 36 km/hr to 30 m/s is 10 : 30 = 1 : 3. 3600 ​","2017 EC entrance"],["If f(x) = x 2 - 5x + 1, then f(x+2) is equal to:",["Not given","x 2 - x - 6","x 2 - 3x + 1","x 2 - x - 5"],3,"To find f(x+2), substitute (x+2) into the function: f(x+2) = (x+2)^2 - 5(x+2) + 1 = x^2 + 4x + 4 - 5x - 10 + 1 = x^2 - x - 5.","2014 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the sum of all even natural numbers less than 99?",["5100","2,450","5050","2,550"],1,"The even natural numbers less than 99 are 2, 4, 6, ..., 98. This is an arithmetic progression with first term a = 2, common difference d = 2, and number of terms n = 49, yielding a sum of S = (49/2)*(2 + 98) = 2,450. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Common: _________; SLIGHT: SEVERE",["expected","dull","extraordinary","usual"],2,"Slight and severe are antonyms, so we need the antonym of common, which is extraordinary.","2016 EC entrance"],["EAGLE is to BIRD as ROSE is to ___________________",["ANIMAL","FLOWER","GENTLEMAN","BEAUTIFUL"],1,"An eagle is a specific type of bird, just as a rose is a specific type of flower.","2012 EC entrance"],["The ratio of the perimeter to the width of a rectangle is 5:1. If the area of the rectangle is 216 cm², what is the\nlength of the rectangle?",["12 cm","16 cm","14 cm","18 cm"],3,"The perimeter ratio P/W = 5/1 implies 2(L + W)/W = 5, which simplifies to 2L = 3W, or W = (2/3)L. Substituting this into the area formula L * W = 216 gives (2/3)L² = 216, which solves to L = 18 cm.","2015 EC entrance"],["The sum of the ages of the father and his son is equal to sixty years. Six years ago the age of the father was five \ntimes the age of the son. What will be the age of the son six years from now?",["23 years","19 years","20 years","22 years"],2,"Letting the father's and son's current ages be F and S , we have F + S = 60 and F − 6 = 5(S − 6), which gives S = 14. Thus, six years from now, the son will be 20 years old. 1 1","2013 EC entrance"],["Which continuation is right?\nI don't trust social medias. ___________",["Never can I and never I will","Never I have and never I will","I never have and I never will","I have never and I will never"],2,"\"I never have and I never will\" is the correct elliptical construction in English to express that one has never done something in the past and has no intention of doing it in the future.","2012 EC entrance"],["Consider the system of linear inequalities 4x-3y≤ 12 x + 2y > 6 Which one of the following belongs to the\nsolution set of the given system of linear inequalities?",["(0,3)","(1, 1)","(0,1)","(1, 4)"],3,"Substituting the point (1, 4) into the system gives 4(1) - 3(4) = -8 ≤ 12 and 1 + 2(4) = 9 > 6, both of which are true. Thus, (1, 4) belongs to the solution set.","2014 EC entrance"],["In a pseudo language called Vandu, dvt means work, gnafu means drives. gnafye means drivers. dvty means\nworker. gnadfaa means drove. What does dvtye gnadfaa mean in Vandu?",["Drivers drove.","Workers drove.","Driver drives.","Worker drives."],1,"The root 'dvt' means work, and suffix '-ye' denotes plural agent (workers). 'gnadfaa' means drove, so 'dvtye gnadfaa' means 'Workers drove.'","2016 EC entrance"],["A woman spent one fifth of her salary for clothing, two fifth her salary for different bills and 100 Birr for her\ntransport. After covering all these costs she is left with 4,500 Birr. What was the salary she received?",["10,500 Birr","13,500 Birr","11,500 Birr","12,500 Birr"],2,"Let x be the salary. The total money spent is (1/5)x + (2/5)x + 100 = (3/5)x + 100. Subtracting this from x gives the remainder: x - (3/5)x - 100 = 4500, which simplifies to (2/5)x = 4600, yielding x = 11,500 Birr.","2015 EC entrance"],["The electric poles were impregnated with chemical solutions for durability.",["washed","varnished","erected","saturated"],3,"'Impregnated' in this context means soaked or thoroughly imbued with a substance, which is synonymous with 'saturated'. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["What is the probability that a number selected at random from the first 50 natural numbers is prime and odd\nnumber?",["8/25","7/25","3/10","3/5"],1,"Among the first 50 natural numbers, there are 15 prime numbers. The only even prime is 2, leaving 14 odd prime numbers, so the probability is 14/50 = 7/25.","2012 EC entrance"],["The premature death of the president was shocking to the nation at large.",["untimely","glorious","long overdue","mysterious"],0,"The prefix 'pre-' means before, so 'premature' describes something occurring before the natural or expected time, which is synonymous with 'untimely'.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the coefficient of x² in the expansion of (x + 2/x)^{10}?",["4860","3360","3430","4230"],1,"The general term in the expansion is C(10, r) * x^{10-r} * (2/x)^r = C(10, r) * 2^r * x^{10-2r}. For the coefficient of x², we set 10 - 2r = 2, giving r = 4. The coefficient is C(10, 4) * 2^4 = 210 * 16 = 3360.","2015 EC entrance"],["The word ' Contemporary ' in the first line denotes:",["Concurrent time","Foreseeable future","Controversial","Glorious past"],0,"The word 'contemporary' refers to things happening, existing, or living at the same time, which is synonymous with concurrent time.","2015 EC entrance"],["The teacher admired the student's ____________ approach to research, showing diligence and critical thinking.",["Conventional","Uncaring","Scholarly","Negligent"],2,"The word 'scholarly' means relating to or characteristic of serious academic study, which perfectly aligns with showing diligence and critical thinking in research.","2018 EC entrance"],["The length of a rectangle is 3 units more than its width. If the width is increased by 4 units and the length is\ndecreased by 2 units then its area will increase by 10 square units. What will be the length of the rectangle?",["6 units","3 units","7 units","4 units"],0,"Let the width be w, so length is w + 3. The new area is (w + 4)(w + 1) = w^2 + 5w + 4, which is 10 units greater than the original area w^2 + 3w. Solving w^2 + 5w + 4 = w^2 + 3w + 10 gives w = 3, so the length of the rectangle is 3 + 3 = 6 units. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Liquid matters are characterized by volatility among other things.",["density","fluidity","acidity","velocity"],1,"Liquids are fundamentally characterized by their ability to flow and change shape easily, which is described as 'fluidity'. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["If 2x^{-0.25} = 8, then what is the value of x?",["1/256","1/64","1/32","1/16"],0,"Dividing both sides by 2 gives x^{-0.25} = 4, or x^{-1/4} = 4. Raising both sides to the power of -4 gives x = 4^{-4} = 1/256.","2015 EC entrance"],["Dida introduces Kaku as the daughter of the only son of his father's wife. How is Kaku related to Dida?",["Cousin","Aunt","Niece","Daughter"],3,"\"His father's wife\" refers to Dida's mother. Since Dida is a male (\"his\"), the \"only son\" of his mother is Dida himself, which makes the daughter of that only son Dida's daughter. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["A man throws a rock in a vertical upward trajectory with velocity of 7 m/s on 90 meters tall roof of his house. Its \nheight can be modeled using the quadratic function h(t) = -5t² + 7t + 90. At what approximate time does the rock\nhit the ground?",["3 second","5 second","4.7 second","6.7 second"],1,"Setting h(t) = −5t2 + 7t + 90 = 0 gives 5t2 − 7t − 90 = 0. Factoring or using the quadratic formula, we find the = 5 seconds. positive solution t = 7+ 49+1800 = 7+43 10 10 ​ ​ ​","2016 EC entrance"],["Tickets numbered 1 to 20 are mixed up and then a ticket is drawn at random. What is the probability that the\nticket drawn has a number which is a multiple of 3 or 5?",["1/2","2/5","9/20","8/15"],2,"In the range 1 to 20, the multiples of 3 are {3, 6, 9, 12, 15, 18} (6 numbers) and the multiples of 5 are {5, 10, 15, 20} (4 numbers). Since 15 is counted twice, the number of successful outcomes is 6 + 4 - 1 = 9, giving a probability of 9/20.","2018 EC entrance"],["By selling a book for 258 birr a publisher gains 20% profit. For how much should the sell it to gain 30% profit?",["379.5 birr","269.5 birr","369.8 birr","279.5 birr"],3,"A selling price of 258 birr with 20% profit gives a cost price of 258/1.2 = 215 birr. To gain a 30% profit, the publisher must sell it for 215 × 1.3 = 279.5 birr.","2014 EC entrance"],["Some African countries suffer from regular drought and famine.",["Perpetual","Constant","Frequent","Unpredictable"],2,"In the context of recurring natural phenomena like drought, 'regular' is synonymous with 'frequent', meaning happening often or at short intervals. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Based on the same seminar scheduling conditions, which of the following is not possible?",["D on Thursday","C on Friday","A on Thursday","E on Wednesday"],0,"From the deduced schedule, D is scheduled on Tuesday and A is scheduled on Thursday; therefore, having D scheduled on Thursday is not possible.","2018 EC entrance"],["The starting cost of getting a certain service is 110 Birr. If you have to pay 12 Birr per hour for each additional\nservice you get, how long a time you use the service for 266 Birr payment",["11 hours","13 hours","12 hours","10 hours"],1,"The cost function is C(t) = 110 + 12t. Setting C(t) = 266 gives 12t = 156, which solves to t = 13 hours.","2015 EC entrance"],["The receptionist apologized for the delay , explaining that it had been a hectic day.",["urgency","hustle","rush","wait"],2,"'Hectic' means full of frantic, rushed activity, so 'rush' is the most appropriate synonym among the given choices.","2018 EC entrance"],["The word timidly in paragraph 1, line 2 is synonymous with:",["angrily","timely","bravely","nervously"],3,"'Timidly' means in a manner that shows a lack of courage or confidence, which is synonymous with 'nervously'.","2016 EC entrance"],["CARAVAN: DESERT; Perch: _________",["Terrestorial","Aquatic","Tropical","Aerial"],1,"A caravan is typically found in a desert environment, while a perch (a type of fish) is found in an aquatic environment.","2015 EC entrance"],["Five seminars A, B, C, D, and E are scheduled from Monday to Friday, one each day. Conditions: A is scheduled\nbefore C. D is scheduled after B. E is scheduled on Wednesday. A is placed before Friday immediately after E.\nWhich of the following is the correct order of seminars?",["B, D, E, A, C","D, B, E, A, C","E, B, D, A, C","B, E, A, D, C"],0,"Since E is scheduled on Wednesday and A is placed immediately after E, A is on Thursday. Since A is before C, C must be on Friday. B is scheduled before D, leaving B on Monday and D on Tuesday, resulting in the order B, D, E, A, C.","2018 EC entrance"],["If f(x) and g(x) are logarithmic functions whose bases are reciprocals of each other, then which one of the\nfollowing statements is true?",["They have opposite signs for all x ≠ 1.","They can never have equal values for any x.","There are some equal values of x for which both f(x) and g(x) are positive.","They have reciprocal values for all x."],0,"If the bases of f(x) and g(x) are reciprocals, we can write f(x) = log_b(x) and g(x) = log_{1/b}(x) = -log_b(x). Thus, g(x) = f(x), meaning they have opposite signs for all x ≠ 1 (where both are equal to 0).","2018 EC entrance"],["The height(h) in meters of an object thrown upwards as a function of time(t) is given by h(t)=-16t2 +96t+ 112.\nWhat is the maximum height that the object can reach?",["288 m","256 m","144 m","400 m"],1,"The height function h(t) = -16t^2 + 96t + 112 is a downward-opening parabola whose maximum height occurs at the vertex, t = -b/(2a) = -96/(2 * -16) = 3 seconds. Substituting t = 3 into the function gives h(3) = -16(9) + 96(3) + 112 = 256 meters. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["The man vehemently denied all the charges of killing that were brought against him.",["carelessly","hysterically","devoutly","forcefully"],3,"The word 'vehemently' means passionately, intensely, or with great force; thus, 'forcefully' is the closest synonym.","2012 EC entrance"],["Practically, very little work could be completed in the last week as it was _____",["a very hectic week","a very busy week","full of working days","full of holidays"],3,"If a week is full of holidays, official and professional operations are closed, which logically explains why practically very little work could be completed. (1)","2014 EC entrance"],["CAR is to TRANSPORTATION as GAME is to ___________________",["ENTERTAINMENT","MANIPULATION","FOOTBALL","INFORMATION"],0,"A car is a primary means of transportation, while a game is a primary means of entertainment.","2012 EC entrance"],["The new trained worker was fast becoming an indispensable member of the technique department , so they had \nno choice but to offer him a higher salary to stay on.",["useless","crucial","creative","active"],1,"\"Indispensable\" means absolutely necessary or essential, making \"crucial\" the closest synonym.","2016 EC entrance"],["_____ : soldier; GOWN: PHYSICIAN.",["tent","army","uniform","gun"],2,"The analogy is item of clothing worn by a profession: a physician wears a gown, and a soldier wears a uniform.","2016 EC entrance"],["The population of a certain colony of insects will double in size every year. The population at the beginning was\nestimated to be 3,150. If p represents the population after n years, then which one of the following equation\nrepresents the class's model of the population after n years?",["p(n) = 3, 150(2)n−1","p(n) = 3, 150(2)n","p(n) = 2(3, 150)n−1","p(n) = 2(3, 150)n"],1,"With an initial population of 3,150 that doubles every year, the population after n years is given by the exponential model p(n) = 3, 150(2)n . (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["Quantity A Quantity B 20% of 80 30% of 60",["The relationship cannot be determined.","The two quantities are equal.","Quantity A is greater than quantity B.","Quantity B is greater than quantity A."],3,"Quantity A is 20% of 80 = 16, while Quantity B is 30% of 60 = 18. Thus, Quantity B is greater than Quantity A.","2016 EC entrance"],["Town O: percentage below = 16%, so above = 84%. Above M:F = 3:2.\nWhat will be the approximate number of females above standard level of line in town O if it is known that the\nstudents of town O is 5500?",["1843","1848","1578","1484"],1,"16 percent of town O is below the line, so 84 percent is above it: 0.84 × 5500 = 4620 students. Above the line the males and females stand in the ratio 3 to 2, which is 5 parts, and the females hold 2 of them: 25 × 4620 = 1848. It is tempting to reach for 35 because 3 is written first in the ratio, but 3 is the male share and the question asks for the females. ​ ​","2017 EC entrance"],["As soon as all the indispensable forms have been filled out, we will process our applications. Choose a word that \nbest substitutes 'indispensable'.",["Requisite","Imprecise","Nonessential","Tentative"],0,"\"Indispensable\" means absolutely necessary or essential. \"Requisite\" is the best substitute as it means made necessary by particular circumstances or regulations.","2018 EC entrance"],["SPEED is to FAST as TEMPERATURE is to __________",["CLIMATE","WARM","ICE","THERMOMETER"],1,"Fast is a characteristic descriptor of a high speed, and warm is a characteristic descriptor of a moderate-to-high temperature.","2013 EC entrance"],["He has reached across the world, fomenting violence against the west.",["planning","instigating","negating","subduing"],1,"\"Fomenting\" means instigating or stirring up an undesirable or violent sentiment, making \"instigating\" the closest synonym.","2013 EC entrance"],["FOOD: LIVELIHOOD; Accountability:",["Dictatorship","Friendship","Relationship","Leadership"],3,"Food is a fundamental prerequisite for livelihood, just as accountability is a fundamental prerequisite for sound leadership.","2017 EC entrance"],["LAUGHTER: DELIGHT; ________: discontent",["satisfaction","sorrow","complaint","excitement"],2,"Laughter is an outward vocal/physical expression of delight, while a complaint is an expression of discontent.","2016 EC entrance"],["As used in the passage, what is the meaning of the word \"imperative\" ?",["conditional","optional","tentative","compulsory"],3,"The word 'imperative' means of vital importance, crucial, or mandatory, which is synonymous with 'compulsory'.","2016 EC entrance"],["The Indian population is predominantly herbivorous in its dietary tradition.",["non-alcoholic","omnivorous","carnivorous","vegetarian"],3,"'Herbivorous' describes an organism that feeds on plants, which in the context of human dietary traditions is synonymous with 'vegetarian'.","2018 EC entrance"],["How can an air pollution-free environment be created for the new generation?",["Tackling the causes of air pollution from the source","By restricting private use of car","By planting trees every year","By devising rules and regulations"],0,"Tackling the causes of air pollution from the source is the most fundamental, comprehensive, and effective way to create a pollution-free environment, encompassing all other partial measures.","2016 EC entrance"],["Potent: powerful: Lethal:______",["flagrant","crass","mean-spirited","deadly"],3,"\"Potent\" and \"powerful\" are synonyms, meaning \"lethal\" must be paired with its synonym, which is \"deadly\".","2016 EC entrance"],["The inhabitants of the island were barbarians who have never lived in the modern world.",["bad","hate","civilized","cruel"],2,"'Barbarians' refers to uncivilized people who do not live in the modern world. The exact opposite of this term in this context is 'civilized'.","2014 EC entrance"],["Unethical work habits jeopardize individuals' development efforts and a country's overall growth potential.",["speed-up","accelerate","facilitate","detriment"],3,"Jeopardize means to put into a situation in which there is danger of loss, harm, or failure; detriment (used here as harm/damage) is the closest synonym.","2016 EC entrance"],["The price of 10 chairs is equal to that of 4 tables. The price of 15 chairs and 2 tables together is Birr 400,000.\nWhat is the total price of 12 chairs and 3 tables?",["388,000","384,000","390,000","375,000"],2,"From 10C = 4T, we get T = 2.5C. Substituting this into 15C + 2T = 400,000 gives 15C + 5C = 400,000, so C = 20,000 and T = 50,000. Therefore, 12C + 3T = 12(20,000) + 3(50,000) = 390,000.","2015 EC entrance"],["On bad days I even felt ___; I just wanted to kill myself.",["suicidal","pleased","causal","poisoned"],0,"Desiring to end one's own life is the definition of feeling 'suicidal'.","2016 EC entrance"],["He inherited a large amount of fortune from his parents. So, he lives a very lavish lifestyle.",["extravagant","humble","stingy","spartan"],0,"'Lavish' means using or giving in great amounts, or expensive and luxurious, which is synonymous with 'extravagant'.","2012 EC entrance"],["PRECAUTION is to ACCIDENT as CLEANLINESS is to ________",["Disease","Filthy","Treatment","Garbage"],0,"Taking precaution is a preventive measure against an accident, just as maintaining cleanliness is a preventive measure against disease.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which of the following linear inequalities define the domain of\nx − y − 2 + log(x + y − 4) ?\n​",["x − 2 ≤ y < x − 4","x − 4 < y ≤ x − 2","x − 2 ≤ y < 4 − x","4 − x < y ≤ x − 2"],3,"For the square root to be defined, x − y − 2 ≥ 0 ⟹ y ≤ x − 2. For the logarithm to be defined, x + y − 4 > 0 ⟹ y > 4 − x. Combining these gives the domain 4 − x < y ≤ x − 2. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["As it contains students from diverse cultural backgrounds, the class is a highly _______ one.",["consistent","homogenous","heterogeneous","invariable"],2,"The term 'heterogeneous' means consisting of diverse or dissimilar ingredients or constituents, which perfectly describes a class with students from diverse cultural backgrounds.","2016 EC entrance"],["ARCHAEOLOGIST is related to REMAINS in the same way as _____ is related to REASONS.",["anarchist","analogist","scientist","linguist"],1,"An archaeologist is a specialist who studies or works with physical remains; similarly, an analogist is a person who reasons or works with analogies (reasons).","2015 EC entrance"],["Lions are rather reticent about expanding their energy in hunting. More than three quarters of kills are made by\nlionesses holding front position and carefully scanning ahead. The cubs lag playfully behind and the males bring\nup the rear and walk slowly with their massive heads nodding with each step as if they were bored with the\nwhole matter. With lionesses' busy hunting, the male functions as guard for the cubs, protecting them\nparticularly from hyenas.\nAccording to the passage how the lionesses hunt their prey?",["reticently","reluctantly","cautiously","carelessly"],2,"The passage states that the lionesses make the kills by \"carefully scanning ahead,\" which means they hunt cautiously. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["As more people settle on areas previously inhabited by wild animals, most of such animals become __________.",["domesticated","endangered","evacuated","frightened"],1,"As humans encroach on and settle in wildlife habitats, the lack of space and resources causes these wild animals to become 'endangered'.","2016 EC entrance"],["DOGMA : RELIGIOUS :: Ideology :",["Theoretical","Hypothetical","Physiological","Political"],3,"Dogma is a characteristic system of authoritative tenets in a religious context, while an ideology is a corresponding system of beliefs in a political context.","2018 EC entrance"],["WILDFIRE; DEFORESTATION; Drought:______",["Desertification","Flooding","Thunderbolt","Landslide"],0,"A wildfire leads to deforestation, and in a similar cause-and-effect relationship, a prolonged drought leads to desertification.","2015 EC entrance"],["Learning to swim was not easy for me, but in the end my ___; paid off.",["strength","experience","tolerance","persistence"],3,"The sentence describes overcoming a difficult task through continued effort, making 'persistence' the most appropriate choice.","2016 EC entrance"],["The practice of tax evasion is harmful to the development of a nation.",["resilience","avoidance","conviction","endorsement"],1,"'Tax evasion' is the illegal non-payment or 'avoidance' of paying taxes.","2015 EC entrance"],["Which of the following is a word in English formed from three consecutive letters?",["bead","feed","face","bad"],1,"The word 'feed' contains the letters F, E, and D, which are three consecutive letters of the alphabet (D, E, F). (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["If 8% of a number is 150, then what is the number?",["1875","1225","1625","1475"],0,"Let the number be x. Since 0.08 * x = 150, we solve for x by dividing 150 by 0.08, which yields 1875.","2015 EC entrance"],["COBBLER is to SHOE as CONTRACTOR is to",["Boot","Horse","Stone","Building"],3,"A cobbler is a professional who makes or repairs shoes, and a contractor is a professional who builds or repairs buildings.","2014 EC entrance"],["According to the passage, what does the word vices most likely denote?",["strengths","ambitions","weaknesses","deputies"],2,"In most contexts involving personal character and professional transitions, 'vices' refers to moral faults or personal weaknesses.","2017 EC entrance"],["Surplus: abundance:: deficit: _____",["amount","enough","efficiency","shortage"],3,"\"Surplus\" and \"abundance\" are synonyms. Therefore, the synonym for \"deficit\" is \"shortage\".","2016 EC entrance"],["What is the nature of the roots of the equation x2 − 3x + 3 = 0?",["Repeated real roots","Distinct real roots","No real roots","one root rational"],2,"The discriminant of the quadratic equation is D = b2 − 4ac = (−3)2 − 4(1)(3) = 9 − 12 = −3. Since D < 0, the equation has no real roots.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following strategies is NOT a democratic aspect of development?",["Top-down approach","Respect for cultural diversity","Empowerment of the people","Integrating social and economic parameters"],0,"A top-down approach involves decisions made solely by authorities at the top without public consultation, which runs contrary to democratic, participatory development.","2015 EC entrance"],["The value of (0.96³ - 0.1³) / (0.96² + 0.96×0.1 + 0.1²) is equal to:",["0.86","0.95","1.06","0.97"],0,"Using the algebraic identity (a³ - b³) / (a² + ab + b²) = a - b, we substitute a = 0.96 and b = 0.1 to obtain 0.96 - 0.1 = 0.86. (1)","2015 EC entrance"],["DESCRIBE: PLACE; _________: idea",["tell","think","explain","give"],2,"One describes a place to represent its characteristics, and one explains an idea to make its meaning clear.","2016 EC entrance"],["BOOK : PUBLISHER :: FILM : ?",["Writer","Director","Producer","Editor"],2,"A publisher is responsible for the production and distribution of a book, while a producer is responsible for the overall production and financing of a film.","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the contradictory term for the word “prey”?",["Animal","Predator","Moth","Chameleon"],1,"In ecological terms, 'predator' (the hunter) is the direct counterpart or opposite of 'prey' (the hunted).","2018 EC entrance"],["DREAM: SHATTERED; Promises: ________",["Denied","Broken","fulfilled","Cancelled"],1,"This is a collocation analogy: we speak of 'shattered dreams' when they fail, and 'broken promises' when they are not kept.","2015 EC entrance"],["The monthly telephone bill of Getachew was Birr 400 and it increases by 10% after 12 months, and another 20%\nincrease is applied six months later. What is the price of getachew's telephone bill after 18 months?",["528 Birr","489 Birr","520 Birr","430 Birr"],0,"After 12 months, the bill increases by 10% to 400 * 1.10 = 440 Birr. Six months later, another 20% increase on 440 yields 440 * 1.20 = 528 Birr.","2012 EC entrance"],["same table\nWhat is the difference in the number of 35hp computers sold in 2001 and 2005?",["24000","35000","39000","28000"],2,"Read down the 35hp column: 84 thousand in 2001 and 45 thousand in 2005. The difference is 84 − 45 = 39 thousand, and the heading says the table is written in thousands, so the answer is 39000 computers. Option C is the trap as a rounder looking figure, but the two entries in the table give 39 thousand exactly. (1)","2017 EC entrance"],["Mount is to horse as ______ is to train",["lift","ride","drive","board"],3,"To get onto a horse is to \"mount\" it, while the appropriate action to get onto a train is to \"board\" it.","2016 EC entrance"],["TEAM: PLAYER: _____ : Member",["Crew","Musician","Vocalist","Trainer"],0,"A player is a constituent of a team, just as a member is a constituent of a crew.","2016 EC entrance"],["How many 4-letter words, with or without meaning, can be formed out of the letters of the word 'LOGARITHMS',\nif repetition of letters is not allowed?",["40","5040","400","2540"],1,"The word 'LOGARITHMS' contains 10 distinct letters. The number of 4-letter words that can be formed without repetition is given by the permutation P(10, 4) = 10 × 9 × 8 × 7 = 5040.","2018 EC entrance"],["If x = 50% of 30 and y = 30% of 15, then which of the following is true?",["x is less than y.","x and y are equal.","The product between x and y cannot be determined.","y is less than x."],3,"Since x = 0.50 * 30 = 15 and y = 0.30 * 15 = 4.5, we can clearly see that y is less than x.","2012 EC entrance"],["I: Haven't you seen this film? ___________________",["Yes, I haven't","No, I have","Yes, I have","Yes, have I"],2,"In English, a negative question is answered affirmatively (\"Yes, I have\") if the speaker indeed has done the action, matching the factual status of the event.","2012 EC entrance"],["If f (x) and g(x) are n and m degree polynomial functions respectively and h(x) is the product of f (x) and\ng(x), then which one of the following is NOT true about h(x)?",["It has at most m + n x-intercepts.","It has at most n + m roots.","It has at most m + n y-intercepts.","It has at most n + m − 1 turning points."],2,"Every polynomial function has exactly one y-intercept, which is the point (0, h(0)), so stating that it has at most m + n y-intercepts is not a correct descriptor of the function's degree-dependent constraints.","2015 EC entrance"],["The _____ of Africans into Western Christianity was the byproduct of Western colonialism.",["dehumanization","trafficking","conversion","exploitation"],2,"'Conversion' is the standard term for the process of changing or being brought into a new religion, fitting the context of adopting Western Christianity.","2017 EC entrance"],["Ali is all the time gluttonous to explore a wide range of topics, seeking to learn more and never satisfied with just \nthe basics. Choose a word that best substitutes 'gluttonous'.",["Disinterested","Limited","Excessive","Voracious"],3,"In this context, \"gluttonous\" is used metaphorically to describe an insatiable eagerness or appetite for knowledge. \"Voracious\" is the perfect synonym for this, often used in phrases like \"a voracious reader\" or \"voracious learner\".","2018 EC entrance"],["What is the sum of all natural numbers between 12 and 300 which are divisible by 8?",["5256","4120","5616","4236"],2,"The natural numbers between 12 and 300 that are divisible by 8 form an arithmetic progression starting at 16 and ending at 296, with a common difference of 8. The number of terms is n = (296 − 16)/8 + 1 = 36, and their sum is S36 = 36 (16 + 296) = 18 × 312 = 5616. 2 ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["Let f ( 23 x − 43 ) = 5x3 + 16x2 + 2x + 1, and x be a real number. Consider the two quantities A and B given\nbelow. Quantity A Quantity B f 600\n​\n​",["The two quantities are equal.","A relationship cannot be determined.","Quantity A is greater than Quantity B.","Quantity A is less than Quantity B."],2,"To find f (2), we set 23 x − 43 = 2 ⟹ x = 5. Evaluating the polynomial at x = 5 gives f (2) = 5(5)3 + 16(5)2 + 2(5) + 1 = 625 + 400 + 11 = 1036. Since 1036 > 600, Quantity A is greater than Quantity B. ​ ​ (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["The ______ forests in western Ethiopia, accompanied by the shrimps and singing of birds and the fresh breeze\nare really inspirational.",["abandoned","deserted","tranquil","empty"],2,"The context of singing birds and a fresh breeze suggests a peaceful environment, making 'tranquil' the correct adjective for the forests. (1)","2016 EC entrance"],["PROLOGUE is to INTRODUCTION as EPILOGUE is to ________",["Chapter","Beginning","Conclusion","Ending"],2,"A prologue serves as an introduction to a literary work, while an epilogue serves as the conclusion. This establishes a clear relationship of structural equivalence.","2018 EC entrance"],["Statement: 'All mathematicians are logical thinkers. Some logical thinkers are not philosophers.' Conclusions: I.\nSome mathematicians are not philosophers. II. All mathematicians are philosophers. III. Some logical thinkers are\nphilosophers.",["Only conclusion III follows","Only conclusion I follows","Only conclusion II follows","Neither conclusion follows"],3,"\"All mathematicians are logical thinkers\" puts every mathematician inside the larger group of logical thinkers. \"Some logical thinkers are not philosophers\" tells you about a part of that larger group, and that part need not contain a single mathematician, so conclusion I is not secure. Conclusion II claims something the statements never say. Conclusion III fails too, because \"some are not\" gives no promise that any of them are. With all three unsupported, the answer is that neither conclusion follows. Conclusion I is the tempting one because it looks like a chain, but a chain would need the \"some\" statement to be about mathematicians in the first place.","2017 EC entrance"],["Harvard is one of the most prestigious universities in the USA.",["privileged","admired","furnished","expensive"],1,"'Prestigious' means inspiring respect and admiration, making 'admired' the best synonym here.","2017 EC entrance"],["Which word is most nearly similar in meaning to DILIGENT?",["Careless","Lazy","Negligent","Hardworking"],3,"Diligent means showing care and conscientiousness in one's work or duties, making 'hardworking' its closest synonym. (1)","2018 EC entrance"],["If you want your country to register economic development, it is __________ that you deal with corruption first.",["imperative","arguable","regrettable","possible"],0,"'Imperative' means of vital importance or crucial. Dealing with corruption is a crucial prerequisite for registering sustainable economic development.","2016 EC entrance"],["Student X and student Y have 2000 Birr. If 15\nof X's share is equal to 25 of Y's share, how much amount does Y\nhave?\n​",["1500 Birr","1200 Birr ​","1100 Birr","800 Birr"],3,"4 From the given relations, 15 X = 25 Y ⟹ X = 1.5Y . Substituting into X + Y = 2000 yields 2.5Y = 2000, which gives Y = 800 Birr. ​ ​","2013 EC entrance"],["Choose the word or phrase that is nearly OPPOSITE IN MEANING as SUBJUGATE.",["Protest","Liberate","Conquer","Oppress"],1,"To subjugate means to bring under domination or control, and its opposite is to liberate, which means to set free.","2018 EC entrance"],["Which one of the following is the sequence (Gn )∞\nn=1 defined recursively by G8 = 384 and Gn = 2G(n−1) for\neach n ≥ 1?\n​",["7, 14, 28, 56, 112 ...","2, 4, 8, 16, 32 ...","3, 6, 12, 24, 48 ...","9, 18, 36, 72, 144 ... ​ ​ ​ ​"],2,"For the geometric sequence with Gn = 2Gn−1 , the common ratio is r = 2. Given G8 = 384, the first term is G1 = 384/27 = 384/128 = 3, leading to the sequence 3, 6, 12, 24, 48, …. ​ ​ ​ ​","2015 EC entrance"],["The designer window treatment in her house, installed 17 years ago, were",["unnecessary","outmoded","unimportant","outlawed"],1,"An item installed 17 years ago is likely to be old-fashioned or no longer in style, which is defined as 'outmoded'.","2014 EC entrance"],["The table shows the number of different categories of electronic devices sold by a company over five years (in\nthousands).\nYear\nLaptops\nTablets\nSmartphones\nSmart watches\nHeadphones\n2013 120\n80\n350\n60\n190\n2014 150\n95\n420\n75\n210\n2015 170\n110\n460\n90\n230\n2016 200\n130\n520\n105\n260\n2017 230\n150\n610\n120\n290\nThe number of smart watches sold in 2015 is what percentage of the headphones sold in 2016?",["40%","36% Total 800 950 1060 1215 1400","34.6%","30%"],2,"Smart watches sold in 2015 were 90 thousand, and headphones sold in 2016 were 260 thousand. So the answer is 90 × 100 = 34.6%. Option C, 36%, is what rounding too early gives you, so carry the division out: 90 ÷ 260 = 0.346. 260 The other common slip is taking both figures from the same year, when the question deliberately names 2015 for one and 2016 for the other. ​","2018 EC entrance"],["same\nWhich of the following shows the correct order of the children in age from the youngest to the oldest?",["Lemma, Tena, Tolani, Gile, and Abebe.","Abebe, Gile, Tolani, Tena, and Lemma.","Lemma, Tolani, Tena, Gile, and Abebe.","Abebe, Gile, Tena, Tolani and Lemma."],0,"The children's birth order from oldest to youngest is Abebe (1st), Gile (2nd), Tolani (3rd), Tena (4th), and Lemma (5th). Reversing this gives the youngest-to-oldest order: Lemma, Tena, Tolani, Gile, and Abebe. (1)","2015 EC entrance"]]}];